-- WEB verses (4505). Requires books and chapters first.
insert into public.verses (chapter_id, number, osis_ref, text)
select c.id, x.verse, x.ref, x.body
from (values
('1KI', 7, 20, '1KI.7.20', 'There were capitals above also on the two pillars, close by the belly which was beside the network. There were two hundred pomegranates in rows around the other capital.'),
('1KI', 7, 21, '1KI.7.21', 'He set up the pillars at the porch of the temple. He set up the right pillar and called its name Jachin; and he set up the left pillar and called its name Boaz.'),
('1KI', 7, 22, '1KI.7.22', 'On the tops of the pillars was lily work. So the work of the pillars was finished.'),
('1KI', 7, 23, '1KI.7.23', 'He made the molten sea ten cubits from brim to brim, round in shape. Its height was five cubits; and a line of thirty cubits encircled it.'),
('1KI', 7, 24, '1KI.7.24', 'Under its brim around there were buds which encircled it for ten cubits, encircling the sea. The buds were in two rows, cast when it was cast.'),
('1KI', 7, 25, '1KI.7.25', 'It stood on twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east; and the sea was set on them above, and all their hindquarters were inward.'),
('1KI', 7, 26, '1KI.7.26', 'It was a hand width thick. Its brim was worked like the brim of a cup, like the flower of a lily. It held two thousand baths.'),
('1KI', 7, 27, '1KI.7.27', 'He made the ten bases of bronze. The length of one base was four cubits, four cubits its width, and three cubits its height.'),
('1KI', 7, 28, '1KI.7.28', 'The work of the bases was like this: they had panels; and there were panels between the ledges;'),
('1KI', 7, 29, '1KI.7.29', 'and on the panels that were between the ledges were lions, oxen, and cherubim; and on the ledges there was a pedestal above; and beneath the lions and oxen were wreaths of hanging work.'),
('1KI', 7, 30, '1KI.7.30', 'Every base had four bronze wheels and axles of bronze; and its four feet had supports. The supports were cast beneath the basin, with wreaths at the side of each.'),
('1KI', 7, 31, '1KI.7.31', 'Its opening within the capital and above was a cubit. Its opening was round like the work of a pedestal, a cubit and a half; and also on its opening were engravings, and their panels were square, not round.'),
('1KI', 7, 32, '1KI.7.32', 'The four wheels were underneath the panels; and the axles of the wheels were in the base. The height of a wheel was a cubit and half a cubit.'),
('1KI', 7, 33, '1KI.7.33', 'The work of the wheels was like the work of a chariot wheel. Their axles, their rims, their spokes, and their hubs were all of cast metal.'),
('1KI', 7, 34, '1KI.7.34', 'There were four supports at the four corners of each base. Its supports were of the base itself.'),
('1KI', 7, 35, '1KI.7.35', 'In the top of the base there was a round band half a cubit high; and on the top of the base its supports and its panels were the same.'),
('1KI', 7, 36, '1KI.7.36', 'On the plates of its supports and on its panels, he engraved cherubim, lions, and palm trees, each in its space, with wreaths all around.'),
('1KI', 7, 37, '1KI.7.37', 'He made the ten bases in this way: all of them had one casting, one measure, and one form.'),
('1KI', 7, 38, '1KI.7.38', 'He made ten basins of bronze. One basin contained forty baths. Every basin measured four cubits. One basin was on every one of the ten bases.'),
('1KI', 7, 39, '1KI.7.39', 'He set the bases, five on the right side of the house and five on the left side of the house. He set the sea on the right side of the house eastward and toward the south.'),
('1KI', 7, 40, '1KI.7.40', 'Hiram made the pots, the shovels, and the basins. So Hiram finished doing all the work that he worked for King Solomon in the LORD’s house:'),
('1KI', 7, 41, '1KI.7.41', 'the two pillars; the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars; the two networks to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars;'),
('1KI', 7, 42, '1KI.7.42', 'the four hundred pomegranates for the two networks; two rows of pomegranates for each network, to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the pillars;'),
('1KI', 7, 43, '1KI.7.43', 'the ten bases; the ten basins on the bases;'),
('1KI', 7, 44, '1KI.7.44', 'the one sea; the twelve oxen under the sea;'),
('1KI', 7, 45, '1KI.7.45', 'the pots; the shovels; and the basins. All of these vessels, which Hiram made for King Solomon for the LORD’s house, were of burnished bronze.'),
('1KI', 7, 46, '1KI.7.46', 'The king cast them in the plain of the Jordan, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zarethan.'),
('1KI', 7, 47, '1KI.7.47', 'Solomon left all the vessels unweighed, because there were so many of them. The weight of the bronze could not be determined.'),
('1KI', 7, 48, '1KI.7.48', 'Solomon made all the vessels that were in the LORD’s house: the golden altar and the table that the show bread was on, of gold;'),
('1KI', 7, 49, '1KI.7.49', 'and the lamp stands, five on the right side and five on the left, in front of the inner sanctuary, of pure gold; and the flowers, the lamps, and the tongs, of gold;'),
('1KI', 7, 50, '1KI.7.50', 'the cups, the snuffers, the basins, the spoons, and the fire pans, of pure gold; and the hinges, both for the doors of the inner house, the most holy place, and for the doors of the house, of the temple, of gold.'),
('1KI', 7, 51, '1KI.7.51', 'Thus all the work that King Solomon did in the LORD’s house was finished. Solomon brought in the things which David his father had dedicated—the silver, the gold, and the vessels—and put them in the treasuries of the LORD’s house.'),
('1KI', 8, 1, '1KI.8.1', 'Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel with all the heads of the tribes, the princes of the fathers’ households of the children of Israel, to King Solomon in Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the LORD’s covenant out of David’s city, which is Zion.'),
('1KI', 8, 2, '1KI.8.2', 'All the men of Israel assembled themselves to King Solomon at the feast in the month Ethanim, which is the seventh month.'),
('1KI', 8, 3, '1KI.8.3', 'All the elders of Israel came, and the priests picked up the ark.'),
('1KI', 8, 4, '1KI.8.4', 'They brought up the LORD’s ark, the Tent of Meeting, and all the holy vessels that were in the Tent. The priests and the Levites brought these up.'),
('1KI', 8, 5, '1KI.8.5', 'King Solomon and all the congregation of Israel, who were assembled to him, were with him before the ark, sacrificing sheep and cattle that could not be counted or numbered for multitude.'),
('1KI', 8, 6, '1KI.8.6', 'The priests brought in the ark of the LORD’s covenant to its place, into the inner sanctuary of the house, to the most holy place, even under the cherubim’s wings.'),
('1KI', 8, 7, '1KI.8.7', 'For the cherubim spread their wings out over the place of the ark, and the cherubim covered the ark and its poles above.'),
('1KI', 8, 8, '1KI.8.8', 'The poles were so long that the ends of the poles were seen from the holy place before the inner sanctuary, but they were not seen outside. They are there to this day.'),
('1KI', 8, 9, '1KI.8.9', 'There was nothing in the ark except the two stone tablets which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of the land of Egypt.'),
('1KI', 8, 10, '1KI.8.10', 'It came to pass, when the priests had come out of the holy place, that the cloud filled the LORD’s house,'),
('1KI', 8, 11, '1KI.8.11', 'so that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud; for the LORD’s glory filled the LORD’s house.'),
('1KI', 8, 12, '1KI.8.12', 'Then Solomon said, “The LORD has said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.'),
('1KI', 8, 13, '1KI.8.13', 'I have surely built you a house of habitation, a place for you to dwell in forever.”'),
('1KI', 8, 14, '1KI.8.14', 'The king turned his face around and blessed all the assembly of Israel; and all the assembly of Israel stood.'),
('1KI', 8, 15, '1KI.8.15', 'He said, “Blessed is the LORD, the God of Israel, who spoke with his mouth to David your father, and has with his hand fulfilled it, saying,'),
('1KI', 8, 16, '1KI.8.16', '‘Since the day that I brought my people Israel out of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel to build a house, that my name might be there; but I chose David to be over my people Israel.’'),
('1KI', 8, 17, '1KI.8.17', '“Now it was in the heart of David my father to build a house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('1KI', 8, 18, '1KI.8.18', 'But the LORD said to David my father, ‘Whereas it was in your heart to build a house for my name, you did well that it was in your heart.'),
('1KI', 8, 19, '1KI.8.19', 'Nevertheless, you shall not build the house; but your son who shall come out of your body, he shall build the house for my name.’'),
('1KI', 8, 20, '1KI.8.20', 'The LORD has established his word that he spoke; for I have risen up in the place of David my father, and I sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised, and have built the house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('1KI', 8, 21, '1KI.8.21', 'There I have set a place for the ark, in which is the LORD’s covenant, which he made with our fathers when he brought them out of the land of Egypt.”'),
('1KI', 8, 22, '1KI.8.22', 'Solomon stood before the LORD’s altar in the presence of all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands toward heaven;'),
('1KI', 8, 23, '1KI.8.23', 'and he said, “LORD, the God of Israel, there is no God like you, in heaven above, or on earth beneath; who keeps covenant and loving kindness with your servants who walk before you with all their heart;'),
('1KI', 8, 24, '1KI.8.24', 'who has kept with your servant David my father that which you promised him. Yes, you spoke with your mouth, and have fulfilled it with your hand, as it is today.'),
('1KI', 8, 25, '1KI.8.25', 'Now therefore, may LORD, the God of Israel, keep with your servant David my father that which you have promised him, saying, ‘There shall not fail from you a man in my sight to sit on the throne of Israel, if only your children take heed to their way, to walk before me as you have walked before me.’'),
('1KI', 8, 26, '1KI.8.26', '“Now therefore, God of Israel, please let your word be verified, which you spoke to your servant David my father.'),
('1KI', 8, 27, '1KI.8.27', 'But will God in very deed dwell on the earth? Behold, heaven and the heaven of heavens can’t contain you; how much less this house that I have built!'),
('1KI', 8, 28, '1KI.8.28', 'Yet have respect for the prayer of your servant and for his supplication, LORD my God, to listen to the cry and to the prayer which your servant prays before you today;'),
('1KI', 8, 29, '1KI.8.29', 'that your eyes may be open toward this house night and day, even toward the place of which you have said, ‘My name shall be there;’ to listen to the prayer which your servant prays toward this place.'),
('1KI', 8, 30, '1KI.8.30', 'Listen to the supplication of your servant, and of your people Israel, when they pray toward this place. Yes, hear in heaven, your dwelling place; and when you hear, forgive.'),
('1KI', 8, 31, '1KI.8.31', '“If a man sins against his neighbor, and an oath is laid on him to cause him to swear, and he comes and swears before your altar in this house,'),
('1KI', 8, 32, '1KI.8.32', 'then hear in heaven, and act, and judge your servants, condemning the wicked, to bring his way on his own head, and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness.'),
('1KI', 8, 33, '1KI.8.33', '“When your people Israel are struck down before the enemy because they have sinned against you, if they turn again to you and confess your name, and pray and make supplication to you in this house,'),
('1KI', 8, 34, '1KI.8.34', 'then hear in heaven, and forgive the sin of your people Israel, and bring them again to the land which you gave to their fathers.'),
('1KI', 8, 35, '1KI.8.35', '“When the sky is shut up and there is no rain because they have sinned against you, if they pray toward this place and confess your name, and turn from their sin when you afflict them,'),
('1KI', 8, 36, '1KI.8.36', 'then hear in heaven, and forgive the sin of your servants, and of your people Israel, when you teach them the good way in which they should walk; and send rain on your land which you have given to your people for an inheritance.'),
('1KI', 8, 37, '1KI.8.37', '“If there is famine in the land, if there is pestilence, if there is blight, mildew, locust or caterpillar; if their enemy besieges them in the land of their cities, whatever plague, whatever sickness there is,'),
('1KI', 8, 38, '1KI.8.38', 'whatever prayer and supplication is made by any man, or by all your people Israel, who shall each know the plague of his own heart, and spread out his hands toward this house,'),
('1KI', 8, 39, '1KI.8.39', 'then hear in heaven, your dwelling place, and forgive, and act, and give to every man according to all his ways, whose heart you know (for you, even you only, know the hearts of all the children of men);'),
('1KI', 8, 40, '1KI.8.40', 'that they may fear you all the days that they live in the land which you gave to our fathers.'),
('1KI', 8, 41, '1KI.8.41', '“Moreover, concerning the foreigner, who is not of your people Israel, when he comes out of a far country for your name’s sake'),
('1KI', 8, 42, '1KI.8.42', '(for they shall hear of your great name and of your mighty hand and of your outstretched arm), when he comes and prays toward this house,'),
('1KI', 8, 43, '1KI.8.43', 'hear in heaven, your dwelling place, and do according to all that the foreigner calls to you for; that all the peoples of the earth may know your name, to fear you, as do your people Israel, and that they may know that this house which I have built is called by your name.'),
('1KI', 8, 44, '1KI.8.44', '“If your people go out to battle against their enemy, by whatever way you shall send them, and they pray to the LORD toward the city which you have chosen, and toward the house which I have built for your name,'),
('1KI', 8, 45, '1KI.8.45', 'then hear in heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.'),
('1KI', 8, 46, '1KI.8.46', 'If they sin against you (for there is no man who doesn’t sin), and you are angry with them and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captive to the land of the enemy, far off or near;'),
('1KI', 8, 47, '1KI.8.47', 'yet if they repent in the land where they are carried captive, and turn again, and make supplication to you in the land of those who carried them captive, saying, ‘We have sinned and have done perversely; we have dealt wickedly,’'),
('1KI', 8, 48, '1KI.8.48', 'if they return to you with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their enemies who carried them captive, and pray to you toward their land which you gave to their fathers, the city which you have chosen and the house which I have built for your name,'),
('1KI', 8, 49, '1KI.8.49', 'then hear their prayer and their supplication in heaven, your dwelling place, and maintain their cause;'),
('1KI', 8, 50, '1KI.8.50', 'and forgive your people who have sinned against you, and all their transgressions in which they have transgressed against you; and give them compassion before those who carried them captive, that they may have compassion on them'),
('1KI', 8, 51, '1KI.8.51', '(for they are your people and your inheritance, which you brought out of Egypt, from the middle of the iron furnace);'),
('1KI', 8, 52, '1KI.8.52', 'that your eyes may be open to the supplication of your servant and to the supplication of your people Israel, to listen to them whenever they cry to you.'),
('1KI', 8, 53, '1KI.8.53', 'For you separated them from among all the peoples of the earth to be your inheritance, as you spoke by Moses your servant, when you brought our fathers out of Egypt, Lord GOD.”'),
('1KI', 8, 54, '1KI.8.54', 'It was so, that when Solomon had finished praying all this prayer and supplication to the LORD, he arose from before the LORD’s altar, from kneeling on his knees with his hands spread out toward heaven.'),
('1KI', 8, 55, '1KI.8.55', 'He stood and blessed all the assembly of Israel with a loud voice, saying,'),
('1KI', 8, 56, '1KI.8.56', '“Blessed be the LORD, who has given rest to his people Israel, according to all that he promised. There has not failed one word of all his good promise, which he promised by Moses his servant.'),
('1KI', 8, 57, '1KI.8.57', 'May the LORD our God be with us as he was with our fathers. Let him not leave us or forsake us,'),
('1KI', 8, 58, '1KI.8.58', 'that he may incline our hearts to him, to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, his statutes, and his ordinances, which he commanded our fathers.'),
('1KI', 8, 59, '1KI.8.59', 'Let these my words, with which I have made supplication before the LORD, be near to the LORD our God day and night, that he may maintain the cause of his servant and the cause of his people Israel, as every day requires;'),
('1KI', 8, 60, '1KI.8.60', 'that all the peoples of the earth may know that the LORD himself is God. There is no one else.'),
('1KI', 8, 61, '1KI.8.61', '“Let your heart therefore be perfect with the LORD our God, to walk in his statutes, and to keep his commandments, as it is today.”'),
('1KI', 8, 62, '1KI.8.62', 'The king, and all Israel with him, offered sacrifice before the LORD.'),
('1KI', 8, 63, '1KI.8.63', 'Solomon offered for the sacrifice of peace offerings, which he offered to the LORD, twenty two thousand head of cattle and one hundred twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the children of Israel dedicated the LORD’s house.'),
('1KI', 8, 64, '1KI.8.64', 'The same day the king made the middle of the court holy that was before the LORD’s house; for there he offered the burnt offering, the meal offering, and the fat of the peace offerings, because the bronze altar that was before the LORD was too little to receive the burnt offering, the meal offering, and the fat of the peace offerings.'),
('1KI', 8, 65, '1KI.8.65', 'So Solomon held the feast at that time, and all Israel with him, a great assembly, from the entrance of Hamath to the brook of Egypt, before the LORD our God, seven days and seven more days, even fourteen days.'),
('1KI', 8, 66, '1KI.8.66', 'On the eighth day he sent the people away; and they blessed the king, and went to their tents joyful and glad in their hearts for all the goodness that the LORD had shown to David his servant, and to Israel his people.'),
('1KI', 9, 1, '1KI.9.1', 'When Solomon had finished the building of the LORD’s house, the king’s house, and all Solomon’s desire which he was pleased to do,'),
('1KI', 9, 2, '1KI.9.2', 'The LORD appeared to Solomon the second time, as he had appeared to him at Gibeon.'),
('1KI', 9, 3, '1KI.9.3', 'The LORD said to him, “I have heard your prayer and your supplication that you have made before me. I have made this house holy, which you have built, to put my name there forever; and my eyes and my heart shall be there perpetually.'),
('1KI', 9, 4, '1KI.9.4', 'As for you, if you will walk before me as David your father walked, in integrity of heart and in uprightness, to do according to all that I have commanded you, and will keep my statutes and my ordinances,'),
('1KI', 9, 5, '1KI.9.5', 'then I will establish the throne of your kingdom over Israel forever, as I promised to David your father, saying, ‘There shall not fail from you a man on the throne of Israel.’'),
('1KI', 9, 6, '1KI.9.6', 'But if you turn away from following me, you or your children, and not keep my commandments and my statutes which I have set before you, but go and serve other gods and worship them,'),
('1KI', 9, 7, '1KI.9.7', 'then I will cut off Israel out of the land which I have given them; and I will cast this house, which I have made holy for my name, out of my sight; and Israel will be a proverb and a byword among all peoples.'),
('1KI', 9, 8, '1KI.9.8', 'Though this house is so high, yet everyone who passes by it will be astonished and hiss; and they will say, ‘Why has the LORD done this to this land and to this house?’'),
('1KI', 9, 9, '1KI.9.9', 'and they will answer, ‘Because they abandoned the LORD their God, who brought their fathers out of the land of Egypt, and embraced other gods, and worshiped them, and served them. Therefore the LORD has brought all this evil on them.’”'),
('1KI', 9, 10, '1KI.9.10', 'At the end of twenty years, in which Solomon had built the two houses, the LORD’s house and the king’s house'),
('1KI', 9, 11, '1KI.9.11', '(now Hiram the king of Tyre had furnished Solomon with cedar trees and cypress trees, and with gold, according to all his desire), King Solomon gave Hiram twenty cities in the land of Galilee.'),
('1KI', 9, 12, '1KI.9.12', 'Hiram came out of Tyre to see the cities which Solomon had given him; and they didn’t please him.'),
('1KI', 9, 13, '1KI.9.13', 'He said, “What cities are these which you have given me, my brother?” He called them the land of Cabul to this day.'),
('1KI', 9, 14, '1KI.9.14', 'Hiram sent to the king one hundred twenty talents of gold.'),
('1KI', 9, 15, '1KI.9.15', 'This is the reason of the forced labor which King Solomon conscripted: to build the LORD’s house, his own house, Millo, Jerusalem’s wall, Hazor, Megiddo, and Gezer.'),
('1KI', 9, 16, '1KI.9.16', 'Pharaoh king of Egypt had gone up, taken Gezer, burned it with fire, killed the Canaanites who lived in the city, and given it for a wedding gift to his daughter, Solomon’s wife.'),
('1KI', 9, 17, '1KI.9.17', 'Solomon built in the land Gezer, Beth Horon the lower,'),
('1KI', 9, 18, '1KI.9.18', 'Baalath, Tamar in the wilderness,'),
('1KI', 9, 19, '1KI.9.19', 'all the storage cities that Solomon had, the cities for his chariots, the cities for his horsemen, and that which Solomon desired to build for his pleasure in Jerusalem, and in Lebanon, and in all the land of his dominion.'),
('1KI', 9, 20, '1KI.9.20', 'As for all the people who were left of the Amorites, the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites, who were not of the children of Israel—'),
('1KI', 9, 21, '1KI.9.21', 'their children who were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel were not able utterly to destroy—of them Solomon raised a levy of bondservants to this day.'),
('1KI', 9, 22, '1KI.9.22', 'But of the children of Israel Solomon made no bondservants; but they were the men of war, his servants, his princes, his captains, and rulers of his chariots and of his horsemen.'),
('1KI', 9, 23, '1KI.9.23', 'These were the five hundred fifty chief officers who were over Solomon’s work, who ruled over the people who labored in the work.'),
('1KI', 9, 24, '1KI.9.24', 'But Pharaoh’s daughter came up out of David’s city to her house which Solomon had built for her. Then he built Millo.'),
('1KI', 9, 25, '1KI.9.25', 'Solomon offered burnt offerings and peace offerings on the altar which he built to the LORD three times per year, burning incense with them on the altar that was before the LORD. So he finished the house.'),
('1KI', 9, 26, '1KI.9.26', 'King Solomon made a fleet of ships in Ezion Geber, which is beside Eloth, on the shore of the Red Sea, in the land of Edom.'),
('1KI', 9, 27, '1KI.9.27', 'Hiram sent in the fleet his servants, sailors who had knowledge of the sea, with the servants of Solomon.'),
('1KI', 9, 28, '1KI.9.28', 'They came to Ophir, and fetched from there gold, four hundred and twenty talents, and brought it to King Solomon.'),
('1KI', 10, 1, '1KI.10.1', 'When the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning the LORD’s name, she came to test him with hard questions.'),
('1KI', 10, 2, '1KI.10.2', 'She came to Jerusalem with a very great caravan, with camels that bore spices, very much gold, and precious stones; and when she had come to Solomon, she talked with him about all that was in her heart.'),
('1KI', 10, 3, '1KI.10.3', 'Solomon answered all her questions. There wasn’t anything hidden from the king which he didn’t tell her.'),
('1KI', 10, 4, '1KI.10.4', 'When the queen of Sheba had seen all the wisdom of Solomon, the house that he had built,'),
('1KI', 10, 5, '1KI.10.5', 'the food of his table, the sitting of his servants, the attendance of his officials, their clothing, his cup bearers, and his ascent by which he went up to the LORD’s house, there was no more spirit in her.'),
('1KI', 10, 6, '1KI.10.6', 'She said to the king, “It was a true report that I heard in my own land of your acts and of your wisdom.'),
('1KI', 10, 7, '1KI.10.7', 'However, I didn’t believe the words until I came and my eyes had seen it. Behold, not even half was told me! Your wisdom and prosperity exceed the fame which I heard.'),
('1KI', 10, 8, '1KI.10.8', 'Happy are your men, happy are these your servants who stand continually before you, who hear your wisdom.'),
('1KI', 10, 9, '1KI.10.9', 'Blessed is the LORD your God, who delighted in you, to set you on the throne of Israel. Because the LORD loved Israel forever, therefore he made you king, to do justice and righteousness.”'),
('1KI', 10, 10, '1KI.10.10', 'She gave the king one hundred twenty talents of gold, and a very great quantity of spices, and precious stones. Never again was there such an abundance of spices as these which the queen of Sheba gave to King Solomon.'),
('1KI', 10, 11, '1KI.10.11', 'The fleet of Hiram that brought gold from Ophir also brought in from Ophir great quantities of almug trees and precious stones.'),
('1KI', 10, 12, '1KI.10.12', 'The king made of the almug trees pillars for the LORD’s house and for the king’s house, harps also and stringed instruments for the singers; no such almug trees came or were seen to this day.'),
('1KI', 10, 13, '1KI.10.13', 'King Solomon gave to the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatever she asked, in addition to that which Solomon gave her of his royal bounty. So she turned and went to her own land, she and her servants.'),
('1KI', 10, 14, '1KI.10.14', 'Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred sixty-six talents of gold,'),
('1KI', 10, 15, '1KI.10.15', 'in addition to that which the traders brought, and the traffic of the merchants, and of all the kings of the mixed people, and of the governors of the country.'),
('1KI', 10, 16, '1KI.10.16', 'King Solomon made two hundred bucklers of beaten gold; six hundred shekels of gold went to one buckler.'),
('1KI', 10, 17, '1KI.10.17', 'He made three hundred shields of beaten gold; three minas of gold went to one shield; and the king put them in the House of the Forest of Lebanon.'),
('1KI', 10, 18, '1KI.10.18', 'Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with the finest gold.'),
('1KI', 10, 19, '1KI.10.19', 'There were six steps to the throne, and the top of the throne was round behind; and there were armrests on either side by the place of the seat, and two lions standing beside the armrests.'),
('1KI', 10, 20, '1KI.10.20', 'Twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other on the six steps. Nothing like it was made in any kingdom.'),
('1KI', 10, 21, '1KI.10.21', 'All King Solomon’s drinking vessels were of gold, and all the vessels of the House of the Forest of Lebanon were of pure gold. None were of silver, because it was considered of little value in the days of Solomon.'),
('1KI', 10, 22, '1KI.10.22', 'For the king had a fleet of ships of Tarshish at sea with Hiram’s fleet. Once every three years the fleet of Tarshish came bringing gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks.'),
('1KI', 10, 23, '1KI.10.23', 'So King Solomon exceeded all the kings of the earth in riches and in wisdom.'),
('1KI', 10, 24, '1KI.10.24', 'All the earth sought the presence of Solomon to hear his wisdom which God had put in his heart.'),
('1KI', 10, 25, '1KI.10.25', 'Year after year, every man brought his tribute, vessels of silver, vessels of gold, clothing, armor, spices, horses, and mules.'),
('1KI', 10, 26, '1KI.10.26', 'Solomon gathered together chariots and horsemen. He had one thousand four hundred chariots and twelve thousand horsemen. He kept them in the chariot cities and with the king at Jerusalem.'),
('1KI', 10, 27, '1KI.10.27', 'The king made silver as common as stones in Jerusalem, and cedars as common as the sycamore trees that are in the lowland.'),
('1KI', 10, 28, '1KI.10.28', 'The horses which Solomon had were brought out of Egypt. The king’s merchants received them in droves, each drove at a price.'),
('1KI', 10, 29, '1KI.10.29', 'A chariot was imported from Egypt for six hundred shekels of silver, and a horse for one hundred fifty shekels; and so they exported them to all the kings of the Hittites and to the kings of Syria.'),
('1KI', 11, 1, '1KI.11.1', 'Now King Solomon loved many foreign women, together with the daughter of Pharaoh: women of the Moabites, Ammonites, Edomites, Sidonians, and Hittites,'),
('1KI', 11, 2, '1KI.11.2', 'of the nations concerning which the LORD said to the children of Israel, “You shall not go among them, neither shall they come among you, for surely they will turn away your heart after their gods.” Solomon joined to these in love.'),
('1KI', 11, 3, '1KI.11.3', 'He had seven hundred wives, princesses, and three hundred concubines. His wives turned his heart away.'),
('1KI', 11, 4, '1KI.11.4', 'When Solomon was old, his wives turned away his heart after other gods; and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as the heart of David his father was.'),
('1KI', 11, 5, '1KI.11.5', 'For Solomon went after Ashtoreth the goddess of the Sidonians, and after Milcom the abomination of the Ammonites.'),
('1KI', 11, 6, '1KI.11.6', 'Solomon did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and didn’t go fully after the LORD, as David his father did.'),
('1KI', 11, 7, '1KI.11.7', 'Then Solomon built a high place for Chemosh the abomination of Moab, on the mountain that is before Jerusalem, and for Molech the abomination of the children of Ammon.'),
('1KI', 11, 8, '1KI.11.8', 'So he did for all his foreign wives, who burned incense and sacrificed to their gods.'),
('1KI', 11, 9, '1KI.11.9', 'The LORD was angry with Solomon, because his heart was turned away from the LORD, the God of Israel, who had appeared to him twice,'),
('1KI', 11, 10, '1KI.11.10', 'and had commanded him concerning this thing, that he should not go after other gods; but he didn’t keep that which the LORD commanded.'),
('1KI', 11, 11, '1KI.11.11', 'Therefore the LORD said to Solomon, “Because this is done by you, and you have not kept my covenant and my statutes, which I have commanded you, I will surely tear the kingdom from you, and will give it to your servant.'),
('1KI', 11, 12, '1KI.11.12', 'Nevertheless, I will not do it in your days, for David your father’s sake; but I will tear it out of your son’s hand.'),
('1KI', 11, 13, '1KI.11.13', 'However, I will not tear away all the kingdom; but I will give one tribe to your son, for David my servant’s sake, and for Jerusalem’s sake which I have chosen.”'),
('1KI', 11, 14, '1KI.11.14', 'The LORD raised up an adversary to Solomon: Hadad the Edomite. He was one of the king’s offspring in Edom.'),
('1KI', 11, 15, '1KI.11.15', 'For when David was in Edom, and Joab the captain of the army had gone up to bury the slain, and had struck every male in Edom'),
('1KI', 11, 16, '1KI.11.16', '(for Joab and all Israel remained there six months, until he had cut off every male in Edom),'),
('1KI', 11, 17, '1KI.11.17', 'Hadad fled, he and certain Edomites of his father’s servants with him, to go into Egypt, when Hadad was still a little child.'),
('1KI', 11, 18, '1KI.11.18', 'They arose out of Midian and came to Paran; and they took men with them out of Paran, and they came to Egypt, to Pharaoh king of Egypt, who gave him a house, and appointed him food, and gave him land.'),
('1KI', 11, 19, '1KI.11.19', 'Hadad found great favor in the sight of Pharaoh, so that he gave him as wife the sister of his own wife, the sister of Tahpenes the queen.'),
('1KI', 11, 20, '1KI.11.20', 'The sister of Tahpenes bore him Genubath his son, whom Tahpenes weaned in Pharaoh’s house; and Genubath was in Pharaoh’s house among the sons of Pharaoh.'),
('1KI', 11, 21, '1KI.11.21', 'When Hadad heard in Egypt that David slept with his fathers, and that Joab the captain of the army was dead, Hadad said to Pharaoh, “Let me depart, that I may go to my own country.”'),
('1KI', 11, 22, '1KI.11.22', 'Then Pharaoh said to him, “But what have you lacked with me, that behold, you seek to go to your own country?” He answered, “Nothing, however only let me depart.”'),
('1KI', 11, 23, '1KI.11.23', 'God raised up an adversary to him, Rezon the son of Eliada, who had fled from his lord, Hadadezer king of Zobah.'),
('1KI', 11, 24, '1KI.11.24', 'He gathered men to himself, and became captain over a troop, when David killed them of Zobah. They went to Damascus and lived there, and reigned in Damascus.'),
('1KI', 11, 25, '1KI.11.25', 'He was an adversary to Israel all the days of Solomon, in addition to the mischief of Hadad. He abhorred Israel, and reigned over Syria.'),
('1KI', 11, 26, '1KI.11.26', 'Jeroboam the son of Nebat, an Ephraimite of Zeredah, a servant of Solomon, whose mother’s name was Zeruah, a widow, also lifted up his hand against the king.'),
('1KI', 11, 27, '1KI.11.27', 'This was the reason why he lifted up his hand against the king: Solomon built Millo, and repaired the breach of his father David’s city.'),
('1KI', 11, 28, '1KI.11.28', 'The man Jeroboam was a mighty man of valor; and Solomon saw that the young man was industrious, and he put him in charge of all the labor of the house of Joseph.'),
('1KI', 11, 29, '1KI.11.29', 'At that time, when Jeroboam went out of Jerusalem, the prophet Ahijah the Shilonite found him on the way. Now Ahijah had clad himself with a new garment; and the two of them were alone in the field.'),
('1KI', 11, 30, '1KI.11.30', 'Ahijah took the new garment that was on him, and tore it in twelve pieces.'),
('1KI', 11, 31, '1KI.11.31', 'He said to Jeroboam, “Take ten pieces; for the LORD, the God of Israel, says, ‘Behold, I will tear the kingdom out of the hand of Solomon and will give ten tribes to you'),
('1KI', 11, 32, '1KI.11.32', '(but he shall have one tribe, for my servant David’s sake and for Jerusalem’s sake, the city which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel),'),
('1KI', 11, 33, '1KI.11.33', 'because they have forsaken me, and have worshiped Ashtoreth the goddess of the Sidonians, Chemosh the god of Moab, and Milcom the god of the children of Ammon. They have not walked in my ways, to do that which is right in my eyes, and to keep my statutes and my ordinances, as David his father did.'),
('1KI', 11, 34, '1KI.11.34', '“‘However, I will not take the whole kingdom out of his hand, but I will make him prince all the days of his life for David my servant’s sake whom I chose, who kept my commandments and my statutes,'),
('1KI', 11, 35, '1KI.11.35', 'but I will take the kingdom out of his son’s hand and will give it to you, even ten tribes.'),
('1KI', 11, 36, '1KI.11.36', 'I will give one tribe to his son, that David my servant may have a lamp always before me in Jerusalem, the city which I have chosen for myself to put my name there.'),
('1KI', 11, 37, '1KI.11.37', 'I will take you, and you shall reign according to all that your soul desires, and shall be king over Israel.'),
('1KI', 11, 38, '1KI.11.38', 'It shall be, if you will listen to all that I command you, and will walk in my ways, and do that which is right in my eyes, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as David my servant did, that I will be with you, and will build you a sure house, as I built for David, and will give Israel to you.'),
('1KI', 11, 39, '1KI.11.39', 'I will afflict the offspring of David for this, but not forever.’”'),
('1KI', 11, 40, '1KI.11.40', 'Therefore Solomon sought to kill Jeroboam, but Jeroboam arose and fled into Egypt, to Shishak king of Egypt, and was in Egypt until the death of Solomon.'),
('1KI', 11, 41, '1KI.11.41', 'Now the rest of the acts of Solomon, and all that he did, and his wisdom, aren’t they written in the book of the acts of Solomon?'),
('1KI', 11, 42, '1KI.11.42', 'The time that Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel was forty years.'),
('1KI', 11, 43, '1KI.11.43', 'Solomon slept with his fathers, and was buried in his father David’s city; and Rehoboam his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 12, 1, '1KI.12.1', 'Rehoboam went to Shechem, for all Israel had come to Shechem to make him king.'),
('1KI', 12, 2, '1KI.12.2', 'When Jeroboam the son of Nebat heard of it (for he was yet in Egypt, where he had fled from the presence of King Solomon, and Jeroboam lived in Egypt;'),
('1KI', 12, 3, '1KI.12.3', 'and they sent and called him), Jeroboam and all the assembly of Israel came, and spoke to Rehoboam, saying,'),
('1KI', 12, 4, '1KI.12.4', '“Your father made our yoke difficult. Now therefore make the hard service of your father, and his heavy yoke which he put on us, lighter, and we will serve you.”'),
('1KI', 12, 5, '1KI.12.5', 'He said to them, “Depart for three days, then come back to me.” So the people departed.'),
('1KI', 12, 6, '1KI.12.6', 'King Rehoboam took counsel with the old men who had stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, saying, “What counsel do you give me to answer these people?”'),
('1KI', 12, 7, '1KI.12.7', 'They replied, “If you will be a servant to this people today, and will serve them, and answer them with good words, then they will be your servants forever.”'),
('1KI', 12, 8, '1KI.12.8', 'But he abandoned the counsel of the old men which they had given him, and took counsel with the young men who had grown up with him, who stood before him.'),
('1KI', 12, 9, '1KI.12.9', 'He said to them, “What counsel do you give, that we may answer these people who have spoken to me, saying, ‘Make the yoke that your father put on us lighter’?”'),
('1KI', 12, 10, '1KI.12.10', 'The young men who had grown up with him said to him, “Tell these people who spoke to you, saying, ‘Your father made our yoke heavy, but make it lighter to us’—tell them, ‘My little finger is thicker than my father’s waist.'),
('1KI', 12, 11, '1KI.12.11', 'Now my father burdened you with a heavy yoke, but I will add to your yoke. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.’”'),
('1KI', 12, 12, '1KI.12.12', 'So Jeroboam and all the people came to Rehoboam the third day, as the king asked, saying, “Come to me again the third day.”'),
('1KI', 12, 13, '1KI.12.13', 'The king answered the people roughly, and abandoned the counsel of the old men which they had given him,'),
('1KI', 12, 14, '1KI.12.14', 'and spoke to them according to the counsel of the young men, saying, “My father made your yoke heavy, but I will add to your yoke. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.”'),
('1KI', 12, 15, '1KI.12.15', 'So the king didn’t listen to the people; for it was a thing brought about from the LORD, that he might establish his word, which the LORD spoke by Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam the son of Nebat.'),
('1KI', 12, 16, '1KI.12.16', 'When all Israel saw that the king didn’t listen to them, the people answered the king, saying, “What portion have we in David? We don’t have an inheritance in the son of Jesse. To your tents, Israel! Now see to your own house, David.” So Israel departed to their tents.'),
('1KI', 12, 17, '1KI.12.17', 'But as for the children of Israel who lived in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them.'),
('1KI', 12, 18, '1KI.12.18', 'Then King Rehoboam sent Adoram, who was over the men subject to forced labor; and all Israel stoned him to death with stones. King Rehoboam hurried to get himself up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.'),
('1KI', 12, 19, '1KI.12.19', 'So Israel rebelled against David’s house to this day.'),
('1KI', 12, 20, '1KI.12.20', 'When all Israel heard that Jeroboam had returned, they sent and called him to the congregation, and made him king over all Israel. There was no one who followed David’s house, except for the tribe of Judah only.'),
('1KI', 12, 21, '1KI.12.21', 'When Rehoboam had come to Jerusalem, he assembled all the house of Judah and the tribe of Benjamin, a hundred and eighty thousand chosen men who were warriors, to fight against the house of Israel, to bring the kingdom again to Rehoboam the son of Solomon.'),
('1KI', 12, 22, '1KI.12.22', 'But the word of God came to Shemaiah the man of God, saying,'),
('1KI', 12, 23, '1KI.12.23', '“Speak to Rehoboam the son of Solomon, king of Judah, and to all the house of Judah and Benjamin, and to the rest of the people, saying,'),
('1KI', 12, 24, '1KI.12.24', '‘The LORD says, “You shall not go up or fight against your brothers, the children of Israel. Everyone return to his house; for this thing is from me.”’” So they listened to the LORD’s word, and returned and went their way, according to the LORD’s word.'),
('1KI', 12, 25, '1KI.12.25', 'Then Jeroboam built Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim, and lived in it; and he went out from there and built Penuel.'),
('1KI', 12, 26, '1KI.12.26', 'Jeroboam said in his heart, “Now the kingdom will return to David’s house.'),
('1KI', 12, 27, '1KI.12.27', 'If this people goes up to offer sacrifices in the LORD’s house at Jerusalem, then the heart of this people will turn again to their lord, even to Rehoboam king of Judah; and they will kill me, and return to Rehoboam king of Judah.”'),
('1KI', 12, 28, '1KI.12.28', 'So the king took counsel, and made two calves of gold; and he said to them, “It is too much for you to go up to Jerusalem. Look and behold your gods, Israel, which brought you up out of the land of Egypt!”'),
('1KI', 12, 29, '1KI.12.29', 'He set the one in Bethel, and the other he put in Dan.'),
('1KI', 12, 30, '1KI.12.30', 'This thing became a sin, for the people went even as far as Dan to worship before the one there.'),
('1KI', 12, 31, '1KI.12.31', 'He made houses of high places, and made priests from among all the people, who were not of the sons of Levi.'),
('1KI', 12, 32, '1KI.12.32', 'Jeroboam ordained a feast in the eighth month, on the fifteenth day of the month, like the feast that is in Judah, and he went up to the altar. He did so in Bethel, sacrificing to the calves that he had made, and he placed in Bethel the priests of the high places that he had made.'),
('1KI', 12, 33, '1KI.12.33', 'He went up to the altar which he had made in Bethel on the fifteenth day in the eighth month, even in the month which he had devised of his own heart; and he ordained a feast for the children of Israel, and went up to the altar to burn incense.'),
('1KI', 13, 1, '1KI.13.1', 'Behold, a man of God came out of Judah by the LORD’s word to Bethel; and Jeroboam was standing by the altar to burn incense.'),
('1KI', 13, 2, '1KI.13.2', 'He cried against the altar by the LORD’s word, and said, “Altar! Altar! The LORD says: ‘Behold, a son will be born to David’s house, Josiah by name. On you he will sacrifice the priests of the high places who burn incense on you, and they will burn men’s bones on you.’”'),
('1KI', 13, 3, '1KI.13.3', 'He gave a sign the same day, saying, “This is the sign which the LORD has spoken: Behold, the altar will be split apart, and the ashes that are on it will be poured out.”'),
('1KI', 13, 4, '1KI.13.4', 'When the king heard the saying of the man of God, which he cried against the altar in Bethel, Jeroboam put out his hand from the altar, saying, “Seize him!” His hand, which he put out against him, dried up, so that he could not draw it back again to himself.'),
('1KI', 13, 5, '1KI.13.5', 'The altar was also split apart, and the ashes poured out from the altar, according to the sign which the man of God had given by the LORD’s word.'),
('1KI', 13, 6, '1KI.13.6', 'The king answered the man of God, “Now intercede for the favor of the LORD your God, and pray for me, that my hand may be restored to me.” The man of God interceded with the LORD, and the king’s hand was restored to him, and became as it was before.'),
('1KI', 13, 7, '1KI.13.7', 'The king said to the man of God, “Come home with me and refresh yourself, and I will give you a reward.”'),
('1KI', 13, 8, '1KI.13.8', 'The man of God said to the king, “Even if you gave me half of your house, I would not go in with you, neither would I eat bread nor drink water in this place;'),
('1KI', 13, 9, '1KI.13.9', 'for so was it commanded me by the LORD’s word, saying, ‘You shall eat no bread, drink no water, and don’t return by the way that you came.’”'),
('1KI', 13, 10, '1KI.13.10', 'So he went another way, and didn’t return by the way that he came to Bethel.'),
('1KI', 13, 11, '1KI.13.11', 'Now an old prophet lived in Bethel, and one of his sons came and told him all the works that the man of God had done that day in Bethel. They also told their father the words which he had spoken to the king.'),
('1KI', 13, 12, '1KI.13.12', 'Their father said to them, “Which way did he go?” Now his sons had seen which way the man of God went, who came from Judah.'),
('1KI', 13, 13, '1KI.13.13', 'He said to his sons, “Saddle the donkey for me.” So they saddled the donkey for him; and he rode on it.'),
('1KI', 13, 14, '1KI.13.14', 'He went after the man of God, and found him sitting under an oak. He said to him, “Are you the man of God who came from Judah?” He said, “I am.”'),
('1KI', 13, 15, '1KI.13.15', 'Then he said to him, “Come home with me and eat bread.”'),
('1KI', 13, 16, '1KI.13.16', 'He said, “I may not return with you, nor go in with you. I will not eat bread or drink water with you in this place.'),
('1KI', 13, 17, '1KI.13.17', 'For it was said to me by the LORD’s word, ‘You shall eat no bread or drink water there, and don’t turn again to go by the way that you came.’”'),
('1KI', 13, 18, '1KI.13.18', 'He said to him, “I also am a prophet as you are; and an angel spoke to me by the LORD’s word, saying, ‘Bring him back with you into your house, that he may eat bread and drink water.’” He lied to him.'),
('1KI', 13, 19, '1KI.13.19', 'So he went back with him, ate bread in his house, and drank water.'),
('1KI', 13, 20, '1KI.13.20', 'As they sat at the table, the LORD’s word came to the prophet who brought him back;'),
('1KI', 13, 21, '1KI.13.21', 'and he cried out to the man of God who came from Judah, saying, “The LORD says, ‘Because you have been disobedient to the LORD’s word, and have not kept the commandment which the LORD your God commanded you,'),
('1KI', 13, 22, '1KI.13.22', 'but came back, and have eaten bread and drank water in the place of which he said to you, “Eat no bread, and drink no water,” your body will not come to the tomb of your fathers.’”'),
('1KI', 13, 23, '1KI.13.23', 'After he had eaten bread and after he drank, he saddled the donkey for the prophet whom he had brought back.'),
('1KI', 13, 24, '1KI.13.24', 'When he had gone, a lion met him by the way and killed him. His body was thrown on the path, and the donkey stood by it. The lion also stood by the body.'),
('1KI', 13, 25, '1KI.13.25', 'Behold, men passed by and saw the body thrown on the path, and the lion standing by the body; and they came and told it in the city where the old prophet lived.'),
('1KI', 13, 26, '1KI.13.26', 'When the prophet who brought him back from the way heard of it, he said, “It is the man of God who was disobedient to the LORD’s word. Therefore the LORD has delivered him to the lion, which has mauled him and slain him, according to the LORD’s word which he spoke to him.”'),
('1KI', 13, 27, '1KI.13.27', 'He said to his sons, saying, “Saddle the donkey for me,” and they saddled it.'),
('1KI', 13, 28, '1KI.13.28', 'He went and found his body thrown on the path, and the donkey and the lion standing by the body. The lion had not eaten the body nor mauled the donkey.'),
('1KI', 13, 29, '1KI.13.29', 'The prophet took up the body of the man of God, and laid it on the donkey, and brought it back. He came to the city of the old prophet to mourn, and to bury him.'),
('1KI', 13, 30, '1KI.13.30', 'He laid his body in his own grave; and they mourned over him, saying, “Alas, my brother!”'),
('1KI', 13, 31, '1KI.13.31', 'After he had buried him, he spoke to his sons, saying, “When I am dead, bury me in the tomb in which the man of God is buried. Lay my bones beside his bones.'),
('1KI', 13, 32, '1KI.13.32', 'For the saying which he cried by the LORD’s word against the altar in Bethel, and against all the houses of the high places which are in the cities of Samaria, will surely happen.”'),
('1KI', 13, 33, '1KI.13.33', 'After this thing, Jeroboam didn’t turn from his evil way, but again made priests of the high places from among all the people. Whoever wanted to, he consecrated him, that there might be priests of the high places.'),
('1KI', 13, 34, '1KI.13.34', 'This thing became sin to the house of Jeroboam, even to cut it off and to destroy it from off the surface of the earth.'),
('1KI', 14, 1, '1KI.14.1', 'At that time Abijah the son of Jeroboam became sick.'),
('1KI', 14, 2, '1KI.14.2', 'Jeroboam said to his wife, “Please get up and disguise yourself, so that you won’t be recognized as Jeroboam’s wife. Go to Shiloh. Behold, Ahijah the prophet is there, who said that I would be king over this people.'),
('1KI', 14, 3, '1KI.14.3', 'Take with you ten loaves of bread, some cakes, and a jar of honey, and go to him. He will tell you what will become of the child.”'),
('1KI', 14, 4, '1KI.14.4', 'Jeroboam’s wife did so, and arose and went to Shiloh, and came to Ahijah’s house. Now Ahijah could not see, for his eyes were set by reason of his age.'),
('1KI', 14, 5, '1KI.14.5', 'The LORD said to Ahijah, “Behold, Jeroboam’s wife is coming to inquire of you concerning her son, for he is sick. Tell her such and such; for it will be, when she comes in, that she will pretend to be another woman.”'),
('1KI', 14, 6, '1KI.14.6', 'So when Ahijah heard the sound of her feet as she came in at the door, he said, “Come in, Jeroboam’s wife! Why do you pretend to be another? For I am sent to you with heavy news.'),
('1KI', 14, 7, '1KI.14.7', 'Go, tell Jeroboam, ‘The LORD, the God of Israel, says: “Because I exalted you from among the people, and made you prince over my people Israel,'),
('1KI', 14, 8, '1KI.14.8', 'and tore the kingdom away from David’s house, and gave it to you; and yet you have not been as my servant David, who kept my commandments, and who followed me with all his heart, to do that only which was right in my eyes,'),
('1KI', 14, 9, '1KI.14.9', 'but have done evil above all who were before you, and have gone and made for yourself other gods, molten images, to provoke me to anger, and have cast me behind your back,'),
('1KI', 14, 10, '1KI.14.10', 'therefore, behold, I will bring evil on the house of Jeroboam, and will cut off from Jeroboam everyone who urinates on a wall, he who is shut up and he who is left at large in Israel, and will utterly sweep away the house of Jeroboam, as a man sweeps away dung until it is all gone.'),
('1KI', 14, 11, '1KI.14.11', 'The dogs will eat whoever belongs to Jeroboam who dies in the city; and the birds of the sky will eat whoever dies in the field, for the LORD has spoken it.”’'),
('1KI', 14, 12, '1KI.14.12', 'Arise therefore, and go to your house. When your feet enter into the city, the child will die.'),
('1KI', 14, 13, '1KI.14.13', 'All Israel will mourn for him and bury him; for he only of Jeroboam will come to the grave, because in him there is found some good thing toward the LORD, the God of Israel, in the house of Jeroboam.'),
('1KI', 14, 14, '1KI.14.14', 'Moreover the LORD will raise up a king for himself over Israel who will cut off the house of Jeroboam. This is the day! What? Even now.'),
('1KI', 14, 15, '1KI.14.15', 'For the LORD will strike Israel, as a reed is shaken in the water; and he will root up Israel out of this good land which he gave to their fathers, and will scatter them beyond the River, because they have made their Asherah poles, provoking the LORD to anger.'),
('1KI', 14, 16, '1KI.14.16', 'He will give Israel up because of the sins of Jeroboam, which he has sinned, and with which he has made Israel to sin.”'),
('1KI', 14, 17, '1KI.14.17', 'Jeroboam’s wife arose and departed, and came to Tirzah. As she came to the threshold of the house, the child died.'),
('1KI', 14, 18, '1KI.14.18', 'All Israel buried him and mourned for him, according to the LORD’s word, which he spoke by his servant Ahijah the prophet.'),
('1KI', 14, 19, '1KI.14.19', 'The rest of the acts of Jeroboam, how he fought and how he reigned, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.'),
('1KI', 14, 20, '1KI.14.20', 'The days which Jeroboam reigned were twenty two years; then he slept with his fathers, and Nadab his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 14, 21, '1KI.14.21', 'Rehoboam the son of Solomon reigned in Judah. Rehoboam was forty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city which the LORD had chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, to put his name there. His mother’s name was Naamah the Ammonitess.'),
('1KI', 14, 22, '1KI.14.22', 'Judah did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and they provoked him to jealousy with their sins which they committed, above all that their fathers had done.'),
('1KI', 14, 23, '1KI.14.23', 'For they also built for themselves high places, sacred pillars, and Asherah poles on every high hill and under every green tree.'),
('1KI', 14, 24, '1KI.14.24', 'There were also sodomites in the land. They did according to all the abominations of the nations which the LORD drove out before the children of Israel.'),
('1KI', 14, 25, '1KI.14.25', 'In the fifth year of King Rehoboam, Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem;'),
('1KI', 14, 26, '1KI.14.26', 'and he took away the treasures of the LORD’s house and the treasures of the king’s house. He even took away all of it, including all the gold shields which Solomon had made.'),
('1KI', 14, 27, '1KI.14.27', 'King Rehoboam made shields of bronze in their place, and committed them to the hands of the captains of the guard, who guarded the door of the king’s house.'),
('1KI', 14, 28, '1KI.14.28', 'It was so, that as often as the king went into the LORD’s house, the guard bore them, and brought them back into the guard room.'),
('1KI', 14, 29, '1KI.14.29', 'Now the rest of the acts of Rehoboam, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('1KI', 14, 30, '1KI.14.30', 'There was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam continually.'),
('1KI', 14, 31, '1KI.14.31', 'Rehoboam slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David’s city. His mother’s name was Naamah the Ammonitess. Abijam his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 15, 1, '1KI.15.1', 'Now in the eighteenth year of King Jeroboam the son of Nebat, Abijam began to reign over Judah.'),
('1KI', 15, 2, '1KI.15.2', 'He reigned three years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Maacah the daughter of Abishalom.'),
('1KI', 15, 3, '1KI.15.3', 'He walked in all the sins of his father, which he had done before him; and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as the heart of David his father.'),
('1KI', 15, 4, '1KI.15.4', 'Nevertheless for David’s sake, the LORD his God gave him a lamp in Jerusalem, to set up his son after him and to establish Jerusalem;'),
('1KI', 15, 5, '1KI.15.5', 'because David did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, and didn’t turn away from anything that he commanded him all the days of his life, except only in the matter of Uriah the Hittite.'),
('1KI', 15, 6, '1KI.15.6', 'Now there was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam all the days of his life.'),
('1KI', 15, 7, '1KI.15.7', 'The rest of the acts of Abijam, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah? There was war between Abijam and Jeroboam.'),
('1KI', 15, 8, '1KI.15.8', 'Abijam slept with his fathers, and they buried him in David’s city; and Asa his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 15, 9, '1KI.15.9', 'In the twentieth year of Jeroboam king of Israel, Asa began to reign over Judah.'),
('1KI', 15, 10, '1KI.15.10', 'He reigned forty-one years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Maacah the daughter of Abishalom.'),
('1KI', 15, 11, '1KI.15.11', 'Asa did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, as David his father did.'),
('1KI', 15, 12, '1KI.15.12', 'He put away the sodomites out of the land, and removed all the idols that his fathers had made.'),
('1KI', 15, 13, '1KI.15.13', 'He also removed Maacah his mother from being queen, because she had made an abominable image for an Asherah. Asa cut down her image and burned it at the brook Kidron.'),
('1KI', 15, 14, '1KI.15.14', 'But the high places were not taken away. Nevertheless the heart of Asa was perfect with the LORD all his days.'),
('1KI', 15, 15, '1KI.15.15', 'He brought into the LORD’s house the things that his father had dedicated, and the things that he himself had dedicated: silver, gold, and utensils.'),
('1KI', 15, 16, '1KI.15.16', 'There was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel all their days.'),
('1KI', 15, 17, '1KI.15.17', 'Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah, and built Ramah, that he might not allow anyone to go out or come in to Asa king of Judah.'),
('1KI', 15, 18, '1KI.15.18', 'Then Asa took all the silver and the gold that was left in the treasures of the LORD’s house, and the treasures of the king’s house, and delivered it into the hand of his servants. Then King Asa sent them to Ben Hadad, the son of Tabrimmon, the son of Hezion, king of Syria, who lived at Damascus, saying,'),
('1KI', 15, 19, '1KI.15.19', '“Let there be a treaty between me and you, like that between my father and your father. Behold, I have sent to you a present of silver and gold. Go, break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.”'),
('1KI', 15, 20, '1KI.15.20', 'Ben Hadad listened to King Asa, and sent the captains of his armies against the cities of Israel, and struck Ijon, and Dan, and Abel Beth Maacah, and all Chinneroth, with all the land of Naphtali.'),
('1KI', 15, 21, '1KI.15.21', 'When Baasha heard of it, he stopped building Ramah, and lived in Tirzah.'),
('1KI', 15, 22, '1KI.15.22', 'Then King Asa made a proclamation to all Judah. No one was exempted. They carried away the stones of Ramah, and its timber, with which Baasha had built; and King Asa used it to build Geba of Benjamin, and Mizpah.'),
('1KI', 15, 23, '1KI.15.23', 'Now the rest of all the acts of Asa, and all his might, and all that he did, and the cities which he built, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah? But in the time of his old age he was diseased in his feet.'),
('1KI', 15, 24, '1KI.15.24', 'Asa slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David’s city; and Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 15, 25, '1KI.15.25', 'Nadab the son of Jeroboam began to reign over Israel in the second year of Asa king of Judah; and he reigned over Israel two years.'),
('1KI', 15, 26, '1KI.15.26', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and walked in the way of his father, and in his sin with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('1KI', 15, 27, '1KI.15.27', 'Baasha the son of Ahijah, of the house of Issachar, conspired against him; and Baasha struck him at Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines; for Nadab and all Israel were besieging Gibbethon.'),
('1KI', 15, 28, '1KI.15.28', 'Even in the third year of Asa king of Judah, Baasha killed him and reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 15, 29, '1KI.15.29', 'As soon as he was king, he struck all the house of Jeroboam. He didn’t leave to Jeroboam any who breathed, until he had destroyed him, according to the saying of the LORD, which he spoke by his servant Ahijah the Shilonite;'),
('1KI', 15, 30, '1KI.15.30', 'for the sins of Jeroboam which he sinned, and with which he made Israel to sin, because of his provocation with which he provoked the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger.'),
('1KI', 15, 31, '1KI.15.31', 'Now the rest of the acts of Nadab, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 15, 32, '1KI.15.32', 'There was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel all their days.'),
('1KI', 15, 33, '1KI.15.33', 'In the third year of Asa king of Judah, Baasha the son of Ahijah began to reign over all Israel in Tirzah for twenty-four years.'),
('1KI', 15, 34, '1KI.15.34', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and walked in the way of Jeroboam, and in his sin with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('1KI', 16, 1, '1KI.16.1', 'The LORD’s word came to Jehu the son of Hanani against Baasha, saying,'),
('1KI', 16, 2, '1KI.16.2', '“Because I exalted you out of the dust and made you prince over my people Israel, and you have walked in the way of Jeroboam and have made my people Israel to sin, to provoke me to anger with their sins,'),
('1KI', 16, 3, '1KI.16.3', 'behold, I will utterly sweep away Baasha and his house; and I will make your house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat.'),
('1KI', 16, 4, '1KI.16.4', 'The dogs will eat Baasha’s descendants who die in the city; and he who dies of his in the field, the birds of the sky will eat.”'),
('1KI', 16, 5, '1KI.16.5', 'Now the rest of the acts of Baasha, and what he did, and his might, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 6, '1KI.16.6', 'Baasha slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirzah; and Elah his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 16, 7, '1KI.16.7', 'Moreover the LORD’s word came by the prophet Jehu the son of Hanani against Baasha and against his house, both because of all the evil that he did in the LORD’s sight, to provoke him to anger with the work of his hands, in being like the house of Jeroboam, and because he struck him.'),
('1KI', 16, 8, '1KI.16.8', 'In the twenty-sixth year of Asa king of Judah, Elah the son of Baasha began to reign over Israel in Tirzah for two years.'),
('1KI', 16, 9, '1KI.16.9', 'His servant Zimri, captain of half his chariots, conspired against him. Now he was in Tirzah, drinking himself drunk in the house of Arza, who was over the household in Tirzah;'),
('1KI', 16, 10, '1KI.16.10', 'and Zimri went in and struck him and killed him in the twenty-seventh year of Asa king of Judah, and reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 16, 11, '1KI.16.11', 'When he began to reign, as soon as he sat on his throne, he attacked all the house of Baasha. He didn’t leave him a single one who urinates on a wall among his relatives or his friends.'),
('1KI', 16, 12, '1KI.16.12', 'Thus Zimri destroyed all the house of Baasha, according to the LORD’s word which he spoke against Baasha by Jehu the prophet,'),
('1KI', 16, 13, '1KI.16.13', 'for all the sins of Baasha, and the sins of Elah his son, which they sinned and with which they made Israel to sin, to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger with their vanities.'),
('1KI', 16, 14, '1KI.16.14', 'Now the rest of the acts of Elah, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 15, '1KI.16.15', 'In the twenty-seventh year of Asa king of Judah, Zimri reigned seven days in Tirzah. Now the people were encamped against Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines.'),
('1KI', 16, 16, '1KI.16.16', 'The people who were encamped heard that Zimri had conspired, and had also killed the king. Therefore all Israel made Omri, the captain of the army, king over Israel that day in the camp.'),
('1KI', 16, 17, '1KI.16.17', 'Omri went up from Gibbethon, and all Israel with him, and they besieged Tirzah.'),
('1KI', 16, 18, '1KI.16.18', 'When Zimri saw that the city was taken, he went into the fortified part of the king’s house and burned the king’s house over him with fire, and died,'),
('1KI', 16, 19, '1KI.16.19', 'for his sins which he sinned in doing that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, in walking in the way of Jeroboam, and in his sin which he did to make Israel to sin.'),
('1KI', 16, 20, '1KI.16.20', 'Now the rest of the acts of Zimri, and his treason that he committed, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 21, '1KI.16.21', 'Then the people of Israel were divided into two parts: half of the people followed Tibni the son of Ginath, to make him king, and half followed Omri.'),
('1KI', 16, 22, '1KI.16.22', 'But the people who followed Omri prevailed against the people who followed Tibni the son of Ginath; so Tibni died, and Omri reigned.'),
('1KI', 16, 23, '1KI.16.23', 'In the thirty-first year of Asa king of Judah, Omri began to reign over Israel for twelve years. He reigned six years in Tirzah.'),
('1KI', 16, 24, '1KI.16.24', 'He bought the hill Samaria of Shemer for two talents of silver; and he built on the hill, and called the name of the city which he built, Samaria, after the name of Shemer, the owner of the hill.'),
('1KI', 16, 25, '1KI.16.25', 'Omri did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and dealt wickedly above all who were before him.'),
('1KI', 16, 26, '1KI.16.26', 'For he walked in all the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and in his sins with which he made Israel to sin, to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger with their vanities.'),
('1KI', 16, 27, '1KI.16.27', 'Now the rest of the acts of Omri which he did, and his might that he showed, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 28, '1KI.16.28', 'So Omri slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria; and Ahab his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 16, 29, '1KI.16.29', 'In the thirty-eighth year of Asa king of Judah, Ahab the son of Omri began to reign over Israel. Ahab the son of Omri reigned over Israel in Samaria twenty-two years.'),
('1KI', 16, 30, '1KI.16.30', 'Ahab the son of Omri did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight above all that were before him.'),
('1KI', 16, 31, '1KI.16.31', 'As if it had been a light thing for him to walk in the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, he took as wife Jezebel the daughter of Ethbaal king of the Sidonians, and went and served Baal and worshiped him.'),
('1KI', 16, 32, '1KI.16.32', 'He raised up an altar for Baal in the house of Baal, which he had built in Samaria.'),
('1KI', 16, 33, '1KI.16.33', 'Ahab made the Asherah; and Ahab did more yet to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger than all the kings of Israel who were before him.'),
('1KI', 16, 34, '1KI.16.34', 'In his days Hiel the Bethelite built Jericho. He laid its foundation with the loss of Abiram his firstborn, and set up its gates with the loss of his youngest son Segub, according to the LORD’s word, which he spoke by Joshua the son of Nun.'),
('1KI', 17, 1, '1KI.17.1', 'Elijah the Tishbite, who was one of the settlers of Gilead, said to Ahab, “As the LORD, the God of Israel, lives, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.”'),
('1KI', 17, 2, '1KI.17.2', 'Then the LORD’s word came to him, saying,'),
('1KI', 17, 3, '1KI.17.3', '“Go away from here, turn eastward, and hide yourself by the brook Cherith, that is before the Jordan.'),
('1KI', 17, 4, '1KI.17.4', 'You shall drink from the brook. I have commanded the ravens to feed you there.”'),
('1KI', 17, 5, '1KI.17.5', 'So he went and did according to the LORD’s word, for he went and lived by the brook Cherith that is before the Jordan.'),
('1KI', 17, 6, '1KI.17.6', 'The ravens brought him bread and meat in the morning, and bread and meat in the evening; and he drank from the brook.'),
('1KI', 17, 7, '1KI.17.7', 'After a while, the brook dried up, because there was no rain in the land.'),
('1KI', 17, 8, '1KI.17.8', 'The LORD’s word came to him, saying,'),
('1KI', 17, 9, '1KI.17.9', '“Arise, go to Zarephath, which belongs to Sidon, and stay there. Behold, I have commanded a widow there to sustain you.”'),
('1KI', 17, 10, '1KI.17.10', 'So he arose and went to Zarephath; and when he came to the gate of the city, behold, a widow was there gathering sticks. He called to her and said, “Please get me a little water in a jar, that I may drink.”'),
('1KI', 17, 11, '1KI.17.11', 'As she was going to get it, he called to her and said, “Please bring me a morsel of bread in your hand.”'),
('1KI', 17, 12, '1KI.17.12', 'She said, “As the LORD your God lives, I don’t have anything baked, but only a handful of meal in a jar and a little oil in a jar. Behold, I am gathering two sticks, that I may go in and bake it for me and my son, that we may eat it, and die.”'),
('1KI', 17, 13, '1KI.17.13', 'Elijah said to her, “Don’t be afraid. Go and do as you have said; but make me a little cake from it first, and bring it out to me, and afterward make some for you and for your son.'),
('1KI', 17, 14, '1KI.17.14', 'For the LORD, the God of Israel, says, ‘The jar of meal will not run out, and the jar of oil will not fail, until the day that the LORD sends rain on the earth.’”'),
('1KI', 17, 15, '1KI.17.15', 'She went and did according to the saying of Elijah; and she, he, and her household ate many days.'),
('1KI', 17, 16, '1KI.17.16', 'The jar of meal didn’t run out and the jar of oil didn’t fail, according to the LORD’s word, which he spoke by Elijah.'),
('1KI', 17, 17, '1KI.17.17', 'After these things, the son of the woman, the mistress of the house, became sick; and his sickness was so severe that there was no breath left in him.'),
('1KI', 17, 18, '1KI.17.18', 'She said to Elijah, “What have I to do with you, you man of God? You have come to me to bring my sin to memory, and to kill my son!”'),
('1KI', 17, 19, '1KI.17.19', 'He said to her, “Give me your son.” He took him out of her bosom, and carried him up into the room where he stayed, and laid him on his own bed.'),
('1KI', 17, 20, '1KI.17.20', 'He cried to the LORD and said, “LORD my God, have you also brought evil on the widow with whom I am staying, by killing her son?”'),
('1KI', 17, 21, '1KI.17.21', 'He stretched himself on the child three times, and cried to the LORD and said, “LORD my God, please let this child’s soul come into him again.”'),
('1KI', 17, 22, '1KI.17.22', 'The LORD listened to the voice of Elijah; and the soul of the child came into him again, and he revived.'),
('1KI', 17, 23, '1KI.17.23', 'Elijah took the child and brought him down out of the room into the house, and delivered him to his mother; and Elijah said, “Behold, your son lives.”'),
('1KI', 17, 24, '1KI.17.24', 'The woman said to Elijah, “Now I know that you are a man of God, and that the LORD’s word in your mouth is truth.”'),
('1KI', 18, 1, '1KI.18.1', 'After many days, the LORD’s word came to Elijah, in the third year, saying, “Go, show yourself to Ahab; and I will send rain on the earth.”'),
('1KI', 18, 2, '1KI.18.2', 'Elijah went to show himself to Ahab. The famine was severe in Samaria.'),
('1KI', 18, 3, '1KI.18.3', 'Ahab called Obadiah, who was over the household. (Now Obadiah feared the LORD greatly;'),
('1KI', 18, 4, '1KI.18.4', 'for when Jezebel cut off the LORD’s prophets, Obadiah took one hundred prophets, and hid them fifty to a cave, and fed them with bread and water.)'),
('1KI', 18, 5, '1KI.18.5', 'Ahab said to Obadiah, “Go through the land, to all the springs of water, and to all the brooks. Perhaps we may find grass and save the horses and mules alive, that we not lose all the animals.”'),
('1KI', 18, 6, '1KI.18.6', 'So they divided the land between them to pass throughout it. Ahab went one way by himself, and Obadiah went another way by himself.'),
('1KI', 18, 7, '1KI.18.7', 'As Obadiah was on the way, behold, Elijah met him. He recognized him, and fell on his face, and said, “Is it you, my lord Elijah?”'),
('1KI', 18, 8, '1KI.18.8', 'He answered him, “It is I. Go, tell your lord, ‘Behold, Elijah is here!’”'),
('1KI', 18, 9, '1KI.18.9', 'He said, “How have I sinned, that you would deliver your servant into the hand of Ahab, to kill me?'),
('1KI', 18, 10, '1KI.18.10', 'As the LORD your God lives, there is no nation or kingdom where my lord has not sent to seek you. When they said, ‘He is not here,’ he took an oath of the kingdom and nation that they didn’t find you.'),
('1KI', 18, 11, '1KI.18.11', 'Now you say, ‘Go, tell your lord, “Behold, Elijah is here.”’'),
('1KI', 18, 12, '1KI.18.12', 'It will happen, as soon as I leave you, that the LORD’s Spirit will carry you I don’t know where; and so when I come and tell Ahab, and he can’t find you, he will kill me. But I, your servant, have feared the LORD from my youth.'),
('1KI', 18, 13, '1KI.18.13', 'Wasn’t it told my lord what I did when Jezebel killed the LORD’s prophets, how I hid one hundred men of the LORD’s prophets with fifty to a cave, and fed them with bread and water?'),
('1KI', 18, 14, '1KI.18.14', 'Now you say, ‘Go, tell your lord, “Behold, Elijah is here”.’ He will kill me.”'),
('1KI', 18, 15, '1KI.18.15', 'Elijah said, “As the LORD of Armies lives, before whom I stand, I will surely show myself to him today.”'),
('1KI', 18, 16, '1KI.18.16', 'So Obadiah went to meet Ahab, and told him; and Ahab went to meet Elijah.'),
('1KI', 18, 17, '1KI.18.17', 'When Ahab saw Elijah, Ahab said to him, “Is that you, you troubler of Israel?”'),
('1KI', 18, 18, '1KI.18.18', 'He answered, “I have not troubled Israel, but you and your father’s house, in that you have forsaken the LORD’s commandments and you have followed the Baals.'),
('1KI', 18, 19, '1KI.18.19', 'Now therefore send, and gather to me all Israel to Mount Carmel, and four hundred fifty of the prophets of Baal, and four hundred of the prophets of the Asherah, who eat at Jezebel’s table.”'),
('1KI', 18, 20, '1KI.18.20', 'So Ahab sent to all the children of Israel, and gathered the prophets together to Mount Carmel.'),
('1KI', 18, 21, '1KI.18.21', 'Elijah came near to all the people, and said, “How long will you waver between the two sides? If the LORD is God, follow him; but if Baal, then follow him.” The people didn’t say a word.'),
('1KI', 18, 22, '1KI.18.22', 'Then Elijah said to the people, “I, even I only, am left as a prophet of the LORD; but Baal’s prophets are four hundred fifty men.'),
('1KI', 18, 23, '1KI.18.23', 'Let them therefore give us two bulls; and let them choose one bull for themselves, and cut it in pieces, and lay it on the wood, and put no fire under; and I will dress the other bull, and lay it on the wood, and put no fire under it.'),
('1KI', 18, 24, '1KI.18.24', 'You call on the name of your god, and I will call on the LORD’s name. The God who answers by fire, let him be God.” All the people answered, “What you say is good.”'),
('1KI', 18, 25, '1KI.18.25', 'Elijah said to the prophets of Baal, “Choose one bull for yourselves, and dress it first, for you are many; and call on the name of your god, but put no fire under it.”'),
('1KI', 18, 26, '1KI.18.26', 'They took the bull which was given them, and they dressed it, and called on the name of Baal from morning even until noon, saying, “Baal, hear us!” But there was no voice, and nobody answered. They leaped about the altar which was made.'),
('1KI', 18, 27, '1KI.18.27', 'At noon, Elijah mocked them, and said, “Cry aloud, for he is a god. Either he is deep in thought, or he has gone somewhere, or he is on a journey, or perhaps he sleeps and must be awakened.”'),
('1KI', 18, 28, '1KI.18.28', 'They cried aloud, and cut themselves in their way with knives and lances until the blood gushed out on them.'),
('1KI', 18, 29, '1KI.18.29', 'When midday was past, they prophesied until the time of the evening offering; but there was no voice, no answer, and nobody paid attention.'),
('1KI', 18, 30, '1KI.18.30', 'Elijah said to all the people, “Come near to me!”; and all the people came near to him. He repaired the LORD’s altar that had been thrown down.'),
('1KI', 18, 31, '1KI.18.31', 'Elijah took twelve stones, according to the number of the tribes of the sons of Jacob, to whom the LORD’s word came, saying, “Israel shall be your name.”'),
('1KI', 18, 32, '1KI.18.32', 'With the stones he built an altar in the LORD’s name. He made a trench around the altar large enough to contain two seahs of seed.'),
('1KI', 18, 33, '1KI.18.33', 'He put the wood in order, and cut the bull in pieces and laid it on the wood. He said, “Fill four jars with water, and pour it on the burnt offering and on the wood.”'),
('1KI', 18, 34, '1KI.18.34', 'He said, “Do it a second time;” and they did it the second time. He said, “Do it a third time;” and they did it the third time.'),
('1KI', 18, 35, '1KI.18.35', 'The water ran around the altar; and he also filled the trench with water.'),
('1KI', 18, 36, '1KI.18.36', 'At the time of the evening offering, Elijah the prophet came near and said, “LORD, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Israel, let it be known today that you are God in Israel and that I am your servant, and that I have done all these things at your word.'),
('1KI', 18, 37, '1KI.18.37', 'Hear me, LORD, hear me, that this people may know that you, LORD, are God, and that you have turned their heart back again.”'),
('1KI', 18, 38, '1KI.18.38', 'Then the LORD’s fire fell and consumed the burnt offering, the wood, the stones, and the dust; and it licked up the water that was in the trench.'),
('1KI', 18, 39, '1KI.18.39', 'When all the people saw it, they fell on their faces. They said, “The LORD, he is God! The LORD, he is God!”'),
('1KI', 18, 40, '1KI.18.40', 'Elijah said to them, “Seize the prophets of Baal! Don’t let one of them escape!” They seized them; and Elijah brought them down to the brook Kishon, and killed them there.'),
('1KI', 18, 41, '1KI.18.41', 'Elijah said to Ahab, “Get up, eat and drink; for there is the sound of abundance of rain.”'),
('1KI', 18, 42, '1KI.18.42', 'So Ahab went up to eat and to drink. Elijah went up to the top of Carmel; and he bowed himself down on the earth, and put his face between his knees.'),
('1KI', 18, 43, '1KI.18.43', 'He said to his servant, “Go up now and look toward the sea.” He went up and looked, then said, “There is nothing.” He said, “Go again” seven times.'),
('1KI', 18, 44, '1KI.18.44', 'On the seventh time, he said, “Behold, a small cloud, like a man’s hand, is rising out of the sea.” He said, “Go up, tell Ahab, ‘Get ready and go down, so that the rain doesn’t stop you.’”'),
('1KI', 18, 45, '1KI.18.45', 'In a little while, the sky grew black with clouds and wind, and there was a great rain. Ahab rode, and went to Jezreel.'),
('1KI', 18, 46, '1KI.18.46', 'The LORD’s hand was on Elijah; and he tucked his cloak into his belt and ran before Ahab to the entrance of Jezreel.'),
('1KI', 19, 1, '1KI.19.1', 'Ahab told Jezebel all that Elijah had done, and how he had killed all the prophets with the sword.'),
('1KI', 19, 2, '1KI.19.2', 'Then Jezebel sent a messenger to Elijah, saying, “So let the gods do to me, and more also, if I don’t make your life as the life of one of them by tomorrow about this time!”'),
('1KI', 19, 3, '1KI.19.3', 'When he saw that, he arose and ran for his life, and came to Beersheba, which belongs to Judah, and left his servant there.'),
('1KI', 19, 4, '1KI.19.4', 'But he himself went a day’s journey into the wilderness, and came and sat down under a juniper tree. Then he requested for himself that he might die, and said, “It is enough. Now, O LORD, take away my life; for I am not better than my fathers.”'),
('1KI', 19, 5, '1KI.19.5', 'He lay down and slept under a juniper tree; and behold, an angel touched him, and said to him, “Arise and eat!”'),
('1KI', 19, 6, '1KI.19.6', 'He looked, and behold, there was at his head a cake baked on the coals, and a jar of water. He ate and drank, and lay down again.'),
('1KI', 19, 7, '1KI.19.7', 'The LORD’s angel came again the second time, and touched him, and said, “Arise and eat, because the journey is too great for you.”'),
('1KI', 19, 8, '1KI.19.8', 'He arose, and ate and drank, and went in the strength of that food forty days and forty nights to Horeb, God’s Mountain.'),
('1KI', 19, 9, '1KI.19.9', 'He came to a cave there, and camped there; and behold, the LORD’s word came to him, and he said to him, “What are you doing here, Elijah?”'),
('1KI', 19, 10, '1KI.19.10', 'He said, “I have been very jealous for the LORD, the God of Armies; for the children of Israel have forsaken your covenant, thrown down your altars, and killed your prophets with the sword. I, even I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.”'),
('1KI', 19, 11, '1KI.19.11', 'He said, “Go out and stand on the mountain before the LORD.” Behold, the LORD passed by, and a great and strong wind tore the mountains and broke in pieces the rocks before the LORD; but the LORD was not in the wind. After the wind there was an earthquake; but the LORD was not in the earthquake.'),
('1KI', 19, 12, '1KI.19.12', 'After the earthquake a fire passed; but the LORD was not in the fire. After the fire, there was a still small voice.'),
('1KI', 19, 13, '1KI.19.13', 'When Elijah heard it, he wrapped his face in his mantle, went out, and stood in the entrance of the cave. Behold, a voice came to him, and said, “What are you doing here, Elijah?”'),
('1KI', 19, 14, '1KI.19.14', 'He said, “I have been very jealous for the LORD, the God of Armies; for the children of Israel have forsaken your covenant, thrown down your altars, and killed your prophets with the sword. I, even I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.”'),
('1KI', 19, 15, '1KI.19.15', 'The LORD said to him, “Go, return on your way to the wilderness of Damascus. When you arrive, anoint Hazael to be king over Syria.'),
('1KI', 19, 16, '1KI.19.16', 'Anoint Jehu the son of Nimshi to be king over Israel; and anoint Elisha the son of Shaphat of Abel Meholah to be prophet in your place.'),
('1KI', 19, 17, '1KI.19.17', 'He who escapes from the sword of Hazael, Jehu will kill; and he who escapes from the sword of Jehu, Elisha will kill.'),
('1KI', 19, 18, '1KI.19.18', 'Yet I reserved seven thousand in Israel, all the knees of which have not bowed to Baal, and every mouth that has not kissed him.”'),
('1KI', 19, 19, '1KI.19.19', 'So he departed from there and found Elisha the son of Shaphat, who was plowing with twelve yoke of oxen before him, and he with the twelfth. Elijah went over to him and put his mantle on him.'),
('1KI', 19, 20, '1KI.19.20', 'Elisha left the oxen and ran after Elijah, and said, “Let me please kiss my father and my mother, and then I will follow you.” He said to him, “Go back again; for what have I done to you?”'),
('1KI', 19, 21, '1KI.19.21', 'He returned from following him, and took the yoke of oxen, killed them, and boiled their meat with the oxen’s equipment, and gave to the people; and they ate. Then he arose, and went after Elijah, and served him.'),
('1KI', 20, 1, '1KI.20.1', 'Ben Hadad the king of Syria gathered all his army together; and there were thirty-two kings with him, with horses and chariots. He went up and besieged Samaria, and fought against it.'),
('1KI', 20, 2, '1KI.20.2', 'He sent messengers into the city to Ahab king of Israel and said to him, “Ben Hadad says,'),
('1KI', 20, 3, '1KI.20.3', '‘Your silver and your gold are mine. Your wives also and your children, even the best, are mine.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 4, '1KI.20.4', 'The king of Israel answered, “It is according to your saying, my lord, O king. I am yours, and all that I have.”'),
('1KI', 20, 5, '1KI.20.5', 'The messengers came again and said, “Ben Hadad says, ‘I sent indeed to you, saying, “You shall deliver me your silver, your gold, your wives, and your children;'),
('1KI', 20, 6, '1KI.20.6', 'but I will send my servants to you tomorrow about this time, and they will search your house and the houses of your servants. Whatever is pleasant in your eyes, they will put it in their hand, and take it away.”’”'),
('1KI', 20, 7, '1KI.20.7', 'Then the king of Israel called all the elders of the land, and said, “Please notice how this man seeks mischief; for he sent to me for my wives, and for my children, and for my silver, and for my gold; and I didn’t deny him.”'),
('1KI', 20, 8, '1KI.20.8', 'All the elders and all the people said to him, “Don’t listen, and don’t consent.”'),
('1KI', 20, 9, '1KI.20.9', 'Therefore he said to the messengers of Ben Hadad, “Tell my lord the king, ‘All that you sent for to your servant at the first I will do, but this thing I cannot do.’” The messengers departed and brought him back the message.'),
('1KI', 20, 10, '1KI.20.10', 'Ben Hadad sent to him, and said, “The gods do so to me, and more also, if the dust of Samaria will be enough for handfuls for all the people who follow me.”'),
('1KI', 20, 11, '1KI.20.11', 'The king of Israel answered, “Tell him, ‘Don’t let him who puts on his armor brag like he who takes it off.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 12, '1KI.20.12', 'When Ben Hadad heard this message as he was drinking, he and the kings in the pavilions, he said to his servants, “Prepare to attack!” So they prepared to attack the city.'),
('1KI', 20, 13, '1KI.20.13', 'Behold, a prophet came near to Ahab king of Israel, and said, “The LORD says, ‘Have you seen all this great multitude? Behold, I will deliver it into your hand today. Then you will know that I am the LORD.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 14, '1KI.20.14', 'Ahab said, “By whom?” He said, “The LORD says, ‘By the young men of the princes of the provinces.’” Then he said, “Who shall begin the battle?” He answered, “You.”'),
('1KI', 20, 15, '1KI.20.15', 'Then he mustered the young men of the princes of the provinces, and they were two hundred and thirty-two. After them, he mustered all the people, even all the children of Israel, being seven thousand.'),
('1KI', 20, 16, '1KI.20.16', 'They went out at noon. But Ben Hadad was drinking himself drunk in the pavilions, he and the kings, the thirty-two kings who helped him.'),
('1KI', 20, 17, '1KI.20.17', 'The young men of the princes of the provinces went out first; and Ben Hadad sent out, and they told him, saying, “Men are coming out from Samaria.”'),
('1KI', 20, 18, '1KI.20.18', 'He said, “If they have come out for peace, take them alive; or if they have come out for war, take them alive.”'),
('1KI', 20, 19, '1KI.20.19', 'So these went out of the city, the young men of the princes of the provinces, and the army which followed them.'),
('1KI', 20, 20, '1KI.20.20', 'They each killed his man. The Syrians fled, and Israel pursued them. Ben Hadad the king of Syria escaped on a horse with horsemen.'),
('1KI', 20, 21, '1KI.20.21', 'The king of Israel went out and struck the horses and chariots, and killed the Syrians with a great slaughter.'),
('1KI', 20, 22, '1KI.20.22', 'The prophet came near to the king of Israel and said to him, “Go, strengthen yourself, and plan what you must do, for at the return of the year, the king of Syria will come up against you.”'),
('1KI', 20, 23, '1KI.20.23', 'The servants of the king of Syria said to him, “Their god is a god of the hills; therefore they were stronger than we. But let’s fight against them in the plain, and surely we will be stronger than they.'),
('1KI', 20, 24, '1KI.20.24', 'Do this thing: take the kings away, every man out of his place, and put captains in their place.'),
('1KI', 20, 25, '1KI.20.25', 'Muster an army like the army that you have lost, horse for horse and chariot for chariot. We will fight against them in the plain, and surely we will be stronger than they are.” He listened to their voice and did so.'),
('1KI', 20, 26, '1KI.20.26', 'At the return of the year, Ben Hadad mustered the Syrians and went up to Aphek to fight against Israel.'),
('1KI', 20, 27, '1KI.20.27', 'The children of Israel were mustered and given provisions, and went against them. The children of Israel encamped before them like two little flocks of young goats, but the Syrians filled the country.'),
('1KI', 20, 28, '1KI.20.28', 'A man of God came near and spoke to the king of Israel, and said, “The LORD says, ‘Because the Syrians have said, “The LORD is a god of the hills, but he is not a god of the valleys,” therefore I will deliver all this great multitude into your hand, and you shall know that I am the LORD.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 29, '1KI.20.29', 'They encamped opposite each other for seven days. Then on the seventh day the battle was joined; and the children of Israel killed one hundred thousand footmen of the Syrians in one day.'),
('1KI', 20, 30, '1KI.20.30', 'But the rest fled to Aphek, into the city; and the wall fell on twenty-seven thousand men who were left. Ben Hadad fled and came into the city, into an inner room.'),
('1KI', 20, 31, '1KI.20.31', 'His servants said to him, “See now, we have heard that the kings of the house of Israel are merciful kings. Please let us put sackcloth on our bodies and ropes on our heads, and go out to the king of Israel. Maybe he will save your life.”'),
('1KI', 20, 32, '1KI.20.32', 'So they put sackcloth on their bodies and ropes on their heads, and came to the king of Israel, and said, “Your servant Ben Hadad says, ‘Please let me live.’” He said, “Is he still alive? He is my brother.”'),
('1KI', 20, 33, '1KI.20.33', 'Now the men observed diligently and hurried to take this phrase; and they said, “Your brother Ben Hadad.” Then he said, “Go, bring him.” Then Ben Hadad came out to him; and he caused him to come up into the chariot.'),
('1KI', 20, 34, '1KI.20.34', 'Ben Hadad said to him, “The cities which my father took from your father I will restore. You shall make streets for yourself in Damascus, as my father made in Samaria.” “I”, said Ahab, “will let you go with this covenant.” So he made a covenant with him and let him go.'),
('1KI', 20, 35, '1KI.20.35', 'A certain man of the sons of the prophets said to his fellow by the LORD’s word, “Please strike me!” The man refused to strike him.'),
('1KI', 20, 36, '1KI.20.36', 'Then he said to him, “Because you have not obeyed the LORD’s voice, behold, as soon as you have departed from me, a lion will kill you.” As soon as he had departed from him, a lion found him and killed him.'),
('1KI', 20, 37, '1KI.20.37', 'Then he found another man, and said, “Please strike me.” The man struck him and wounded him.'),
('1KI', 20, 38, '1KI.20.38', 'So the prophet departed and waited for the king by the way, and disguised himself with his headband over his eyes.'),
('1KI', 20, 39, '1KI.20.39', 'As the king passed by, he cried to the king, and he said, “Your servant went out into the middle of the battle; and behold, a man came over and brought a man to me, and said, ‘Guard this man! If by any means he is missing, then your life shall be for his life, or else you shall pay a talent of silver.’'),
('1KI', 20, 40, '1KI.20.40', 'As your servant was busy here and there, he was gone.” The king of Israel said to him, “So shall your judgment be. You yourself have decided it.”'),
('1KI', 20, 41, '1KI.20.41', 'He hurried, and took the headband away from his eyes; and the king of Israel recognized that he was one of the prophets.'),
('1KI', 20, 42, '1KI.20.42', 'He said to him, “The LORD says, ‘Because you have let go out of your hand the man whom I had devoted to destruction, therefore your life will take the place of his life, and your people take the place of his people.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 43, '1KI.20.43', 'The king of Israel went to his house sullen and angry, and came to Samaria.'),
('1KI', 21, 1, '1KI.21.1', 'After these things, Naboth the Jezreelite had a vineyard which was in Jezreel, next to the palace of Ahab king of Samaria.'),
('1KI', 21, 2, '1KI.21.2', 'Ahab spoke to Naboth, saying, “Give me your vineyard, that I may have it for a garden of herbs, because it is near my house; and I will give you for it a better vineyard than it. Or, if it seems good to you, I will give you its worth in money.”'),
('1KI', 21, 3, '1KI.21.3', 'Naboth said to Ahab, “May the LORD forbid me, that I should give the inheritance of my fathers to you!”'),
('1KI', 21, 4, '1KI.21.4', 'Ahab came into his house sullen and angry because of the word which Naboth the Jezreelite had spoken to him, for he had said, “I will not give you the inheritance of my fathers.” He laid himself down on his bed, and turned away his face, and would eat no bread.'),
('1KI', 21, 5, '1KI.21.5', 'But Jezebel his wife came to him, and said to him, “Why is your spirit so sad that you eat no bread?”'),
('1KI', 21, 6, '1KI.21.6', 'He said to her, “Because I spoke to Naboth the Jezreelite, and said to him, ‘Give me your vineyard for money; or else, if it pleases you, I will give you another vineyard for it.’ He answered, ‘I will not give you my vineyard.’”'),
('1KI', 21, 7, '1KI.21.7', 'Jezebel his wife said to him, “Do you now govern the kingdom of Israel? Arise, and eat bread, and let your heart be merry. I will give you the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite.”'),
('1KI', 21, 8, '1KI.21.8', 'So she wrote letters in Ahab’s name and sealed them with his seal, and sent the letters to the elders and to the nobles who were in his city, who lived with Naboth.'),
('1KI', 21, 9, '1KI.21.9', 'She wrote in the letters, saying, “Proclaim a fast, and set Naboth on high among the people.'),
('1KI', 21, 10, '1KI.21.10', 'Set two men, wicked fellows, before him, and let them testify against him, saying, ‘You cursed God and the king!’ Then carry him out, and stone him to death.”'),
('1KI', 21, 11, '1KI.21.11', 'The men of his city, even the elders and the nobles who lived in his city, did as Jezebel had instructed them in the letters which she had written and sent to them.'),
('1KI', 21, 12, '1KI.21.12', 'They proclaimed a fast, and set Naboth on high among the people.'),
('1KI', 21, 13, '1KI.21.13', 'The two men, the wicked fellows, came in and sat before him. The wicked fellows testified against him, even against Naboth, in the presence of the people, saying, “Naboth cursed God and the king!” Then they carried him out of the city and stoned him to death with stones.'),
('1KI', 21, 14, '1KI.21.14', 'Then they sent to Jezebel, saying, “Naboth has been stoned and is dead.”'),
('1KI', 21, 15, '1KI.21.15', 'When Jezebel heard that Naboth had been stoned and was dead, Jezebel said to Ahab, “Arise, take possession of the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, which he refused to give you for money; for Naboth is not alive, but dead.”'),
('1KI', 21, 16, '1KI.21.16', 'When Ahab heard that Naboth was dead, Ahab rose up to go down to the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, to take possession of it.'),
('1KI', 21, 17, '1KI.21.17', 'The LORD’s word came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,'),
('1KI', 21, 18, '1KI.21.18', '“Arise, go down to meet Ahab king of Israel, who dwells in Samaria. Behold, he is in the vineyard of Naboth, where he has gone down to take possession of it.'),
('1KI', 21, 19, '1KI.21.19', 'You shall speak to him, saying, ‘The LORD says, “Have you killed and also taken possession?”’ You shall speak to him, saying, ‘The LORD says, “In the place where dogs licked the blood of Naboth, dogs will lick your blood, even yours.”’”'),
('1KI', 21, 20, '1KI.21.20', 'Ahab said to Elijah, “Have you found me, my enemy?” He answered, “I have found you, because you have sold yourself to do that which is evil in the LORD’s sight.'),
('1KI', 21, 21, '1KI.21.21', 'Behold, I will bring evil on you, and will utterly sweep you away and will cut off from Ahab everyone who urinates against a wall, and him who is shut up and him who is left at large in Israel.'),
('1KI', 21, 22, '1KI.21.22', 'I will make your house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah, for the provocation with which you have provoked me to anger, and have made Israel to sin.”'),
('1KI', 21, 23, '1KI.21.23', 'The LORD also spoke of Jezebel, saying, “The dogs will eat Jezebel by the rampart of Jezreel.'),
('1KI', 21, 24, '1KI.21.24', 'The dogs will eat whoever dies of Ahab in the city; and the birds of the sky will eat whoever dies in the field.”'),
('1KI', 21, 25, '1KI.21.25', 'But there was no one like Ahab, who sold himself to do that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, whom Jezebel his wife stirred up.'),
('1KI', 21, 26, '1KI.21.26', 'He did very abominably in following idols, according to all that the Amorites did, whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.'),
('1KI', 21, 27, '1KI.21.27', 'When Ahab heard those words, he tore his clothes, put sackcloth on his body, fasted, lay in sackcloth, and went about despondently.'),
('1KI', 21, 28, '1KI.21.28', 'The LORD’s word came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,'),
('1KI', 21, 29, '1KI.21.29', '“See how Ahab humbles himself before me? Because he humbles himself before me, I will not bring the evil in his days; but I will bring the evil on his house in his son’s day.”'),
('1KI', 22, 1, '1KI.22.1', 'They continued three years without war between Syria and Israel.'),
('1KI', 22, 2, '1KI.22.2', 'In the third year, Jehoshaphat the king of Judah came down to the king of Israel.'),
('1KI', 22, 3, '1KI.22.3', 'The king of Israel said to his servants, “You know that Ramoth Gilead is ours, and we do nothing, and don’t take it out of the hand of the king of Syria?”'),
('1KI', 22, 4, '1KI.22.4', 'He said to Jehoshaphat, “Will you go with me to battle to Ramoth Gilead?” Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, “I am as you are, my people as your people, my horses as your horses.”'),
('1KI', 22, 5, '1KI.22.5', 'Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, “Please inquire first for the LORD’s word.”'),
('1KI', 22, 6, '1KI.22.6', 'Then the king of Israel gathered the prophets together, about four hundred men, and said to them, “Should I go against Ramoth Gilead to battle, or should I refrain?” They said, “Go up; for the Lord will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('1KI', 22, 7, '1KI.22.7', 'But Jehoshaphat said, “Isn’t there here a prophet of the LORD, that we may inquire of him?”'),
('1KI', 22, 8, '1KI.22.8', 'The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “There is yet one man by whom we may inquire of the LORD, Micaiah the son of Imlah; but I hate him, for he does not prophesy good concerning me, but evil.” Jehoshaphat said, “Don’t let the king say so.”'),
('1KI', 22, 9, '1KI.22.9', 'Then the king of Israel called an officer, and said, “Quickly get Micaiah the son of Imlah.”'),
('1KI', 22, 10, '1KI.22.10', 'Now the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah were sitting each on his throne, arrayed in their robes, in an open place at the entrance of the gate of Samaria; and all the prophets were prophesying before them.'),
('1KI', 22, 11, '1KI.22.11', 'Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah made himself horns of iron, and said, “The LORD says, ‘With these you will push the Syrians, until they are consumed.’”'),
('1KI', 22, 12, '1KI.22.12', 'All the prophets prophesied so, saying, “Go up to Ramoth Gilead and prosper; for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('1KI', 22, 13, '1KI.22.13', 'The messenger who went to call Micaiah spoke to him, saying, “See now, the prophets declare good to the king with one mouth. Please let your word be like the word of one of them, and speak good.”'),
('1KI', 22, 14, '1KI.22.14', 'Micaiah said, “As the LORD lives, what the LORD says to me, that I will speak.”'),
('1KI', 22, 15, '1KI.22.15', 'When he had come to the king, the king said to him, “Micaiah, shall we go to Ramoth Gilead to battle, or shall we forbear?” He answered him, “Go up and prosper; and the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('1KI', 22, 16, '1KI.22.16', 'The king said to him, “How many times do I have to adjure you that you speak to me nothing but the truth in the LORD’s name?”'),
('1KI', 22, 17, '1KI.22.17', 'He said, “I saw all Israel scattered on the mountains, as sheep that have no shepherd. The LORD said, ‘These have no master. Let them each return to his house in peace.’”'),
('1KI', 22, 18, '1KI.22.18', 'The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “Didn’t I tell you that he would not prophesy good concerning me, but evil?”'),
('1KI', 22, 19, '1KI.22.19', 'Micaiah said, “Therefore hear the LORD’s word. I saw the LORD sitting on his throne, and all the army of heaven standing by him on his right hand and on his left.'),
('1KI', 22, 20, '1KI.22.20', 'The LORD said, ‘Who will entice Ahab, that he may go up and fall at Ramoth Gilead?’ One said one thing, and another said another.'),
('1KI', 22, 21, '1KI.22.21', 'A spirit came out and stood before the LORD, and said, ‘I will entice him.’'),
('1KI', 22, 22, '1KI.22.22', 'The LORD said to him, ‘How?’ He said, ‘I will go out and will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets.’ He said, ‘You will entice him, and will also prevail. Go out and do so.’'),
('1KI', 22, 23, '1KI.22.23', 'Now therefore, behold, the LORD has put a lying spirit in the mouth of all these your prophets; and the LORD has spoken evil concerning you.”'),
('1KI', 22, 24, '1KI.22.24', 'Then Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah came near and struck Micaiah on the cheek, and said, “Which way did the LORD’s Spirit go from me to speak to you?”'),
('1KI', 22, 25, '1KI.22.25', 'Micaiah said, “Behold, you will see on that day when you go into an inner room to hide yourself.”'),
('1KI', 22, 26, '1KI.22.26', 'The king of Israel said, “Take Micaiah, and carry him back to Amon the governor of the city and to Joash the king’s son.'),
('1KI', 22, 27, '1KI.22.27', 'Say, ‘The king says, “Put this fellow in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I come in peace.”’”'),
('1KI', 22, 28, '1KI.22.28', 'Micaiah said, “If you return at all in peace, the LORD has not spoken by me.” He said, “Listen, all you people!”'),
('1KI', 22, 29, '1KI.22.29', 'So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went up to Ramoth Gilead.'),
('1KI', 22, 30, '1KI.22.30', 'The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “I will disguise myself and go into the battle, but you put on your robes.” The king of Israel disguised himself and went into the battle.'),
('1KI', 22, 31, '1KI.22.31', 'Now the king of Syria had commanded the thirty-two captains of his chariots, saying, “Don’t fight with small nor great, except only with the king of Israel.”'),
('1KI', 22, 32, '1KI.22.32', 'When the captains of the chariots saw Jehoshaphat, they said, “Surely that is the king of Israel!” and they came over to fight against him. Jehoshaphat cried out.'),
('1KI', 22, 33, '1KI.22.33', 'When the captains of the chariots saw that it was not the king of Israel, they turned back from pursuing him.'),
('1KI', 22, 34, '1KI.22.34', 'A certain man drew his bow at random, and struck the king of Israel between the joints of the armor. Therefore he said to the driver of his chariot, “Turn around, and carry me out of the battle, for I am severely wounded.”'),
('1KI', 22, 35, '1KI.22.35', 'The battle increased that day. The king was propped up in his chariot facing the Syrians, and died at evening. The blood ran out of the wound into the bottom of the chariot.'),
('1KI', 22, 36, '1KI.22.36', 'A cry went throughout the army about the going down of the sun, saying, “Every man to his city, and every man to his country!”'),
('1KI', 22, 37, '1KI.22.37', 'So the king died, and was brought to Samaria; and they buried the king in Samaria.'),
('1KI', 22, 38, '1KI.22.38', 'They washed the chariot by the pool of Samaria; and the dogs licked up his blood where the prostitutes washed themselves, according to the LORD’s word which he spoke.'),
('1KI', 22, 39, '1KI.22.39', 'Now the rest of the acts of Ahab, and all that he did, and the ivory house which he built, and all the cities that he built, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 22, 40, '1KI.22.40', 'So Ahab slept with his fathers; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 22, 41, '1KI.22.41', 'Jehoshaphat the son of Asa began to reign over Judah in the fourth year of Ahab king of Israel.'),
('1KI', 22, 42, '1KI.22.42', 'Jehoshaphat was thirty-five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty-five years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Azubah the daughter of Shilhi.'),
('1KI', 22, 43, '1KI.22.43', 'He walked in all the way of Asa his father. He didn’t turn away from it, doing that which was right in the LORD’s eyes. However, the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense on the high places.'),
('1KI', 22, 44, '1KI.22.44', 'Jehoshaphat made peace with the king of Israel.'),
('1KI', 22, 45, '1KI.22.45', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, and his might that he showed, and how he fought, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('1KI', 22, 46, '1KI.22.46', 'The remnant of the sodomites, that remained in the days of his father Asa, he put away out of the land.'),
('1KI', 22, 47, '1KI.22.47', 'There was no king in Edom. A deputy ruled.'),
('1KI', 22, 48, '1KI.22.48', 'Jehoshaphat made ships of Tarshish to go to Ophir for gold, but they didn’t go, for the ships wrecked at Ezion Geber.'),
('1KI', 22, 49, '1KI.22.49', 'Then Ahaziah the son of Ahab said to Jehoshaphat, “Let my servants go with your servants in the ships.” But Jehoshaphat would not.'),
('1KI', 22, 50, '1KI.22.50', 'Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David’s city. Jehoram his son reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 22, 51, '1KI.22.51', 'Ahaziah the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria in the seventeenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and he reigned two years over Israel.'),
('1KI', 22, 52, '1KI.22.52', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and walked in the way of his father, and in the way of his mother, and in the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, in which he made Israel to sin.'),
('1KI', 22, 53, '1KI.22.53', 'He served Baal and worshiped him, and provoked the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger in all the ways that his father had done so.'),
('2KI', 1, 1, '2KI.1.1', 'Moab rebelled against Israel after the death of Ahab.'),
('2KI', 1, 2, '2KI.1.2', 'Ahaziah fell down through the lattice in his upper room that was in Samaria, and was sick. So he sent messengers, and said to them, “Go, inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron, whether I will recover from this sickness.”'),
('2KI', 1, 3, '2KI.1.3', 'But the LORD’s angel said to Elijah the Tishbite, “Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and tell them, ‘Is it because there is no God in Israel that you go to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron?'),
('2KI', 1, 4, '2KI.1.4', 'Now therefore the LORD says, “You will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.”’” Then Elijah departed.'),
('2KI', 1, 5, '2KI.1.5', 'The messengers returned to him, and he said to them, “Why is it that you have returned?”'),
('2KI', 1, 6, '2KI.1.6', 'They said to him, “A man came up to meet us, and said to us, ‘Go, return to the king who sent you, and tell him, “The LORD says, ‘Is it because there is no God in Israel that you send to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron? Therefore you will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.’”’”'),
('2KI', 1, 7, '2KI.1.7', 'He said to them, “What kind of man was he who came up to meet you and told you these words?”'),
('2KI', 1, 8, '2KI.1.8', 'They answered him, “He was a hairy man, and wearing a leather belt around his waist.” He said, “It’s Elijah the Tishbite.”'),
('2KI', 1, 9, '2KI.1.9', 'Then the king sent a captain of fifty with his fifty to him. He went up to him; and behold, he was sitting on the top of the hill. He said to him, “Man of God, the king has said, ‘Come down!’”'),
('2KI', 1, 10, '2KI.1.10', 'Elijah answered to the captain of fifty, “If I am a man of God, then let fire come down from the sky and consume you and your fifty!” Then fire came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty.'),
('2KI', 1, 11, '2KI.1.11', 'Again he sent to him another captain of fifty with his fifty. He answered him, “Man of God, the king has said, ‘Come down quickly!’”'),
('2KI', 1, 12, '2KI.1.12', 'Elijah answered them, “If I am a man of God, then let fire come down from the sky and consume you and your fifty!” Then God’s fire came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty.'),
('2KI', 1, 13, '2KI.1.13', 'Again he sent the captain of a third fifty with his fifty. The third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Elijah, and begged him, and said to him, “Man of God, please let my life and the life of these fifty of your servants be precious in your sight.'),
('2KI', 1, 14, '2KI.1.14', 'Behold, fire came down from the sky and consumed the last two captains of fifty with their fifties. But now let my life be precious in your sight.”'),
('2KI', 1, 15, '2KI.1.15', 'The LORD’s angel said to Elijah, “Go down with him. Don’t be afraid of him.” Then he arose and went down with him to the king.'),
('2KI', 1, 16, '2KI.1.16', 'He said to him, “The LORD says, ‘Because you have sent messengers to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron, is it because there is no God in Israel to inquire of his word? Therefore you will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.’”'),
('2KI', 1, 17, '2KI.1.17', 'So he died according to the LORD’s word which Elijah had spoken. Jehoram began to reign in his place in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, because he had no son.'),
('2KI', 1, 18, '2KI.1.18', 'Now the rest of the acts of Ahaziah which he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 2, 1, '2KI.2.1', 'When the LORD was about to take Elijah up by a whirlwind into heaven, Elijah went with Elisha from Gilgal.'),
('2KI', 2, 2, '2KI.2.2', 'Elijah said to Elisha, “Please wait here, for the LORD has sent me as far as Bethel.” Elisha said, “As the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.” So they went down to Bethel.'),
('2KI', 2, 3, '2KI.2.3', 'The sons of the prophets who were at Bethel came out to Elisha, and said to him, “Do you know that the LORD will take away your master from over you today?” He said, “Yes, I know it. Hold your peace.”'),
('2KI', 2, 4, '2KI.2.4', 'Elijah said to him, “Elisha, please wait here, for the LORD has sent me to Jericho.” He said, “As the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.” So they came to Jericho.'),
('2KI', 2, 5, '2KI.2.5', 'The sons of the prophets who were at Jericho came near to Elisha, and said to him, “Do you know that the LORD will take away your master from over you today?” He answered, “Yes, I know it. Hold your peace.”'),
('2KI', 2, 6, '2KI.2.6', 'Elijah said to him, “Please wait here, for the LORD has sent me to the Jordan.” He said, “As the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.” Then they both went on.'),
('2KI', 2, 7, '2KI.2.7', 'Fifty men of the sons of the prophets went and stood opposite them at a distance; and they both stood by the Jordan.'),
('2KI', 2, 8, '2KI.2.8', 'Elijah took his mantle, and rolled it up, and struck the waters; and they were divided here and there, so that they both went over on dry ground.'),
('2KI', 2, 9, '2KI.2.9', 'When they had gone over, Elijah said to Elisha, “Ask what I shall do for you, before I am taken from you.” Elisha said, “Please let a double portion of your spirit be on me.”'),
('2KI', 2, 10, '2KI.2.10', 'He said, “You have asked a hard thing. If you see me when I am taken from you, it will be so for you; but if not, it will not be so.”'),
('2KI', 2, 11, '2KI.2.11', 'As they continued on and talked, behold, a chariot of fire and horses of fire separated them; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.'),
('2KI', 2, 12, '2KI.2.12', 'Elisha saw it, and he cried, “My father, my father, the chariots of Israel and its horsemen!” He saw him no more. Then he took hold of his own clothes and tore them in two pieces.'),
('2KI', 2, 13, '2KI.2.13', 'He also took up Elijah’s mantle that fell from him, and went back and stood by the bank of the Jordan.'),
('2KI', 2, 14, '2KI.2.14', 'He took Elijah’s mantle that fell from him, and struck the waters, and said, “Where is the LORD, the God of Elijah?” When he also had struck the waters, they were divided apart, and Elisha went over.'),
('2KI', 2, 15, '2KI.2.15', 'When the sons of the prophets who were at Jericho facing him saw him, they said, “The spirit of Elijah rests on Elisha.” They came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him.'),
('2KI', 2, 16, '2KI.2.16', 'They said to him, “See now, there are with your servants fifty strong men. Please let them go and seek your master. Perhaps the LORD’s Spirit has taken him up, and put him on some mountain or into some valley.” He said, “Don’t send them.”'),
('2KI', 2, 17, '2KI.2.17', 'When they urged him until he was ashamed, he said, “Send them.” Therefore they sent fifty men; and they searched for three days, but didn’t find him.'),
('2KI', 2, 18, '2KI.2.18', 'They came back to him while he stayed at Jericho; and he said to them, “Didn’t I tell you, ‘Don’t go’?”'),
('2KI', 2, 19, '2KI.2.19', 'The men of the city said to Elisha, “Behold, please, the situation of this city is pleasant, as my lord sees; but the water is bad, and the land is barren.”'),
('2KI', 2, 20, '2KI.2.20', 'He said, “Bring me a new jar, and put salt in it.” Then they brought it to him.'),
('2KI', 2, 21, '2KI.2.21', 'He went out to the spring of the waters, and threw salt into it, and said, “The LORD says, ‘I have healed these waters. There shall not be from there any more death or barren wasteland.’”'),
('2KI', 2, 22, '2KI.2.22', 'So the waters were healed to this day, according to Elisha’s word which he spoke.'),
('2KI', 2, 23, '2KI.2.23', 'He went up from there to Bethel. As he was going up by the way, some youths came out of the city and mocked him, and said to him, “Go up, you baldy! Go up, you baldy!”'),
('2KI', 2, 24, '2KI.2.24', 'He looked behind him and saw them, and cursed them in the LORD’s name. Then two female bears came out of the woods and mauled forty-two of those youths.'),
('2KI', 2, 25, '2KI.2.25', 'He went from there to Mount Carmel, and from there he returned to Samaria.'),
('2KI', 3, 1, '2KI.3.1', 'Now Jehoram the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria in the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned twelve years.'),
('2KI', 3, 2, '2KI.3.2', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, but not like his father and like his mother, for he put away the pillar of Baal that his father had made.'),
('2KI', 3, 3, '2KI.3.3', 'Nevertheless he held to the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin. He didn’t depart from them.'),
('2KI', 3, 4, '2KI.3.4', 'Now Mesha king of Moab was a sheep breeder; and he supplied the king of Israel with one hundred thousand lambs and the wool of one hundred thousand rams.'),
('2KI', 3, 5, '2KI.3.5', 'But when Ahab was dead, the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel.'),
('2KI', 3, 6, '2KI.3.6', 'King Jehoram went out of Samaria at that time, and mustered all Israel.'),
('2KI', 3, 7, '2KI.3.7', 'He went and sent to Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, saying, “The king of Moab has rebelled against me. Will you go with me against Moab to battle?” He said, “I will go up. I am as you are, my people as your people, my horses as your horses.”'),
('2KI', 3, 8, '2KI.3.8', 'Then he said, “Which way shall we go up?” Jehoram answered, “The way of the wilderness of Edom.”'),
('2KI', 3, 9, '2KI.3.9', 'So the king of Israel went with the king of Judah and the king of Edom, and they marched for seven days along a circuitous route. There was no water for the army or for the animals that followed them.'),
('2KI', 3, 10, '2KI.3.10', 'The king of Israel said, “Alas! For the LORD has called these three kings together to deliver them into the hand of Moab.”'),
('2KI', 3, 11, '2KI.3.11', 'But Jehoshaphat said, “Isn’t there a prophet of the LORD here, that we may inquire of the LORD by him?” One of the king of Israel’s servants answered, “Elisha the son of Shaphat, who poured water on the hands of Elijah, is here.”'),
('2KI', 3, 12, '2KI.3.12', 'Jehoshaphat said, “The LORD’s word is with him.” So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him.'),
('2KI', 3, 13, '2KI.3.13', 'Elisha said to the king of Israel, “What have I to do with you? Go to the prophets of your father, and to the prophets of your mother.” The king of Israel said to him, “No, for the LORD has called these three kings together to deliver them into the hand of Moab.”'),
('2KI', 3, 14, '2KI.3.14', 'Elisha said, “As the LORD of Armies lives, before whom I stand, surely, were it not that I respect the presence of Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, I would not look toward you, nor see you.'),
('2KI', 3, 15, '2KI.3.15', 'But now bring me a musician.” When the musician played, the LORD’s hand came on him.'),
('2KI', 3, 16, '2KI.3.16', 'He said, “The LORD says, ‘Make this valley full of trenches.’'),
('2KI', 3, 17, '2KI.3.17', 'For the LORD says, ‘You will not see wind, neither will you see rain, yet that valley will be filled with water, and you will drink, both you and your livestock and your other animals.'),
('2KI', 3, 18, '2KI.3.18', 'This is an easy thing in the LORD’s sight. He will also deliver the Moabites into your hand.'),
('2KI', 3, 19, '2KI.3.19', 'You shall strike every fortified city and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree, and stop all springs of water, and mar every good piece of land with stones.’”'),
('2KI', 3, 20, '2KI.3.20', 'In the morning, about the time of offering the sacrifice, behold, water came by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water.'),
('2KI', 3, 21, '2KI.3.21', 'Now when all the Moabites heard that the kings had come up to fight against them, they gathered themselves together, all who were able to put on armor, young and old, and stood on the border.'),
('2KI', 3, 22, '2KI.3.22', 'They rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone on the water, and the Moabites saw the water opposite them as red as blood.'),
('2KI', 3, 23, '2KI.3.23', 'They said, “This is blood. The kings are surely destroyed, and they have struck each other. Now therefore, Moab, to the plunder!”'),
('2KI', 3, 24, '2KI.3.24', 'When they came to the camp of Israel, the Israelites rose up and struck the Moabites, so that they fled before them; and they went forward into the land attacking the Moabites.'),
('2KI', 3, 25, '2KI.3.25', 'They beat down the cities; and on every good piece of land each man cast his stone, and filled it. They also stopped all the springs of water and cut down all the good trees, until in Kir Hareseth all they left was its stones; however the men armed with slings went around it and attacked it.'),
('2KI', 3, 26, '2KI.3.26', 'When the king of Moab saw that the battle was too severe for him, he took with him seven hundred men who drew a sword, to break through to the king of Edom; but they could not.'),
('2KI', 3, 27, '2KI.3.27', 'Then he took his oldest son who would have reigned in his place, and offered him for a burnt offering on the wall. There was great wrath against Israel; and they departed from him, and returned to their own land.'),
('2KI', 4, 1, '2KI.4.1', 'Now a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets cried out to Elisha, saying, “Your servant my husband is dead. You know that your servant feared the LORD. Now the creditor has come to take for himself my two children to be slaves.”'),
('2KI', 4, 2, '2KI.4.2', 'Elisha said to her, “What should I do for you? Tell me, what do you have in the house?” She said, “Your servant has nothing in the house, except a pot of oil.”'),
('2KI', 4, 3, '2KI.4.3', 'Then he said, “Go, borrow empty containers from all your neighbors. Don’t borrow just a few containers.'),
('2KI', 4, 4, '2KI.4.4', 'Go in and shut the door on you and on your sons, and pour oil into all those containers; and set aside those which are full.”'),
('2KI', 4, 5, '2KI.4.5', 'So she went from him, and shut the door on herself and on her sons. They brought the containers to her, and she poured oil.'),
('2KI', 4, 6, '2KI.4.6', 'When the containers were full, she said to her son, “Bring me another container.” He said to her, “There isn’t another container.” Then the oil stopped flowing.'),
('2KI', 4, 7, '2KI.4.7', 'Then she came and told the man of God. He said, “Go, sell the oil, and pay your debt; and you and your sons live on the rest.”'),
('2KI', 4, 8, '2KI.4.8', 'One day Elisha went to Shunem, where there was a prominent woman; and she persuaded him to eat bread. So it was, that as often as he passed by, he turned in there to eat bread.'),
('2KI', 4, 9, '2KI.4.9', 'She said to her husband, “See now, I perceive that this is a holy man of God who passes by us continually.'),
('2KI', 4, 10, '2KI.4.10', 'Please, let’s make a little room on the roof. Let’s set a bed, a table, a chair, and a lamp stand for him there. When he comes to us, he can stay there.”'),
('2KI', 4, 11, '2KI.4.11', 'One day he came there, and he went to the room and lay there.'),
('2KI', 4, 12, '2KI.4.12', 'He said to Gehazi his servant, “Call this Shunammite.” When he had called her, she stood before him.'),
('2KI', 4, 13, '2KI.4.13', 'He said to him, “Say now to her, ‘Behold, you have cared for us with all this care. What is to be done for you? Would you like to be spoken for to the king, or to the captain of the army?’” She answered, “I dwell among my own people.”'),
('2KI', 4, 14, '2KI.4.14', 'He said, “What then is to be done for her?” Gehazi answered, “Most certainly she has no son, and her husband is old.”'),
('2KI', 4, 15, '2KI.4.15', 'He said, “Call her.” When he had called her, she stood in the door.'),
('2KI', 4, 16, '2KI.4.16', 'He said, “At this season next year, you will embrace a son.” She said, “No, my lord, you man of God, do not lie to your servant.”'),
('2KI', 4, 17, '2KI.4.17', 'The woman conceived, and bore a son at that season when the time came around, as Elisha had said to her.'),
('2KI', 4, 18, '2KI.4.18', 'When the child was grown, one day he went out to his father to the reapers.'),
('2KI', 4, 19, '2KI.4.19', 'He said to his father, “My head! My head!” He said to his servant, “Carry him to his mother.”'),
('2KI', 4, 20, '2KI.4.20', 'When he had taken him and brought him to his mother, he sat on her knees until noon, and then died.'),
('2KI', 4, 21, '2KI.4.21', 'She went up and laid him on the man of God’s bed, and shut the door on him, and went out.'),
('2KI', 4, 22, '2KI.4.22', 'She called to her husband and said, “Please send me one of the servants, and one of the donkeys, that I may run to the man of God and come again.”'),
('2KI', 4, 23, '2KI.4.23', 'He said, “Why would you want to go to him today? It is not a new moon or a Sabbath.” She said, “It’s all right.”'),
('2KI', 4, 24, '2KI.4.24', 'Then she saddled a donkey, and said to her servant, “Drive, and go forward! Don’t slow down for me, unless I ask you to.”'),
('2KI', 4, 25, '2KI.4.25', 'So she went, and came to the man of God to Mount Carmel. When the man of God saw her afar off, he said to Gehazi his servant, “Behold, there is the Shunammite.'),
('2KI', 4, 26, '2KI.4.26', 'Please run now to meet her, and ask her, ‘Is it well with you? Is it well with your husband? Is it well with your child?’” She answered, “It is well.”'),
('2KI', 4, 27, '2KI.4.27', 'When she came to the man of God to the hill, she caught hold of his feet. Gehazi came near to thrust her away; but the man of God said, “Leave her alone, for her soul is troubled within her; and the LORD has hidden it from me, and has not told me.”'),
('2KI', 4, 28, '2KI.4.28', 'Then she said, “Did I ask you for a son, my lord? Didn’t I say, ‘Do not deceive me’?”'),
('2KI', 4, 29, '2KI.4.29', 'Then he said to Gehazi, “Tuck your cloak into your belt, take my staff in your hand, and go your way. If you meet any man, don’t greet him; and if anyone greets you, don’t answer him again. Then lay my staff on the child’s face.”'),
('2KI', 4, 30, '2KI.4.30', 'The child’s mother said, “As the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.” So he arose, and followed her.'),
('2KI', 4, 31, '2KI.4.31', 'Gehazi went ahead of them, and laid the staff on the child’s face; but there was no voice and no hearing. Therefore he returned to meet him, and told him, “The child has not awakened.”'),
('2KI', 4, 32, '2KI.4.32', 'When Elisha had come into the house, behold, the child was dead, and lying on his bed.'),
('2KI', 4, 33, '2KI.4.33', 'He went in therefore, and shut the door on them both, and prayed to the LORD.'),
('2KI', 4, 34, '2KI.4.34', 'He went up and lay on the child, and put his mouth on his mouth, and his eyes on his eyes, and his hands on his hands. He stretched himself on him; and the child’s flesh grew warm.'),
('2KI', 4, 35, '2KI.4.35', 'Then he returned, and walked in the house once back and forth, then went up and stretched himself out on him. Then the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes.'),
('2KI', 4, 36, '2KI.4.36', 'He called Gehazi, and said, “Call this Shunammite!” So he called her. When she had come in to him, he said, “Take up your son.”'),
('2KI', 4, 37, '2KI.4.37', 'Then she went in, fell at his feet, and bowed herself to the ground; then she picked up her son, and went out.'),
('2KI', 4, 38, '2KI.4.38', 'Elisha came again to Gilgal. There was a famine in the land; and the sons of the prophets were sitting before him; and he said to his servant, “Get the large pot, and boil stew for the sons of the prophets.”'),
('2KI', 4, 39, '2KI.4.39', 'One went out into the field to gather herbs, and found a wild vine, and gathered a lap full of wild gourds from it, and came and cut them up into the pot of stew; for they didn’t recognize them.'),
('2KI', 4, 40, '2KI.4.40', 'So they poured out for the men to eat. As they were eating some of the stew, they cried out and said, “Man of God, there is death in the pot!” And they could not eat it.'),
('2KI', 4, 41, '2KI.4.41', 'But he said, “Then bring meal.” He threw it into the pot; and he said, “Serve it to the people, that they may eat.” And there was nothing harmful in the pot.'),
('2KI', 4, 42, '2KI.4.42', 'A man from Baal Shalishah came, and brought the man of God some bread of the first fruits: twenty loaves of barley and fresh ears of grain in his sack. Elisha said, “Give to the people, that they may eat.”'),
('2KI', 4, 43, '2KI.4.43', 'His servant said, “What, should I set this before a hundred men?” But he said, “Give it to the people, that they may eat; for the LORD says, ‘They will eat, and will have some left over.’”'),
('2KI', 4, 44, '2KI.4.44', 'So he set it before them and they ate and had some left over, according to the LORD’s word.'),
('2KI', 5, 1, '2KI.5.1', 'Now Naaman, captain of the army of the king of Syria, was a great man with his master, and honorable, because by him the LORD had given victory to Syria; he was also a mighty man of valor, but he was a leper.'),
('2KI', 5, 2, '2KI.5.2', 'The Syrians had gone out in bands, and had brought away captive out of the land of Israel a little girl, and she waited on Naaman’s wife.'),
('2KI', 5, 3, '2KI.5.3', 'She said to her mistress, “I wish that my lord were with the prophet who is in Samaria! Then he would heal him of his leprosy.”'),
('2KI', 5, 4, '2KI.5.4', 'Someone went in and told his lord, saying, “The girl who is from the land of Israel said this.”'),
('2KI', 5, 5, '2KI.5.5', 'The king of Syria said, “Go now, and I will send a letter to the king of Israel.” He departed, and took with him ten talents of silver, six thousand pieces of gold, and ten changes of clothing.'),
('2KI', 5, 6, '2KI.5.6', 'He brought the letter to the king of Israel, saying, “Now when this letter has come to you, behold, I have sent Naaman my servant to you, that you may heal him of his leprosy.”'),
('2KI', 5, 7, '2KI.5.7', 'When the king of Israel had read the letter, he tore his clothes and said, “Am I God, to kill and to make alive, that this man sends to me to heal a man of his leprosy? But please consider and see how he seeks a quarrel against me.”'),
('2KI', 5, 8, '2KI.5.8', 'It was so, when Elisha the man of God heard that the king of Israel had torn his clothes, that he sent to the king, saying, “Why have you torn your clothes? Let him come now to me, and he shall know that there is a prophet in Israel.”'),
('2KI', 5, 9, '2KI.5.9', 'So Naaman came with his horses and with his chariots, and stood at the door of the house of Elisha.'),
('2KI', 5, 10, '2KI.5.10', 'Elisha sent a messenger to him, saying, “Go and wash in the Jordan seven times, and your flesh shall come again to you, and you shall be clean.”'),
('2KI', 5, 11, '2KI.5.11', 'But Naaman was angry, and went away and said, “Behold, I thought, ‘He will surely come out to me, and stand, and call on the name of the LORD his God, and wave his hand over the place, and heal the leper.’'),
('2KI', 5, 12, '2KI.5.12', 'Aren’t Abanah and Pharpar, the rivers of Damascus, better than all the waters of Israel? Couldn’t I wash in them and be clean?” So he turned and went away in a rage.'),
('2KI', 5, 13, '2KI.5.13', 'His servants came near and spoke to him, and said, “My father, if the prophet had asked you to do some great thing, wouldn’t you have done it? How much rather then, when he says to you, ‘Wash, and be clean’?”'),
('2KI', 5, 14, '2KI.5.14', 'Then he went down and dipped himself seven times in the Jordan, according to the saying of the man of God; and his flesh was restored like the flesh of a little child, and he was clean.'),
('2KI', 5, 15, '2KI.5.15', 'He returned to the man of God, he and all his company, and came, and stood before him; and he said, “See now, I know that there is no God in all the earth, but in Israel. Now therefore, please take a gift from your servant.”'),
('2KI', 5, 16, '2KI.5.16', 'But he said, “As the LORD lives, before whom I stand, I will receive none.” He urged him to take it; but he refused.'),
('2KI', 5, 17, '2KI.5.17', 'Naaman said, “If not, then, please let two mules’ load of earth be given to your servant; for your servant will from now on offer neither burnt offering nor sacrifice to other gods, but to the LORD.'),
('2KI', 5, 18, '2KI.5.18', 'In this thing may the LORD pardon your servant: when my master goes into the house of Rimmon to worship there, and he leans on my hand, and I bow myself in the house of Rimmon. When I bow myself in the house of Rimmon, may the LORD pardon your servant in this thing.”'),
('2KI', 5, 19, '2KI.5.19', 'He said to him, “Go in peace.” So he departed from him a little way.'),
('2KI', 5, 20, '2KI.5.20', 'But Gehazi the servant of Elisha the man of God, said, “Behold, my master has spared this Naaman the Syrian, in not receiving at his hands that which he brought. As the LORD lives, I will run after him, and take something from him.”'),
('2KI', 5, 21, '2KI.5.21', 'So Gehazi followed after Naaman. When Naaman saw one running after him, he came down from the chariot to meet him, and said, “Is all well?”'),
('2KI', 5, 22, '2KI.5.22', 'He said, “All is well. My master has sent me, saying, ‘Behold, even now two young men of the sons of the prophets have come to me from the hill country of Ephraim. Please give them a talent of silver and two changes of clothing.’”'),
('2KI', 5, 23, '2KI.5.23', 'Naaman said, “Be pleased to take two talents.” He urged him, and bound two talents of silver in two bags, with two changes of clothing, and laid them on two of his servants; and they carried them before him.'),
('2KI', 5, 24, '2KI.5.24', 'When he came to the hill, he took them from their hand, and stored them in the house. Then he let the men go, and they departed.'),
('2KI', 5, 25, '2KI.5.25', 'But he went in, and stood before his master. Elisha said to him, “Where did you come from, Gehazi?” He said, “Your servant went nowhere.”'),
('2KI', 5, 26, '2KI.5.26', 'He said to him, “Didn’t my heart go with you when the man turned from his chariot to meet you? Is it a time to receive money, and to receive garments, and olive groves and vineyards, and sheep and cattle, and male servants and female servants?'),
('2KI', 5, 27, '2KI.5.27', 'Therefore the leprosy of Naaman will cling to you and to your offspring forever.” He went out from his presence a leper, as white as snow.'),
('2KI', 6, 1, '2KI.6.1', 'The sons of the prophets said to Elisha, “See now, the place where we live and meet with you is too small for us.'),
('2KI', 6, 2, '2KI.6.2', 'Please let us go to the Jordan, and each man take a beam from there, and let’s make us a place there, where we may live.” He answered, “Go!”'),
('2KI', 6, 3, '2KI.6.3', 'One said, “Please be pleased to go with your servants.” He answered, “I will go.”'),
('2KI', 6, 4, '2KI.6.4', 'So he went with them. When they came to the Jordan, they cut down wood.'),
('2KI', 6, 5, '2KI.6.5', 'But as one was cutting down a tree, the ax head fell into the water. Then he cried out and said, “Alas, my master! For it was borrowed.”'),
('2KI', 6, 6, '2KI.6.6', 'The man of God asked, “Where did it fall?” He showed him the place. He cut down a stick, threw it in there, and made the iron float.'),
('2KI', 6, 7, '2KI.6.7', 'He said, “Take it.” So he put out his hand and took it.'),
('2KI', 6, 8, '2KI.6.8', 'Now the king of Syria was at war against Israel; and he took counsel with his servants, saying, “My camp will be in such and such a place.”'),
('2KI', 6, 9, '2KI.6.9', 'The man of God sent to the king of Israel, saying, “Beware that you not pass this place, for the Syrians are coming down there.”'),
('2KI', 6, 10, '2KI.6.10', 'The king of Israel sent to the place which the man of God told him and warned him of; and he saved himself there, not once or twice.'),
('2KI', 6, 11, '2KI.6.11', 'The king of Syria’s heart was very troubled about this. He called his servants, and said to them, “Won’t you show me which of us is for the king of Israel?”'),
('2KI', 6, 12, '2KI.6.12', 'One of his servants said, “No, my lord, O king; but Elisha, the prophet who is in Israel, tells the king of Israel the words that you speak in your bedroom.”'),
('2KI', 6, 13, '2KI.6.13', 'He said, “Go and see where he is, that I may send and get him.” He was told, “Behold, he is in Dothan.”'),
('2KI', 6, 14, '2KI.6.14', 'Therefore he sent horses, chariots, and a great army there. They came by night and surrounded the city.'),
('2KI', 6, 15, '2KI.6.15', 'When the servant of the man of God had risen early and gone out, behold, an army with horses and chariots was around the city. His servant said to him, “Alas, my master! What shall we do?”'),
('2KI', 6, 16, '2KI.6.16', 'He answered, “Don’t be afraid, for those who are with us are more than those who are with them.”'),
('2KI', 6, 17, '2KI.6.17', 'Elisha prayed, and said, “LORD, please open his eyes, that he may see.” the LORD opened the young man’s eyes, and he saw; and behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire around Elisha.'),
('2KI', 6, 18, '2KI.6.18', 'When they came down to him, Elisha prayed to the LORD, and said, “Please strike this people with blindness.” He struck them with blindness according to Elisha’s word.'),
('2KI', 6, 19, '2KI.6.19', 'Elisha said to them, “This is not the way, neither is this the city. Follow me, and I will bring you to the man whom you seek.” He led them to Samaria.'),
('2KI', 6, 20, '2KI.6.20', 'When they had come into Samaria, Elisha said, “LORD, open these men’s eyes, that they may see.” The LORD opened their eyes, and they saw; and behold, they were in the middle of Samaria.'),
('2KI', 6, 21, '2KI.6.21', 'The king of Israel said to Elisha, when he saw them, “My father, shall I strike them? Shall I strike them?”'),
('2KI', 6, 22, '2KI.6.22', 'He answered, “You shall not strike them. Would you strike those whom you have taken captive with your sword and with your bow? Set bread and water before them, that they may eat and drink, then go to their master.”'),
('2KI', 6, 23, '2KI.6.23', 'He prepared a great feast for them. After they ate and drank, he sent them away and they went to their master. So the bands of Syria stopped raiding the land of Israel.'),
('2KI', 6, 24, '2KI.6.24', 'After this, Benhadad king of Syria gathered all his army, and went up and besieged Samaria.'),
('2KI', 6, 25, '2KI.6.25', 'There was a great famine in Samaria. Behold, they besieged it until a donkey’s head was sold for eighty pieces of silver, and the fourth part of a kab of dove’s dung for five pieces of silver.'),
('2KI', 6, 26, '2KI.6.26', 'As the king of Israel was passing by on the wall, a woman cried to him, saying, “Help, my lord, O king!”'),
('2KI', 6, 27, '2KI.6.27', 'He said, “If the LORD doesn’t help you, where could I get help for you? From the threshing floor, or from the wine press?”'),
('2KI', 6, 28, '2KI.6.28', 'Then the king asked her, “What is your problem?” She answered, “This woman said to me, ‘Give your son, that we may eat him today, and we will eat my son tomorrow.’'),
('2KI', 6, 29, '2KI.6.29', 'So we boiled my son and ate him; and I said to her on the next day, ‘Give up your son, that we may eat him;’ and she has hidden her son.”'),
('2KI', 6, 30, '2KI.6.30', 'When the king heard the words of the woman, he tore his clothes. Now he was passing by on the wall, and the people looked, and behold, he had sackcloth underneath on his body.'),
('2KI', 6, 31, '2KI.6.31', 'Then he said, “God do so to me, and more also, if the head of Elisha the son of Shaphat stays on him today.”'),
('2KI', 6, 32, '2KI.6.32', 'But Elisha was sitting in his house, and the elders were sitting with him. Then the king sent a man from before him; but before the messenger came to him, he said to the elders, “Do you see how this son of a murderer has sent to take away my head? Behold, when the messenger comes, shut the door, and hold the door shut against him. Isn’t the sound of his master’s feet behind him?”'),
('2KI', 6, 33, '2KI.6.33', 'While he was still talking with them, behold, the messenger came down to him. Then he said, “Behold, this evil is from the LORD. Why should I wait for the LORD any longer?”'),
('2KI', 7, 1, '2KI.7.1', 'Elisha said, “Hear the LORD’s word. The LORD says, ‘Tomorrow about this time a seah of fine flour will be sold for a shekel, and two seahs of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria.’”'),
('2KI', 7, 2, '2KI.7.2', 'Then the captain on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, “Behold, if the LORD made windows in heaven, could this thing be?” He said, “Behold, you will see it with your eyes, but will not eat of it.”'),
('2KI', 7, 3, '2KI.7.3', 'Now there were four leprous men at the entrance of the gate. They said to one another, “Why do we sit here until we die?'),
('2KI', 7, 4, '2KI.7.4', 'If we say, ‘We will enter into the city,’ then the famine is in the city, and we will die there. If we sit still here, we also die. Now therefore come, and let’s surrender to the army of the Syrians. If they save us alive, we will live; and if they kill us, we will only die.”'),
('2KI', 7, 5, '2KI.7.5', 'They rose up in the twilight to go to the camp of the Syrians. When they had come to the outermost part of the camp of the Syrians, behold, no man was there.'),
('2KI', 7, 6, '2KI.7.6', 'For the Lord had made the army of the Syrians to hear the sound of chariots and the sound of horses, even the noise of a great army; and they said to one another, “Behold, the king of Israel has hired against us the kings of the Hittites and the kings of the Egyptians to attack us.”'),
('2KI', 7, 7, '2KI.7.7', 'Therefore they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, their horses, and their donkeys, even the camp as it was, and fled for their life.'),
('2KI', 7, 8, '2KI.7.8', 'When these lepers came to the outermost part of the camp, they went into one tent, and ate and drank, then carried away silver, gold, and clothing and went and hid it. Then they came back, and entered into another tent and carried things from there also, and went and hid them.'),
('2KI', 7, 9, '2KI.7.9', 'Then they said to one another, “We aren’t doing right. Today is a day of good news, and we keep silent. If we wait until the morning light, punishment will overtake us. Now therefore come, let’s go and tell the king’s household.”'),
('2KI', 7, 10, '2KI.7.10', 'So they came and called to the city gatekeepers; and they told them, “We came to the camp of the Syrians, and, behold, there was no man there, not even a man’s voice, but the horses tied, and the donkeys tied, and the tents as they were.”'),
('2KI', 7, 11, '2KI.7.11', 'Then the gatekeepers called out and told it to the king’s household within.'),
('2KI', 7, 12, '2KI.7.12', 'The king arose in the night, and said to his servants, “I will now show you what the Syrians have done to us. They know that we are hungry. Therefore they have gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, ‘When they come out of the city, we shall take them alive, and get into the city.’”'),
('2KI', 7, 13, '2KI.7.13', 'One of his servants answered, “Please let some people take five of the horses that remain, which are left in the city. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are left in it. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are consumed. Let’s send and see.”'),
('2KI', 7, 14, '2KI.7.14', 'Therefore they took two chariots with horses; and the king sent them out to the Syrian army, saying, “Go and see.”'),
('2KI', 7, 15, '2KI.7.15', 'They went after them to the Jordan; and behold, all the path was full of garments and equipment which the Syrians had cast away in their haste. The messengers returned and told the king.'),
('2KI', 7, 16, '2KI.7.16', 'The people went out and plundered the camp of the Syrians. So a seah of fine flour was sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the LORD’s word.'),
('2KI', 7, 17, '2KI.7.17', 'The king had appointed the captain on whose hand he leaned to be in charge of the gate; and the people trampled over him in the gate, and he died as the man of God had said, who spoke when the king came down to him.'),
('2KI', 7, 18, '2KI.7.18', 'It happened as the man of God had spoken to the king, saying, “Two seahs of barley for a shekel, and a seah of fine flour for a shekel, shall be tomorrow about this time in the gate of Samaria;”'),
('2KI', 7, 19, '2KI.7.19', 'and that captain answered the man of God, and said, “Now, behold, if the LORD made windows in heaven, might such a thing be?” and he said, “Behold, you will see it with your eyes, but will not eat of it.”'),
('2KI', 7, 20, '2KI.7.20', 'It happened like that to him, for the people trampled over him in the gate, and he died.'),
('2KI', 8, 1, '2KI.8.1', 'Now Elisha had spoken to the woman whose son he had restored to life, saying, “Arise, and go, you and your household, and stay for a while wherever you can; for the LORD has called for a famine. It will also come on the land for seven years.”'),
('2KI', 8, 2, '2KI.8.2', 'The woman arose, and did according to the man of God’s word. She went with her household, and lived in the land of the Philistines for seven years.'),
('2KI', 8, 3, '2KI.8.3', 'At the end of seven years, the woman returned from the land of the Philistines. Then she went out to beg the king for her house and for her land.'),
('2KI', 8, 4, '2KI.8.4', 'Now the king was talking with Gehazi the servant of the man of God, saying, “Please tell me all the great things that Elisha has done.”'),
('2KI', 8, 5, '2KI.8.5', 'As he was telling the king how he had restored to life him who was dead, behold, the woman whose son he had restored to life begged the king for her house and for her land. Gehazi said, “My lord, O king, this is the woman, and this is her son, whom Elisha restored to life.”'),
('2KI', 8, 6, '2KI.8.6', 'When the king asked the woman, she told him. So the king appointed to her a certain officer, saying, “Restore all that was hers, and all the fruits of the field since the day that she left the land, even until now.”'),
('2KI', 8, 7, '2KI.8.7', 'Elisha came to Damascus; and Benhadad the king of Syria was sick. He was told, “The man of God has come here.”'),
('2KI', 8, 8, '2KI.8.8', 'The king said to Hazael, “Take a present in your hand, and go meet the man of God, and inquire of the LORD by him, saying, ‘Will I recover from this sickness?’”'),
('2KI', 8, 9, '2KI.8.9', 'So Hazael went to meet him and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels’ burden, and came and stood before him and said, “Your son Benhadad king of Syria has sent me to you, saying, ‘Will I recover from this sickness?’”'),
('2KI', 8, 10, '2KI.8.10', 'Elisha said to him, “Go, tell him, ‘You will surely recover;’ however the LORD has shown me that he will surely die.”'),
('2KI', 8, 11, '2KI.8.11', 'He settled his gaze steadfastly on him, until he was ashamed. Then the man of God wept.'),
('2KI', 8, 12, '2KI.8.12', 'Hazael said, “Why do you weep, my lord?” He answered, “Because I know the evil that you will do to the children of Israel. You will set their strongholds on fire, and you will kill their young men with the sword, and will dash their little ones in pieces, and rip up their pregnant women.”'),
('2KI', 8, 13, '2KI.8.13', 'Hazael said, “But what is your servant, who is but a dog, that he could do this great thing?” Elisha answered, “The LORD has shown me that you will be king over Syria.”'),
('2KI', 8, 14, '2KI.8.14', 'Then he departed from Elisha, and came to his master, who said to him, “What did Elisha say to you?” He answered, “He told me that you would surely recover.”'),
('2KI', 8, 15, '2KI.8.15', 'On the next day, he took a thick cloth, dipped it in water, and spread it on the king’s face, so that he died. Then Hazael reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 8, 16, '2KI.8.16', 'In the fifth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel, Jehoshaphat being king of Judah then, Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah began to reign.'),
('2KI', 8, 17, '2KI.8.17', 'He was thirty-two years old when he began to reign. He reigned eight years in Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 8, 18, '2KI.8.18', 'He walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did Ahab’s house, for he married Ahab’s daughter. He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight.'),
('2KI', 8, 19, '2KI.8.19', 'However, the LORD would not destroy Judah, for David his servant’s sake, as he promised him to give to him a lamp for his children always.'),
('2KI', 8, 20, '2KI.8.20', 'In his days Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah, and made a king over themselves.'),
('2KI', 8, 21, '2KI.8.21', 'Then Joram crossed over to Zair, and all his chariots with him; and he rose up by night and struck the Edomites who surrounded him with the captains of the chariots; and the people fled to their tents.'),
('2KI', 8, 22, '2KI.8.22', 'So Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah to this day. Then Libnah revolted at the same time.'),
('2KI', 8, 23, '2KI.8.23', 'The rest of the acts of Joram, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 8, 24, '2KI.8.24', 'Joram slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David’s city; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 8, 25, '2KI.8.25', 'In the twelfth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel, Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah began to reign.'),
('2KI', 8, 26, '2KI.8.26', 'Ahaziah was twenty-two years old when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Athaliah the daughter of Omri king of Israel.'),
('2KI', 8, 27, '2KI.8.27', 'He walked in the way of Ahab’s house and did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, as did Ahab’s house, for he was the son-in-law of Ahab’s house.'),
('2KI', 8, 28, '2KI.8.28', 'He went with Joram the son of Ahab to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth Gilead, and the Syrians wounded Joram.'),
('2KI', 8, 29, '2KI.8.29', 'King Joram returned to be healed in Jezreel from the wounds which the Syrians had given him at Ramah, when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. Ahaziah the son of Jehoram, king of Judah, went down to see Joram the son of Ahab in Jezreel, because he was sick.'),
('2KI', 9, 1, '2KI.9.1', 'Elisha the prophet called one of the sons of the prophets, and said to him, “Put your belt on your waist, take this vial of oil in your hand, and go to Ramoth Gilead.'),
('2KI', 9, 2, '2KI.9.2', 'When you come there, find Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, and go in and make him rise up from among his brothers, and take him to an inner room.'),
('2KI', 9, 3, '2KI.9.3', 'Then take the vial of oil, and pour it on his head, and say, ‘The LORD says, “I have anointed you king over Israel.”’ Then open the door, flee, and don’t wait.”'),
('2KI', 9, 4, '2KI.9.4', 'So the young man, the young prophet, went to Ramoth Gilead.'),
('2KI', 9, 5, '2KI.9.5', 'When he came, behold, the captains of the army were sitting. Then he said, “I have a message for you, captain.” Jehu said, “To which one of us?” He said, “To you, O captain.”'),
('2KI', 9, 6, '2KI.9.6', 'He arose, and went into the house. Then he poured the oil on his head, and said to him, “The LORD, the God of Israel, says, ‘I have anointed you king over the people of the LORD, even over Israel.'),
('2KI', 9, 7, '2KI.9.7', 'You must strike your master Ahab’s house, that I may avenge the blood of my servants the prophets, and the blood of all the servants of the LORD, at the hand of Jezebel.'),
('2KI', 9, 8, '2KI.9.8', 'For the whole house of Ahab will perish. I will cut off from Ahab everyone who urinates against a wall, both him who is shut up and him who is left at large in Israel.'),
('2KI', 9, 9, '2KI.9.9', 'I will make Ahab’s house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah.'),
('2KI', 9, 10, '2KI.9.10', 'The dogs will eat Jezebel on the plot of ground of Jezreel, and there shall be no one to bury her.’” Then he opened the door and fled.'),
('2KI', 9, 11, '2KI.9.11', 'When Jehu came out to the servants of his lord and one said to him, “Is all well? Why did this madman come to you?” He said to them, “You know the man and how he talks.”'),
('2KI', 9, 12, '2KI.9.12', 'They said, “That is a lie. Tell us now.” He said, “He said to me, ‘The LORD says, I have anointed you king over Israel.’”'),
('2KI', 9, 13, '2KI.9.13', 'Then they hurried, and each man took his cloak, and put it under him on the top of the stairs, and blew the trumpet, saying, “Jehu is king.”'),
('2KI', 9, 14, '2KI.9.14', 'So Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi conspired against Joram. (Now Joram was defending Ramoth Gilead, he and all Israel, because of Hazael king of Syria;'),
('2KI', 9, 15, '2KI.9.15', 'but King Joram had returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which the Syrians had given him when he fought with Hazael king of Syria.) Jehu said, “If this is your thinking, then let no one escape and go out of the city to go to tell it in Jezreel.”'),
('2KI', 9, 16, '2KI.9.16', 'So Jehu rode in a chariot and went to Jezreel, for Joram lay there. Ahaziah king of Judah had come down to see Joram.'),
('2KI', 9, 17, '2KI.9.17', 'Now the watchman was standing on the tower in Jezreel, and he spied the company of Jehu as he came, and said, “I see a company.” Joram said, “Take a horseman, and send to meet them, and let him say, ‘Is it peace?’”'),
('2KI', 9, 18, '2KI.9.18', 'So one went on horseback to meet him, and said, “The king says, ‘Is it peace?’” Jehu said, “What do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!” The watchman said, “The messenger came to them, but he isn’t coming back.”'),
('2KI', 9, 19, '2KI.9.19', 'Then he sent out a second on horseback, who came to them and said, “The king says, ‘Is it peace?’” Jehu answered, “What do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!”'),
('2KI', 9, 20, '2KI.9.20', 'The watchman said, “He came to them, and isn’t coming back. The driving is like the driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi, for he drives furiously.”'),
('2KI', 9, 21, '2KI.9.21', 'Joram said, “Get ready!” They got his chariot ready. Then Joram king of Israel and Ahaziah king of Judah went out, each in his chariot; and they went out to meet Jehu, and found him on Naboth the Jezreelite’s land.'),
('2KI', 9, 22, '2KI.9.22', 'When Joram saw Jehu, he said, “Is it peace, Jehu?” He answered, “What peace, so long as the prostitution of your mother Jezebel and her witchcraft abound?”'),
('2KI', 9, 23, '2KI.9.23', 'Joram turned his hands and fled, and said to Ahaziah, “This is treason, Ahaziah!”'),
('2KI', 9, 24, '2KI.9.24', 'Jehu drew his bow with his full strength, and struck Joram between his arms; and the arrow went out at his heart, and he sunk down in his chariot.'),
('2KI', 9, 25, '2KI.9.25', 'Then Jehu said to Bidkar his captain, “Pick him up, and throw him in the plot of the field of Naboth the Jezreelite; for remember how, when you and I rode together after Ahab his father, the LORD laid this burden on him:'),
('2KI', 9, 26, '2KI.9.26', '‘Surely I have seen yesterday the blood of Naboth, and the blood of his sons,’ says the LORD; ‘and I will repay you in this plot of ground,’ says the LORD. Now therefore take and cast him onto the plot of ground, according to the LORD’s word.”'),
('2KI', 9, 27, '2KI.9.27', 'But when Ahaziah the king of Judah saw this, he fled by the way of the garden house. Jehu followed after him, and said, “Strike him also in the chariot!” They struck him at the ascent of Gur, which is by Ibleam. He fled to Megiddo, and died there.'),
('2KI', 9, 28, '2KI.9.28', 'His servants carried him in a chariot to Jerusalem, and buried him in his tomb with his fathers in David’s city.'),
('2KI', 9, 29, '2KI.9.29', 'In the eleventh year of Joram the son of Ahab, Ahaziah began to reign over Judah.'),
('2KI', 9, 30, '2KI.9.30', 'When Jehu had come to Jezreel, Jezebel heard of it; and she painted her eyes, and adorned her head, and looked out at the window.'),
('2KI', 9, 31, '2KI.9.31', 'As Jehu entered in at the gate, she said, “Do you come in peace, Zimri, you murderer of your master?”'),
('2KI', 9, 32, '2KI.9.32', 'He lifted up his face to the window, and said, “Who is on my side? Who?” Two or three eunuchs looked out at him.'),
('2KI', 9, 33, '2KI.9.33', 'He said, “Throw her down!” So they threw her down; and some of her blood was sprinkled on the wall, and on the horses. Then he trampled her under foot.'),
('2KI', 9, 34, '2KI.9.34', 'When he had come in, he ate and drank. Then he said, “See now to this cursed woman, and bury her; for she is a king’s daughter.”'),
('2KI', 9, 35, '2KI.9.35', 'They went to bury her, but they found no more of her than the skull, the feet, and the palms of her hands.'),
('2KI', 9, 36, '2KI.9.36', 'Therefore they came back, and told him. He said, “This is the LORD’s word, which he spoke by his servant Elijah the Tishbite, saying, ‘The dogs will eat the flesh of Jezebel on the plot of Jezreel,'),
('2KI', 9, 37, '2KI.9.37', 'and the body of Jezebel will be as dung on the surface of the field on Jezreel’s land, so that they won’t say, “This is Jezebel.”’”'),
('2KI', 10, 1, '2KI.10.1', 'Now Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. Jehu wrote letters and sent them to Samaria, to the rulers of Jezreel, even the elders, and to those who brought up Ahab’s sons, saying,'),
('2KI', 10, 2, '2KI.10.2', '“Now as soon as this letter comes to you, since your master’s sons are with you, and you have chariots and horses, a fortified city also, and armor,'),
('2KI', 10, 3, '2KI.10.3', 'select the best and fittest of your master’s sons, set him on his father’s throne, and fight for your master’s house.”'),
('2KI', 10, 4, '2KI.10.4', 'But they were exceedingly afraid, and said, “Behold, the two kings didn’t stand before him! How then shall we stand?”'),
('2KI', 10, 5, '2KI.10.5', 'He who was over the household, and he who was over the city, the elders also, and those who raised the children, sent to Jehu, saying, “We are your servants, and will do all that you ask us. We will not make any man king. You do that which is good in your eyes.”'),
('2KI', 10, 6, '2KI.10.6', 'Then he wrote a letter the second time to them, saying, “If you are on my side, and if you will listen to my voice, take the heads of the men who are your master’s sons, and come to me to Jezreel by tomorrow this time.” Now the king’s sons, being seventy persons, were with the great men of the city, who brought them up.'),
('2KI', 10, 7, '2KI.10.7', 'When the letter came to them, they took the king’s sons and killed them, even seventy people, and put their heads in baskets, and sent them to him to Jezreel.'),
('2KI', 10, 8, '2KI.10.8', 'A messenger came and told him, “They have brought the heads of the king’s sons.” He said, “Lay them in two heaps at the entrance of the gate until the morning.”'),
('2KI', 10, 9, '2KI.10.9', 'In the morning, he went out and stood, and said to all the people, “You are righteous. Behold, I conspired against my master and killed him, but who killed all these?'),
('2KI', 10, 10, '2KI.10.10', 'Know now that nothing will fall to the earth of the LORD’s word, which the LORD spoke concerning Ahab’s house. For the LORD has done that which he spoke by his servant Elijah.”'),
('2KI', 10, 11, '2KI.10.11', 'So Jehu struck all that remained of Ahab’s house in Jezreel, with all his great men, his familiar friends, and his priests, until he left him no one remaining.'),
('2KI', 10, 12, '2KI.10.12', 'He arose and departed, and went to Samaria. As he was at the shearing house of the shepherds on the way,'),
('2KI', 10, 13, '2KI.10.13', 'Jehu met with the brothers of Ahaziah king of Judah, and said, “Who are you?” They answered, “We are the brothers of Ahaziah. We are going down to greet the children of the king and the children of the queen.”'),
('2KI', 10, 14, '2KI.10.14', 'He said, “Take them alive!” They took them alive, and killed them at the pit of the shearing house, even forty-two men. He didn’t leave any of them.'),
('2KI', 10, 15, '2KI.10.15', 'When he had departed from there, he met Jehonadab the son of Rechab coming to meet him. He greeted him, and said to him, “Is your heart right, as my heart is with your heart?” Jehonadab answered, “It is.” “If it is, give me your hand.” He gave him his hand; and he took him up to him into the chariot.'),
('2KI', 10, 16, '2KI.10.16', 'He said, “Come with me, and see my zeal for the LORD.” So they made him ride in his chariot.'),
('2KI', 10, 17, '2KI.10.17', 'When he came to Samaria, he struck all who remained to Ahab in Samaria, until he had destroyed them, according to the LORD’s word which he spoke to Elijah.'),
('2KI', 10, 18, '2KI.10.18', 'Jehu gathered all the people together, and said to them, “Ahab served Baal a little, but Jehu will serve him much.'),
('2KI', 10, 19, '2KI.10.19', 'Now therefore call to me all the prophets of Baal, all of his worshipers, and all of his priests. Let no one be absent, for I have a great sacrifice to Baal. Whoever is absent, he shall not live.” But Jehu did deceptively, intending to destroy the worshipers of Baal.'),
('2KI', 10, 20, '2KI.10.20', 'Jehu said, “Sanctify a solemn assembly for Baal!” So they proclaimed it.'),
('2KI', 10, 21, '2KI.10.21', 'Jehu sent through all Israel; and all the worshipers of Baal came, so that there was not a man left that didn’t come. They came into the house of Baal; and the house of Baal was filled from one end to another.'),
('2KI', 10, 22, '2KI.10.22', 'He said to him who kept the wardrobe, “Bring out robes for all the worshipers of Baal!” So he brought robes out to them.'),
('2KI', 10, 23, '2KI.10.23', 'Jehu went with Jehonadab the son of Rechab into the house of Baal. Then he said to the worshipers of Baal, “Search, and see that none of the servants of the LORD are here with you, but only the worshipers of Baal.”'),
('2KI', 10, 24, '2KI.10.24', 'So they went in to offer sacrifices and burnt offerings. Now Jehu had appointed for himself eighty men outside, and said, “If any of the men whom I bring into your hands escape, he who lets him go, his life shall be for the life of him.”'),
('2KI', 10, 25, '2KI.10.25', 'As soon as he had finished offering the burnt offering, Jehu said to the guard and to the captains, “Go in and kill them! Let no one escape.” So they struck them with the edge of the sword. The guard and the captains threw the bodies out, and went to the inner shrine of the house of Baal.'),
('2KI', 10, 26, '2KI.10.26', 'They brought out the pillars that were in the house of Baal and burned them.'),
('2KI', 10, 27, '2KI.10.27', 'They broke down the pillar of Baal, and broke down the house of Baal, and made it a latrine, to this day.'),
('2KI', 10, 28, '2KI.10.28', 'Thus Jehu destroyed Baal out of Israel.'),
('2KI', 10, 29, '2KI.10.29', 'However, Jehu didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin—the golden calves that were in Bethel and that were in Dan.'),
('2KI', 10, 30, '2KI.10.30', 'The LORD said to Jehu, “Because you have done well in executing that which is right in my eyes, and have done to Ahab’s house according to all that was in my heart, your descendants shall sit on the throne of Israel to the fourth generation.”'),
('2KI', 10, 31, '2KI.10.31', 'But Jehu took no heed to walk in the law of the LORD, the God of Israel, with all his heart. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam, with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('2KI', 10, 32, '2KI.10.32', 'In those days the LORD began to cut away parts of Israel; and Hazael struck them in all the borders of Israel'),
('2KI', 10, 33, '2KI.10.33', 'from the Jordan eastward, all the land of Gilead, the Gadites, and the Reubenites, and the Manassites, from Aroer, which is by the valley of the Arnon, even Gilead and Bashan.'),
('2KI', 10, 34, '2KI.10.34', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehu, and all that he did, and all his might, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 10, 35, '2KI.10.35', 'Jehu slept with his fathers; and they buried him in Samaria. Jehoahaz his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 10, 36, '2KI.10.36', 'The time that Jehu reigned over Israel in Samaria was twenty-eight years.'),
('2KI', 11, 1, '2KI.11.1', 'Now when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the royal offspring.'),
('2KI', 11, 2, '2KI.11.2', 'But Jehosheba, the daughter of King Joram, sister of Ahaziah, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stole him away from among the king’s sons who were slain, even him and his nurse, and put them in the bedroom; and they hid him from Athaliah, so that he was not slain.'),
('2KI', 11, 3, '2KI.11.3', 'He was with her hidden in the LORD’s house six years while Athaliah reigned over the land.'),
('2KI', 11, 4, '2KI.11.4', 'In the seventh year Jehoiada sent and fetched the captains over hundreds of the Carites and of the guard, and brought them to him into the LORD’s house; and he made a covenant with them, and made a covenant with them in the LORD’s house, and showed them the king’s son.'),
('2KI', 11, 5, '2KI.11.5', 'He commanded them, saying, “This is what you must do: a third of you, who come in on the Sabbath, shall be keepers of the watch of the king’s house;'),
('2KI', 11, 6, '2KI.11.6', 'a third of you shall be at the gate Sur; and a third of you at the gate behind the guard. So you shall keep the watch of the house, and be a barrier.'),
('2KI', 11, 7, '2KI.11.7', 'The two companies of you, even all who go out on the Sabbath, shall keep the watch of the LORD’s house around the king.'),
('2KI', 11, 8, '2KI.11.8', 'You shall surround the king, every man with his weapons in his hand; and he who comes within the ranks, let him be slain. Be with the king when he goes out, and when he comes in.”'),
('2KI', 11, 9, '2KI.11.9', 'The captains over hundreds did according to all that Jehoiada the priest commanded; and they each took his men, those who were to come in on the Sabbath with those who were to go out on the Sabbath, and came to Jehoiada the priest.'),
('2KI', 11, 10, '2KI.11.10', 'The priest delivered to the captains over hundreds the spears and shields that had been King David’s, which were in the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 11, 11, '2KI.11.11', 'The guard stood, every man with his weapons in his hand, from the right side of the house to the left side of the house, along by the altar and the house, around the king.'),
('2KI', 11, 12, '2KI.11.12', 'Then he brought out the king’s son, and put the crown on him, and gave him the covenant; and they made him king and anointed him; and they clapped their hands, and said, “Long live the king!”'),
('2KI', 11, 13, '2KI.11.13', 'When Athaliah heard the noise of the guard and of the people, she came to the people into the LORD’s house;'),
('2KI', 11, 14, '2KI.11.14', 'and she looked, and behold, the king stood by the pillar, as the tradition was, with the captains and the trumpets by the king; and all the people of the land rejoiced, and blew trumpets. Then Athaliah tore her clothes and cried, “Treason! Treason!”'),
('2KI', 11, 15, '2KI.11.15', 'Jehoiada the priest commanded the captains of hundreds who were set over the army, and said to them, “Bring her out between the ranks. Kill anyone who follows her with the sword.” For the priest said, “Don’t let her be slain in the LORD’s house.”'),
('2KI', 11, 16, '2KI.11.16', 'So they seized her; and she went by the way of the horses’ entry to the king’s house, and she was slain there.'),
('2KI', 11, 17, '2KI.11.17', 'Jehoiada made a covenant between the LORD and the king and the people, that they should be the LORD’s people; also between the king and the people.'),
('2KI', 11, 18, '2KI.11.18', 'All the people of the land went to the house of Baal, and broke it down. They broke his altars and his images in pieces thoroughly, and killed Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars. The priest appointed officers over the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 11, 19, '2KI.11.19', 'He took the captains over hundreds, and the Carites, and the guard, and all the people of the land; and they brought down the king from the LORD’s house, and came by the way of the gate of the guard to the king’s house. He sat on the throne of the kings.'),
('2KI', 11, 20, '2KI.11.20', 'So all the people of the land rejoiced, and the city was quiet. They had slain Athaliah with the sword at the king’s house.'),
('2KI', 11, 21, '2KI.11.21', 'Jehoash was seven years old when he began to reign.'),
('2KI', 12, 1, '2KI.12.1', 'Jehoash began to reign in the seventh year of Jehu, and he reigned forty years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Zibiah of Beersheba.'),
('2KI', 12, 2, '2KI.12.2', 'Jehoash did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes all his days in which Jehoiada the priest instructed him.'),
('2KI', 12, 3, '2KI.12.3', 'However, the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places.'),
('2KI', 12, 4, '2KI.12.4', 'Jehoash said to the priests, “All the money of the holy things that is brought into the LORD’s house, in current money, the money of the people for whom each man is evaluated, and all the money that it comes into any man’s heart to bring into the LORD’s house,'),
('2KI', 12, 5, '2KI.12.5', 'let the priests take it to them, each man from his donor; and they shall repair the damage to the house, wherever any damage is found.”'),
('2KI', 12, 6, '2KI.12.6', 'But it was so, that in the twenty-third year of King Jehoash the priests had not repaired the damage to the house.'),
('2KI', 12, 7, '2KI.12.7', 'Then King Jehoash called for Jehoiada the priest, and for the other priests, and said to them, “Why aren’t you repairing the damage to the house? Now therefore take no more money from your treasurers, but deliver it for repair of the damage to the house.”'),
('2KI', 12, 8, '2KI.12.8', 'The priests consented that they should take no more money from the people, and not repair the damage to the house.'),
('2KI', 12, 9, '2KI.12.9', 'But Jehoiada the priest took a chest and bored a hole in its lid, and set it beside the altar, on the right side as one comes into the LORD’s house; and the priests who kept the threshold put all the money that was brought into the LORD’s house into it.'),
('2KI', 12, 10, '2KI.12.10', 'When they saw that there was much money in the chest, the king’s scribe and the high priest came up, and they put it in bags and counted the money that was found in the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 12, 11, '2KI.12.11', 'They gave the money that was weighed out into the hands of those who did the work, who had the oversight of the LORD’s house; and they paid it out to the carpenters and the builders who worked on the LORD’s house,'),
('2KI', 12, 12, '2KI.12.12', 'and to the masons and the stone cutters, and for buying timber and cut stone to repair the damage to the LORD’s house, and for all that was laid out for the house to repair it.'),
('2KI', 12, 13, '2KI.12.13', 'But there were not made for the LORD’s house cups of silver, snuffers, basins, trumpets, any vessels of gold or vessels of silver, of the money that was brought into the LORD’s house;'),
('2KI', 12, 14, '2KI.12.14', 'for they gave that to those who did the work, and repaired the LORD’s house with it.'),
('2KI', 12, 15, '2KI.12.15', 'Moreover they didn’t demand an accounting from the men into whose hand they delivered the money to give to those who did the work; for they dealt faithfully.'),
('2KI', 12, 16, '2KI.12.16', 'The money for the trespass offerings and the money for the sin offerings was not brought into the LORD’s house. It was the priests’.'),
('2KI', 12, 17, '2KI.12.17', 'Then Hazael king of Syria went up and fought against Gath, and took it; and Hazael set his face to go up to Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 12, 18, '2KI.12.18', 'Jehoash king of Judah took all the holy things that Jehoshaphat and Jehoram and Ahaziah, his fathers, kings of Judah, had dedicated, and his own holy things, and all the gold that was found in the treasures of the LORD’s house, and of the king’s house, and sent it to Hazael king of Syria; and he went away from Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 12, 19, '2KI.12.19', 'Now the rest of the acts of Joash, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 12, 20, '2KI.12.20', 'His servants arose and made a conspiracy, and struck Joash at the house of Millo, on the way that goes down to Silla.'),
('2KI', 12, 21, '2KI.12.21', 'For Jozacar the son of Shimeath, and Jehozabad the son of Shomer, his servants, struck him, and he died; and they buried him with his fathers in David’s city; and Amaziah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 13, 1, '2KI.13.1', 'In the twenty-third year of Joash the son of Ahaziah, king of Judah, Jehoahaz the son of Jehu began to reign over Israel in Samaria for seventeen years.'),
('2KI', 13, 2, '2KI.13.2', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and followed the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin. He didn’t depart from it.'),
('2KI', 13, 3, '2KI.13.3', 'The LORD’s anger burned against Israel, and he delivered them into the hand of Hazael king of Syria, and into the hand of Benhadad the son of Hazael, continually.'),
('2KI', 13, 4, '2KI.13.4', 'Jehoahaz begged the LORD, and the LORD listened to him; for he saw the oppression of Israel, how the king of Syria oppressed them.'),
('2KI', 13, 5, '2KI.13.5', '(The LORD gave Israel a savior, so that they went out from under the hand of the Syrians; and the children of Israel lived in their tents as before.'),
('2KI', 13, 6, '2KI.13.6', 'Nevertheless they didn’t depart from the sins of the house of Jeroboam, with which he made Israel to sin, but walked in them; and the Asherah also remained in Samaria.)'),
('2KI', 13, 7, '2KI.13.7', 'For he didn’t leave to Jehoahaz of the people any more than fifty horsemen, and ten chariots, and ten thousand footmen; for the king of Syria destroyed them and made them like the dust in threshing.'),
('2KI', 13, 8, '2KI.13.8', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoahaz, and all that he did, and his might, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 13, 9, '2KI.13.9', 'Jehoahaz slept with his fathers; and they buried him in Samaria; and Joash his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 13, 10, '2KI.13.10', 'In the thirty-seventh year of Joash king of Judah, Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz began to reign over Israel in Samaria for sixteen years.'),
('2KI', 13, 11, '2KI.13.11', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin; but he walked in them.'),
('2KI', 13, 12, '2KI.13.12', 'Now the rest of the acts of Joash, and all that he did, and his might with which he fought against Amaziah king of Judah, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 13, 13, '2KI.13.13', 'Joash slept with his fathers; and Jeroboam sat on his throne. Joash was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 13, 14, '2KI.13.14', 'Now Elisha became sick with the illness of which he died; and Joash the king of Israel came down to him, and wept over him, and said, “My father, my father, the chariots of Israel and its horsemen!”'),
('2KI', 13, 15, '2KI.13.15', 'Elisha said to him, “Take bow and arrows;” and he took bow and arrows for himself.'),
('2KI', 13, 16, '2KI.13.16', 'He said to the king of Israel, “Put your hand on the bow;” and he put his hand on it. Elisha laid his hands on the king’s hands.'),
('2KI', 13, 17, '2KI.13.17', 'He said, “Open the window eastward;” and he opened it. Then Elisha said, “Shoot!” and he shot. He said, “The LORD’s arrow of victory, even the arrow of victory over Syria; for you will strike the Syrians in Aphek until you have consumed them.”'),
('2KI', 13, 18, '2KI.13.18', 'He said, “Take the arrows;” and he took them. He said to the king of Israel, “Strike the ground;” and he struck three times, and stopped.'),
('2KI', 13, 19, '2KI.13.19', 'The man of God was angry with him, and said, “You should have struck five or six times. Then you would have struck Syria until you had consumed it, but now you will strike Syria just three times.”'),
('2KI', 13, 20, '2KI.13.20', 'Elisha died, and they buried him. Now the bands of the Moabites invaded the land at the coming in of the year.'),
('2KI', 13, 21, '2KI.13.21', 'As they were burying a man, behold, they saw a band of raiders; and they threw the man into Elisha’s tomb. As soon as the man touched Elisha’s bones, he revived, and stood up on his feet.'),
('2KI', 13, 22, '2KI.13.22', 'Hazael king of Syria oppressed Israel all the days of Jehoahaz.'),
('2KI', 13, 23, '2KI.13.23', 'But the LORD was gracious to them, and had compassion on them, and favored them because of his covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and would not destroy them and he didn’t cast them from his presence as yet.'),
('2KI', 13, 24, '2KI.13.24', 'Hazael king of Syria died; and Benhadad his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 13, 25, '2KI.13.25', 'Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz took again out of the hand of Benhadad the son of Hazael the cities which he had taken out of the hand of Jehoahaz his father by war. Joash struck him three times, and recovered the cities of Israel.'),
('2KI', 14, 1, '2KI.14.1', 'In the second year of Joash, son of Joahaz, king of Israel, Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah began to reign.'),
('2KI', 14, 2, '2KI.14.2', 'He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Jehoaddin of Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 14, 3, '2KI.14.3', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, yet not like David his father. He did according to all that Joash his father had done.'),
('2KI', 14, 4, '2KI.14.4', 'However the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places.'),
('2KI', 14, 5, '2KI.14.5', 'As soon as the kingdom was established in his hand, he killed his servants who had slain the king his father,'),
('2KI', 14, 6, '2KI.14.6', 'but the children of the murderers he didn’t put to death, according to that which is written in the book of the law of Moses, as the LORD commanded, saying, “The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, nor the children be put to death for the fathers; but every man shall die for his own sin.”'),
('2KI', 14, 7, '2KI.14.7', 'He killed ten thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt, and took Sela by war, and called its name Joktheel, to this day.'),
('2KI', 14, 8, '2KI.14.8', 'Then Amaziah sent messengers to Jehoash, the son of Jehoahaz son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, “Come, let’s look one another in the face.”'),
('2KI', 14, 9, '2KI.14.9', 'Jehoash the king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, “The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, ‘Give your daughter to my son as wife.’ Then a wild animal that was in Lebanon passed by, and trampled down the thistle.'),
('2KI', 14, 10, '2KI.14.10', 'You have indeed struck Edom, and your heart has lifted you up. Enjoy the glory of it, and stay at home; for why should you meddle to your harm, that you fall, even you, and Judah with you?”'),
('2KI', 14, 11, '2KI.14.11', 'But Amaziah would not listen. So Jehoash king of Israel went up; and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Beth Shemesh, which belongs to Judah.'),
('2KI', 14, 12, '2KI.14.12', 'Judah was defeated by Israel; and each man fled to his tent.'),
('2KI', 14, 13, '2KI.14.13', 'Jehoash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Jehoash the son of Ahaziah, at Beth Shemesh and came to Jerusalem, then broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate, four hundred cubits.'),
('2KI', 14, 14, '2KI.14.14', 'He took all the gold and silver and all the vessels that were found in the LORD’s house and in the treasures of the king’s house, the hostages also, and returned to Samaria.'),
('2KI', 14, 15, '2KI.14.15', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoash which he did, and his might, and how he fought with Amaziah king of Judah, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 14, 16, '2KI.14.16', 'Jehoash slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel; and Jeroboam his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 14, 17, '2KI.14.17', 'Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah lived after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz, king of Israel, fifteen years.'),
('2KI', 14, 18, '2KI.14.18', 'Now the rest of the acts of Amaziah, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 14, 19, '2KI.14.19', 'They made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem, and he fled to Lachish; but they sent after him to Lachish and killed him there.'),
('2KI', 14, 20, '2KI.14.20', 'They brought him on horses, and he was buried at Jerusalem with his fathers in David’s city.'),
('2KI', 14, 21, '2KI.14.21', 'All the people of Judah took Azariah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in the place of his father Amaziah.'),
('2KI', 14, 22, '2KI.14.22', 'He built Elath and restored it to Judah. After that the king slept with his fathers.'),
('2KI', 14, 23, '2KI.14.23', 'In the fifteenth year of Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah, Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel began to reign in Samaria for forty-one years.'),
('2KI', 14, 24, '2KI.14.24', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('2KI', 14, 25, '2KI.14.25', 'He restored the border of Israel from the entrance of Hamath to the sea of the Arabah, according to the LORD, the God of Israel’s word, which he spoke by his servant Jonah the son of Amittai, the prophet, who was from Gath Hepher.'),
('2KI', 14, 26, '2KI.14.26', 'For the LORD saw the affliction of Israel, that it was very bitter for all, slave and free; and there was no helper for Israel.'),
('2KI', 14, 27, '2KI.14.27', 'The LORD didn’t say that he would blot out the name of Israel from under the sky; but he saved them by the hand of Jeroboam the son of Joash.'),
('2KI', 14, 28, '2KI.14.28', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, and all that he did, and his might, how he fought, and how he recovered Damascus, and Hamath, which had belonged to Judah, for Israel, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 14, 29, '2KI.14.29', 'Jeroboam slept with his fathers, even with the kings of Israel; and Zechariah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 1, '2KI.15.1', 'In the twenty-seventh year of Jeroboam king of Israel, Azariah son of Amaziah king of Judah began to reign.'),
('2KI', 15, 2, '2KI.15.2', 'He was sixteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-two years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Jecoliah of Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 15, 3, '2KI.15.3', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, according to all that his father Amaziah had done.'),
('2KI', 15, 4, '2KI.15.4', 'However, the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places.'),
('2KI', 15, 5, '2KI.15.5', 'The LORD struck the king, so that he was a leper to the day of his death, and lived in a separate house. Jotham, the king’s son, was over the household, judging the people of the land.'),
('2KI', 15, 6, '2KI.15.6', 'Now the rest of the acts of Azariah, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 15, 7, '2KI.15.7', 'Azariah slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in David’s city; and Jotham his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 8, '2KI.15.8', 'In the thirty-eighth year of Azariah king of Judah, Zechariah the son of Jeroboam reigned over Israel in Samaria six months.'),
('2KI', 15, 9, '2KI.15.9', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, as his fathers had done. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('2KI', 15, 10, '2KI.15.10', 'Shallum the son of Jabesh conspired against him, and struck him before the people and killed him, and reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 11, '2KI.15.11', 'Now the rest of the acts of Zechariah, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 12, '2KI.15.12', 'This was the LORD’s word which he spoke to Jehu, saying, “Your sons to the fourth generation shall sit on the throne of Israel.” So it came to pass.'),
('2KI', 15, 13, '2KI.15.13', 'Shallum the son of Jabesh began to reign in the thirty-ninth year of Uzziah king of Judah, and he reigned for a month in Samaria.'),
('2KI', 15, 14, '2KI.15.14', 'Menahem the son of Gadi went up from Tirzah, came to Samaria, struck Shallum the son of Jabesh in Samaria, killed him, and reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 15, '2KI.15.15', 'Now the rest of the acts of Shallum, and his conspiracy which he made, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 16, '2KI.15.16', 'Then Menahem attacked Tiphsah and all who were in it and its border areas, from Tirzah. He attacked it because they didn’t open their gates to him, and he ripped up all their women who were with child.'),
('2KI', 15, 17, '2KI.15.17', 'In the thirty ninth year of Azariah king of Judah, Menahem the son of Gadi began to reign over Israel for ten years in Samaria.'),
('2KI', 15, 18, '2KI.15.18', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart all his days from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('2KI', 15, 19, '2KI.15.19', 'Pul the king of Assyria came against the land, and Menahem gave Pul one thousand talents of silver, that his hand might be with him to confirm the kingdom in his hand.'),
('2KI', 15, 20, '2KI.15.20', 'Menahem exacted the money from Israel, even from all the mighty men of wealth, from each man fifty shekels of silver, to give to the king of Assyria. So the king of Assyria turned back, and didn’t stay there in the land.'),
('2KI', 15, 21, '2KI.15.21', 'Now the rest of the acts of Menahem, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 15, 22, '2KI.15.22', 'Menahem slept with his fathers, and Pekahiah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 23, '2KI.15.23', 'In the fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah, Pekahiah the son of Menahem began to reign over Israel in Samaria for two years.'),
('2KI', 15, 24, '2KI.15.24', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('2KI', 15, 25, '2KI.15.25', 'Pekah the son of Remaliah, his captain, conspired against him and attacked him in Samaria, in the fortress of the king’s house, with Argob and Arieh; and with him were fifty men of the Gileadites. He killed him, and reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 26, '2KI.15.26', 'Now the rest of the acts of Pekahiah, and all that he did, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 27, '2KI.15.27', 'In the fifty-second year of Azariah king of Judah, Pekah the son of Remaliah began to reign over Israel in Samaria for twenty years.'),
('2KI', 15, 28, '2KI.15.28', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin.'),
('2KI', 15, 29, '2KI.15.29', 'In the days of Pekah king of Israel, Tiglath Pileser king of Assyria came and took Ijon, Abel Beth Maacah, Janoah, Kedesh, Hazor, Gilead, and Galilee, all the land of Naphtali; and he carried them captive to Assyria.'),
('2KI', 15, 30, '2KI.15.30', 'Hoshea the son of Elah made a conspiracy against Pekah the son of Remaliah, attacked him, killed him, and reigned in his place, in the twentieth year of Jotham the son of Uzziah.'),
('2KI', 15, 31, '2KI.15.31', 'Now the rest of the acts of Pekah, and all that he did, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 32, '2KI.15.32', 'In the second year of Pekah the son of Remaliah king of Israel, Jotham the son of Uzziah king of Judah began to reign.'),
('2KI', 15, 33, '2KI.15.33', 'He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Jerusha the daughter of Zadok.'),
('2KI', 15, 34, '2KI.15.34', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes. He did according to all that his father Uzziah had done.'),
('2KI', 15, 35, '2KI.15.35', 'However the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places. He built the upper gate of the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 15, 36, '2KI.15.36', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jotham, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 15, 37, '2KI.15.37', 'In those days, the LORD began to send Rezin the king of Syria and Pekah the son of Remaliah against Judah.'),
('2KI', 15, 38, '2KI.15.38', 'Jotham slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David’s city; and Ahaz his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 16, 1, '2KI.16.1', 'In the seventeenth year of Pekah the son of Remaliah, Ahaz the son of Jotham king of Judah began to reign.'),
('2KI', 16, 2, '2KI.16.2', 'Ahaz was twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. He didn’t do that which was right in the LORD his God’s eyes, like David his father.'),
('2KI', 16, 3, '2KI.16.3', 'But he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, and even made his son to pass through the fire, according to the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel.'),
('2KI', 16, 4, '2KI.16.4', 'He sacrificed and burned incense in the high places, on the hills, and under every green tree.'),
('2KI', 16, 5, '2KI.16.5', 'Then Rezin king of Syria and Pekah son of Remaliah king of Israel came up to Jerusalem to wage war. They besieged Ahaz, but could not overcome him.'),
('2KI', 16, 6, '2KI.16.6', 'At that time Rezin king of Syria recovered Elath to Syria, and drove the Jews from Elath; and the Syrians came to Elath, and live there to this day.'),
('2KI', 16, 7, '2KI.16.7', 'So Ahaz sent messengers to Tiglath Pileser king of Assyria, saying, “I am your servant and your son. Come up and save me out of the hand of the king of Syria and out of the hand of the king of Israel, who rise up against me.”'),
('2KI', 16, 8, '2KI.16.8', 'Ahaz took the silver and gold that was found in the LORD’s house, and in the treasures of the king’s house, and sent it for a present to the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 16, 9, '2KI.16.9', 'The king of Assyria listened to him; and the king of Assyria went up against Damascus and took it, and carried its people captive to Kir, and killed Rezin.'),
('2KI', 16, 10, '2KI.16.10', 'King Ahaz went to Damascus to meet Tiglath Pileser king of Assyria, and saw the altar that was at Damascus; and King Ahaz sent to Urijah the priest a drawing of the altar and plans to build it.'),
('2KI', 16, 11, '2KI.16.11', 'Urijah the priest built an altar. According to all that King Ahaz had sent from Damascus, so Urijah the priest made it for the coming of King Ahaz from Damascus.'),
('2KI', 16, 12, '2KI.16.12', 'When the king had come from Damascus, the king saw the altar; and the king came near to the altar, and offered on it.'),
('2KI', 16, 13, '2KI.16.13', 'He burned his burnt offering and his meal offering, poured his drink offering, and sprinkled the blood of his peace offerings on the altar.'),
('2KI', 16, 14, '2KI.16.14', 'The bronze altar, which was before the LORD, he brought from the front of the house, from between his altar and the LORD’s house, and put it on the north side of his altar.'),
('2KI', 16, 15, '2KI.16.15', 'King Ahaz commanded Urijah the priest, saying, “On the great altar burn the morning burnt offering, the evening meal offering, the king’s burnt offering and his meal offering, with the burnt offering of all the people of the land, their meal offering, and their drink offerings; and sprinkle on it all the blood of the burnt offering, and all the blood of the sacrifice; but the bronze altar will be for me to inquire by.”'),
('2KI', 16, 16, '2KI.16.16', 'Urijah the priest did so, according to all that King Ahaz commanded.'),
('2KI', 16, 17, '2KI.16.17', 'King Ahaz cut off the panels of the bases, and removed the basin from off them, and took down the sea from off the bronze oxen that were under it, and put it on a pavement of stone.'),
('2KI', 16, 18, '2KI.16.18', 'He removed the covered way for the Sabbath that they had built in the house, and the king’s outer entrance to the LORD’s house, because of the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 16, 19, '2KI.16.19', 'Now the rest of the acts of Ahaz which he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 16, 20, '2KI.16.20', 'Ahaz slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David’s city; and Hezekiah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 17, 1, '2KI.17.1', 'In the twelfth year of Ahaz king of Judah, Hoshea the son of Elah began to reign in Samaria over Israel for nine years.'),
('2KI', 17, 2, '2KI.17.2', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, yet not as the kings of Israel who were before him.'),
('2KI', 17, 3, '2KI.17.3', 'Shalmaneser king of Assyria came up against him; and Hoshea became his servant, and brought him tribute.'),
('2KI', 17, 4, '2KI.17.4', 'The king of Assyria discovered a conspiracy in Hoshea; for he had sent messengers to So king of Egypt, and offered no tribute to the king of Assyria, as he had done year by year. Therefore the king of Assyria seized him, and bound him in prison.'),
('2KI', 17, 5, '2KI.17.5', 'Then the king of Assyria came up throughout all the land, went up to Samaria, and besieged it three years.'),
('2KI', 17, 6, '2KI.17.6', 'In the ninth year of Hoshea the king of Assyria took Samaria and carried Israel away to Assyria, and placed them in Halah, and on the Habor, the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes.'),
('2KI', 17, 7, '2KI.17.7', 'It was so because the children of Israel had sinned against the LORD their God, who brought them up out of the land of Egypt from under the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and had feared other gods,'),
('2KI', 17, 8, '2KI.17.8', 'and walked in the statutes of the nations whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel, and of the kings of Israel, which they made.'),
('2KI', 17, 9, '2KI.17.9', 'The children of Israel secretly did things that were not right against the LORD their God; and they built high places for themselves in all their cities, from the tower of the watchmen to the fortified city;'),
('2KI', 17, 10, '2KI.17.10', 'and they set up for themselves pillars and Asherah poles on every high hill and under every green tree;'),
('2KI', 17, 11, '2KI.17.11', 'and there they burned incense in all the high places, as the nations whom the LORD carried away before them did; and they did wicked things to provoke the LORD to anger;'),
('2KI', 17, 12, '2KI.17.12', 'and they served idols, of which the LORD had said to them, “You shall not do this thing.”'),
('2KI', 17, 13, '2KI.17.13', 'Yet the LORD testified to Israel and to Judah, by every prophet and every seer, saying, “Turn from your evil ways, and keep my commandments and my statutes, according to all the law which I commanded your fathers, and which I sent to you by my servants the prophets.”'),
('2KI', 17, 14, '2KI.17.14', 'Notwithstanding, they would not listen, but hardened their neck like the neck of their fathers who didn’t believe in the LORD their God.'),
('2KI', 17, 15, '2KI.17.15', 'They rejected his statutes and his covenant that he made with their fathers, and his testimonies which he testified to them; and they followed vanity, and became vain, and followed the nations that were around them, concerning whom the LORD had commanded them that they should not do like them.'),
('2KI', 17, 16, '2KI.17.16', 'They abandoned all the commandments of the LORD their God, and made molten images for themselves, even two calves, and made an Asherah, and worshiped all the army of the sky, and served Baal.'),
('2KI', 17, 17, '2KI.17.17', 'They caused their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire, used divination and enchantments, and sold themselves to do that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, to provoke him to anger.'),
('2KI', 17, 18, '2KI.17.18', 'Therefore the LORD was very angry with Israel, and removed them out of his sight. There was none left but the tribe of Judah only.'),
('2KI', 17, 19, '2KI.17.19', 'Also Judah didn’t keep the commandments of the LORD their God, but walked in the statutes of Israel which they made.'),
('2KI', 17, 20, '2KI.17.20', 'The LORD rejected all the offspring of Israel, afflicted them, and delivered them into the hands of raiders, until he had cast them out of his sight.'),
('2KI', 17, 21, '2KI.17.21', 'For he tore Israel from David’s house; and they made Jeroboam the son of Nebat king; and Jeroboam drove Israel from following the LORD, and made them sin a great sin.'),
('2KI', 17, 22, '2KI.17.22', 'The children of Israel walked in all the sins of Jeroboam which he did; they didn’t depart from them'),
('2KI', 17, 23, '2KI.17.23', 'until the LORD removed Israel out of his sight, as he said by all his servants the prophets. So Israel was carried away out of their own land to Assyria to this day.'),
('2KI', 17, 24, '2KI.17.24', 'The king of Assyria brought people from Babylon, from Cuthah, from Avva, and from Hamath and Sepharvaim, and placed them in the cities of Samaria instead of the children of Israel; and they possessed Samaria and lived in its cities.'),
('2KI', 17, 25, '2KI.17.25', 'So it was, at the beginning of their dwelling there, that they didn’t fear the LORD. Therefore the LORD sent lions among them, which killed some of them.'),
('2KI', 17, 26, '2KI.17.26', 'Therefore they spoke to the king of Assyria, saying, “The nations which you have carried away and placed in the cities of Samaria don’t know the law of the god of the land. Therefore he has sent lions among them; and behold, they kill them, because they don’t know the law of the god of the land.”'),
('2KI', 17, 27, '2KI.17.27', 'Then the king of Assyria commanded, saying, “Carry there one of the priests whom you brought from there; and let him go and dwell there, and let him teach them the law of the god of the land.”'),
('2KI', 17, 28, '2KI.17.28', 'So one of the priests whom they had carried away from Samaria came and lived in Bethel, and taught them how they should fear the LORD.'),
('2KI', 17, 29, '2KI.17.29', 'However every nation made gods of their own, and put them in the houses of the high places which the Samaritans had made, every nation in their cities in which they lived.'),
('2KI', 17, 30, '2KI.17.30', 'The men of Babylon made Succoth Benoth, and the men of Cuth made Nergal, and the men of Hamath made Ashima,'),
('2KI', 17, 31, '2KI.17.31', 'and the Avvites made Nibhaz and Tartak; and the Sepharvites burned their children in the fire to Adrammelech and Anammelech, the gods of Sepharvaim.'),
('2KI', 17, 32, '2KI.17.32', 'So they feared the LORD, and also made from among themselves priests of the high places for themselves, who sacrificed for them in the houses of the high places.'),
('2KI', 17, 33, '2KI.17.33', 'They feared the LORD, and also served their own gods, after the ways of the nations from among whom they had been carried away.'),
('2KI', 17, 34, '2KI.17.34', 'To this day they do what they did before. They don’t fear the LORD, and they do not follow the statutes, or the ordinances, or the law, or the commandment which the LORD commanded the children of Jacob, whom he named Israel;'),
('2KI', 17, 35, '2KI.17.35', 'with whom the LORD had made a covenant and commanded them, saying, “You shall not fear other gods, nor bow yourselves to them, nor serve them, nor sacrifice to them;'),
('2KI', 17, 36, '2KI.17.36', 'but you shall fear the LORD, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt with great power and with an outstretched arm, and you shall bow yourselves to him, and you shall sacrifice to him.'),
('2KI', 17, 37, '2KI.17.37', 'The statutes and the ordinances, and the law and the commandment which he wrote for you, you shall observe to do forever more. You shall not fear other gods.'),
('2KI', 17, 38, '2KI.17.38', 'You shall not forget the covenant that I have made with you. You shall not fear other gods.'),
('2KI', 17, 39, '2KI.17.39', 'But you shall fear the LORD your God, and he will deliver you out of the hand of all your enemies.”'),
('2KI', 17, 40, '2KI.17.40', 'However they didn’t listen, but they did what they did before.'),
('2KI', 17, 41, '2KI.17.41', 'So these nations feared the LORD, and also served their engraved images. Their children did likewise, and so did their children’s children. They do as their fathers did to this day.'),
('2KI', 18, 1, '2KI.18.1', 'Now in the third year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, Hezekiah the son of Ahaz king of Judah began to reign.'),
('2KI', 18, 2, '2KI.18.2', 'He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Abi the daughter of Zechariah.'),
('2KI', 18, 3, '2KI.18.3', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, according to all that David his father had done.'),
('2KI', 18, 4, '2KI.18.4', 'He removed the high places, broke the pillars, and cut down the Asherah. He also broke in pieces the bronze serpent that Moses had made, because in those days the children of Israel burned incense to it; and he called it Nehushtan.'),
('2KI', 18, 5, '2KI.18.5', 'He trusted in the LORD, the God of Israel, so that after him was no one like him among all the kings of Judah, nor among them that were before him.'),
('2KI', 18, 6, '2KI.18.6', 'For he joined with the LORD. He didn’t depart from following him, but kept his commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses.'),
('2KI', 18, 7, '2KI.18.7', 'The LORD was with him. Wherever he went, he prospered. He rebelled against the king of Assyria, and didn’t serve him.'),
('2KI', 18, 8, '2KI.18.8', 'He struck the Philistines to Gaza and its borders, from the tower of the watchmen to the fortified city.'),
('2KI', 18, 9, '2KI.18.9', 'In the fourth year of King Hezekiah, which was the seventh year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, Shalmaneser king of Assyria came up against Samaria and besieged it.'),
('2KI', 18, 10, '2KI.18.10', 'At the end of three years they took it. In the sixth year of Hezekiah, which was the ninth year of Hoshea king of Israel, Samaria was taken.'),
('2KI', 18, 11, '2KI.18.11', 'The king of Assyria carried Israel away to Assyria, and put them in Halah, and on the Habor, the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes,'),
('2KI', 18, 12, '2KI.18.12', 'because they didn’t obey the LORD their God’s voice, but transgressed his covenant, even all that Moses the servant of the LORD commanded, and would not hear it or do it.'),
('2KI', 18, 13, '2KI.18.13', 'Now in the fourteenth year of King Hezekiah, Sennacherib king of Assyria came up against all the fortified cities of Judah and took them.'),
('2KI', 18, 14, '2KI.18.14', 'Hezekiah king of Judah sent to the king of Assyria at Lachish, saying, “I have offended you. Withdraw from me. That which you put on me, I will bear.” The king of Assyria appointed to Hezekiah king of Judah three hundred talents of silver and thirty talents of gold.'),
('2KI', 18, 15, '2KI.18.15', 'Hezekiah gave him all the silver that was found in the LORD’s house and in the treasures of the king’s house.'),
('2KI', 18, 16, '2KI.18.16', 'At that time, Hezekiah cut off the gold from the doors of the LORD’s temple, and from the pillars which Hezekiah king of Judah had overlaid, and gave it to the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 18, 17, '2KI.18.17', 'The king of Assyria sent Tartan, Rabsaris, and Rabshakeh from Lachish to King Hezekiah with a great army to Jerusalem. They went up and came to Jerusalem. When they had come up, they came and stood by the conduit of the upper pool, which is in the highway of the fuller’s field.'),
('2KI', 18, 18, '2KI.18.18', 'When they had called to the king, Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, and Shebnah the scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder came out to them.'),
('2KI', 18, 19, '2KI.18.19', 'Rabshakeh said to them, “Say now to Hezekiah, ‘The great king, the king of Assyria, says, “What confidence is this in which you trust?'),
('2KI', 18, 20, '2KI.18.20', 'You say (but they are but vain words), ‘There is counsel and strength for war.’ Now on whom do you trust, that you have rebelled against me?'),
('2KI', 18, 21, '2KI.18.21', 'Now, behold, you trust in the staff of this bruised reed, even in Egypt. If a man leans on it, it will go into his hand and pierce it. So is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all who trust on him.'),
('2KI', 18, 22, '2KI.18.22', 'But if you tell me, ‘We trust in the LORD our God,’ isn’t that he whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah has taken away, and has said to Judah and to Jerusalem, ‘You shall worship before this altar in Jerusalem’?'),
('2KI', 18, 23, '2KI.18.23', 'Now therefore, please give pledges to my master the king of Assyria, and I will give you two thousand horses if you are able on your part to set riders on them.'),
('2KI', 18, 24, '2KI.18.24', 'How then can you turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master’s servants, and put your trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?'),
('2KI', 18, 25, '2KI.18.25', 'Have I now come up without the LORD against this place to destroy it? The LORD said to me, ‘Go up against this land, and destroy it.’”’”'),
('2KI', 18, 26, '2KI.18.26', 'Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, Shebnah, and Joah, said to Rabshakeh, “Please speak to your servants in the Syrian language, for we understand it. Don’t speak with us in the Jews’ language, in the hearing of the people who are on the wall.”'),
('2KI', 18, 27, '2KI.18.27', 'But Rabshakeh said to them, “Has my master sent me to your master and to you, to speak these words? Hasn’t he sent me to the men who sit on the wall, to eat their own dung, and to drink their own urine with you?”'),
('2KI', 18, 28, '2KI.18.28', 'Then Rabshakeh stood and cried with a loud voice in the Jews’ language, and spoke, saying, “Hear the word of the great king, the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 18, 29, '2KI.18.29', 'The king says, ‘Don’t let Hezekiah deceive you, for he will not be able to deliver you out of his hand.'),
('2KI', 18, 30, '2KI.18.30', 'Don’t let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, “The LORD will surely deliver us, and this city shall not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.”'),
('2KI', 18, 31, '2KI.18.31', 'Don’t listen to Hezekiah.’ For the king of Assyria says, ‘Make your peace with me, and come out to me; and everyone of you eat from his own vine, and everyone from his own fig tree, and everyone drink water from his own cistern;'),
('2KI', 18, 32, '2KI.18.32', 'until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of grain and new wine, a land of bread and vineyards, a land of olive trees and of honey, that you may live and not die. Don’t listen to Hezekiah when he persuades you, saying, “The LORD will deliver us.”'),
('2KI', 18, 33, '2KI.18.33', 'Has any of the gods of the nations ever delivered his land out of the hand of the king of Assyria?'),
('2KI', 18, 34, '2KI.18.34', 'Where are the gods of Hamath and of Arpad? Where are the gods of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivvah? Have they delivered Samaria out of my hand?'),
('2KI', 18, 35, '2KI.18.35', 'Who are they among all the gods of the countries, that have delivered their country out of my hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of my hand?’”'),
('2KI', 18, 36, '2KI.18.36', 'But the people stayed quiet, and answered him not a word; for the king’s commandment was, “Don’t answer him.”'),
('2KI', 18, 37, '2KI.18.37', 'Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, came with Shebna the scribe and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder to Hezekiah with their clothes torn, and told him Rabshakeh’s words.'),
('2KI', 19, 1, '2KI.19.1', 'When King Hezekiah heard it, he tore his clothes, covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 19, 2, '2KI.19.2', 'He sent Eliakim, who was over the household, Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.'),
('2KI', 19, 3, '2KI.19.3', 'They said to him, “Hezekiah says, ‘Today is a day of trouble, of rebuke, and of rejection; for the children have come to the point of birth, and there is no strength to deliver them.'),
('2KI', 19, 4, '2KI.19.4', 'It may be the LORD your God will hear all the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master has sent to defy the living God, and will rebuke the words which the LORD your God has heard. Therefore lift up your prayer for the remnant that is left.’”'),
('2KI', 19, 5, '2KI.19.5', 'So the servants of King Hezekiah came to Isaiah.'),
('2KI', 19, 6, '2KI.19.6', 'Isaiah said to them, “Tell your master this: ‘The LORD says, “Don’t be afraid of the words that you have heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me.'),
('2KI', 19, 7, '2KI.19.7', 'Behold, I will put a spirit in him, and he will hear news, and will return to his own land. I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.”’”'),
('2KI', 19, 8, '2KI.19.8', 'So Rabshakeh returned and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah; for he had heard that he had departed from Lachish.'),
('2KI', 19, 9, '2KI.19.9', 'When he heard it said of Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, “Behold, he has come out to fight against you,” he sent messengers again to Hezekiah, saying,'),
('2KI', 19, 10, '2KI.19.10', '“Tell Hezekiah king of Judah this: ‘Don’t let your God in whom you trust deceive you, saying, Jerusalem will not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 19, 11, '2KI.19.11', 'Behold, you have heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands, by destroying them utterly. Will you be delivered?'),
('2KI', 19, 12, '2KI.19.12', 'Have the gods of the nations delivered them, which my fathers have destroyed—Gozan, Haran, Rezeph, and the children of Eden who were in Telassar?'),
('2KI', 19, 13, '2KI.19.13', 'Where is the king of Hamath, the king of Arpad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivvah?’”'),
('2KI', 19, 14, '2KI.19.14', 'Hezekiah received the letter from the hand of the messengers and read it. Then Hezekiah went up to the LORD’s house, and spread it before the LORD.'),
('2KI', 19, 15, '2KI.19.15', 'Hezekiah prayed before the LORD, and said, “LORD, the God of Israel, enthroned above the cherubim, you are the God, even you alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth. You have made heaven and earth.'),
('2KI', 19, 16, '2KI.19.16', 'Incline your ear, LORD, and hear. Open your eyes, LORD, and see. Hear the words of Sennacherib, which he has sent to defy the living God.'),
('2KI', 19, 17, '2KI.19.17', 'Truly, LORD, the kings of Assyria have laid waste the nations and their lands,'),
('2KI', 19, 18, '2KI.19.18', 'and have cast their gods into the fire; for they were no gods, but the work of men’s hands, wood and stone. Therefore they have destroyed them.'),
('2KI', 19, 19, '2KI.19.19', 'Now therefore, LORD our God, save us, I beg you, out of his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that you, LORD, are God alone.”'),
('2KI', 19, 20, '2KI.19.20', 'Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to Hezekiah, saying, “The LORD, the God of Israel, says ‘You have prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria, and I have heard you.'),
('2KI', 19, 21, '2KI.19.21', 'This is the word that the LORD has spoken concerning him: The virgin daughter of Zion has despised you and ridiculed you. The daughter of Jerusalem has shaken her head at you.'),
('2KI', 19, 22, '2KI.19.22', 'Whom have you defied and blasphemed? Against whom have you exalted your voice and lifted up your eyes on high? Against the Holy One of Israel!'),
('2KI', 19, 23, '2KI.19.23', 'By your messengers, you have defied the Lord, and have said, “With the multitude of my chariots, I have come up to the height of the mountains, to the innermost parts of Lebanon, and I will cut down its tall cedars and its choice cypress trees; and I will enter into his farthest lodging place, the forest of his fruitful field.'),
('2KI', 19, 24, '2KI.19.24', 'I have dug and drunk strange waters, and I will dry up all the rivers of Egypt with the sole of my feet.”'),
('2KI', 19, 25, '2KI.19.25', 'Haven’t you heard how I have done it long ago, and formed it of ancient times? Now I have brought it to pass, that it should be yours to lay waste fortified cities into ruinous heaps.'),
('2KI', 19, 26, '2KI.19.26', 'Therefore their inhabitants had little power. They were dismayed and confounded. They were like the grass of the field and like the green herb, like the grass on the housetops and like grain blasted before it has grown up.'),
('2KI', 19, 27, '2KI.19.27', 'But I know your sitting down, your going out, your coming in, and your raging against me.'),
('2KI', 19, 28, '2KI.19.28', 'Because of your raging against me, and because your arrogance has come up into my ears, therefore I will put my hook in your nose, and my bridle in your lips, and I will turn you back by the way by which you came.’'),
('2KI', 19, 29, '2KI.19.29', '“This will be the sign to you: This year, you will eat that which grows of itself, and in the second year that which springs from that; and in the third year sow and reap, and plant vineyards and eat their fruit.'),
('2KI', 19, 30, '2KI.19.30', 'The remnant that has escaped of the house of Judah will again take root downward, and bear fruit upward.'),
('2KI', 19, 31, '2KI.19.31', 'For out of Jerusalem a remnant will go out, and out of Mount Zion those who shall escape. The LORD’s zeal will perform this.'),
('2KI', 19, 32, '2KI.19.32', '“Therefore the LORD says concerning the king of Assyria, ‘He will not come to this city, nor shoot an arrow there. He will not come before it with shield, nor cast up a mound against it.'),
('2KI', 19, 33, '2KI.19.33', 'He will return the same way that he came, and he will not come to this city,’ says the LORD.'),
('2KI', 19, 34, '2KI.19.34', '‘For I will defend this city to save it, for my own sake and for my servant David’s sake.’”'),
('2KI', 19, 35, '2KI.19.35', 'That night, the LORD’s angel went out and struck one hundred eighty-five thousand in the camp of the Assyrians. When men arose early in the morning, behold, these were all dead bodies.'),
('2KI', 19, 36, '2KI.19.36', 'So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, went home, and lived at Nineveh.'),
('2KI', 19, 37, '2KI.19.37', 'As he was worshiping in the house of Nisroch his god, Adrammelech and Sharezer struck him with the sword; and they escaped into the land of Ararat. Esar Haddon his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 20, 1, '2KI.20.1', 'In those days Hezekiah was sick and dying. Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz came to him, and said to him, “The LORD says, ‘Set your house in order; for you will die, and not live.’”'),
('2KI', 20, 2, '2KI.20.2', 'Then he turned his face to the wall, and prayed to the LORD, saying,'),
('2KI', 20, 3, '2KI.20.3', '“Remember now, LORD, I beg you, how I have walked before you in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in your sight.” And Hezekiah wept bitterly.'),
('2KI', 20, 4, '2KI.20.4', 'Before Isaiah had gone out into the middle part of the city, the LORD’s word came to him, saying,'),
('2KI', 20, 5, '2KI.20.5', '“Turn back, and tell Hezekiah the prince of my people, ‘The LORD, the God of David your father, says, “I have heard your prayer. I have seen your tears. Behold, I will heal you. On the third day, you will go up to the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 20, 6, '2KI.20.6', 'I will add to your days fifteen years. I will deliver you and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria. I will defend this city for my own sake, and for my servant David’s sake.”’”'),
('2KI', 20, 7, '2KI.20.7', 'Isaiah said, “Take a cake of figs.” They took and laid it on the boil, and he recovered.'),
('2KI', 20, 8, '2KI.20.8', 'Hezekiah said to Isaiah, “What will be the sign that the LORD will heal me, and that I will go up to the LORD’s house the third day?”'),
('2KI', 20, 9, '2KI.20.9', 'Isaiah said, “This will be the sign to you from the LORD, that the LORD will do the thing that he has spoken: should the shadow go forward ten steps, or go back ten steps?”'),
('2KI', 20, 10, '2KI.20.10', 'Hezekiah answered, “It is a light thing for the shadow to go forward ten steps. No, but let the shadow return backward ten steps.”'),
('2KI', 20, 11, '2KI.20.11', 'Isaiah the prophet cried to the LORD; and he brought the shadow ten steps backward, by which it had gone down on the sundial of Ahaz.'),
('2KI', 20, 12, '2KI.20.12', 'At that time Berodach Baladan the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah, for he had heard that Hezekiah had been sick.'),
('2KI', 20, 13, '2KI.20.13', 'Hezekiah listened to them, and showed them all the storehouse of his precious things—the silver, the gold, the spices, and the precious oil, and the house of his armor, and all that was found in his treasures. There was nothing in his house, or in all his dominion, that Hezekiah didn’t show them.'),
('2KI', 20, 14, '2KI.20.14', 'Then Isaiah the prophet came to King Hezekiah, and said to him, “What did these men say? From where did they come to you?” Hezekiah said, “They have come from a far country, even from Babylon.”'),
('2KI', 20, 15, '2KI.20.15', 'He said, “What have they seen in your house?” Hezekiah answered, “They have seen all that is in my house. There is nothing among my treasures that I have not shown them.”'),
('2KI', 20, 16, '2KI.20.16', 'Isaiah said to Hezekiah, “Hear the LORD’s word.'),
('2KI', 20, 17, '2KI.20.17', '‘Behold, the days come that all that is in your house, and that which your fathers have laid up in store to this day, will be carried to Babylon. Nothing will be left,’ says the LORD.'),
('2KI', 20, 18, '2KI.20.18', '‘They will take away some of your sons who will issue from you, whom you will father; and they will be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.’”'),
('2KI', 20, 19, '2KI.20.19', 'Then Hezekiah said to Isaiah, “The LORD’s word which you have spoken is good.” He said moreover, “Isn’t it so, if peace and truth will be in my days?”'),
('2KI', 20, 20, '2KI.20.20', 'Now the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, and all his might, and how he made the pool, and the conduit, and brought water into the city, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 20, 21, '2KI.20.21', 'Hezekiah slept with his fathers, and Manasseh his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 21, 1, '2KI.21.1', 'Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-five years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Hephzibah.'),
('2KI', 21, 2, '2KI.21.2', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, after the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.'),
('2KI', 21, 3, '2KI.21.3', 'For he built again the high places which Hezekiah his father had destroyed; and he raised up altars for Baal, and made an Asherah, as Ahab king of Israel did, and worshiped all the army of the sky, and served them.'),
('2KI', 21, 4, '2KI.21.4', 'He built altars in the LORD’s house, of which the LORD said, “I will put my name in Jerusalem.”'),
('2KI', 21, 5, '2KI.21.5', 'He built altars for all the army of the sky in the two courts of the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 21, 6, '2KI.21.6', 'He made his son to pass through the fire, practiced sorcery, used enchantments, and dealt with those who had familiar spirits and with wizards. He did much evil in the LORD’s sight, to provoke him to anger.'),
('2KI', 21, 7, '2KI.21.7', 'He set the engraved image of Asherah that he had made in the house of which the LORD said to David and to Solomon his son, “In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will put my name forever;'),
('2KI', 21, 8, '2KI.21.8', 'I will not cause the feet of Israel to wander any more out of the land which I gave their fathers, if only they will observe to do according to all that I have commanded them, and according to all the law that my servant Moses commanded them.”'),
('2KI', 21, 9, '2KI.21.9', 'But they didn’t listen, and Manasseh seduced them to do that which is evil more than the nations did whom the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel.'),
('2KI', 21, 10, '2KI.21.10', 'The LORD spoke by his servants the prophets, saying,'),
('2KI', 21, 11, '2KI.21.11', '“Because Manasseh king of Judah has done these abominations, and has done wickedly above all that the Amorites did, who were before him, and has also made Judah to sin with his idols;'),
('2KI', 21, 12, '2KI.21.12', 'therefore the LORD the God of Israel says, ‘Behold, I will bring such evil on Jerusalem and Judah that whoever hears of it, both his ears will tingle.'),
('2KI', 21, 13, '2KI.21.13', 'I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plumb line of Ahab’s house; and I will wipe Jerusalem as a man wipes a dish, wiping it and turning it upside down.'),
('2KI', 21, 14, '2KI.21.14', 'I will cast off the remnant of my inheritance and deliver them into the hands of their enemies. They will become a prey and a plunder to all their enemies,'),
('2KI', 21, 15, '2KI.21.15', 'because they have done that which is evil in my sight, and have provoked me to anger since the day their fathers came out of Egypt, even to this day.’”'),
('2KI', 21, 16, '2KI.21.16', 'Moreover Manasseh shed innocent blood very much, until he had filled Jerusalem from one end to another; in addition to his sin with which he made Judah to sin, in doing that which was evil in the LORD’s sight.'),
('2KI', 21, 17, '2KI.21.17', 'Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and all that he did, and his sin that he sinned, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 21, 18, '2KI.21.18', 'Manasseh slept with his fathers, and was buried in the garden of his own house, in the garden of Uzza; and Amon his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 21, 19, '2KI.21.19', 'Amon was twenty-two years old when he began to reign; and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Meshullemeth the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah.'),
('2KI', 21, 20, '2KI.21.20', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, as Manasseh his father did.'),
('2KI', 21, 21, '2KI.21.21', 'He walked in all the ways that his father walked in, and served the idols that his father served, and worshiped them;'),
('2KI', 21, 22, '2KI.21.22', 'and he abandoned the LORD, the God of his fathers, and didn’t walk in the way of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 21, 23, '2KI.21.23', 'The servants of Amon conspired against him, and put the king to death in his own house.'),
('2KI', 21, 24, '2KI.21.24', 'But the people of the land killed all those who had conspired against King Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his place.'),
('2KI', 21, 25, '2KI.21.25', 'Now the rest of the acts of Amon which he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 21, 26, '2KI.21.26', 'He was buried in his tomb in the garden of Uzza, and Josiah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 22, 1, '2KI.22.1', 'Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty-one years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Jedidah the daughter of Adaiah of Bozkath.'),
('2KI', 22, 2, '2KI.22.2', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, and walked in all the ways of David his father, and didn’t turn away to the right hand or to the left.'),
('2KI', 22, 3, '2KI.22.3', 'In the eighteenth year of King Josiah, the king sent Shaphan, the son of Azaliah the son of Meshullam, the scribe, to the LORD’s house, saying,'),
('2KI', 22, 4, '2KI.22.4', '“Go up to Hilkiah the high priest, that he may count the money which is brought into the LORD’s house, which the keepers of the threshold have gathered of the people.'),
('2KI', 22, 5, '2KI.22.5', 'Let them deliver it into the hand of the workers who have the oversight of the LORD’s house; and let them give it to the workers who are in the LORD’s house, to repair the damage to the house,'),
('2KI', 22, 6, '2KI.22.6', 'to the carpenters, and to the builders, and to the masons, and for buying timber and cut stone to repair the house.'),
('2KI', 22, 7, '2KI.22.7', 'However, no accounting shall be asked of them for the money delivered into their hand, for they deal faithfully.”'),
('2KI', 22, 8, '2KI.22.8', 'Hilkiah the high priest said to Shaphan the scribe, “I have found the book of the law in the LORD’s house.” Hilkiah delivered the book to Shaphan, and he read it.'),
('2KI', 22, 9, '2KI.22.9', 'Shaphan the scribe came to the king, and brought the king word again, and said, “Your servants have emptied out the money that was found in the house, and have delivered it into the hands of the workmen who have the oversight of the LORD’s house.”'),
('2KI', 22, 10, '2KI.22.10', 'Shaphan the scribe told the king, saying, “Hilkiah the priest has delivered a book to me.” Then Shaphan read it before the king.'),
('2KI', 22, 11, '2KI.22.11', 'When the king had heard the words of the book of the law, he tore his clothes.'),
('2KI', 22, 12, '2KI.22.12', 'The king commanded Hilkiah the priest, Ahikam the son of Shaphan, Achbor the son of Micaiah, Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah the king’s servant, saying,'),
('2KI', 22, 13, '2KI.22.13', '“Go inquire of the LORD for me, and for the people, and for all Judah, concerning the words of this book that is found; for great is the LORD’s wrath that is kindled against us, because our fathers have not listened to the words of this book, to do according to all that which is written concerning us.”'),
('2KI', 22, 14, '2KI.22.14', 'So Hilkiah the priest, Ahikam, Achbor, Shaphan, and Asaiah went to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tikvah, the son of Harhas, keeper of the wardrobe (now she lived in Jerusalem in the second quarter); and they talked with her.'),
('2KI', 22, 15, '2KI.22.15', 'She said to them, “The LORD the God of Israel says, ‘Tell the man who sent you to me,'),
('2KI', 22, 16, '2KI.22.16', '“The LORD says, ‘Behold, I will bring evil on this place and on its inhabitants, even all the words of the book which the king of Judah has read.'),
('2KI', 22, 17, '2KI.22.17', 'Because they have forsaken me and have burned incense to other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the work of their hands, therefore my wrath shall be kindled against this place, and it will not be quenched.’”'),
('2KI', 22, 18, '2KI.22.18', 'But to the king of Judah, who sent you to inquire of the LORD, tell him, “The LORD the God of Israel says, ‘Concerning the words which you have heard,'),
('2KI', 22, 19, '2KI.22.19', 'because your heart was tender, and you humbled yourself before the LORD when you heard what I spoke against this place and against its inhabitants, that they should become a desolation and a curse, and have torn your clothes and wept before me, I also have heard you,’ says the LORD.'),
('2KI', 22, 20, '2KI.22.20', '‘Therefore behold, I will gather you to your fathers, and you will be gathered to your grave in peace. Your eyes will not see all the evil which I will bring on this place.’”’” So they brought this message back to the king.'),
('2KI', 23, 1, '2KI.23.1', 'The king sent, and they gathered to him all the elders of Judah and of Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 23, 2, '2KI.23.2', 'The king went up to the LORD’s house, and all the men of Judah and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem with him—with the priests, the prophets, and all the people, both small and great; and he read in their hearing all the words of the book of the covenant which was found in the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 23, 3, '2KI.23.3', 'The king stood by the pillar and made a covenant before the LORD to walk after the LORD and to keep his commandments, his testimonies, and his statutes with all his heart and all his soul, to confirm the words of this covenant that were written in this book; and all the people agreed to the covenant.'),
('2KI', 23, 4, '2KI.23.4', 'The king commanded Hilkiah the high priest, and the priests of the second order, and the keepers of the threshold, to bring out of the LORD’s temple all the vessels that were made for Baal, for the Asherah, and for all the army of the sky; and he burned them outside of Jerusalem in the fields of the Kidron, and carried their ashes to Bethel.'),
('2KI', 23, 5, '2KI.23.5', 'He got rid of the idolatrous priests whom the kings of Judah had ordained to burn incense in the high places in the cities of Judah and in the places around Jerusalem; those also who burned incense to Baal, to the sun, to the moon, to the planets, and to all the army of the sky.'),
('2KI', 23, 6, '2KI.23.6', 'He brought out the Asherah from the LORD’s house, outside of Jerusalem, to the brook Kidron, and burned it at the brook Kidron, and beat it to dust, and cast its dust on the graves of the common people.'),
('2KI', 23, 7, '2KI.23.7', 'He broke down the houses of the male shrine prostitutes that were in the LORD’s house, where the women wove hangings for the Asherah.'),
('2KI', 23, 8, '2KI.23.8', 'He brought all the priests out of the cities of Judah, and defiled the high places where the priests had burned incense, from Geba to Beersheba; and he broke down the high places of the gates that were at the entrance of the gate of Joshua the governor of the city, which were on a man’s left hand at the gate of the city.'),
('2KI', 23, 9, '2KI.23.9', 'Nevertheless the priests of the high places didn’t come up to the LORD’s altar in Jerusalem, but they ate unleavened bread among their brothers.'),
('2KI', 23, 10, '2KI.23.10', 'He defiled Topheth, which is in the valley of the children of Hinnom, that no man might make his son or his daughter to pass through the fire to Molech.'),
('2KI', 23, 11, '2KI.23.11', 'He took away the horses that the kings of Judah had dedicated to the sun, at the entrance of the LORD’s house, by the room of Nathan Melech the officer who was in the court; and he burned the chariots of the sun with fire.'),
('2KI', 23, 12, '2KI.23.12', 'The king broke down the altars that were on the roof of the upper room of Ahaz, which the kings of Judah had made, and the altars which Manasseh had made in the two courts of the LORD’s house, and beat them down from there, and cast their dust into the brook Kidron.'),
('2KI', 23, 13, '2KI.23.13', 'The king defiled the high places that were before Jerusalem, which were on the right hand of the mountain of corruption, which Solomon the king of Israel had built for Ashtoreth the abomination of the Sidonians, and for Chemosh the abomination of Moab, and for Milcom the abomination of the children of Ammon.'),
('2KI', 23, 14, '2KI.23.14', 'He broke in pieces the pillars, cut down the Asherah poles, and filled their places with men’s bones.'),
('2KI', 23, 15, '2KI.23.15', 'Moreover the altar that was at Bethel and the high place which Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin, had made, even that altar and the high place he broke down; and he burned the high place and beat it to dust, and burned the Asherah.'),
('2KI', 23, 16, '2KI.23.16', 'As Josiah turned himself, he spied the tombs that were there in the mountain; and he sent, and took the bones out of the tombs, and burned them on the altar, and defiled it, according to the LORD’s word which the man of God proclaimed, who proclaimed these things.'),
('2KI', 23, 17, '2KI.23.17', 'Then he said, “What monument is that which I see?” The men of the city told him, “It is the tomb of the man of God who came from Judah and proclaimed these things that you have done against the altar of Bethel.”'),
('2KI', 23, 18, '2KI.23.18', 'He said, “Let him be! Let no one move his bones.” So they let his bones alone, with the bones of the prophet who came out of Samaria.'),
('2KI', 23, 19, '2KI.23.19', 'All the houses also of the high places that were in the cities of Samaria, which the kings of Israel had made to provoke the LORD to anger, Josiah took away, and did to them according to all the acts that he had done in Bethel.'),
('2KI', 23, 20, '2KI.23.20', 'He killed all the priests of the high places that were there, on the altars, and burned men’s bones on them; and he returned to Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 23, 21, '2KI.23.21', 'The king commanded all the people, saying, “Keep the Passover to the LORD your God, as it is written in this book of the covenant.”'),
('2KI', 23, 22, '2KI.23.22', 'Surely there was not kept such a Passover from the days of the judges who judged Israel, nor in all the days of the kings of Israel, nor of the kings of Judah;'),
('2KI', 23, 23, '2KI.23.23', 'but in the eighteenth year of King Josiah, this Passover was kept to the LORD in Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 23, 24, '2KI.23.24', 'Moreover, Josiah removed those who had familiar spirits, the wizards, and the teraphim, and the idols, and all the abominations that were seen in the land of Judah and in Jerusalem, that he might confirm the words of the law which were written in the book that Hilkiah the priest found in the LORD’s house.'),
('2KI', 23, 25, '2KI.23.25', 'There was no king like him before him, who turned to the LORD with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with all his might, according to all the law of Moses; and there was none like him who arose after him.'),
('2KI', 23, 26, '2KI.23.26', 'Notwithstanding, the LORD didn’t turn from the fierceness of his great wrath, with which his anger burned against Judah, because of all the provocation with which Manasseh had provoked him.'),
('2KI', 23, 27, '2KI.23.27', 'The LORD said, “I will also remove Judah out of my sight, as I have removed Israel; and I will cast off this city which I have chosen, even Jerusalem, and the house of which I said, ‘My name shall be there.’”'),
('2KI', 23, 28, '2KI.23.28', 'Now the rest of the acts of Josiah, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 23, 29, '2KI.23.29', 'In his days Pharaoh Necoh king of Egypt went up against the king of Assyria to the river Euphrates; and King Josiah went against him, but Pharaoh Necoh killed him at Megiddo when he saw him.'),
('2KI', 23, 30, '2KI.23.30', 'His servants carried him dead in a chariot from Megiddo, brought him to Jerusalem, and buried him in his own tomb. The people of the land took Jehoahaz the son of Josiah, and anointed him, and made him king in his father’s place.'),
('2KI', 23, 31, '2KI.23.31', 'Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he began to reign; and he reigned three months in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Hamutal the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.'),
('2KI', 23, 32, '2KI.23.32', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, according to all that his fathers had done.'),
('2KI', 23, 33, '2KI.23.33', 'Pharaoh Necoh put him in bonds at Riblah in the land of Hamath, that he might not reign in Jerusalem; and put the land to a tribute of one hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold.'),
('2KI', 23, 34, '2KI.23.34', 'Pharaoh Necoh made Eliakim the son of Josiah king in the place of Josiah his father, and changed his name to Jehoiakim; but he took Jehoahaz away, and he came to Egypt and died there.'),
('2KI', 23, 35, '2KI.23.35', 'Jehoiakim gave the silver and the gold to Pharaoh; but he taxed the land to give the money according to the commandment of Pharaoh. He exacted the silver and the gold of the people of the land, from everyone according to his assessment, to give it to Pharaoh Necoh.'),
('2KI', 23, 36, '2KI.23.36', 'Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Zebidah the daughter of Pedaiah of Rumah.'),
('2KI', 23, 37, '2KI.23.37', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, according to all that his fathers had done.'),
('2KI', 24, 1, '2KI.24.1', 'In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant for three years. Then he turned and rebelled against him.'),
('2KI', 24, 2, '2KI.24.2', 'The LORD sent against him bands of the Chaldeans, bands of the Syrians, bands of the Moabites, and bands of the children of Ammon, and sent them against Judah to destroy it, according to the LORD’s word which he spoke by his servants the prophets.'),
('2KI', 24, 3, '2KI.24.3', 'Surely at the commandment of the LORD this came on Judah, to remove them out of his sight for the sins of Manasseh, according to all that he did,'),
('2KI', 24, 4, '2KI.24.4', 'and also for the innocent blood that he shed; for he filled Jerusalem with innocent blood, and the LORD would not pardon.'),
('2KI', 24, 5, '2KI.24.5', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, and all that he did, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 24, 6, '2KI.24.6', 'So Jehoiakim slept with his fathers, and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 24, 7, '2KI.24.7', 'The king of Egypt didn’t come out of his land any more; for the king of Babylon had taken, from the brook of Egypt to the river Euphrates, all that belonged to the king of Egypt.'),
('2KI', 24, 8, '2KI.24.8', 'Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. His mother’s name was Nehushta the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 24, 9, '2KI.24.9', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, according to all that his father had done.'),
('2KI', 24, 10, '2KI.24.10', 'At that time the servants of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up to Jerusalem, and the city was besieged.'),
('2KI', 24, 11, '2KI.24.11', 'Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to the city while his servants were besieging it,'),
('2KI', 24, 12, '2KI.24.12', 'and Jehoiachin the king of Judah went out to the king of Babylon—he, his mother, his servants, his princes, and his officers; and the king of Babylon captured him in the eighth year of his reign.'),
('2KI', 24, 13, '2KI.24.13', 'He carried out from there all the treasures of the LORD’s house and the treasures of the king’s house, and cut in pieces all the vessels of gold which Solomon king of Israel had made in the LORD’s temple, as the LORD had said.'),
('2KI', 24, 14, '2KI.24.14', 'He carried away all Jerusalem, and all the princes, and all the mighty men of valor, even ten thousand captives, and all the craftsmen and the smiths. No one remained except the poorest people of the land.'),
('2KI', 24, 15, '2KI.24.15', 'He carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon, with the king’s mother, the king’s wives, his officers, and the chief men of the land. He carried them into captivity from Jerusalem to Babylon.'),
('2KI', 24, 16, '2KI.24.16', 'All the men of might, even seven thousand, and the craftsmen and the smiths one thousand, all of them strong and fit for war, even them the king of Babylon brought captive to Babylon.'),
('2KI', 24, 17, '2KI.24.17', 'The king of Babylon made Mattaniah, Jehoiachin’s father’s brother, king in his place, and changed his name to Zedekiah.'),
('2KI', 24, 18, '2KI.24.18', 'Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Hamutal the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.'),
('2KI', 24, 19, '2KI.24.19', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, according to all that Jehoiakim had done.'),
('2KI', 24, 20, '2KI.24.20', 'For through the anger of the LORD, this happened in Jerusalem and Judah, until he had cast them out from his presence. Then Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon.'),
('2KI', 25, 1, '2KI.25.1', 'In the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came, he and all his army, against Jerusalem, and encamped against it; and they built forts against it around it.'),
('2KI', 25, 2, '2KI.25.2', 'So the city was besieged until the eleventh year of King Zedekiah.'),
('2KI', 25, 3, '2KI.25.3', 'On the ninth day of the fourth month, the famine was severe in the city, so that there was no bread for the people of the land.'),
('2KI', 25, 4, '2KI.25.4', 'Then a breach was made in the city, and all the men of war fled by night by the way of the gate between the two walls, which was by the king’s garden (now the Chaldeans were against the city around it); and the king went by the way of the Arabah.'),
('2KI', 25, 5, '2KI.25.5', 'But the Chaldean army pursued the king, and overtook him in the plains of Jericho; and all his army was scattered from him.'),
('2KI', 25, 6, '2KI.25.6', 'Then they captured the king and carried him up to the king of Babylon to Riblah; and they passed judgment on him.'),
('2KI', 25, 7, '2KI.25.7', 'They killed Zedekiah’s sons before his eyes, then put out Zedekiah’s eyes, bound him in fetters, and carried him to Babylon.'),
('2KI', 25, 8, '2KI.25.8', 'Now in the fifth month, on the seventh day of the month, which was the nineteenth year of King Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, came to Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 25, 9, '2KI.25.9', 'He burned the LORD’s house, the king’s house, and all the houses of Jerusalem. He burned every great house with fire.'),
('2KI', 25, 10, '2KI.25.10', 'All the army of the Chaldeans, who were with the captain of the guard, broke down the walls around Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 25, 11, '2KI.25.11', 'Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive the rest of the people who were left in the city and those who had deserted to the king of Babylon—all the rest of the multitude.'),
('2KI', 25, 12, '2KI.25.12', 'But the captain of the guard left some of the poorest of the land to work the vineyards and fields.'),
('2KI', 25, 13, '2KI.25.13', 'The Chaldeans broke up the pillars of bronze that were in the LORD’s house and the bases and the bronze sea that were in the LORD’s house, and carried the bronze pieces to Babylon.'),
('2KI', 25, 14, '2KI.25.14', 'They took away the pots, the shovels, the snuffers, the spoons, and all the vessels of bronze with which they ministered.'),
('2KI', 25, 15, '2KI.25.15', 'The captain of the guard took away the fire pans, the basins, that which was of gold, for gold, and that which was of silver, for silver.'),
('2KI', 25, 16, '2KI.25.16', 'The two pillars, the one sea, and the bases, which Solomon had made for the LORD’s house, the bronze of all these vessels was not weighed.'),
('2KI', 25, 17, '2KI.25.17', 'The height of the one pillar was eighteen cubits, and a capital of bronze was on it. The height of the capital was three cubits, with network and pomegranates on the capital around it, all of bronze; and the second pillar with its network was like these.'),
('2KI', 25, 18, '2KI.25.18', 'The captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the threshold;'),
('2KI', 25, 19, '2KI.25.19', 'and out of the city he took an officer who was set over the men of war; and five men of those who saw the king’s face, who were found in the city; and the scribe, the captain of the army, who mustered the people of the land, and sixty men of the people of the land who were found in the city.'),
('2KI', 25, 20, '2KI.25.20', 'Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard took them, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah.'),
('2KI', 25, 21, '2KI.25.21', 'The king of Babylon attacked them and put them to death at Riblah in the land of Hamath. So Judah was carried away captive out of his land.'),
('2KI', 25, 22, '2KI.25.22', 'As for the people who were left in the land of Judah whom Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had left, even over them he made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, governor.'),
('2KI', 25, 23, '2KI.25.23', 'Now when all the captains of the forces, they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah governor, they came to Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, Johanan the son of Kareah, Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and Jaazaniah the son of the Maacathite, they and their men.'),
('2KI', 25, 24, '2KI.25.24', 'Gedaliah swore to them and to their men, and said to them, “Don’t be afraid because of the servants of the Chaldeans. Dwell in the land and serve the king of Babylon, and it will be well with you.”'),
('2KI', 25, 25, '2KI.25.25', 'But in the seventh month, Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, of the royal offspring came, and ten men with him, and struck Gedaliah so that he died, with the Jews and the Chaldeans that were with him at Mizpah.'),
('2KI', 25, 26, '2KI.25.26', 'All the people, both small and great, and the captains of the forces arose and came to Egypt; for they were afraid of the Chaldeans.'),
('2KI', 25, 27, '2KI.25.27', 'In the thirty-seventh year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the twenty-seventh day of the month, Evilmerodach king of Babylon, in the year that he began to reign, released Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison,'),
('2KI', 25, 28, '2KI.25.28', 'and he spoke kindly to him and set his throne above the throne of the kings who were with him in Babylon,'),
('2KI', 25, 29, '2KI.25.29', 'and changed his prison garments. Jehoiachin ate bread before him continually all the days of his life;'),
('2KI', 25, 30, '2KI.25.30', 'and for his allowance, there was a continual allowance given him from the king, every day a portion, all the days of his life.'),
('1CH', 1, 1, '1CH.1.1', 'Adam, Seth, Enosh,'),
('1CH', 1, 2, '1CH.1.2', 'Kenan, Mahalalel, Jared,'),
('1CH', 1, 3, '1CH.1.3', 'Enoch, Methuselah, Lamech,'),
('1CH', 1, 4, '1CH.1.4', 'Noah, Shem, Ham, and Japheth.'),
('1CH', 1, 5, '1CH.1.5', 'The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras.'),
('1CH', 1, 6, '1CH.1.6', 'The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Diphath, and Togarmah.'),
('1CH', 1, 7, '1CH.1.7', 'The sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, Kittim, and Rodanim.'),
('1CH', 1, 8, '1CH.1.8', 'The sons of Ham: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan.'),
('1CH', 1, 9, '1CH.1.9', 'The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabta, Raama, Sabteca. The sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan.'),
('1CH', 1, 10, '1CH.1.10', 'Cush became the father of Nimrod. He began to be a mighty one on the earth.'),
('1CH', 1, 11, '1CH.1.11', 'Mizraim became the father of Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim,'),
('1CH', 1, 12, '1CH.1.12', 'Pathrusim, Casluhim (where the Philistines came from), and Caphtorim.'),
('1CH', 1, 13, '1CH.1.13', 'Canaan became the father of Sidon his firstborn, Heth,'),
('1CH', 1, 14, '1CH.1.14', 'the Jebusite, the Amorite, the Girgashite,'),
('1CH', 1, 15, '1CH.1.15', 'the Hivite, the Arkite, the Sinite,'),
('1CH', 1, 16, '1CH.1.16', 'the Arvadite, the Zemarite, and the Hamathite.'),
('1CH', 1, 17, '1CH.1.17', 'The sons of Shem: Elam, Asshur, Arpachshad, Lud, Aram, Uz, Hul, Gether, and Meshech.'),
('1CH', 1, 18, '1CH.1.18', 'Arpachshad became the father of Shelah, and Shelah became the father of Eber.'),
('1CH', 1, 19, '1CH.1.19', 'To Eber were born two sons: the name of the one was Peleg, for in his days the earth was divided; and his brother’s name was Joktan.'),
('1CH', 1, 20, '1CH.1.20', 'Joktan became the father of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah,'),
('1CH', 1, 21, '1CH.1.21', 'Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah,'),
('1CH', 1, 22, '1CH.1.22', 'Ebal, Abimael, Sheba,'),
('1CH', 1, 23, '1CH.1.23', 'Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab. All these were the sons of Joktan.'),
('1CH', 1, 24, '1CH.1.24', 'Shem, Arpachshad, Shelah,'),
('1CH', 1, 25, '1CH.1.25', 'Eber, Peleg, Reu,'),
('1CH', 1, 26, '1CH.1.26', 'Serug, Nahor, Terah,'),
('1CH', 1, 27, '1CH.1.27', 'Abram (also called Abraham).'),
('1CH', 1, 28, '1CH.1.28', 'The sons of Abraham: Isaac and Ishmael.'),
('1CH', 1, 29, '1CH.1.29', 'These are their generations: the firstborn of Ishmael, Nebaioth; then Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam,'),
('1CH', 1, 30, '1CH.1.30', 'Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema,'),
('1CH', 1, 31, '1CH.1.31', 'Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. These are the sons of Ishmael.'),
('1CH', 1, 32, '1CH.1.32', 'The sons of Keturah, Abraham’s concubine: she bore Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah. The sons of Jokshan: Sheba and Dedan.'),
('1CH', 1, 33, '1CH.1.33', 'The sons of Midian: Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abida, and Eldaah. All these were the sons of Keturah.'),
('1CH', 1, 34, '1CH.1.34', 'Abraham became the father of Isaac. The sons of Isaac: Esau and Israel.'),
('1CH', 1, 35, '1CH.1.35', 'The sons of Esau: Eliphaz, Reuel, Jeush, Jalam, and Korah.'),
('1CH', 1, 36, '1CH.1.36', 'The sons of Eliphaz: Teman, Omar, Zephi, Gatam, Kenaz, Timna, and Amalek.'),
('1CH', 1, 37, '1CH.1.37', 'The sons of Reuel: Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Mizzah.'),
('1CH', 1, 38, '1CH.1.38', 'The sons of Seir: Lotan, Shobal, Zibeon, Anah, Dishon, Ezer, and Dishan.'),
('1CH', 1, 39, '1CH.1.39', 'The sons of Lotan: Hori and Homam; and Timna was Lotan’s sister.'),
('1CH', 1, 40, '1CH.1.40', 'The sons of Shobal: Alian, Manahath, Ebal, Shephi, and Onam. The sons of Zibeon: Aiah and Anah.'),
('1CH', 1, 41, '1CH.1.41', 'The son of Anah: Dishon. The sons of Dishon: Hamran, Eshban, Ithran, and Cheran.'),
('1CH', 1, 42, '1CH.1.42', 'The sons of Ezer: Bilhan, Zaavan, and Jaakan. The sons of Dishan: Uz and Aran.'),
('1CH', 1, 43, '1CH.1.43', 'Now these are the kings who reigned in the land of Edom, before any king reigned over the children of Israel: Bela the son of Beor; and the name of his city was Dinhabah.'),
('1CH', 1, 44, '1CH.1.44', 'Bela died, and Jobab the son of Zerah of Bozrah reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 45, '1CH.1.45', 'Jobab died, and Husham of the land of the Temanites reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 46, '1CH.1.46', 'Husham died, and Hadad the son of Bedad, who struck Midian in the field of Moab, reigned in his place; and the name of his city was Avith.'),
('1CH', 1, 47, '1CH.1.47', 'Hadad died, and Samlah of Masrekah reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 48, '1CH.1.48', 'Samlah died, and Shaul of Rehoboth by the River reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 49, '1CH.1.49', 'Shaul died, and Baal Hanan the son of Achbor reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 50, '1CH.1.50', 'Baal Hanan died, and Hadad reigned in his place; and the name of his city was Pai. His wife’s name was Mehetabel, the daughter of Matred, the daughter of Mezahab.'),
('1CH', 1, 51, '1CH.1.51', 'Then Hadad died. The chiefs of Edom were: chief Timna, chief Aliah, chief Jetheth,'),
('1CH', 1, 52, '1CH.1.52', 'chief Oholibamah, chief Elah, chief Pinon,'),
('1CH', 1, 53, '1CH.1.53', 'chief Kenaz, chief Teman, chief Mibzar,'),
('1CH', 1, 54, '1CH.1.54', 'chief Magdiel, and chief Iram. These are the chiefs of Edom.'),
('1CH', 2, 1, '1CH.2.1', 'These are the sons of Israel: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Zebulun,'),
('1CH', 2, 2, '1CH.2.2', 'Dan, Joseph, Benjamin, Naphtali, Gad, and Asher.'),
('1CH', 2, 3, '1CH.2.3', 'The sons of Judah: Er, Onan, and Shelah, which three were born to him of Shua’s daughter the Canaanitess. Er, Judah’s firstborn, was wicked in the LORD’s sight; and he killed him.'),
('1CH', 2, 4, '1CH.2.4', 'Tamar his daughter-in-law bore him Perez and Zerah. All the sons of Judah were five.'),
('1CH', 2, 5, '1CH.2.5', 'The sons of Perez: Hezron and Hamul.'),
('1CH', 2, 6, '1CH.2.6', 'The sons of Zerah: Zimri, Ethan, Heman, Calcol, and Dara—five of them in all.'),
('1CH', 2, 7, '1CH.2.7', 'The son of Carmi: Achar, the troubler of Israel, who committed a trespass in the devoted thing.'),
('1CH', 2, 8, '1CH.2.8', 'The son of Ethan: Azariah.'),
('1CH', 2, 9, '1CH.2.9', 'The sons also of Hezron, who were born to him: Jerahmeel, Ram, and Chelubai.'),
('1CH', 2, 10, '1CH.2.10', 'Ram became the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab became the father of Nahshon, prince of the children of Judah;'),
('1CH', 2, 11, '1CH.2.11', 'and Nahshon became the father of Salma, and Salma became the father of Boaz,'),
('1CH', 2, 12, '1CH.2.12', 'and Boaz became the father of Obed, and Obed became the father of Jesse;'),
('1CH', 2, 13, '1CH.2.13', 'and Jesse became the father of his firstborn Eliab, Abinadab the second, Shimea the third,'),
('1CH', 2, 14, '1CH.2.14', 'Nethanel the fourth, Raddai the fifth,'),
('1CH', 2, 15, '1CH.2.15', 'Ozem the sixth, and David the seventh;'),
('1CH', 2, 16, '1CH.2.16', 'and their sisters were Zeruiah and Abigail. The sons of Zeruiah: Abishai, Joab, and Asahel, three.'),
('1CH', 2, 17, '1CH.2.17', 'Abigail bore Amasa; and the father of Amasa was Jether the Ishmaelite.'),
('1CH', 2, 18, '1CH.2.18', 'Caleb the son of Hezron became the father of children by Azubah his wife, and by Jerioth; and these were her sons: Jesher, Shobab, and Ardon.'),
('1CH', 2, 19, '1CH.2.19', 'Azubah died, and Caleb married Ephrath, who bore him Hur.'),
('1CH', 2, 20, '1CH.2.20', 'Hur became the father of Uri, and Uri became the father of Bezalel.'),
('1CH', 2, 21, '1CH.2.21', 'Afterward Hezron went in to the daughter of Machir the father of Gilead, whom he took as wife when he was sixty years old; and she bore him Segub.'),
('1CH', 2, 22, '1CH.2.22', 'Segub became the father of Jair, who had twenty-three cities in the land of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 2, 23, '1CH.2.23', 'Geshur and Aram took the towns of Jair from them, with Kenath, and its villages, even sixty cities. All these were the sons of Machir the father of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 2, 24, '1CH.2.24', 'After Hezron died in Caleb Ephrathah, Abijah, Hezron’s wife, bore him Ashhur the father of Tekoa.'),
('1CH', 2, 25, '1CH.2.25', 'The sons of Jerahmeel the firstborn of Hezron were Ram the firstborn, Bunah, Oren, Ozem, and Ahijah.'),
('1CH', 2, 26, '1CH.2.26', 'Jerahmeel had another wife, whose name was Atarah. She was the mother of Onam.'),
('1CH', 2, 27, '1CH.2.27', 'The sons of Ram the firstborn of Jerahmeel were Maaz, Jamin, and Eker.'),
('1CH', 2, 28, '1CH.2.28', 'The sons of Onam were Shammai and Jada. The sons of Shammai: Nadab and Abishur.'),
('1CH', 2, 29, '1CH.2.29', 'The name of the wife of Abishur was Abihail; and she bore him Ahban and Molid.'),
('1CH', 2, 30, '1CH.2.30', 'The sons of Nadab: Seled and Appaim; but Seled died without children.'),
('1CH', 2, 31, '1CH.2.31', 'The son of Appaim: Ishi. The son of Ishi: Sheshan. The son of Sheshan: Ahlai.'),
('1CH', 2, 32, '1CH.2.32', 'The sons of Jada the brother of Shammai: Jether and Jonathan; and Jether died without children.'),
('1CH', 2, 33, '1CH.2.33', 'The sons of Jonathan: Peleth and Zaza. These were the sons of Jerahmeel.'),
('1CH', 2, 34, '1CH.2.34', 'Now Sheshan had no sons, but only daughters. Sheshan had a servant, an Egyptian, whose name was Jarha.'),
('1CH', 2, 35, '1CH.2.35', 'Sheshan gave his daughter to Jarha his servant as wife; and she bore him Attai.'),
('1CH', 2, 36, '1CH.2.36', 'Attai became the father of Nathan, and Nathan became the father of Zabad,'),
('1CH', 2, 37, '1CH.2.37', 'and Zabad became the father of Ephlal, and Ephlal became the father of Obed,'),
('1CH', 2, 38, '1CH.2.38', 'and Obed became the father of Jehu, and Jehu became the father of Azariah,'),
('1CH', 2, 39, '1CH.2.39', 'and Azariah became the father of Helez, and Helez became the father of Eleasah,'),
('1CH', 2, 40, '1CH.2.40', 'and Eleasah became the father of Sismai, and Sismai became the father of Shallum,'),
('1CH', 2, 41, '1CH.2.41', 'and Shallum became the father of Jekamiah, and Jekamiah became the father of Elishama.'),
('1CH', 2, 42, '1CH.2.42', 'The sons of Caleb the brother of Jerahmeel were Mesha his firstborn, who was the father of Ziph, and the sons of Mareshah the father of Hebron.'),
('1CH', 2, 43, '1CH.2.43', 'The sons of Hebron: Korah, Tappuah, Rekem, and Shema.'),
('1CH', 2, 44, '1CH.2.44', 'Shema became the father of Raham, the father of Jorkeam; and Rekem became the father of Shammai.'),
('1CH', 2, 45, '1CH.2.45', 'The son of Shammai was Maon; and Maon was the father of Beth Zur.'),
('1CH', 2, 46, '1CH.2.46', 'Ephah, Caleb’s concubine, bore Haran, Moza, and Gazez; and Haran became the father of Gazez.'),
('1CH', 2, 47, '1CH.2.47', 'The sons of Jahdai: Regem, Jothan, Geshan, Pelet, Ephah, and Shaaph.'),
('1CH', 2, 48, '1CH.2.48', 'Maacah, Caleb’s concubine, bore Sheber and Tirhanah.'),
('1CH', 2, 49, '1CH.2.49', 'She bore also Shaaph the father of Madmannah, Sheva the father of Machbena and the father of Gibea; and the daughter of Caleb was Achsah.'),
('1CH', 2, 50, '1CH.2.50', 'These were the sons of Caleb, the son of Hur, the firstborn of Ephrathah: Shobal the father of Kiriath Jearim,'),
('1CH', 2, 51, '1CH.2.51', 'Salma the father of Bethlehem, and Hareph the father of Beth Gader.'),
('1CH', 2, 52, '1CH.2.52', 'Shobal the father of Kiriath Jearim had sons: Haroeh, half of the Menuhoth.'),
('1CH', 2, 53, '1CH.2.53', 'The families of Kiriath Jearim: the Ithrites, the Puthites, the Shumathites, and the Mishraites; from them came the Zorathites and the Eshtaolites.'),
('1CH', 2, 54, '1CH.2.54', 'The sons of Salma: Bethlehem, the Netophathites, Atroth Beth Joab, and half of the Manahathites, the Zorites.'),
('1CH', 2, 55, '1CH.2.55', 'The families of scribes who lived at Jabez: the Tirathites, the Shimeathites, and the Sucathites. These are the Kenites who came from Hammath, the father of the house of Rechab.'),
('1CH', 3, 1, '1CH.3.1', 'Now these were the sons of David, who were born to him in Hebron: the firstborn, Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess; the second, Daniel, of Abigail the Carmelitess;'),
('1CH', 3, 2, '1CH.3.2', 'the third, Absalom the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur; the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith;'),
('1CH', 3, 3, '1CH.3.3', 'the fifth, Shephatiah of Abital; the sixth, Ithream by Eglah his wife:'),
('1CH', 3, 4, '1CH.3.4', 'six were born to him in Hebron; and he reigned there seven years and six months. He reigned thirty-three years in Jerusalem;'),
('1CH', 3, 5, '1CH.3.5', 'and these were born to him in Jerusalem: Shimea, Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon, four, by Bathshua the daughter of Ammiel;'),
('1CH', 3, 6, '1CH.3.6', 'and Ibhar, Elishama, Eliphelet,'),
('1CH', 3, 7, '1CH.3.7', 'Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia,'),
('1CH', 3, 8, '1CH.3.8', 'Elishama, Eliada, and Eliphelet, nine.'),
('1CH', 3, 9, '1CH.3.9', 'All these were the sons of David, in addition to the sons of the concubines; and Tamar was their sister.'),
('1CH', 3, 10, '1CH.3.10', 'Solomon’s son was Rehoboam, Abijah his son, Asa his son, Jehoshaphat his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 11, '1CH.3.11', 'Joram his son, Ahaziah his son, Joash his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 12, '1CH.3.12', 'Amaziah his son, Azariah his son, Jotham his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 13, '1CH.3.13', 'Ahaz his son, Hezekiah his son, Manasseh his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 14, '1CH.3.14', 'Amon his son, and Josiah his son.'),
('1CH', 3, 15, '1CH.3.15', 'The sons of Josiah: the firstborn Johanan, the second Jehoiakim, the third Zedekiah, and the fourth Shallum.'),
('1CH', 3, 16, '1CH.3.16', 'The sons of Jehoiakim: Jeconiah his son, and Zedekiah his son.'),
('1CH', 3, 17, '1CH.3.17', 'The sons of Jeconiah, the captive: Shealtiel his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 18, '1CH.3.18', 'Malchiram, Pedaiah, Shenazzar, Jekamiah, Hoshama, and Nedabiah.'),
('1CH', 3, 19, '1CH.3.19', 'The sons of Pedaiah: Zerubbabel and Shimei. The sons of Zerubbabel: Meshullam and Hananiah; and Shelomith was their sister;'),
('1CH', 3, 20, '1CH.3.20', 'and Hashubah, Ohel, Berechiah, Hasadiah, and Jushab Hesed, five.'),
('1CH', 3, 21, '1CH.3.21', 'The sons of Hananiah: Pelatiah and Jeshaiah; the sons of Rephaiah, the sons of Arnan, the sons of Obadiah, the sons of Shecaniah.'),
('1CH', 3, 22, '1CH.3.22', 'The son of Shecaniah: Shemaiah. The sons of Shemaiah: Hattush, Igal, Bariah, Neariah, and Shaphat, six.'),
('1CH', 3, 23, '1CH.3.23', 'The sons of Neariah: Elioenai, Hizkiah, and Azrikam, three.'),
('1CH', 3, 24, '1CH.3.24', 'The sons of Elioenai: Hodaviah, Eliashib, Pelaiah, Akkub, Johanan, Delaiah, and Anani, seven.'),
('1CH', 4, 1, '1CH.4.1', 'The sons of Judah: Perez, Hezron, Carmi, Hur, and Shobal.'),
('1CH', 4, 2, '1CH.4.2', 'Reaiah the son of Shobal became the father of Jahath; and Jahath became the father of Ahumai and Lahad. These are the families of the Zorathites.'),
('1CH', 4, 3, '1CH.4.3', 'These were the sons of the father of Etam: Jezreel, Ishma, and Idbash. The name of their sister was Hazzelelponi.'),
('1CH', 4, 4, '1CH.4.4', 'Penuel was the father of Gedor and Ezer the father of Hushah. These are the sons of Hur, the firstborn of Ephrathah, the father of Bethlehem.'),
('1CH', 4, 5, '1CH.4.5', 'Ashhur the father of Tekoa had two wives, Helah and Naarah.'),
('1CH', 4, 6, '1CH.4.6', 'Naarah bore him Ahuzzam, Hepher, Temeni, and Haahashtari. These were the sons of Naarah.'),
('1CH', 4, 7, '1CH.4.7', 'The sons of Helah were Zereth, Izhar, and Ethnan.'),
('1CH', 4, 8, '1CH.4.8', 'Hakkoz became the father of Anub, Zobebah, and the families of Aharhel the son of Harum.'),
('1CH', 4, 9, '1CH.4.9', 'Jabez was more honorable than his brothers. His mother named him Jabez, saying, “Because I bore him with sorrow.”'),
('1CH', 4, 10, '1CH.4.10', 'Jabez called on the God of Israel, saying, “Oh that you would bless me indeed, and enlarge my border! May your hand be with me, and may you keep me from evil, that I may not cause pain!” God granted him that which he requested.'),
('1CH', 4, 11, '1CH.4.11', 'Chelub the brother of Shuhah became the father of Mehir, who was the father of Eshton.'),
('1CH', 4, 12, '1CH.4.12', 'Eshton became the father of Beth Rapha, Paseah, and Tehinnah the father of Ir Nahash. These are the men of Recah.'),
('1CH', 4, 13, '1CH.4.13', 'The sons of Kenaz: Othniel and Seraiah. The sons of Othniel: Hathath.'),
('1CH', 4, 14, '1CH.4.14', 'Meonothai became the father of Ophrah: and Seraiah became the father of Joab the father of Ge Harashim, for they were craftsmen.'),
('1CH', 4, 15, '1CH.4.15', 'The sons of Caleb the son of Jephunneh: Iru, Elah, and Naam. The son of Elah: Kenaz.'),
('1CH', 4, 16, '1CH.4.16', 'The sons of Jehallelel: Ziph, Ziphah, Tiria, and Asarel.'),
('1CH', 4, 17, '1CH.4.17', 'The sons of Ezrah: Jether, Mered, Epher, and Jalon; and Mered’s wife bore Miriam, Shammai, and Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa.'),
('1CH', 4, 18, '1CH.4.18', 'His wife the Jewess bore Jered the father of Gedor, Heber the father of Soco, and Jekuthiel the father of Zanoah. These are the sons of Bithiah the daughter of Pharaoh, whom Mered took.'),
('1CH', 4, 19, '1CH.4.19', 'The sons of the wife of Hodiah, the sister of Naham, were the fathers of Keilah the Garmite and Eshtemoa the Maacathite.'),
('1CH', 4, 20, '1CH.4.20', 'The sons of Shimon: Amnon, Rinnah, Ben Hanan, and Tilon. The sons of Ishi: Zoheth, and Ben Zoheth.'),
('1CH', 4, 21, '1CH.4.21', 'The sons of Shelah the son of Judah: Er the father of Lecah, Laadah the father of Mareshah, and the families of the house of those who worked fine linen, of the house of Ashbea;'),
('1CH', 4, 22, '1CH.4.22', 'and Jokim, and the men of Cozeba, and Joash, and Saraph, who had dominion in Moab, and Jashubilehem. These records are ancient.'),
('1CH', 4, 23, '1CH.4.23', 'These were the potters, and the inhabitants of Netaim and Gederah; they lived there with the king for his work.'),
('1CH', 4, 24, '1CH.4.24', 'The sons of Simeon: Nemuel, Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, Shaul;'),
('1CH', 4, 25, '1CH.4.25', 'Shallum his son, Mibsam his son, and Mishma his son.'),
('1CH', 4, 26, '1CH.4.26', 'The sons of Mishma: Hammuel his son, Zaccur his son, Shimei his son.'),
('1CH', 4, 27, '1CH.4.27', 'Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters; but his brothers didn’t have many children, and all their family didn’t multiply like the children of Judah.'),
('1CH', 4, 28, '1CH.4.28', 'They lived at Beersheba, Moladah, Hazarshual,'),
('1CH', 4, 29, '1CH.4.29', 'at Bilhah, at Ezem, at Tolad,'),
('1CH', 4, 30, '1CH.4.30', 'at Bethuel, at Hormah, at Ziklag,'),
('1CH', 4, 31, '1CH.4.31', 'at Beth Marcaboth, Hazar Susim, at Beth Biri, and at Shaaraim. These were their cities until David’s reign.'),
('1CH', 4, 32, '1CH.4.32', 'Their villages were Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Tochen, and Ashan, five cities;'),
('1CH', 4, 33, '1CH.4.33', 'and all their villages that were around the same cities, as far as Baal. These were their settlements, and they kept their genealogy.'),
('1CH', 4, 34, '1CH.4.34', 'Meshobab, Jamlech, Joshah the son of Amaziah,'),
('1CH', 4, 35, '1CH.4.35', 'Joel, Jehu the son of Joshibiah, the son of Seraiah, the son of Asiel,'),
('1CH', 4, 36, '1CH.4.36', 'Elioenai, Jaakobah, Jeshohaiah, Asaiah, Adiel, Jesimiel, Benaiah,'),
('1CH', 4, 37, '1CH.4.37', 'and Ziza the son of Shiphi, the son of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah—'),
('1CH', 4, 38, '1CH.4.38', 'these mentioned by name were princes in their families. Their fathers’ houses increased greatly.'),
('1CH', 4, 39, '1CH.4.39', 'They went to the entrance of Gedor, even to the east side of the valley, to seek pasture for their flocks.'),
('1CH', 4, 40, '1CH.4.40', 'They found rich, good pasture, and the land was wide, and quiet, and peaceful, for those who lived there before were descended from Ham.'),
('1CH', 4, 41, '1CH.4.41', 'These written by name came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and struck their tents and the Meunim who were found there; and they destroyed them utterly to this day, and lived in their place, because there was pasture there for their flocks.'),
('1CH', 4, 42, '1CH.4.42', 'Some of them, even of the sons of Simeon, five hundred men, went to Mount Seir, having for their captains Pelatiah, Neariah, Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi.'),
('1CH', 4, 43, '1CH.4.43', 'They struck the remnant of the Amalekites who escaped, and have lived there to this day.'),
('1CH', 5, 1, '1CH.5.1', 'The sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel (for he was the firstborn, but because he defiled his father’s couch, his birthright was given to the sons of Joseph the son of Israel; and the genealogy is not to be listed according to the birthright.'),
('1CH', 5, 2, '1CH.5.2', 'For Judah prevailed above his brothers, and from him came the prince; but the birthright was Joseph’s)—'),
('1CH', 5, 3, '1CH.5.3', 'the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel: Hanoch, Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi.'),
('1CH', 5, 4, '1CH.5.4', 'The sons of Joel: Shemaiah his son, Gog his son, Shimei his son,'),
('1CH', 5, 5, '1CH.5.5', 'Micah his son, Reaiah his son, Baal his son,'),
('1CH', 5, 6, '1CH.5.6', 'and Beerah his son, whom Tilgath Pilneser king of Assyria carried away captive. He was prince of the Reubenites.'),
('1CH', 5, 7, '1CH.5.7', 'His brothers by their families, when the genealogy of their generations was listed: the chief, Jeiel, and Zechariah,'),
('1CH', 5, 8, '1CH.5.8', 'and Bela the son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel, who lived in Aroer, even to Nebo and Baal Meon;'),
('1CH', 5, 9, '1CH.5.9', 'and he lived eastward even to the entrance of the wilderness from the river Euphrates, because their livestock were multiplied in the land of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 5, 10, '1CH.5.10', 'In the days of Saul, they made war with the Hagrites, who fell by their hand; and they lived in their tents throughout all the land east of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 5, 11, '1CH.5.11', 'The sons of Gad lived beside them in the land of Bashan to Salecah:'),
('1CH', 5, 12, '1CH.5.12', 'Joel the chief, Shapham the second, Janai, and Shaphat in Bashan.'),
('1CH', 5, 13, '1CH.5.13', 'Their brothers of their fathers’ houses: Michael, Meshullam, Sheba, Jorai, Jacan, Zia, and Eber, seven.'),
('1CH', 5, 14, '1CH.5.14', 'These were the sons of Abihail, the son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz;'),
('1CH', 5, 15, '1CH.5.15', 'Ahi the son of Abdiel, the son of Guni, chief of their fathers’ houses.'),
('1CH', 5, 16, '1CH.5.16', 'They lived in Gilead in Bashan and in its towns, and in all the pasture lands of Sharon as far as their borders.'),
('1CH', 5, 17, '1CH.5.17', 'All these were listed by genealogies in the days of Jotham king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam king of Israel.'),
('1CH', 5, 18, '1CH.5.18', 'The sons of Reuben, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh, of valiant men, men able to bear buckler and sword, able to shoot with bow, and skillful in war, were forty-four thousand seven hundred sixty that were able to go out to war.'),
('1CH', 5, 19, '1CH.5.19', 'They made war with the Hagrites, with Jetur, and Naphish, and Nodab.'),
('1CH', 5, 20, '1CH.5.20', 'They were helped against them, and the Hagrites were delivered into their hand, and all who were with them; for they cried to God in the battle, and he answered them because they put their trust in him.'),
('1CH', 5, 21, '1CH.5.21', 'They took away their livestock: of their camels fifty thousand, and of sheep two hundred fifty thousand, and of donkeys two thousand, and of men one hundred thousand.'),
('1CH', 5, 22, '1CH.5.22', 'For many fell slain, because the war was of God. They lived in their place until the captivity.'),
('1CH', 5, 23, '1CH.5.23', 'The children of the half-tribe of Manasseh lived in the land. They increased from Bashan to Baal Hermon, Senir, and Mount Hermon.'),
('1CH', 5, 24, '1CH.5.24', 'These were the heads of their fathers’ houses: Epher, Ishi, Eliel, Azriel, Jeremiah, Hodaviah, and Jahdiel—mighty men of valor, famous men, heads of their fathers’ houses.'),
('1CH', 5, 25, '1CH.5.25', 'They trespassed against the God of their fathers, and played the prostitute after the gods of the peoples of the land whom God destroyed before them.'),
('1CH', 5, 26, '1CH.5.26', 'So the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria, and the spirit of Tilgath Pilneser king of Assyria, and he carried away the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh, and brought them to Halah, Habor, Hara, and to the river of Gozan, to this day.'),
('1CH', 6, 1, '1CH.6.1', 'The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.'),
('1CH', 6, 2, '1CH.6.2', 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.'),
('1CH', 6, 3, '1CH.6.3', 'The children of Amram: Aaron, Moses, and Miriam. The sons of Aaron: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 6, 4, '1CH.6.4', 'Eleazar became the father of Phinehas, Phinehas became the father of Abishua,'),
('1CH', 6, 5, '1CH.6.5', 'Abishua became the father of Bukki. Bukki became the father of Uzzi.'),
('1CH', 6, 6, '1CH.6.6', 'Uzzi became the father of Zerahiah. Zerahiah became the father of Meraioth.'),
('1CH', 6, 7, '1CH.6.7', 'Meraioth became the father of Amariah. Amariah became the father of Ahitub.'),
('1CH', 6, 8, '1CH.6.8', 'Ahitub became the father of Zadok. Zadok became the father of Ahimaaz.'),
('1CH', 6, 9, '1CH.6.9', 'Ahimaaz became the father of Azariah. Azariah became the father of Johanan.'),
('1CH', 6, 10, '1CH.6.10', 'Johanan became the father of Azariah, who executed the priest’s office in the house that Solomon built in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 6, 11, '1CH.6.11', 'Azariah became the father of Amariah. Amariah became the father of Ahitub.'),
('1CH', 6, 12, '1CH.6.12', 'Ahitub became the father of Zadok. Zadok became the father of Shallum.'),
('1CH', 6, 13, '1CH.6.13', 'Shallum became the father of Hilkiah. Hilkiah became the father of Azariah.'),
('1CH', 6, 14, '1CH.6.14', 'Azariah became the father of Seraiah. Seraiah became the father of Jehozadak.'),
('1CH', 6, 15, '1CH.6.15', 'Jehozadak went into captivity when the LORD carried Judah and Jerusalem away by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar.'),
('1CH', 6, 16, '1CH.6.16', 'The sons of Levi: Gershom, Kohath, and Merari.'),
('1CH', 6, 17, '1CH.6.17', 'These are the names of the sons of Gershom: Libni and Shimei.'),
('1CH', 6, 18, '1CH.6.18', 'The sons of Kohath were Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.'),
('1CH', 6, 19, '1CH.6.19', 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. These are the families of the Levites according to their fathers’ households.'),
('1CH', 6, 20, '1CH.6.20', 'Of Gershom: Libni his son, Jahath his son, Zimmah his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 21, '1CH.6.21', 'Joah his son, Iddo his son, Zerah his son, and Jeatherai his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 22, '1CH.6.22', 'The sons of Kohath: Amminadab his son, Korah his son, Assir his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 23, '1CH.6.23', 'Elkanah his son, Ebiasaph his son, Assir his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 24, '1CH.6.24', 'Tahath his son, Uriel his son, Uzziah his son, and Shaul his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 25, '1CH.6.25', 'The sons of Elkanah: Amasai and Ahimoth.'),
('1CH', 6, 26, '1CH.6.26', 'As for Elkanah, the sons of Elkanah: Zophai his son, Nahath his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 27, '1CH.6.27', 'Eliab his son, Jeroham his son, and Elkanah his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 28, '1CH.6.28', 'The sons of Samuel: the firstborn, Joel, and the second, Abijah.'),
('1CH', 6, 29, '1CH.6.29', 'The sons of Merari: Mahli, Libni his son, Shimei his son, Uzzah his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 30, '1CH.6.30', 'Shimea his son, Haggiah his son, Asaiah his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 31, '1CH.6.31', 'These are they whom David set over the service of song in the LORD’s house after the ark came to rest there.'),
('1CH', 6, 32, '1CH.6.32', 'They ministered with song before the tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting until Solomon had built the LORD’s house in Jerusalem. They performed the duties of their office according to their order.'),
('1CH', 6, 33, '1CH.6.33', 'These are those who served, and their sons. Of the sons of the Kohathites: Heman the singer, the son of Joel, the son of Samuel,'),
('1CH', 6, 34, '1CH.6.34', 'the son of Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Eliel, the son of Toah,'),
('1CH', 6, 35, '1CH.6.35', 'the son of Zuph, the son of Elkanah, the son of Mahath, the son of Amasai,'),
('1CH', 6, 36, '1CH.6.36', 'the son of Elkanah, the son of Joel, the son of Azariah, the son of Zephaniah,'),
('1CH', 6, 37, '1CH.6.37', 'the son of Tahath, the son of Assir, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah,'),
('1CH', 6, 38, '1CH.6.38', 'the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, the son of Israel.'),
('1CH', 6, 39, '1CH.6.39', 'His brother Asaph, who stood on his right hand, even Asaph the son of Berechiah, the son of Shimea,'),
('1CH', 6, 40, '1CH.6.40', 'the son of Michael, the son of Baaseiah, the son of Malchijah,'),
('1CH', 6, 41, '1CH.6.41', 'the son of Ethni, the son of Zerah, the son of Adaiah,'),
('1CH', 6, 42, '1CH.6.42', 'the son of Ethan, the son of Zimmah, the son of Shimei,'),
('1CH', 6, 43, '1CH.6.43', 'the son of Jahath, the son of Gershom, the son of Levi.'),
('1CH', 6, 44, '1CH.6.44', 'On the left hand their brothers the sons of Merari: Ethan the son of Kishi, the son of Abdi, the son of Malluch,'),
('1CH', 6, 45, '1CH.6.45', 'the son of Hashabiah, the son of Amaziah, the son of Hilkiah,'),
('1CH', 6, 46, '1CH.6.46', 'the son of Amzi, the son of Bani, the son of Shemer,'),
('1CH', 6, 47, '1CH.6.47', 'the son of Mahli, the son of Mushi, the son of Merari, the son of Levi.'),
('1CH', 6, 48, '1CH.6.48', 'Their brothers the Levites were appointed for all the service of the tabernacle of God’s house.'),
('1CH', 6, 49, '1CH.6.49', 'But Aaron and his sons offered on the altar of burnt offering, and on the altar of incense, for all the work of the most holy place, and to make atonement for Israel, according to all that Moses the servant of God had commanded.'),
('1CH', 6, 50, '1CH.6.50', 'These are the sons of Aaron: Eleazar his son, Phinehas his son, Abishua his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 51, '1CH.6.51', 'Bukki his son, Uzzi his son, Zerahiah his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 52, '1CH.6.52', 'Meraioth his son, Amariah his son, Ahitub his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 53, '1CH.6.53', 'Zadok his son, and Ahimaaz his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 54, '1CH.6.54', 'Now these are their dwelling places according to their encampments in their borders: to the sons of Aaron, of the families of the Kohathites (for theirs was the first lot),'),
('1CH', 6, 55, '1CH.6.55', 'to them they gave Hebron in the land of Judah, and its pasture lands around it;'),
('1CH', 6, 56, '1CH.6.56', 'but the fields of the city and its villages, they gave to Caleb the son of Jephunneh.'),
('1CH', 6, 57, '1CH.6.57', 'To the sons of Aaron they gave the cities of refuge, Hebron, Libnah also with its pasture lands, Jattir, Eshtemoa with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 58, '1CH.6.58', 'Hilen with its pasture lands, Debir with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 59, '1CH.6.59', 'Ashan with its pasture lands, and Beth Shemesh with its pasture lands;'),
('1CH', 6, 60, '1CH.6.60', 'and out of the tribe of Benjamin, Geba with its pasture lands, Allemeth with its pasture lands, and Anathoth with its pasture lands. All their cities throughout their families were thirteen cities.'),
('1CH', 6, 61, '1CH.6.61', 'To the rest of the sons of Kohath were given by lot, out of the family of the tribe, out of the half-tribe, the half of Manasseh, ten cities.'),
('1CH', 6, 62, '1CH.6.62', 'To the sons of Gershom, according to their families, out of the tribe of Issachar, and out of the tribe of Asher, and out of the tribe of Naphtali, and out of the tribe of Manasseh in Bashan, thirteen cities.'),
('1CH', 6, 63, '1CH.6.63', 'To the sons of Merari were given by lot, according to their families, out of the tribe of Reuben, and out of the tribe of Gad, and out of the tribe of Zebulun, twelve cities.'),
('1CH', 6, 64, '1CH.6.64', 'The children of Israel gave to the Levites the cities with their pasture lands.'),
('1CH', 6, 65, '1CH.6.65', 'They gave by lot out of the tribe of the children of Judah, and out of the tribe of the children of Simeon, and out of the tribe of the children of Benjamin, these cities which are mentioned by name.'),
('1CH', 6, 66, '1CH.6.66', 'Some of the families of the sons of Kohath had cities of their borders out of the tribe of Ephraim.'),
('1CH', 6, 67, '1CH.6.67', 'They gave to them the cities of refuge, Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim with its pasture lands and Gezer with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 68, '1CH.6.68', 'Jokmeam with its pasture lands, Beth Horon with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 69, '1CH.6.69', 'Aijalon with its pasture lands, Gath Rimmon with its pasture lands;'),
('1CH', 6, 70, '1CH.6.70', 'and out of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Aner with its pasture lands, and Bileam with its pasture lands, for the rest of the family of the sons of Kohath.'),
('1CH', 6, 71, '1CH.6.71', 'To the sons of Gershom were given, out of the family of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Golan in Bashan with its pasture lands, and Ashtaroth with its pasture lands;'),
('1CH', 6, 72, '1CH.6.72', 'and out of the tribe of Issachar, Kedesh with its pasture lands, Daberath with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 73, '1CH.6.73', 'Ramoth with its pasture lands, and Anem with its pasture lands;'),
('1CH', 6, 74, '1CH.6.74', 'and out of the tribe of Asher, Mashal with its pasture lands, Abdon with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 75, '1CH.6.75', 'Hukok with its pasture lands, and Rehob with its pasture lands;'),
('1CH', 6, 76, '1CH.6.76', 'and out of the tribe of Naphtali, Kedesh in Galilee with its pasture lands, Hammon with its pasture lands, and Kiriathaim with its pasture lands.'),
('1CH', 6, 77, '1CH.6.77', 'To the rest of the Levites, the sons of Merari, were given, out of the tribe of Zebulun, Rimmono with its pasture lands, and Tabor with its pasture lands;'),
('1CH', 6, 78, '1CH.6.78', 'and beyond the Jordan at Jericho, on the east side of the Jordan, were given them out of the tribe of Reuben: Bezer in the wilderness with its pasture lands, Jahzah with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 79, '1CH.6.79', 'Kedemoth with its pasture lands, and Mephaath with its pasture lands;'),
('1CH', 6, 80, '1CH.6.80', 'and out of the tribe of Gad, Ramoth in Gilead with its pasture lands, Mahanaim with its pasture lands,'),
('1CH', 6, 81, '1CH.6.81', 'Heshbon with its pasture lands, and Jazer with its pasture lands.'),
('1CH', 7, 1, '1CH.7.1', 'Of the sons of Issachar: Tola, Puah, Jashub, and Shimron, four.'),
('1CH', 7, 2, '1CH.7.2', 'The sons of Tola: Uzzi, Rephaiah, Jeriel, Jahmai, Ibsam, and Shemuel, heads of their fathers’ houses, of Tola; mighty men of valor in their generations. Their number in the days of David was twenty-two thousand six hundred.'),
('1CH', 7, 3, '1CH.7.3', 'The son of Uzzi: Izrahiah. The sons of Izrahiah: Michael, Obadiah, Joel, and Isshiah, five; all of them chief men.'),
('1CH', 7, 4, '1CH.7.4', 'With them, by their generations, after their fathers’ houses, were bands of the army for war, thirty-six thousand; for they had many wives and sons.'),
('1CH', 7, 5, '1CH.7.5', 'Their brothers among all the families of Issachar, mighty men of valor, listed in all by genealogy, were eighty-seven thousand.'),
('1CH', 7, 6, '1CH.7.6', 'The sons of Benjamin: Bela, Becher, and Jediael, three.'),
('1CH', 7, 7, '1CH.7.7', 'The sons of Bela: Ezbon, Uzzi, Uzziel, Jerimoth, and Iri, five; heads of fathers’ houses, mighty men of valor; and they were listed by genealogy twenty-two thousand thirty-four.'),
('1CH', 7, 8, '1CH.7.8', 'The sons of Becher: Zemirah, Joash, Eliezer, Elioenai, Omri, Jeremoth, Abijah, Anathoth, and Alemeth. All these were the sons of Becher.'),
('1CH', 7, 9, '1CH.7.9', 'They were listed by genealogy, after their generations, heads of their fathers’ houses, mighty men of valor, twenty thousand two hundred.'),
('1CH', 7, 10, '1CH.7.10', 'The son of Jediael: Bilhan. The sons of Bilhan: Jeush, Benjamin, Ehud, Chenaanah, Zethan, Tarshish, and Ahishahar.'),
('1CH', 7, 11, '1CH.7.11', 'All these were sons of Jediael, according to the heads of their fathers’ households, mighty men of valor, seventeen thousand two hundred, who were able to go out in the army for war.'),
('1CH', 7, 12, '1CH.7.12', 'So were Shuppim, Huppim, the sons of Ir, Hushim, and the sons of Aher.'),
('1CH', 7, 13, '1CH.7.13', 'The sons of Naphtali: Jahziel, Guni, Jezer, Shallum, and the sons of Bilhah.'),
('1CH', 7, 14, '1CH.7.14', 'The sons of Manasseh: Asriel, whom his concubine the Aramitess bore. She bore Machir the father of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 7, 15, '1CH.7.15', 'Machir took a wife of Huppim and Shuppim, whose sister’s name was Maacah. The name of the second was Zelophehad; and Zelophehad had daughters.'),
('1CH', 7, 16, '1CH.7.16', 'Maacah the wife of Machir bore a son, and she named him Peresh. The name of his brother was Sheresh; and his sons were Ulam and Rakem.'),
('1CH', 7, 17, '1CH.7.17', 'The sons of Ulam: Bedan. These were the sons of Gilead the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh.'),
('1CH', 7, 18, '1CH.7.18', 'His sister Hammolecheth bore Ishhod, Abiezer, and Mahlah.'),
('1CH', 7, 19, '1CH.7.19', 'The sons of Shemida were Ahian, Shechem, Likhi, and Aniam.'),
('1CH', 7, 20, '1CH.7.20', 'The sons of Ephraim: Shuthelah, Bered his son, Tahath his son, Eleadah his son, Tahath his son,'),
('1CH', 7, 21, '1CH.7.21', 'Zabad his son, Shuthelah his son, Ezer, and Elead, whom the men of Gath who were born in the land killed, because they came down to take away their livestock.'),
('1CH', 7, 22, '1CH.7.22', 'Ephraim their father mourned many days, and his brothers came to comfort him.'),
('1CH', 7, 23, '1CH.7.23', 'He went in to his wife, and she conceived and bore a son, and he named him Beriah, because there was trouble with his house.'),
('1CH', 7, 24, '1CH.7.24', 'His daughter was Sheerah, who built Beth Horon the lower and the upper, and Uzzen Sheerah.'),
('1CH', 7, 25, '1CH.7.25', 'Rephah was his son, Resheph his son, Telah his son, Tahan his son,'),
('1CH', 7, 26, '1CH.7.26', 'Ladan his son, Ammihud his son, Elishama his son,'),
('1CH', 7, 27, '1CH.7.27', 'Nun his son, and Joshua his son.'),
('1CH', 7, 28, '1CH.7.28', 'Their possessions and settlements were Bethel and its towns, and eastward Naaran, and westward Gezer with its towns; Shechem also and its towns, to Azzah and its towns;'),
('1CH', 7, 29, '1CH.7.29', 'and by the borders of the children of Manasseh, Beth Shean and its towns, Taanach and its towns, Megiddo and its towns, and Dor and its towns. The children of Joseph the son of Israel lived in these.'),
('1CH', 7, 30, '1CH.7.30', 'The sons of Asher: Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi, and Beriah. Serah was their sister.'),
('1CH', 7, 31, '1CH.7.31', 'The sons of Beriah: Heber and Malchiel, who was the father of Birzaith.'),
('1CH', 7, 32, '1CH.7.32', 'Heber became the father of Japhlet, Shomer, Hotham, and Shua their sister.'),
('1CH', 7, 33, '1CH.7.33', 'The sons of Japhlet: Pasach, Bimhal, and Ashvath. These are the children of Japhlet.'),
('1CH', 7, 34, '1CH.7.34', 'The sons of Shemer: Ahi, Rohgah, Jehubbah, and Aram.'),
('1CH', 7, 35, '1CH.7.35', 'The sons of Helem his brother: Zophah, Imna, Shelesh, and Amal.'),
('1CH', 7, 36, '1CH.7.36', 'The sons of Zophah: Suah, Harnepher, Shual, Beri, Imrah,'),
('1CH', 7, 37, '1CH.7.37', 'Bezer, Hod, Shamma, Shilshah, Ithran, and Beera.'),
('1CH', 7, 38, '1CH.7.38', 'The sons of Jether: Jephunneh, Pispa, and Ara.'),
('1CH', 7, 39, '1CH.7.39', 'The sons of Ulla: Arah, Hanniel, and Rizia.'),
('1CH', 7, 40, '1CH.7.40', 'All these were the children of Asher, heads of the fathers’ houses, choice and mighty men of valor, chief of the princes. The number of them listed by genealogy for service in war was twenty-six thousand men.'),
('1CH', 8, 1, '1CH.8.1', 'Benjamin became the father of Bela his firstborn, Ashbel the second, Aharah the third,'),
('1CH', 8, 2, '1CH.8.2', 'Nohah the fourth, and Rapha the fifth.'),
('1CH', 8, 3, '1CH.8.3', 'Bela had sons: Addar, Gera, Abihud,'),
('1CH', 8, 4, '1CH.8.4', 'Abishua, Naaman, Ahoah,'),
('1CH', 8, 5, '1CH.8.5', 'Gera, Shephuphan, and Huram.'),
('1CH', 8, 6, '1CH.8.6', 'These are the sons of Ehud. These are the heads of fathers’ households of the inhabitants of Geba, who were carried captive to Manahath:'),
('1CH', 8, 7, '1CH.8.7', 'Naaman, Ahijah, and Gera, who carried them captive; and he became the father of Uzza and Ahihud.'),
('1CH', 8, 8, '1CH.8.8', 'Shaharaim became the father of children in the field of Moab, after he had sent them away. Hushim and Baara were his wives.'),
('1CH', 8, 9, '1CH.8.9', 'By Hodesh his wife, he became the father of Jobab, Zibia, Mesha, Malcam,'),
('1CH', 8, 10, '1CH.8.10', 'Jeuz, Shachia, and Mirmah. These were his sons, heads of fathers’ households.'),
('1CH', 8, 11, '1CH.8.11', 'By Hushim, he became the father of Abitub and Elpaal.'),
('1CH', 8, 12, '1CH.8.12', 'The sons of Elpaal: Eber, Misham, and Shemed, who built Ono and Lod, with its towns;'),
('1CH', 8, 13, '1CH.8.13', 'and Beriah and Shema, who were heads of fathers’ households of the inhabitants of Aijalon, who put to flight the inhabitants of Gath;'),
('1CH', 8, 14, '1CH.8.14', 'and Ahio, Shashak, Jeremoth,'),
('1CH', 8, 15, '1CH.8.15', 'Zebadiah, Arad, Eder,'),
('1CH', 8, 16, '1CH.8.16', 'Michael, Ishpah, Joha, the sons of Beriah,'),
('1CH', 8, 17, '1CH.8.17', 'Zebadiah, Meshullam, Hizki, Heber,'),
('1CH', 8, 18, '1CH.8.18', 'Ishmerai, Izliah, Jobab, the sons of Elpaal,'),
('1CH', 8, 19, '1CH.8.19', 'Jakim, Zichri, Zabdi,'),
('1CH', 8, 20, '1CH.8.20', 'Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel,'),
('1CH', 8, 21, '1CH.8.21', 'Adaiah, Beraiah, Shimrath, the sons of Shimei,'),
('1CH', 8, 22, '1CH.8.22', 'Ishpan, Eber, Eliel,'),
('1CH', 8, 23, '1CH.8.23', 'Abdon, Zichri, Hanan,'),
('1CH', 8, 24, '1CH.8.24', 'Hananiah, Elam, Anthothijah,'),
('1CH', 8, 25, '1CH.8.25', 'Iphdeiah, Penuel, the sons of Shashak,'),
('1CH', 8, 26, '1CH.8.26', 'Shamsherai, Shehariah, Athaliah,'),
('1CH', 8, 27, '1CH.8.27', 'Jaareshiah, Elijah, Zichri, and the sons of Jeroham.'),
('1CH', 8, 28, '1CH.8.28', 'These were heads of fathers’ households throughout their generations, chief men. These lived in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 8, 29, '1CH.8.29', 'The father of Gibeon, whose wife’s name was Maacah, lived in Gibeon'),
('1CH', 8, 30, '1CH.8.30', 'with his firstborn son Abdon, Zur, Kish, Baal, Nadab,'),
('1CH', 8, 31, '1CH.8.31', 'Gedor, Ahio, Zecher,'),
('1CH', 8, 32, '1CH.8.32', 'and Mikloth, who became the father of Shimeah. They also lived with their families in Jerusalem, near their relatives.'),
('1CH', 8, 33, '1CH.8.33', 'Ner became the father of Kish. Kish became the father of Saul. Saul became the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Eshbaal.'),
('1CH', 8, 34, '1CH.8.34', 'The son of Jonathan was Merib-baal. Merib-baal became the father of Micah.'),
('1CH', 8, 35, '1CH.8.35', 'The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tarea, and Ahaz.'),
('1CH', 8, 36, '1CH.8.36', 'Ahaz became the father of Jehoaddah. Jehoaddah became the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri. Zimri became the father of Moza.'),
('1CH', 8, 37, '1CH.8.37', 'Moza became the father of Binea. Raphah was his son, Eleasah his son, and Azel his son.'),
('1CH', 8, 38, '1CH.8.38', 'Azel had six sons, whose names are these: Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. All these were the sons of Azel.'),
('1CH', 8, 39, '1CH.8.39', 'The sons of Eshek his brother: Ulam his firstborn, Jeush the second, and Eliphelet the third.'),
('1CH', 8, 40, '1CH.8.40', 'The sons of Ulam were mighty men of valor, archers, and had many sons, and grandsons, one hundred fifty. All these were of the sons of Benjamin.'),
('1CH', 9, 1, '1CH.9.1', 'So all Israel were listed by genealogies; and behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel. Judah was carried away captive to Babylon for their disobedience.'),
('1CH', 9, 2, '1CH.9.2', 'Now the first inhabitants who lived in their possessions in their cities were Israel, the priests, the Levites, and the temple servants.'),
('1CH', 9, 3, '1CH.9.3', 'In Jerusalem, there lived of the children of Judah, of the children of Benjamin, and of the children of Ephraim and Manasseh:'),
('1CH', 9, 4, '1CH.9.4', 'Uthai the son of Ammihud, the son of Omri, the son of Imri, the son of Bani, of the children of Perez the son of Judah.'),
('1CH', 9, 5, '1CH.9.5', 'Of the Shilonites: Asaiah the firstborn and his sons.'),
('1CH', 9, 6, '1CH.9.6', 'Of the sons of Zerah: Jeuel and their brothers, six hundred ninety.'),
('1CH', 9, 7, '1CH.9.7', 'Of the sons of Benjamin: Sallu the son of Meshullam, the son of Hodaviah, the son of Hassenuah;'),
('1CH', 9, 8, '1CH.9.8', 'and Ibneiah the son of Jeroham, and Elah the son of Uzzi, the son of Michri; and Meshullam the son of Shephatiah, the son of Reuel, the son of Ibnijah;'),
('1CH', 9, 9, '1CH.9.9', 'and their brothers, according to their generations, nine hundred fifty-six. All these men were heads of fathers’ households by their fathers’ houses.'),
('1CH', 9, 10, '1CH.9.10', 'Of the priests: Jedaiah, Jehoiarib, Jachin,'),
('1CH', 9, 11, '1CH.9.11', 'and Azariah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the ruler of God’s house;'),
('1CH', 9, 12, '1CH.9.12', 'and Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah; and Maasai the son of Adiel, the son of Jahzerah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Meshillemith, the son of Immer;'),
('1CH', 9, 13, '1CH.9.13', 'and their brothers, heads of their fathers’ houses, one thousand seven hundred sixty; they were very able men for the work of the service of God’s house.'),
('1CH', 9, 14, '1CH.9.14', 'Of the Levites: Shemaiah the son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, of the sons of Merari;'),
('1CH', 9, 15, '1CH.9.15', 'and Bakbakkar, Heresh, Galal, and Mattaniah the son of Mica, the son of Zichri, the son of Asaph,'),
('1CH', 9, 16, '1CH.9.16', 'and Obadiah the son of Shemaiah, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun; and Berechiah the son of Asa, the son of Elkanah, who lived in the villages of the Netophathites.'),
('1CH', 9, 17, '1CH.9.17', 'The gatekeepers: Shallum, Akkub, Talmon, Ahiman, and their brothers (Shallum was the chief),'),
('1CH', 9, 18, '1CH.9.18', 'who previously served in the king’s gate eastward. They were the gatekeepers for the camp of the children of Levi.'),
('1CH', 9, 19, '1CH.9.19', 'Shallum was the son of Kore, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah, and his brothers, of his father’s house, the Korahites, were over the work of the service, keepers of the thresholds of the tent. Their fathers had been over the LORD’s camp, keepers of the entry.'),
('1CH', 9, 20, '1CH.9.20', 'Phinehas the son of Eleazar was ruler over them in time past, and the LORD was with him.'),
('1CH', 9, 21, '1CH.9.21', 'Zechariah the son of Meshelemiah was gatekeeper of the door of the Tent of Meeting.'),
('1CH', 9, 22, '1CH.9.22', 'All these who were chosen to be gatekeepers in the thresholds were two hundred twelve. These were listed by genealogy in their villages, whom David and Samuel the seer ordained in their office of trust.'),
('1CH', 9, 23, '1CH.9.23', 'So they and their children had the oversight of the gates of the LORD’s house, even the house of the tent, as guards.'),
('1CH', 9, 24, '1CH.9.24', 'On the four sides were the gatekeepers, toward the east, west, north, and south.'),
('1CH', 9, 25, '1CH.9.25', 'Their brothers, in their villages, were to come in every seven days from time to time to be with them,'),
('1CH', 9, 26, '1CH.9.26', 'for the four chief gatekeepers, who were Levites, were in an office of trust, and were over the rooms and over the treasuries in God’s house.'),
('1CH', 9, 27, '1CH.9.27', 'They stayed around God’s house, because that was their duty; and it was their duty to open it morning by morning.'),
('1CH', 9, 28, '1CH.9.28', 'Certain of them were in charge of the vessels of service, for these were brought in by count, and these were taken out by count.'),
('1CH', 9, 29, '1CH.9.29', 'Some of them also were appointed over the furniture, and over all the vessels of the sanctuary, over the fine flour, the wine, the oil, the frankincense, and the spices.'),
('1CH', 9, 30, '1CH.9.30', 'Some of the sons of the priests prepared the mixing of the spices.'),
('1CH', 9, 31, '1CH.9.31', 'Mattithiah, one of the Levites, who was the firstborn of Shallum the Korahite, had the office of trust over the things that were baked in pans.'),
('1CH', 9, 32, '1CH.9.32', 'Some of their brothers, of the sons of the Kohathites, were over the show bread, to prepare it every Sabbath.'),
('1CH', 9, 33, '1CH.9.33', 'These are the singers, heads of fathers’ households of the Levites, who lived in the rooms and were free from other service, for they were employed in their work day and night.'),
('1CH', 9, 34, '1CH.9.34', 'These were heads of fathers’ households of the Levites, throughout their generations, chief men. They lived at Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 9, 35, '1CH.9.35', 'Jeiel the father of Gibeon, whose wife’s name was Maacah, lived in Gibeon.'),
('1CH', 9, 36, '1CH.9.36', 'His firstborn son was Abdon, then Zur, Kish, Baal, Ner, Nadab,'),
('1CH', 9, 37, '1CH.9.37', 'Gedor, Ahio, Zechariah, and Mikloth.'),
('1CH', 9, 38, '1CH.9.38', 'Mikloth became the father of Shimeam. They also lived with their relatives in Jerusalem, near their relatives.'),
('1CH', 9, 39, '1CH.9.39', 'Ner became the father of Kish. Kish became the father of Saul. Saul became the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Eshbaal.'),
('1CH', 9, 40, '1CH.9.40', 'The son of Jonathan was Merib-baal. Merib-baal became the father of Micah.'),
('1CH', 9, 41, '1CH.9.41', 'The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tahrea, and Ahaz.'),
('1CH', 9, 42, '1CH.9.42', 'Ahaz became the father of Jarah. Jarah became the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri. Zimri became the father of Moza.'),
('1CH', 9, 43, '1CH.9.43', 'Moza became the father of Binea, Rephaiah his son, Eleasah his son, and Azel his son.'),
('1CH', 9, 44, '1CH.9.44', 'Azel had six sons, whose names are Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. These were the sons of Azel.'),
('1CH', 10, 1, '1CH.10.1', 'Now the Philistines fought against Israel; and the men of Israel fled from before the Philistines, and fell down slain on Mount Gilboa.'),
('1CH', 10, 2, '1CH.10.2', 'The Philistines followed hard after Saul and after his sons; and the Philistines killed Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchishua, the sons of Saul.'),
('1CH', 10, 3, '1CH.10.3', 'The battle went hard against Saul, and the archers overtook him; and he was distressed by reason of the archers.'),
('1CH', 10, 4, '1CH.10.4', 'Then Saul said to his armor bearer, “Draw your sword, and thrust me through with it, lest these uncircumcised come and abuse me.” But his armor bearer would not, for he was terrified. Therefore Saul took his sword and fell on it.'),
('1CH', 10, 5, '1CH.10.5', 'When his armor bearer saw that Saul was dead, he likewise fell on his sword and died.'),
('1CH', 10, 6, '1CH.10.6', 'So Saul died with his three sons; and all his house died together.'),
('1CH', 10, 7, '1CH.10.7', 'When all the men of Israel who were in the valley saw that they fled, and that Saul and his sons were dead, they abandoned their cities, and fled; and the Philistines came and lived in them.'),
('1CH', 10, 8, '1CH.10.8', 'On the next day, when the Philistines came to strip the slain, they found Saul and his sons fallen on Mount Gilboa.'),
('1CH', 10, 9, '1CH.10.9', 'They stripped him and took his head and his armor, then sent into the land of the Philistines all around to carry the news to their idols and to the people.'),
('1CH', 10, 10, '1CH.10.10', 'They put his armor in the house of their gods, and fastened his head in the house of Dagon.'),
('1CH', 10, 11, '1CH.10.11', 'When all Jabesh Gilead heard all that the Philistines had done to Saul,'),
('1CH', 10, 12, '1CH.10.12', 'all the valiant men arose and took away the body of Saul and the bodies of his sons, and brought them to Jabesh, and buried their bones under the oak in Jabesh, and fasted seven days.'),
('1CH', 10, 13, '1CH.10.13', 'So Saul died for his trespass which he committed against the LORD, because of the LORD’s word, which he didn’t keep, and also because he asked counsel of one who had a familiar spirit, to inquire,'),
('1CH', 10, 14, '1CH.10.14', 'and didn’t inquire of the LORD. Therefore he killed him, and turned the kingdom over to David the son of Jesse.'),
('1CH', 11, 1, '1CH.11.1', 'Then all Israel gathered themselves to David to Hebron, saying, “Behold, we are your bone and your flesh.'),
('1CH', 11, 2, '1CH.11.2', 'In times past, even when Saul was king, it was you who led out and brought in Israel. The LORD your God said to you, ‘You shall be shepherd of my people Israel, and you shall be prince over my people Israel.’”'),
('1CH', 11, 3, '1CH.11.3', 'So all the elders of Israel came to the king to Hebron; and David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the LORD. They anointed David king over Israel, according to the LORD’s word by Samuel.'),
('1CH', 11, 4, '1CH.11.4', 'David and all Israel went to Jerusalem (also called Jebus); and the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the land, were there.'),
('1CH', 11, 5, '1CH.11.5', 'The inhabitants of Jebus said to David, “You will not come in here!” Nevertheless David took the stronghold of Zion. The same is David’s city.'),
('1CH', 11, 6, '1CH.11.6', 'David had said, “Whoever strikes the Jebusites first shall be chief and captain.” Joab the son of Zeruiah went up first, and was made chief.'),
('1CH', 11, 7, '1CH.11.7', 'David lived in the stronghold; therefore they called it David’s city.'),
('1CH', 11, 8, '1CH.11.8', 'He built the city all around, from Millo even around; and Joab repaired the rest of the city.'),
('1CH', 11, 9, '1CH.11.9', 'David grew greater and greater, for the LORD of Armies was with him.'),
('1CH', 11, 10, '1CH.11.10', 'Now these are the chief of the mighty men whom David had, who showed themselves strong with him in his kingdom, together with all Israel, to make him king, according to the LORD’s word concerning Israel.'),
('1CH', 11, 11, '1CH.11.11', 'This is the number of the mighty men whom David had: Jashobeam, the son of a Hachmonite, the chief of the thirty; he lifted up his spear against three hundred and killed them at one time.'),
('1CH', 11, 12, '1CH.11.12', 'After him was Eleazar the son of Dodo, the Ahohite, who was one of the three mighty men.'),
('1CH', 11, 13, '1CH.11.13', 'He was with David at Pasdammim, and there the Philistines were gathered together to battle, where there was a plot of ground full of barley; and the people fled from before the Philistines.'),
('1CH', 11, 14, '1CH.11.14', 'They stood in the middle of the plot, defended it, and killed the Philistines; and the LORD saved them by a great victory.'),
('1CH', 11, 15, '1CH.11.15', 'Three of the thirty chief men went down to the rock to David, into the cave of Adullam; and the army of the Philistines were encamped in the valley of Rephaim.'),
('1CH', 11, 16, '1CH.11.16', 'David was then in the stronghold, and the garrison of the Philistines was in Bethlehem at that time.'),
('1CH', 11, 17, '1CH.11.17', 'David longed, and said, “Oh, that someone would give me water to drink from the well of Bethlehem, which is by the gate!”'),
('1CH', 11, 18, '1CH.11.18', 'The three broke through the army of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem that was by the gate, took it, and brought it to David; but David would not drink any of it, but poured it out to the LORD,'),
('1CH', 11, 19, '1CH.11.19', 'and said, “My God forbid me, that I should do this! Shall I drink the blood of these men who have put their lives in jeopardy?” For they risked their lives to bring it. Therefore he would not drink it. The three mighty men did these things.'),
('1CH', 11, 20, '1CH.11.20', 'Abishai, the brother of Joab, was chief of the three; for he lifted up his spear against three hundred and killed them, and had a name among the three.'),
('1CH', 11, 21, '1CH.11.21', 'Of the three, he was more honorable than the two, and was made their captain; however he wasn’t included in the three.'),
('1CH', 11, 22, '1CH.11.22', 'Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had done mighty deeds, killed the two sons of Ariel of Moab. He also went down and killed a lion in the middle of a pit on a snowy day.'),
('1CH', 11, 23, '1CH.11.23', 'He killed an Egyptian, a man of great stature, five cubits high. In the Egyptian’s hand was a spear like a weaver’s beam; and he went down to him with a staff, plucked the spear out of the Egyptian’s hand, and killed him with his own spear.'),
('1CH', 11, 24, '1CH.11.24', 'Benaiah the son of Jehoiada did these things and had a name among the three mighty men.'),
('1CH', 11, 25, '1CH.11.25', 'Behold, he was more honorable than the thirty, but he didn’t attain to the three; and David set him over his guard.'),
('1CH', 11, 26, '1CH.11.26', 'The mighty men of the armies also include Asahel the brother of Joab, Elhanan the son of Dodo of Bethlehem,'),
('1CH', 11, 27, '1CH.11.27', 'Shammoth the Harorite, Helez the Pelonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 28, '1CH.11.28', 'Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite, Abiezer the Anathothite,'),
('1CH', 11, 29, '1CH.11.29', 'Sibbecai the Hushathite, Ilai the Ahohite,'),
('1CH', 11, 30, '1CH.11.30', 'Maharai the Netophathite, Heled the son of Baanah the Netophathite,'),
('1CH', 11, 31, '1CH.11.31', 'Ithai the son of Ribai of Gibeah of the children of Benjamin, Benaiah the Pirathonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 32, '1CH.11.32', 'Hurai of the brooks of Gaash, Abiel the Arbathite,'),
('1CH', 11, 33, '1CH.11.33', 'Azmaveth the Baharumite, Eliahba the Shaalbonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 34, '1CH.11.34', 'the sons of Hashem the Gizonite, Jonathan the son of Shagee the Hararite,'),
('1CH', 11, 35, '1CH.11.35', 'Ahiam the son of Sacar the Hararite, Eliphal the son of Ur,'),
('1CH', 11, 36, '1CH.11.36', 'Hepher the Mecherathite, Ahijah the Pelonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 37, '1CH.11.37', 'Hezro the Carmelite, Naarai the son of Ezbai,'),
('1CH', 11, 38, '1CH.11.38', 'Joel the brother of Nathan, Mibhar the son of Hagri,'),
('1CH', 11, 39, '1CH.11.39', 'Zelek the Ammonite, Naharai the Berothite (the armor bearer of Joab the son of Zeruiah),'),
('1CH', 11, 40, '1CH.11.40', 'Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite,'),
('1CH', 11, 41, '1CH.11.41', 'Uriah the Hittite, Zabad the son of Ahlai,'),
('1CH', 11, 42, '1CH.11.42', 'Adina the son of Shiza the Reubenite (a chief of the Reubenites), and thirty with him,'),
('1CH', 11, 43, '1CH.11.43', 'Hanan the son of Maacah, Joshaphat the Mithnite,'),
('1CH', 11, 44, '1CH.11.44', 'Uzzia the Ashterathite, Shama and Jeiel the sons of Hotham the Aroerite,'),
('1CH', 11, 45, '1CH.11.45', 'Jediael the son of Shimri, and Joha his brother, the Tizite,'),
('1CH', 11, 46, '1CH.11.46', 'Eliel the Mahavite, and Jeribai, and Joshaviah, the sons of Elnaam, and Ithmah the Moabite,'),
('1CH', 11, 47, '1CH.11.47', 'Eliel, Obed, and Jaasiel the Mezobaite.'),
('1CH', 12, 1, '1CH.12.1', 'Now these are those who came to David to Ziklag while he was a fugitive from Saul the son of Kish. They were among the mighty men, his helpers in war.'),
('1CH', 12, 2, '1CH.12.2', 'They were armed with bows, and could use both the right hand and the left in slinging stones and in shooting arrows from the bow. They were of Saul’s relatives of the tribe of Benjamin.'),
('1CH', 12, 3, '1CH.12.3', 'The chief was Ahiezer, then Joash, the sons of Shemaah the Gibeathite; Jeziel and Pelet, the sons of Azmaveth; Beracah; Jehu the Anathothite;'),
('1CH', 12, 4, '1CH.12.4', 'Ishmaiah the Gibeonite, a mighty man among the thirty and a leader of the thirty; Jeremiah; Jahaziel; Johanan; Jozabad the Gederathite;'),
('1CH', 12, 5, '1CH.12.5', 'Eluzai; Jerimoth; Bealiah; Shemariah; Shephatiah the Haruphite;'),
('1CH', 12, 6, '1CH.12.6', 'Elkanah, Isshiah, Azarel, Joezer, and Jashobeam, the Korahites;'),
('1CH', 12, 7, '1CH.12.7', 'and Joelah and Zebadiah, the sons of Jeroham of Gedor.'),
('1CH', 12, 8, '1CH.12.8', 'Some Gadites joined David in the stronghold in the wilderness, mighty men of valor, men trained for war, who could handle shield and spear; whose faces were like the faces of lions, and they were as swift as the gazelles on the mountains:'),
('1CH', 12, 9, '1CH.12.9', 'Ezer the chief, Obadiah the second, Eliab the third,'),
('1CH', 12, 10, '1CH.12.10', 'Mishmannah the fourth, Jeremiah the fifth,'),
('1CH', 12, 11, '1CH.12.11', 'Attai the sixth, Eliel the seventh,'),
('1CH', 12, 12, '1CH.12.12', 'Johanan the eighth, Elzabad the ninth,'),
('1CH', 12, 13, '1CH.12.13', 'Jeremiah the tenth, and Machbannai the eleventh.'),
('1CH', 12, 14, '1CH.12.14', 'These of the sons of Gad were captains of the army. He who was least was equal to one hundred, and the greatest to one thousand.'),
('1CH', 12, 15, '1CH.12.15', 'These are those who went over the Jordan in the first month, when it had overflowed all its banks; and they put to flight all who lived in the valleys, both toward the east and toward the west.'),
('1CH', 12, 16, '1CH.12.16', 'Some of the children of Benjamin and Judah came to the stronghold to David.'),
('1CH', 12, 17, '1CH.12.17', 'David went out to meet them, and answered them, “If you have come peaceably to me to help me, my heart will be united with you; but if you have come to betray me to my adversaries, since there is no wrong in my hands, may the God of our fathers see this and rebuke it.”'),
('1CH', 12, 18, '1CH.12.18', 'Then the Spirit came on Amasai, who was chief of the thirty, and he said, “We are yours, David, and on your side, you son of Jesse. Peace, peace be to you, and peace be to your helpers; for your God helps you.” Then David received them and made them captains of the band.'),
('1CH', 12, 19, '1CH.12.19', 'Some of Manasseh also joined David when he came with the Philistines against Saul to battle, but they didn’t help them, for the lords of the Philistines sent him away after consultation, saying, “He will desert to his master Saul to the jeopardy of our heads.”'),
('1CH', 12, 20, '1CH.12.20', 'As he went to Ziklag, some from Manasseh joined him: Adnah, Jozabad, Jediael, Michael, Jozabad, Elihu, and Zillethai, captains of thousands who were of Manasseh.'),
('1CH', 12, 21, '1CH.12.21', 'They helped David against the band of raiders, for they were all mighty men of valor and were captains in the army.'),
('1CH', 12, 22, '1CH.12.22', 'For from day to day men came to David to help him, until there was a great army, like God’s army.'),
('1CH', 12, 23, '1CH.12.23', 'These are the numbers of the heads of those who were armed for war, who came to David to Hebron to turn the kingdom of Saul to him, according to the LORD’s word.'),
('1CH', 12, 24, '1CH.12.24', 'The children of Judah who bore shield and spear were six thousand eight hundred, armed for war.'),
('1CH', 12, 25, '1CH.12.25', 'Of the children of Simeon, mighty men of valor for the war: seven thousand one hundred.'),
('1CH', 12, 26, '1CH.12.26', 'Of the children of Levi: four thousand six hundred.'),
('1CH', 12, 27, '1CH.12.27', 'Jehoiada was the leader of the household of Aaron; and with him were three thousand seven hundred,'),
('1CH', 12, 28, '1CH.12.28', 'and Zadok, a young man mighty of valor, and of his father’s house twenty-two captains.'),
('1CH', 12, 29, '1CH.12.29', 'Of the children of Benjamin, Saul’s relatives: three thousand, for until then, the greatest part of them had kept their allegiance to Saul’s house.'),
('1CH', 12, 30, '1CH.12.30', 'Of the children of Ephraim: twenty thousand eight hundred, mighty men of valor, famous men in their fathers’ houses.'),
('1CH', 12, 31, '1CH.12.31', 'Of the half-tribe of Manasseh: eighteen thousand, who were mentioned by name, to come and make David king.'),
('1CH', 12, 32, '1CH.12.32', 'Of the children of Issachar, men who had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do, their heads were two hundred; and all their brothers were at their command.'),
('1CH', 12, 33, '1CH.12.33', 'Of Zebulun, such as were able to go out in the army, who could set the battle in array with all kinds of instruments of war: fifty thousand who could command and were not of double heart.'),
('1CH', 12, 34, '1CH.12.34', 'Of Naphtali: one thousand captains, and with them with shield and spear thirty-seven thousand.'),
('1CH', 12, 35, '1CH.12.35', 'Of the Danites who could set the battle in array: twenty-eight thousand six hundred.'),
('1CH', 12, 36, '1CH.12.36', 'Of Asher, such as were able to go out in the army, who could set the battle in array: forty thousand.'),
('1CH', 12, 37, '1CH.12.37', 'On the other side of the Jordan, of the Reubenites, the Gadites, and of the half-tribe of Manasseh, with all kinds of instruments of war for the battle: one hundred twenty thousand.'),
('1CH', 12, 38, '1CH.12.38', 'All these were men of war who could order the battle array, and came with a perfect heart to Hebron to make David king over all Israel; and all the rest also of Israel were of one heart to make David king.'),
('1CH', 12, 39, '1CH.12.39', 'They were there with David three days, eating and drinking; for their brothers had supplied provisions for them.'),
('1CH', 12, 40, '1CH.12.40', 'Moreover those who were near to them, as far as Issachar, Zebulun, and Naphtali, brought bread on donkeys, on camels, on mules, and on oxen: supplies of flour, cakes of figs, clusters of raisins, wine, oil, cattle, and sheep in abundance; for there was joy in Israel.'),
('1CH', 13, 1, '1CH.13.1', 'David consulted with the captains of thousands and of hundreds, even with every leader.'),
('1CH', 13, 2, '1CH.13.2', 'David said to all the assembly of Israel, “If it seems good to you, and if it is of the LORD our God, let’s send word everywhere to our brothers who are left in all the land of Israel, with whom the priests and Levites are in their cities that have pasture lands, that they may gather themselves to us.'),
('1CH', 13, 3, '1CH.13.3', 'Also, let’s bring the ark of our God back to us again, for we didn’t seek it in the days of Saul.”'),
('1CH', 13, 4, '1CH.13.4', 'All the assembly said that they would do so, for the thing was right in the eyes of all the people.'),
('1CH', 13, 5, '1CH.13.5', 'So David assembled all Israel together, from the Shihor River of Egypt even to the entrance of Hamath, to bring God’s ark from Kiriath Jearim.'),
('1CH', 13, 6, '1CH.13.6', 'David went up with all Israel to Baalah, that is, to Kiriath Jearim, which belonged to Judah, to bring up from there God the LORD’s ark that sits above the cherubim, that is called by the Name.'),
('1CH', 13, 7, '1CH.13.7', 'They carried God’s ark on a new cart, and brought it out of Abinadab’s house; and Uzza and Ahio drove the cart.'),
('1CH', 13, 8, '1CH.13.8', 'David and all Israel played before God with all their might, even with songs, with harps, with stringed instruments, with tambourines, with cymbals, and with trumpets.'),
('1CH', 13, 9, '1CH.13.9', 'When they came to Chidon’s threshing floor, Uzza put out his hand to hold the ark, for the oxen stumbled.'),
('1CH', 13, 10, '1CH.13.10', 'The LORD’s anger burned against Uzza, and he struck him because he put his hand on the ark; and he died there before God.'),
('1CH', 13, 11, '1CH.13.11', 'David was displeased, because the LORD had broken out against Uzza. He called that place Perez Uzza, to this day.'),
('1CH', 13, 12, '1CH.13.12', 'David was afraid of God that day, saying, “How can I bring God’s ark home to me?”'),
('1CH', 13, 13, '1CH.13.13', 'So David didn’t move the ark with him into David’s city, but carried it aside into Obed-Edom the Gittite’s house.'),
('1CH', 13, 14, '1CH.13.14', 'God’s ark remained with the family of Obed-Edom in his house three months; and the LORD blessed Obed-Edom’s house and all that he had.'),
('1CH', 14, 1, '1CH.14.1', 'Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David with cedar trees, masons, and carpenters, to build him a house.'),
('1CH', 14, 2, '1CH.14.2', 'David perceived that the LORD had established him king over Israel, for his kingdom was highly exalted, for his people Israel’s sake.'),
('1CH', 14, 3, '1CH.14.3', 'David took more wives in Jerusalem, and David became the father of more sons and daughters.'),
('1CH', 14, 4, '1CH.14.4', 'These are the names of the children whom he had in Jerusalem: Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon,'),
('1CH', 14, 5, '1CH.14.5', 'Ibhar, Elishua, Elpelet,'),
('1CH', 14, 6, '1CH.14.6', 'Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia,'),
('1CH', 14, 7, '1CH.14.7', 'Elishama, Beeliada, and Eliphelet.'),
('1CH', 14, 8, '1CH.14.8', 'When the Philistines heard that David was anointed king over all Israel, all the Philistines went up to seek David; and David heard of it, and went out against them.'),
('1CH', 14, 9, '1CH.14.9', 'Now the Philistines had come and made a raid in the valley of Rephaim.'),
('1CH', 14, 10, '1CH.14.10', 'David inquired of God, saying, “Shall I go up against the Philistines? Will you deliver them into my hand?” The LORD said to him, “Go up; for I will deliver them into your hand.”'),
('1CH', 14, 11, '1CH.14.11', 'So they came up to Baal Perazim, and David defeated them there. David said, “God has broken my enemies by my hand, like waters breaking out.” Therefore they called the name of that place Baal Perazim.'),
('1CH', 14, 12, '1CH.14.12', 'They left their gods there; and David gave a command, and they were burned with fire.'),
('1CH', 14, 13, '1CH.14.13', 'The Philistines made another raid in the valley.'),
('1CH', 14, 14, '1CH.14.14', 'David inquired again of God; and God said to him, “You shall not go up after them. Turn away from them, and come on them opposite the mulberry trees.'),
('1CH', 14, 15, '1CH.14.15', 'When you hear the sound of marching in the tops of the mulberry trees, then go out to battle; for God has gone out before you to strike the army of the Philistines.”'),
('1CH', 14, 16, '1CH.14.16', 'David did as God commanded him; and they attacked the army of the Philistines from Gibeon even to Gezer.'),
('1CH', 14, 17, '1CH.14.17', 'The fame of David went out into all lands; and the LORD brought the fear of him on all nations.'),
('1CH', 15, 1, '1CH.15.1', 'David made himself houses in David’s city; and he prepared a place for God’s ark, and pitched a tent for it.'),
('1CH', 15, 2, '1CH.15.2', 'Then David said, “No one ought to carry God’s ark but the Levites. For the LORD has chosen them to carry God’s ark, and to minister to him forever.”'),
('1CH', 15, 3, '1CH.15.3', 'David assembled all Israel at Jerusalem, to bring up the LORD’s ark to its place, which he had prepared for it.'),
('1CH', 15, 4, '1CH.15.4', 'David gathered together the sons of Aaron and the Levites:'),
('1CH', 15, 5, '1CH.15.5', 'of the sons of Kohath, Uriel the chief, and his brothers one hundred twenty;'),
('1CH', 15, 6, '1CH.15.6', 'of the sons of Merari, Asaiah the chief, and his brothers two hundred twenty;'),
('1CH', 15, 7, '1CH.15.7', 'of the sons of Gershom, Joel the chief, and his brothers one hundred thirty;'),
('1CH', 15, 8, '1CH.15.8', 'of the sons of Elizaphan, Shemaiah the chief, and his brothers two hundred;'),
('1CH', 15, 9, '1CH.15.9', 'of the sons of Hebron, Eliel the chief, and his brothers eighty;'),
('1CH', 15, 10, '1CH.15.10', 'of the sons of Uzziel, Amminadab the chief, and his brothers one hundred twelve.'),
('1CH', 15, 11, '1CH.15.11', 'David called for Zadok and Abiathar the priests, and for the Levites: for Uriel, Asaiah, Joel, Shemaiah, Eliel, and Amminadab,'),
('1CH', 15, 12, '1CH.15.12', 'and said to them, “You are the heads of the fathers’ households of the Levites. Sanctify yourselves, both you and your brothers, that you may bring the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel, up to the place that I have prepared for it.'),
('1CH', 15, 13, '1CH.15.13', 'For because you didn’t carry it at first, the LORD our God broke out in anger against us, because we didn’t seek him according to the ordinance.”'),
('1CH', 15, 14, '1CH.15.14', 'So the priests and the Levites sanctified themselves to bring up the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('1CH', 15, 15, '1CH.15.15', 'The children of the Levites bore God’s ark on their shoulders with its poles, as Moses commanded according to the LORD’s word.'),
('1CH', 15, 16, '1CH.15.16', 'David spoke to the chief of the Levites to appoint their brothers as singers with instruments of music, stringed instruments, harps, and cymbals, sounding aloud and lifting up their voices with joy.'),
('1CH', 15, 17, '1CH.15.17', 'So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; and of his brothers, Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari their brothers, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;'),
('1CH', 15, 18, '1CH.15.18', 'and with them their brothers of the second rank: Zechariah, Ben, Jaaziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, Obed-Edom, and Jeiel, the doorkeepers.'),
('1CH', 15, 19, '1CH.15.19', 'So the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, were given cymbals of bronze to sound aloud;'),
('1CH', 15, 20, '1CH.15.20', 'and Zechariah, Aziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Maaseiah, and Benaiah, with stringed instruments set to Alamoth;'),
('1CH', 15, 21, '1CH.15.21', 'and Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, Obed-Edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah, with harps tuned to the eight-stringed lyre, to lead.'),
('1CH', 15, 22, '1CH.15.22', 'Chenaniah, chief of the Levites, was over the singing. He taught the singers, because he was skillful.'),
('1CH', 15, 23, '1CH.15.23', 'Berechiah and Elkanah were doorkeepers for the ark.'),
('1CH', 15, 24, '1CH.15.24', 'Shebaniah, Joshaphat, Nethanel, Amasai, Zechariah, Benaiah, and Eliezer, the priests, blew the trumpets before God’s ark; and Obed-Edom and Jehiah were doorkeepers for the ark.'),
('1CH', 15, 25, '1CH.15.25', 'So David, the elders of Israel, and the captains over thousands went to bring the ark of the LORD’s covenant up out of the house of Obed-Edom with joy.'),
('1CH', 15, 26, '1CH.15.26', 'When God helped the Levites who bore the ark of the LORD’s covenant, they sacrificed seven bulls and seven rams.'),
('1CH', 15, 27, '1CH.15.27', 'David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, as were all the Levites who bore the ark, the singers, and Chenaniah the choir master with the singers; and David had an ephod of linen on him.'),
('1CH', 15, 28, '1CH.15.28', 'Thus all Israel brought the ark of the LORD’s covenant up with shouting, with sound of the cornet, with trumpets, and with cymbals, sounding aloud with stringed instruments and harps.'),
('1CH', 15, 29, '1CH.15.29', 'As the ark of the LORD’s covenant came to David’s city, Michal the daughter of Saul looked out at the window, and saw king David dancing and playing; and she despised him in her heart.'),
('1CH', 16, 1, '1CH.16.1', 'They brought in God’s ark, and set it in the middle of the tent that David had pitched for it; and they offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before God.'),
('1CH', 16, 2, '1CH.16.2', 'When David had finished offering the burnt offering and the peace offerings, he blessed the people in the LORD’s name.'),
('1CH', 16, 3, '1CH.16.3', 'He gave to everyone of Israel, both man and woman, to everyone a loaf of bread, a portion of meat, and a cake of raisins.'),
('1CH', 16, 4, '1CH.16.4', 'He appointed some of the Levites to minister before the LORD’s ark, and to commemorate, to thank, and to praise the LORD, the God of Israel:'),
('1CH', 16, 5, '1CH.16.5', 'Asaph the chief, and second to him Zechariah, then Jeiel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Mattithiah, Eliab, Benaiah, Obed-Edom, and Jeiel, with stringed instruments and with harps; and Asaph with cymbals, sounding aloud;'),
('1CH', 16, 6, '1CH.16.6', 'with Benaiah and Jahaziel the priests with trumpets continually, before the ark of the covenant of God.'),
('1CH', 16, 7, '1CH.16.7', 'Then on that day David first ordained giving of thanks to the LORD by the hand of Asaph and his brothers.'),
('1CH', 16, 8, '1CH.16.8', 'Oh give thanks to the LORD. Call on his name. Make what he has done known among the peoples.'),
('1CH', 16, 9, '1CH.16.9', 'Sing to him. Sing praises to him. Tell of all his marvelous works.'),
('1CH', 16, 10, '1CH.16.10', 'Glory in his holy name. Let the heart of those who seek the LORD rejoice.'),
('1CH', 16, 11, '1CH.16.11', 'Seek the LORD and his strength. Seek his face forever more.'),
('1CH', 16, 12, '1CH.16.12', 'Remember his marvelous works that he has done, his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth,'),
('1CH', 16, 13, '1CH.16.13', 'you offspring of Israel his servant, you children of Jacob, his chosen ones.'),
('1CH', 16, 14, '1CH.16.14', 'He is the LORD our God. His judgments are in all the earth.'),
('1CH', 16, 15, '1CH.16.15', 'Remember his covenant forever, the word which he commanded to a thousand generations,'),
('1CH', 16, 16, '1CH.16.16', 'the covenant which he made with Abraham, his oath to Isaac.'),
('1CH', 16, 17, '1CH.16.17', 'He confirmed it to Jacob for a statute, and to Israel for an everlasting covenant,'),
('1CH', 16, 18, '1CH.16.18', 'saying, “I will give you the land of Canaan, The lot of your inheritance,”'),
('1CH', 16, 19, '1CH.16.19', 'when you were but a few men in number, yes, very few, and foreigners in it.'),
('1CH', 16, 20, '1CH.16.20', 'They went about from nation to nation, from one kingdom to another people.'),
('1CH', 16, 21, '1CH.16.21', 'He allowed no man to do them wrong. Yes, he reproved kings for their sakes,'),
('1CH', 16, 22, '1CH.16.22', '“Don’t touch my anointed ones! Do my prophets no harm!”'),
('1CH', 16, 23, '1CH.16.23', 'Sing to the LORD, all the earth! Display his salvation from day to day.'),
('1CH', 16, 24, '1CH.16.24', 'Declare his glory among the nations, and his marvelous works among all the peoples.'),
('1CH', 16, 25, '1CH.16.25', 'For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised. He also is to be feared above all gods.'),
('1CH', 16, 26, '1CH.16.26', 'For all the gods of the peoples are idols, but the LORD made the heavens.'),
('1CH', 16, 27, '1CH.16.27', 'Honor and majesty are before him. Strength and gladness are in his place.'),
('1CH', 16, 28, '1CH.16.28', 'Ascribe to the LORD, you families of the peoples, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength!'),
('1CH', 16, 29, '1CH.16.29', 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his name. Bring an offering, and come before him. Worship the LORD in holy array.'),
('1CH', 16, 30, '1CH.16.30', 'Tremble before him, all the earth. The world also is established that it can’t be moved.'),
('1CH', 16, 31, '1CH.16.31', 'Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice! Let them say among the nations, “The LORD reigns!”'),
('1CH', 16, 32, '1CH.16.32', 'Let the sea roar, and its fullness! Let the field exult, and all that is in it!'),
('1CH', 16, 33, '1CH.16.33', 'Then the trees of the forest will sing for joy before the LORD, for he comes to judge the earth.'),
('1CH', 16, 34, '1CH.16.34', 'Oh give thanks to the LORD, for he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('1CH', 16, 35, '1CH.16.35', 'Say, “Save us, God of our salvation! Gather us together and deliver us from the nations, to give thanks to your holy name, to triumph in your praise.”'),
('1CH', 16, 36, '1CH.16.36', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting even to everlasting. All the people said, “Amen,” and praised the LORD.'),
('1CH', 16, 37, '1CH.16.37', 'So he left Asaph and his brothers there before the ark of the LORD’s covenant, to minister before the ark continually, as every day’s work required;'),
('1CH', 16, 38, '1CH.16.38', 'and Obed-Edom with their sixty-eight relatives; Obed-Edom also the son of Jeduthun and Hosah to be doorkeepers;'),
('1CH', 16, 39, '1CH.16.39', 'and Zadok the priest and his brothers the priests, before the LORD’s tabernacle in the high place that was at Gibeon,'),
('1CH', 16, 40, '1CH.16.40', 'to offer burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of burnt offering continually morning and evening, even according to all that is written in the LORD’s law, which he commanded to Israel;'),
('1CH', 16, 41, '1CH.16.41', 'and with them Heman and Jeduthun and the rest who were chosen, who were mentioned by name, to give thanks to the LORD, because his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('1CH', 16, 42, '1CH.16.42', 'and with them Heman and Jeduthun with trumpets and cymbals for those that should sound aloud, and with instruments for the songs of God, and the sons of Jeduthun to be at the gate.'),
('1CH', 16, 43, '1CH.16.43', 'All the people departed, each man to his house; and David returned to bless his house.'),
('1CH', 17, 1, '1CH.17.1', 'When David was living in his house, David said to Nathan the prophet, “Behold, I live in a cedar house, but the ark of the LORD’s covenant is in a tent.”'),
('1CH', 17, 2, '1CH.17.2', 'Nathan said to David, “Do all that is in your heart; for God is with you.”'),
('1CH', 17, 3, '1CH.17.3', 'That same night, the word of God came to Nathan, saying,'),
('1CH', 17, 4, '1CH.17.4', '“Go and tell David my servant, ‘The LORD says, “You shall not build me a house to dwell in;'),
('1CH', 17, 5, '1CH.17.5', 'for I have not lived in a house since the day that I brought up Israel to this day, but have gone from tent to tent, and from one tent to another.'),
('1CH', 17, 6, '1CH.17.6', 'In all places in which I have walked with all Israel, did I speak a word with any of the judges of Israel, whom I commanded to be shepherd of my people, saying, ‘Why have you not built me a house of cedar?’”’'),
('1CH', 17, 7, '1CH.17.7', '“Now therefore, you shall tell my servant David, ‘The LORD of Armies says, “I took you from the sheep pen, from following the sheep, to be prince over my people Israel.'),
('1CH', 17, 8, '1CH.17.8', 'I have been with you wherever you have gone, and have cut off all your enemies from before you. I will make you a name like the name of the great ones who are on the earth.'),
('1CH', 17, 9, '1CH.17.9', 'I will appoint a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, that they may dwell in their own place, and be moved no more. The children of wickedness will not waste them any more, as at the first,'),
('1CH', 17, 10, '1CH.17.10', 'and from the day that I commanded judges to be over my people Israel. I will subdue all your enemies. Moreover I tell you that the LORD will build you a house.'),
('1CH', 17, 11, '1CH.17.11', 'It will happen, when your days are fulfilled that you must go to be with your fathers, that I will set up your offspring after you, who will be of your sons; and I will establish his kingdom.'),
('1CH', 17, 12, '1CH.17.12', 'He will build me a house, and I will establish his throne forever.'),
('1CH', 17, 13, '1CH.17.13', 'I will be his father, and he will be my son. I will not take my loving kindness away from him, as I took it from him who was before you;'),
('1CH', 17, 14, '1CH.17.14', 'but I will settle him in my house and in my kingdom forever. His throne will be established forever.”’”'),
('1CH', 17, 15, '1CH.17.15', 'According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so Nathan spoke to David.'),
('1CH', 17, 16, '1CH.17.16', 'Then David the king went in and sat before the LORD; and he said, “Who am I, LORD God, and what is my house, that you have brought me this far?'),
('1CH', 17, 17, '1CH.17.17', 'This was a small thing in your eyes, O God, but you have spoken of your servant’s house for a great while to come, and have respected me according to the standard of a man of high degree, LORD God.'),
('1CH', 17, 18, '1CH.17.18', 'What can David say yet more to you concerning the honor which is done to your servant? For you know your servant.'),
('1CH', 17, 19, '1CH.17.19', 'LORD, for your servant’s sake, and according to your own heart, you have done all this greatness, to make known all these great things.'),
('1CH', 17, 20, '1CH.17.20', 'LORD, there is no one like you, neither is there any God besides you, according to all that we have heard with our ears.'),
('1CH', 17, 21, '1CH.17.21', 'What one nation on the earth is like your people Israel, whom God went to redeem to himself for a people, to make you a name by great and awesome things, in driving out nations from before your people whom you redeemed out of Egypt?'),
('1CH', 17, 22, '1CH.17.22', 'For you made your people Israel your own people forever; and you, LORD, became their God.'),
('1CH', 17, 23, '1CH.17.23', 'Now, LORD, let the word that you have spoken concerning your servant, and concerning his house, be established forever, and do as you have spoken.'),
('1CH', 17, 24, '1CH.17.24', 'Let your name be established and magnified forever, saying, ‘The LORD of Armies is the God of Israel, even a God to Israel. The house of David your servant is established before you.’'),
('1CH', 17, 25, '1CH.17.25', 'For you, my God, have revealed to your servant that you will build him a house. Therefore your servant has found courage to pray before you.'),
('1CH', 17, 26, '1CH.17.26', 'Now, LORD, you are God, and have promised this good thing to your servant.'),
('1CH', 17, 27, '1CH.17.27', 'Now it has pleased you to bless the house of your servant, that it may continue forever before you; for you, LORD, have blessed, and it is blessed forever.”'),
('1CH', 18, 1, '1CH.18.1', 'After this, David defeated the Philistines and subdued them, and took Gath and its towns out of the hand of the Philistines.'),
('1CH', 18, 2, '1CH.18.2', 'He defeated Moab; and the Moabites became servants to David and brought tribute.'),
('1CH', 18, 3, '1CH.18.3', 'David defeated Hadadezer king of Zobah, toward Hamath, as he went to establish his dominion by the river Euphrates.'),
('1CH', 18, 4, '1CH.18.4', 'David took from him one thousand chariots, seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen; and David hamstrung all the chariot horses, but reserved of them enough for one hundred chariots.'),
('1CH', 18, 5, '1CH.18.5', 'When the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadadezer king of Zobah, David struck twenty-two thousand men of the Syrians.'),
('1CH', 18, 6, '1CH.18.6', 'Then David put garrisons in Syria of Damascus; and the Syrians became servants to David and brought tribute. The LORD gave victory to David wherever he went.'),
('1CH', 18, 7, '1CH.18.7', 'David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 18, 8, '1CH.18.8', 'From Tibhath and from Cun, cities of Hadadezer, David took very much bronze, with which Solomon made the bronze sea, the pillars, and the vessels of bronze.'),
('1CH', 18, 9, '1CH.18.9', 'When Tou king of Hamath heard that David had struck all the army of Hadadezer king of Zobah,'),
('1CH', 18, 10, '1CH.18.10', 'he sent Hadoram his son to King David to greet him and to bless him, because he had fought against Hadadezer and struck him (for Hadadezer had wars with Tou); and he had with him all kinds of vessels of gold and silver and bronze.'),
('1CH', 18, 11, '1CH.18.11', 'King David also dedicated these to the LORD, with the silver and the gold that he carried away from all the nations: from Edom, from Moab, from the children of Ammon, from the Philistines, and from Amalek.'),
('1CH', 18, 12, '1CH.18.12', 'Moreover Abishai the son of Zeruiah struck eighteen thousand of the Edomites in the Valley of Salt.'),
('1CH', 18, 13, '1CH.18.13', 'He put garrisons in Edom; and all the Edomites became servants to David. The LORD gave victory to David wherever he went.'),
('1CH', 18, 14, '1CH.18.14', 'David reigned over all Israel; and he executed justice and righteousness for all his people.'),
('1CH', 18, 15, '1CH.18.15', 'Joab the son of Zeruiah was over the army; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud was recorder;'),
('1CH', 18, 16, '1CH.18.16', 'Zadok the son of Ahitub and Abimelech the son of Abiathar were priests; Shavsha was scribe;'),
('1CH', 18, 17, '1CH.18.17', 'and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and the sons of David were chief officials serving the king.'),
('1CH', 19, 1, '1CH.19.1', 'After this, Nahash the king of the children of Ammon died, and his son reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 19, 2, '1CH.19.2', 'David said, “I will show kindness to Hanun the son of Nahash, because his father showed kindness to me.” So David sent messengers to comfort him concerning his father. David’s servants came into the land of the children of Ammon to Hanun to comfort him.'),
('1CH', 19, 3, '1CH.19.3', 'But the princes of the children of Ammon said to Hanun, “Do you think that David honors your father, in that he has sent comforters to you? Haven’t his servants come to you to search, to overthrow, and to spy out the land?”'),
('1CH', 19, 4, '1CH.19.4', 'So Hanun took David’s servants, shaved them, and cut off their garments in the middle at their buttocks, and sent them away.'),
('1CH', 19, 5, '1CH.19.5', 'Then some people went and told David how the men were treated. He sent to meet them; for the men were greatly humiliated. The king said, “Stay at Jericho until your beards have grown, and then return.”'),
('1CH', 19, 6, '1CH.19.6', 'When the children of Ammon saw that they had made themselves odious to David, Hanun and the children of Ammon sent one thousand talents of silver to hire chariots and horsemen out of Mesopotamia, out of Aram-maacah, and out of Zobah.'),
('1CH', 19, 7, '1CH.19.7', 'So they hired for themselves thirty-two thousand chariots, and the king of Maacah with his people, who came and encamped near Medeba. The children of Ammon gathered themselves together from their cities, and came to battle.'),
('1CH', 19, 8, '1CH.19.8', 'When David heard of it, he sent Joab with all the army of the mighty men.'),
('1CH', 19, 9, '1CH.19.9', 'The children of Ammon came out, and put the battle in array at the gate of the city; and the kings who had come were by themselves in the field.'),
('1CH', 19, 10, '1CH.19.10', 'Now when Joab saw that the battle was set against him before and behind, he chose some of all the choice men of Israel, and put them in array against the Syrians.'),
('1CH', 19, 11, '1CH.19.11', 'The rest of the people he committed into the hand of Abishai his brother; and they put themselves in array against the children of Ammon.'),
('1CH', 19, 12, '1CH.19.12', 'He said, “If the Syrians are too strong for me, then you are to help me; but if the children of Ammon are too strong for you, then I will help you.'),
('1CH', 19, 13, '1CH.19.13', 'Be courageous, and let’s be strong for our people and for the cities of our God. May the LORD do that which seems good to him.”'),
('1CH', 19, 14, '1CH.19.14', 'So Joab and the people who were with him came near to the front of the Syrians to the battle; and they fled before him.'),
('1CH', 19, 15, '1CH.19.15', 'When the children of Ammon saw that the Syrians had fled, they likewise fled before Abishai his brother, and entered into the city. Then Joab came to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 19, 16, '1CH.19.16', 'When the Syrians saw that they were defeated by Israel, they sent messengers and called out the Syrians who were beyond the River, with Shophach the captain of the army of Hadadezer leading them.'),
('1CH', 19, 17, '1CH.19.17', 'David was told that, so he gathered all Israel together, passed over the Jordan, came to them, and set the battle in array against them. So when David had put the battle in array against the Syrians, they fought with him.'),
('1CH', 19, 18, '1CH.19.18', 'The Syrians fled before Israel; and David killed of the Syrian men seven thousand charioteers and forty thousand footmen, and also killed Shophach the captain of the army.'),
('1CH', 19, 19, '1CH.19.19', 'When the servants of Hadadezer saw that they were defeated by Israel, they made peace with David and served him. The Syrians would not help the children of Ammon any more.'),
('1CH', 20, 1, '1CH.20.1', 'At the time of the return of the year, at the time when kings go out, Joab led out the army and wasted the country of the children of Ammon, and came and besieged Rabbah. But David stayed at Jerusalem. Joab struck Rabbah, and overthrew it.'),
('1CH', 20, 2, '1CH.20.2', 'David took the crown of their king from off his head, and found it to weigh a talent of gold, and there were precious stones in it. It was set on David’s head, and he brought very much plunder out of the city.'),
('1CH', 20, 3, '1CH.20.3', 'He brought out the people who were in it, and had them cut with saws, with iron picks, and with axes. David did so to all the cities of the children of Ammon. Then David and all the people returned to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 20, 4, '1CH.20.4', 'After this, war arose at Gezer with the Philistines. Then Sibbecai the Hushathite killed Sippai, of the sons of the giant; and they were subdued.'),
('1CH', 20, 5, '1CH.20.5', 'Again there was war with the Philistines; and Elhanan the son of Jair killed Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the staff of whose spear was like a weaver’s beam.'),
('1CH', 20, 6, '1CH.20.6', 'There was again war at Gath, where there was a man of great stature, who had twenty-four fingers and toes, six on each hand and six on each foot; and he also was born to the giant.'),
('1CH', 20, 7, '1CH.20.7', 'When he defied Israel, Jonathan the son of Shimea, David’s brother, killed him.'),
('1CH', 20, 8, '1CH.20.8', 'These were born to the giant in Gath; and they fell by the hand of David and by the hand of his servants.'),
('1CH', 21, 1, '1CH.21.1', 'Satan stood up against Israel, and moved David to take a census of Israel.'),
('1CH', 21, 2, '1CH.21.2', 'David said to Joab and to the princes of the people, “Go, count Israel from Beersheba even to Dan; and bring me word, that I may know how many there are.”'),
('1CH', 21, 3, '1CH.21.3', 'Joab said, “May the LORD make his people a hundred times as many as they are. But, my lord the king, aren’t they all my lord’s servants? Why does my lord require this thing? Why will he be a cause of guilt to Israel?”'),
('1CH', 21, 4, '1CH.21.4', 'Nevertheless the king’s word prevailed against Joab. Therefore Joab departed and went throughout all Israel, then came to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 21, 5, '1CH.21.5', 'Joab gave the sum of the census of the people to David. All those of Israel were one million one hundred thousand men who drew a sword; and in Judah were four hundred seventy thousand men who drew a sword.'),
('1CH', 21, 6, '1CH.21.6', 'But he didn’t count Levi and Benjamin among them, for the king’s word was abominable to Joab.'),
('1CH', 21, 7, '1CH.21.7', 'God was displeased with this thing; therefore he struck Israel.'),
('1CH', 21, 8, '1CH.21.8', 'David said to God, “I have sinned greatly, in that I have done this thing. But now put away, I beg you, the iniquity of your servant, for I have done very foolishly.”'),
('1CH', 21, 9, '1CH.21.9', 'The LORD spoke to Gad, David’s seer, saying,'),
('1CH', 21, 10, '1CH.21.10', '“Go and speak to David, saying, ‘The LORD says, “I offer you three things. Choose one of them, that I may do it to you.”’”'),
('1CH', 21, 11, '1CH.21.11', 'So Gad came to David and said to him, “The LORD says, ‘Take your choice:'),
('1CH', 21, 12, '1CH.21.12', 'either three years of famine; or three months to be consumed before your foes, while the sword of your enemies overtakes you; or else three days of the sword of the LORD, even pestilence in the land, and the LORD’s angel destroying throughout all the borders of Israel. Now therefore consider what answer I shall return to him who sent me.’”'),
('1CH', 21, 13, '1CH.21.13', 'David said to Gad, “I am in distress. Let me fall, I pray, into the LORD’s hand, for his mercies are very great. Don’t let me fall into man’s hand.”'),
('1CH', 21, 14, '1CH.21.14', 'So the LORD sent a pestilence on Israel, and seventy thousand men of Israel fell.'),
('1CH', 21, 15, '1CH.21.15', 'God sent an angel to Jerusalem to destroy it. As he was about to destroy, the LORD saw, and he relented of the disaster, and said to the destroying angel, “It is enough. Now withdraw your hand.” the LORD’s angel was standing by the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
('1CH', 21, 16, '1CH.21.16', 'David lifted up his eyes, and saw the LORD’s angel standing between earth and the sky, having a drawn sword in his hand stretched out over Jerusalem. Then David and the elders, clothed in sackcloth, fell on their faces.'),
('1CH', 21, 17, '1CH.21.17', 'David said to God, “Isn’t it I who commanded the people to be counted? It is even I who have sinned and done very wickedly; but these sheep, what have they done? Please let your hand, O LORD my God, be against me and against my father’s house; but not against your people, that they should be plagued.”'),
('1CH', 21, 18, '1CH.21.18', 'Then the LORD’s angel commanded Gad to tell David that David should go up and raise an altar to the LORD on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
('1CH', 21, 19, '1CH.21.19', 'David went up at the saying of Gad, which he spoke in the LORD’s name.'),
('1CH', 21, 20, '1CH.21.20', 'Ornan turned back and saw the angel; and his four sons who were with him hid themselves. Now Ornan was threshing wheat.'),
('1CH', 21, 21, '1CH.21.21', 'As David came to Ornan, Ornan looked and saw David, and went out of the threshing floor, and bowed himself to David with his face to the ground.'),
('1CH', 21, 22, '1CH.21.22', 'Then David said to Ornan, “Sell me the place of this threshing floor, that I may build an altar to the LORD on it. You shall sell it to me for the full price, that the plague may be stopped from afflicting the people.”'),
('1CH', 21, 23, '1CH.21.23', 'Ornan said to David, “Take it for yourself, and let my lord the king do that which is good in his eyes. Behold, I give the oxen for burnt offerings, and the threshing instruments for wood, and the wheat for the meal offering. I give it all.”'),
('1CH', 21, 24, '1CH.21.24', 'King David said to Ornan, “No, but I will most certainly buy it for the full price. For I will not take that which is yours for the LORD, nor offer a burnt offering that costs me nothing.”'),
('1CH', 21, 25, '1CH.21.25', 'So David gave to Ornan six hundred shekels of gold by weight for the place.'),
('1CH', 21, 26, '1CH.21.26', 'David built an altar to the LORD there, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings, and called on the LORD; and he answered him from the sky by fire on the altar of burnt offering.'),
('1CH', 21, 27, '1CH.21.27', 'Then the LORD commanded the angel, and he put his sword back into its sheath.'),
('1CH', 21, 28, '1CH.21.28', 'At that time, when David saw that the LORD had answered him in the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite, then he sacrificed there.'),
('1CH', 21, 29, '1CH.21.29', 'For the LORD’s tabernacle, which Moses made in the wilderness, and the altar of burnt offering, were at that time in the high place at Gibeon.'),
('1CH', 21, 30, '1CH.21.30', 'But David couldn’t go before it to inquire of God, for he was afraid because of the sword of the LORD’s angel.'),
('1CH', 22, 1, '1CH.22.1', 'Then David said, “This is the house of the LORD God, and this is the altar of burnt offering for Israel.”'),
('1CH', 22, 2, '1CH.22.2', 'David gave orders to gather together the foreigners who were in the land of Israel; and he set masons to cut dressed stones to build God’s house.'),
('1CH', 22, 3, '1CH.22.3', 'David prepared iron in abundance for the nails for the doors of the gates and for the couplings, and bronze in abundance without weight,'),
('1CH', 22, 4, '1CH.22.4', 'and cedar trees without number, for the Sidonians and the people of Tyre brought cedar trees in abundance to David.'),
('1CH', 22, 5, '1CH.22.5', 'David said, “Solomon my son is young and tender, and the house that is to be built for the LORD must be exceedingly magnificent, of fame and of glory throughout all countries. I will therefore make preparation for it.” So David prepared abundantly before his death.'),
('1CH', 22, 6, '1CH.22.6', 'Then he called for Solomon his son, and commanded him to build a house for the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('1CH', 22, 7, '1CH.22.7', 'David said to Solomon his son, “As for me, it was in my heart to build a house to the name of the LORD my God.'),
('1CH', 22, 8, '1CH.22.8', 'But the LORD’s word came to me, saying, ‘You have shed blood abundantly and have made great wars. You shall not build a house to my name, because you have shed much blood on the earth in my sight.'),
('1CH', 22, 9, '1CH.22.9', 'Behold, a son shall be born to you, who shall be a man of peace. I will give him rest from all his enemies all around; for his name shall be Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness to Israel in his days.'),
('1CH', 22, 10, '1CH.22.10', 'He shall build a house for my name; and he will be my son, and I will be his father; and I will establish the throne of his kingdom over Israel forever.’'),
('1CH', 22, 11, '1CH.22.11', 'Now, my son, may the LORD be with you and prosper you, and build the house of the LORD your God, as he has spoken concerning you.'),
('1CH', 22, 12, '1CH.22.12', 'May the LORD give you discretion and understanding, and put you in charge of Israel, so that you may keep the law of the LORD your God.'),
('1CH', 22, 13, '1CH.22.13', 'Then you will prosper, if you observe to do the statutes and the ordinances which the LORD gave Moses concerning Israel. Be strong and courageous. Don’t be afraid and don’t be dismayed.'),
('1CH', 22, 14, '1CH.22.14', 'Now, behold, in my affliction I have prepared for the LORD’s house one hundred thousand talents of gold, one million talents of silver, and bronze and iron without weight; for it is in abundance. I have also prepared timber and stone; and you may add to them.'),
('1CH', 22, 15, '1CH.22.15', 'There are also workmen with you in abundance—cutters and workers of stone and timber, and all kinds of men who are skillful in every kind of work;'),
('1CH', 22, 16, '1CH.22.16', 'of the gold, the silver, the bronze, and the iron, there is no number. Arise and be doing, and may the LORD be with you.”'),
('1CH', 22, 17, '1CH.22.17', 'David also commanded all the princes of Israel to help Solomon his son, saying,'),
('1CH', 22, 18, '1CH.22.18', '“Isn’t the LORD your God with you? Hasn’t he given you rest on every side? For he has delivered the inhabitants of the land into my hand; and the land is subdued before the LORD and before his people.'),
('1CH', 22, 19, '1CH.22.19', 'Now set your heart and your soul to follow the LORD your God. Arise therefore, and build the sanctuary of the LORD God, to bring the ark of the LORD’s covenant and the holy vessels of God into the house that is to be built for the LORD’s name.”'),
('1CH', 23, 1, '1CH.23.1', 'Now David was old and full of days; and he made Solomon his son king over Israel.'),
('1CH', 23, 2, '1CH.23.2', 'He gathered together all the princes of Israel, with the priests and the Levites.'),
('1CH', 23, 3, '1CH.23.3', 'The Levites were counted from thirty years old and upward; and their number by their polls, man by man, was thirty-eight thousand.'),
('1CH', 23, 4, '1CH.23.4', 'David said, “Of these, twenty-four thousand were to oversee the work of the LORD’s house, six thousand were officers and judges,'),
('1CH', 23, 5, '1CH.23.5', 'four thousand were doorkeepers, and four thousand praised the LORD with the instruments which I made for giving praise.”'),
('1CH', 23, 6, '1CH.23.6', 'David divided them into divisions according to the sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.'),
('1CH', 23, 7, '1CH.23.7', 'Of the Gershonites: Ladan and Shimei.'),
('1CH', 23, 8, '1CH.23.8', 'The sons of Ladan: Jehiel the chief, Zetham, and Joel, three.'),
('1CH', 23, 9, '1CH.23.9', 'The sons of Shimei: Shelomoth, Haziel, and Haran, three. These were the heads of the fathers’ households of Ladan.'),
('1CH', 23, 10, '1CH.23.10', 'The sons of Shimei: Jahath, Zina, Jeush, and Beriah. These four were the sons of Shimei.'),
('1CH', 23, 11, '1CH.23.11', 'Jahath was the chief, and Zizah the second; but Jeush and Beriah didn’t have many sons; therefore they became a fathers’ house in one reckoning.'),
('1CH', 23, 12, '1CH.23.12', 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel, four.'),
('1CH', 23, 13, '1CH.23.13', 'The sons of Amram: Aaron and Moses; and Aaron was separated that he should sanctify the most holy things, he and his sons forever, to burn incense before the LORD, to minister to him, and to bless in his name forever.'),
('1CH', 23, 14, '1CH.23.14', 'But as for Moses the man of God, his sons were named among the tribe of Levi.'),
('1CH', 23, 15, '1CH.23.15', 'The sons of Moses: Gershom and Eliezer.'),
('1CH', 23, 16, '1CH.23.16', 'The sons of Gershom: Shebuel the chief.'),
('1CH', 23, 17, '1CH.23.17', 'The son of Eliezer was Rehabiah the chief; and Eliezer had no other sons, but the sons of Rehabiah were very many.'),
('1CH', 23, 18, '1CH.23.18', 'The son of Izhar: Shelomith the chief.'),
('1CH', 23, 19, '1CH.23.19', 'The sons of Hebron: Jeriah the chief, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth.'),
('1CH', 23, 20, '1CH.23.20', 'The sons of Uzziel: Micah the chief, and Isshiah the second.'),
('1CH', 23, 21, '1CH.23.21', 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The sons of Mahli: Eleazar and Kish.'),
('1CH', 23, 22, '1CH.23.22', 'Eleazar died, and had no sons, but daughters only; and their relatives, the sons of Kish, took them as wives.'),
('1CH', 23, 23, '1CH.23.23', 'The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jeremoth, three.'),
('1CH', 23, 24, '1CH.23.24', 'These were the sons of Levi after their fathers’ houses, even the heads of the fathers’ houses of those who were counted individually, in the number of names by their polls, who did the work for the service of the LORD’s house, from twenty years old and upward.'),
('1CH', 23, 25, '1CH.23.25', 'For David said, “The LORD, the God of Israel, has given rest to his people; and he dwells in Jerusalem forever.'),
('1CH', 23, 26, '1CH.23.26', 'Also the Levites will no longer need to carry the tabernacle and all its vessels for its service.”'),
('1CH', 23, 27, '1CH.23.27', 'For by the last words of David the sons of Levi were counted, from twenty years old and upward.'),
('1CH', 23, 28, '1CH.23.28', 'For their duty was to wait on the sons of Aaron for the service of the LORD’s house—in the courts, in the rooms, and in the purifying of all holy things, even the work of the service of God’s house;'),
('1CH', 23, 29, '1CH.23.29', 'for the show bread also, and for the fine flour for a meal offering, whether of unleavened wafers, or of that which is baked in the pan, or of that which is soaked, and for all measurements of quantity and size;'),
('1CH', 23, 30, '1CH.23.30', 'and to stand every morning to thank and praise the LORD, and likewise in the evening;'),
('1CH', 23, 31, '1CH.23.31', 'and to offer all burnt offerings to the LORD on the Sabbaths, on the new moons, and on the set feasts, in number according to the ordinance concerning them, continually before the LORD;'),
('1CH', 23, 32, '1CH.23.32', 'and that they should keep the duty of the Tent of Meeting, the duty of the holy place, and the duty of the sons of Aaron their brothers for the service of the LORD’s house.'),
('1CH', 24, 1, '1CH.24.1', 'These were the divisions of the sons of Aaron. The sons of Aaron: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 24, 2, '1CH.24.2', 'But Nadab and Abihu died before their father, and had no children; therefore Eleazar and Ithamar served as priests.'),
('1CH', 24, 3, '1CH.24.3', 'David, with Zadok of the sons of Eleazar and Ahimelech of the sons of Ithamar, divided them according to their ordering in their service.'),
('1CH', 24, 4, '1CH.24.4', 'There were more chief men found of the sons of Eleazar than of the sons of Ithamar; and they were divided like this: of the sons of Eleazar there were sixteen, heads of fathers’ houses; and of the sons of Ithamar, according to their fathers’ houses, eight.'),
('1CH', 24, 5, '1CH.24.5', 'Thus they were divided impartially by drawing lots; for there were princes of the sanctuary and princes of God, both of the sons of Eleazar, and of the sons of Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 24, 6, '1CH.24.6', 'Shemaiah the son of Nethanel the scribe, who was of the Levites, wrote them in the presence of the king, the princes, Zadok the priest, Ahimelech the son of Abiathar, and the heads of the fathers’ households of the priests and of the Levites; one fathers’ house being taken for Eleazar, and one taken for Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 24, 7, '1CH.24.7', 'Now the first lot came out to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah,'),
('1CH', 24, 8, '1CH.24.8', 'the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,'),
('1CH', 24, 9, '1CH.24.9', 'the fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin,'),
('1CH', 24, 10, '1CH.24.10', 'the seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah,'),
('1CH', 24, 11, '1CH.24.11', 'the ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shecaniah,'),
('1CH', 24, 12, '1CH.24.12', 'the eleventh to Eliashib, the twelfth to Jakim,'),
('1CH', 24, 13, '1CH.24.13', 'the thirteenth to Huppah, the fourteenth to Jeshebeab,'),
('1CH', 24, 14, '1CH.24.14', 'the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,'),
('1CH', 24, 15, '1CH.24.15', 'the seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Happizzez,'),
('1CH', 24, 16, '1CH.24.16', 'the nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentieth to Jehezkel,'),
('1CH', 24, 17, '1CH.24.17', 'the twenty-first to Jachin, the twenty-second to Gamul,'),
('1CH', 24, 18, '1CH.24.18', 'the twenty-third to Delaiah, and the twenty-fourth to Maaziah.'),
('1CH', 24, 19, '1CH.24.19', 'This was their ordering in their service, to come into the LORD’s house according to the ordinance given to them by Aaron their father, as the LORD, the God of Israel, had commanded him.'),
('1CH', 24, 20, '1CH.24.20', 'Of the rest of the sons of Levi: of the sons of Amram, Shubael; of the sons of Shubael, Jehdeiah.'),
('1CH', 24, 21, '1CH.24.21', 'Of Rehabiah: of the sons of Rehabiah, Isshiah the chief.'),
('1CH', 24, 22, '1CH.24.22', 'Of the Izharites, Shelomoth; of the sons of Shelomoth, Jahath.'),
('1CH', 24, 23, '1CH.24.23', 'The sons of Hebron: Jeriah, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth.'),
('1CH', 24, 24, '1CH.24.24', 'The sons of Uzziel: Micah; of the sons of Micah, Shamir.'),
('1CH', 24, 25, '1CH.24.25', 'The brother of Micah: Isshiah; of the sons of Isshiah, Zechariah.'),
('1CH', 24, 26, '1CH.24.26', 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The son of Jaaziah: Beno.'),
('1CH', 24, 27, '1CH.24.27', 'The sons of Merari by Jaaziah: Beno, Shoham, Zaccur, and Ibri.'),
('1CH', 24, 28, '1CH.24.28', 'Of Mahli: Eleazar, who had no sons.'),
('1CH', 24, 29, '1CH.24.29', 'Of Kish, the son of Kish: Jerahmeel.'),
('1CH', 24, 30, '1CH.24.30', 'The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of the Levites after their fathers’ houses.'),
('1CH', 24, 31, '1CH.24.31', 'These likewise cast lots even as their brothers the sons of Aaron in the presence of David the king, Zadok, Ahimelech, and the heads of the fathers’ households of the priests and of the Levites, the fathers’ households of the chief even as those of his younger brother.'),
('1CH', 25, 1, '1CH.25.1', 'Moreover, David and the captains of the army set apart for the service certain of the sons of Asaph, of Heman, and of Jeduthun, who were to prophesy with harps, with stringed instruments, and with cymbals. The number of those who did the work according to their service was:'),
('1CH', 25, 2, '1CH.25.2', 'of the sons of Asaph: Zaccur, Joseph, Nethaniah, and Asharelah. The sons of Asaph were under the hand of Asaph, who prophesied at the order of the king.'),
('1CH', 25, 3, '1CH.25.3', 'Of Jeduthun, the sons of Jeduthun: Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Shimei, Hashabiah, and Mattithiah, six, under the hands of their father Jeduthun, who prophesied in giving thanks and praising the LORD with the harp.'),
('1CH', 25, 4, '1CH.25.4', 'Of Heman, the sons of Heman: Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, Romamti-Ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, and Mahazioth.'),
('1CH', 25, 5, '1CH.25.5', 'All these were the sons of Heman the king’s seer in the words of God, to lift up the horn. God gave to Heman fourteen sons and three daughters.'),
('1CH', 25, 6, '1CH.25.6', 'All these were under the hands of their father for song in the LORD’s house, with cymbals, stringed instruments, and harps, for the service of God’s house: Asaph, Jeduthun, and Heman being under the order of the king.'),
('1CH', 25, 7, '1CH.25.7', 'The number of them, with their brothers who were instructed in singing to the LORD, even all who were skillful, was two hundred eighty-eight.'),
('1CH', 25, 8, '1CH.25.8', 'They cast lots for their offices, all alike, the small as well as the great, the teacher as well as the student.'),
('1CH', 25, 9, '1CH.25.9', 'Now the first lot came out for Asaph to Joseph; the second to Gedaliah, he and his brothers and sons were twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 10, '1CH.25.10', 'the third to Zaccur, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 11, '1CH.25.11', 'the fourth to Izri, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 12, '1CH.25.12', 'the fifth to Nethaniah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 13, '1CH.25.13', 'the sixth to Bukkiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 14, '1CH.25.14', 'the seventh to Jesharelah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 15, '1CH.25.15', 'the eighth to Jeshaiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 16, '1CH.25.16', 'the ninth to Mattaniah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 17, '1CH.25.17', 'the tenth to Shimei, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 18, '1CH.25.18', 'the eleventh to Azarel, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 19, '1CH.25.19', 'the twelfth to Hashabiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 20, '1CH.25.20', 'for the thirteenth, Shubael, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 21, '1CH.25.21', 'for the fourteenth, Mattithiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 22, '1CH.25.22', 'for the fifteenth to Jeremoth, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 23, '1CH.25.23', 'for the sixteenth to Hananiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 24, '1CH.25.24', 'for the seventeenth to Joshbekashah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 25, '1CH.25.25', 'for the eighteenth to Hanani, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 26, '1CH.25.26', 'for the nineteenth to Mallothi, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 27, '1CH.25.27', 'for the twentieth to Eliathah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 28, '1CH.25.28', 'for the twenty-first to Hothir, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 29, '1CH.25.29', 'for the twenty-second to Giddalti, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 30, '1CH.25.30', 'for the twenty-third to Mahazioth, his sons and his brothers, twelve;'),
('1CH', 25, 31, '1CH.25.31', 'for the twenty-fourth to Romamti-Ezer, his sons and his brothers, twelve.'),
('1CH', 26, 1, '1CH.26.1', 'For the divisions of the doorkeepers: of the Korahites, Meshelemiah the son of Kore, of the sons of Asaph.'),
('1CH', 26, 2, '1CH.26.2', 'Meshelemiah had sons: Zechariah the firstborn, Jediael the second, Zebadiah the third, Jathniel the fourth,'),
('1CH', 26, 3, '1CH.26.3', 'Elam the fifth, Jehohanan the sixth, and Eliehoenai the seventh.'),
('1CH', 26, 4, '1CH.26.4', 'Obed-Edom had sons: Shemaiah the firstborn, Jehozabad the second, Joah the third, Sacar the fourth, Nethanel the fifth,'),
('1CH', 26, 5, '1CH.26.5', 'Ammiel the sixth, Issachar the seventh, and Peullethai the eighth; for God blessed him.'),
('1CH', 26, 6, '1CH.26.6', 'Sons were also born to Shemaiah his son, who ruled over the house of their father; for they were mighty men of valor.'),
('1CH', 26, 7, '1CH.26.7', 'The sons of Shemaiah: Othni, Rephael, Obed, and Elzabad, whose relatives were valiant men, Elihu, and Semachiah.'),
('1CH', 26, 8, '1CH.26.8', 'All these were of the sons of Obed-Edom with their sons and their brothers, able men in strength for the service: sixty-two of Obed-Edom.'),
('1CH', 26, 9, '1CH.26.9', 'Meshelemiah had sons and brothers, eighteen valiant men.'),
('1CH', 26, 10, '1CH.26.10', 'Also Hosah, of the children of Merari, had sons: Shimri the chief (for though he was not the firstborn, yet his father made him chief),'),
('1CH', 26, 11, '1CH.26.11', 'Hilkiah the second, Tebaliah the third, and Zechariah the fourth. All the sons and brothers of Hosah were thirteen.'),
('1CH', 26, 12, '1CH.26.12', 'Of these were the divisions of the doorkeepers, even of the chief men, having offices like their brothers, to minister in the LORD’s house.'),
('1CH', 26, 13, '1CH.26.13', 'They cast lots, the small as well as the great, according to their fathers’ houses, for every gate.'),
('1CH', 26, 14, '1CH.26.14', 'The lot eastward fell to Shelemiah. Then for Zechariah his son, a wise counselor, they cast lots; and his lot came out northward.'),
('1CH', 26, 15, '1CH.26.15', 'To Obed-Edom southward; and to his sons the storehouse.'),
('1CH', 26, 16, '1CH.26.16', 'To Shuppim and Hosah westward, by the gate of Shallecheth, at the causeway that goes up, watchman opposite watchman.'),
('1CH', 26, 17, '1CH.26.17', 'Eastward were six Levites, northward four a day, southward four a day, and for the storehouse two and two.'),
('1CH', 26, 18, '1CH.26.18', 'For Parbar westward, four at the causeway, and two at Parbar.'),
('1CH', 26, 19, '1CH.26.19', 'These were the divisions of the doorkeepers; of the sons of the Korahites, and of the sons of Merari.'),
('1CH', 26, 20, '1CH.26.20', 'Of the Levites, Ahijah was over the treasures of God’s house and over the treasures of the dedicated things.'),
('1CH', 26, 21, '1CH.26.21', 'The sons of Ladan, the sons of the Gershonites belonging to Ladan, the heads of the fathers’ households belonging to Ladan the Gershonite: Jehieli.'),
('1CH', 26, 22, '1CH.26.22', 'The sons of Jehieli: Zetham, and Joel his brother, over the treasures of the LORD’s house.'),
('1CH', 26, 23, '1CH.26.23', 'Of the Amramites, of the Izharites, of the Hebronites, of the Uzzielites:'),
('1CH', 26, 24, '1CH.26.24', 'Shebuel the son of Gershom, the son of Moses, was ruler over the treasuries.'),
('1CH', 26, 25, '1CH.26.25', 'His brothers: of Eliezer, Rehabiah his son, and Jeshaiah his son, and Joram his son, and Zichri his son, and Shelomoth his son.'),
('1CH', 26, 26, '1CH.26.26', 'This Shelomoth and his brothers were over all the treasuries of the dedicated things, which David the king, and the heads of the fathers’ households, the captains over thousands and hundreds, and the captains of the army, had dedicated.'),
('1CH', 26, 27, '1CH.26.27', 'They dedicated some of the plunder won in battles to repair the LORD’s house.'),
('1CH', 26, 28, '1CH.26.28', 'All that Samuel the seer, Saul the son of Kish, Abner the son of Ner, and Joab the son of Zeruiah had dedicated, whoever had dedicated anything, it was under the hand of Shelomoth and of his brothers.'),
('1CH', 26, 29, '1CH.26.29', 'Of the Izharites, Chenaniah and his sons were appointed to the outward business over Israel, for officers and judges.'),
('1CH', 26, 30, '1CH.26.30', 'Of the Hebronites, Hashabiah and his brothers, one thousand seven hundred men of valor, had the oversight of Israel beyond the Jordan westward, for all the business of the LORD and for the service of the king.'),
('1CH', 26, 31, '1CH.26.31', 'Of the Hebronites, Jerijah was the chief of the Hebronites, according to their generations by fathers’ households. They were sought for in the fortieth year of the reign of David, and mighty men of valor were found among them at Jazer of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 26, 32, '1CH.26.32', 'His relatives, men of valor, were two thousand seven hundred, heads of fathers’ households, whom King David made overseers over the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of the Manassites, for every matter pertaining to God and for the affairs of the king.'),
('1CH', 27, 1, '1CH.27.1', 'Now the children of Israel after their number, the heads of fathers’ households and the captains of thousands and of hundreds, and their officers who served the king in any matter of the divisions which came in and went out month by month throughout all the months of the year—of every division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 2, '1CH.27.2', 'Over the first division for the first month was Jashobeam the son of Zabdiel. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 3, '1CH.27.3', 'He was of the children of Perez, the chief of all the captains of the army for the first month.'),
('1CH', 27, 4, '1CH.27.4', 'Over the division of the second month was Dodai the Ahohite and his division, and Mikloth the ruler; and in his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 5, '1CH.27.5', 'The third captain of the army for the third month was Benaiah, the son of Jehoiada the chief priest. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 6, '1CH.27.6', 'This is that Benaiah who was the mighty man of the thirty and over the thirty. Of his division was Ammizabad his son.'),
('1CH', 27, 7, '1CH.27.7', 'The fourth captain for the fourth month was Asahel the brother of Joab, and Zebadiah his son after him. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 8, '1CH.27.8', 'The fifth captain for the fifth month was Shamhuth the Izrahite. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 9, '1CH.27.9', 'The sixth captain for the sixth month was Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 10, '1CH.27.10', 'The seventh captain for the seventh month was Helez the Pelonite, of the children of Ephraim. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 11, '1CH.27.11', 'The eighth captain for the eighth month was Sibbecai the Hushathite, of the Zerahites. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 12, '1CH.27.12', 'The ninth captain for the ninth month was Abiezer the Anathothite, of the Benjamites. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 13, '1CH.27.13', 'The tenth captain for the tenth month was Maharai the Netophathite, of the Zerahites. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 14, '1CH.27.14', 'The eleventh captain for the eleventh month was Benaiah the Pirathonite, of the children of Ephraim. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 15, '1CH.27.15', 'The twelfth captain for the twelfth month was Heldai the Netophathite, of Othniel. In his division were twenty-four thousand.'),
('1CH', 27, 16, '1CH.27.16', 'Furthermore over the tribes of Israel: of the Reubenites, Eliezer the son of Zichri was the ruler; of the Simeonites, Shephatiah the son of Maacah;'),
('1CH', 27, 17, '1CH.27.17', 'of Levi, Hashabiah the son of Kemuel; of Aaron, Zadok;'),
('1CH', 27, 18, '1CH.27.18', 'of Judah, Elihu, one of the brothers of David; of Issachar, Omri the son of Michael;'),
('1CH', 27, 19, '1CH.27.19', 'of Zebulun, Ishmaiah the son of Obadiah; of Naphtali, Jeremoth the son of Azriel;'),
('1CH', 27, 20, '1CH.27.20', 'of the children of Ephraim, Hoshea the son of Azaziah; of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Joel the son of Pedaiah;'),
('1CH', 27, 21, '1CH.27.21', 'of the half-tribe of Manasseh in Gilead, Iddo the son of Zechariah; of Benjamin, Jaasiel the son of Abner;'),
('1CH', 27, 22, '1CH.27.22', 'of Dan, Azarel the son of Jeroham. These were the captains of the tribes of Israel.'),
('1CH', 27, 23, '1CH.27.23', 'But David didn’t take the number of them from twenty years old and under, because the LORD had said he would increase Israel like the stars of the sky.'),
('1CH', 27, 24, '1CH.27.24', 'Joab the son of Zeruiah began to take a census, but didn’t finish; and wrath came on Israel for this. The number wasn’t put into the account in the chronicles of King David.'),
('1CH', 27, 25, '1CH.27.25', 'Over the king’s treasures was Azmaveth the son of Adiel. Over the treasures in the fields, in the cities, in the villages, and in the towers was Jonathan the son of Uzziah;'),
('1CH', 27, 26, '1CH.27.26', 'Over those who did the work of the field for tillage of the ground was Ezri the son of Chelub.'),
('1CH', 27, 27, '1CH.27.27', 'Over the vineyards was Shimei the Ramathite. Over the increase of the vineyards for the wine cellars was Zabdi the Shiphmite.'),
('1CH', 27, 28, '1CH.27.28', 'Over the olive trees and the sycamore trees that were in the lowland was Baal Hanan the Gederite. Over the cellars of oil was Joash.'),
('1CH', 27, 29, '1CH.27.29', 'Over the herds that fed in Sharon was Shitrai the Sharonite. Over the herds that were in the valleys was Shaphat the son of Adlai.'),
('1CH', 27, 30, '1CH.27.30', 'Over the camels was Obil the Ishmaelite. Over the donkeys was Jehdeiah the Meronothite. Over the flocks was Jaziz the Hagrite.'),
('1CH', 27, 31, '1CH.27.31', 'All these were the rulers of the property which was King David’s.'),
('1CH', 27, 32, '1CH.27.32', 'Also Jonathan, David’s uncle, was a counselor, a man of understanding, and a scribe. Jehiel the son of Hachmoni was with the king’s sons.'),
('1CH', 27, 33, '1CH.27.33', 'Ahithophel was the king’s counselor. Hushai the Archite was the king’s friend.'),
('1CH', 27, 34, '1CH.27.34', 'After Ahithophel was Jehoiada the son of Benaiah, and Abiathar. Joab was the captain of the king’s army.'),
('1CH', 28, 1, '1CH.28.1', 'David assembled all the princes of Israel, the princes of the tribes, the captains of the companies who served the king by division, the captains of thousands, the captains of hundreds, and the rulers over all the substance and possessions of the king and of his sons, with the officers and the mighty men, even all the mighty men of valor, to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 28, 2, '1CH.28.2', 'Then David the king stood up on his feet and said, “Hear me, my brothers and my people! As for me, it was in my heart to build a house of rest for the ark of the LORD’s covenant, and for the footstool of our God; and I had prepared for the building.'),
('1CH', 28, 3, '1CH.28.3', 'But God said to me, ‘You shall not build a house for my name, because you are a man of war and have shed blood.’'),
('1CH', 28, 4, '1CH.28.4', 'However the LORD, the God of Israel, chose me out of all the house of my father to be king over Israel forever. For he has chosen Judah to be prince; and in the house of Judah, the house of my father; and among the sons of my father he took pleasure in me to make me king over all Israel.'),
('1CH', 28, 5, '1CH.28.5', 'Of all my sons (for the LORD has given me many sons), he has chosen Solomon my son to sit on the throne of the LORD’s kingdom over Israel.'),
('1CH', 28, 6, '1CH.28.6', 'He said to me, ‘Solomon, your son, shall build my house and my courts; for I have chosen him to be my son, and I will be his father.'),
('1CH', 28, 7, '1CH.28.7', 'I will establish his kingdom forever if he continues to do my commandments and my ordinances, as it is today.’'),
('1CH', 28, 8, '1CH.28.8', 'Now therefore, in the sight of all Israel, the LORD’s assembly, and in the audience of our God, observe and seek out all the commandments of the LORD your God, that you may possess this good land, and leave it for an inheritance to your children after you forever.'),
('1CH', 28, 9, '1CH.28.9', 'You, Solomon my son, know the God of your father, and serve him with a perfect heart and with a willing mind; for the LORD searches all hearts, and understands all the imaginations of the thoughts. If you seek him, he will be found by you; but if you forsake him, he will cast you off forever.'),
('1CH', 28, 10, '1CH.28.10', 'Take heed now, for the LORD has chosen you to build a house for the sanctuary. Be strong, and do it.”'),
('1CH', 28, 11, '1CH.28.11', 'Then David gave to Solomon his son the plans for the porch of the temple, for its houses, for its treasuries, for its upper rooms, for its inner rooms, for the place of the mercy seat;'),
('1CH', 28, 12, '1CH.28.12', 'and the plans of all that he had by the Spirit, for the courts of the LORD’s house, for all the surrounding rooms, for the treasuries of God’s house, and for the treasuries of the dedicated things;'),
('1CH', 28, 13, '1CH.28.13', 'also for the divisions of the priests and the Levites, for all the work of the service of the LORD’s house, and for all the vessels of service in the LORD’s house—'),
('1CH', 28, 14, '1CH.28.14', 'of gold by weight for the gold for all vessels of every kind of service, for all the vessels of silver by weight, for all vessels of every kind of service;'),
('1CH', 28, 15, '1CH.28.15', 'by weight also for the lamp stands of gold, and for its lamps, of gold, by weight for every lamp stand and for its lamps; and for the lamp stands of silver, by weight for every lamp stand and for its lamps, according to the use of every lamp stand;'),
('1CH', 28, 16, '1CH.28.16', 'and the gold by weight for the tables of show bread, for every table; and silver for the tables of silver;'),
('1CH', 28, 17, '1CH.28.17', 'and the forks, the basins, and the cups, of pure gold; and for the golden bowls by weight for every bowl; and for the silver bowls by weight for every bowl;'),
('1CH', 28, 18, '1CH.28.18', 'and for the altar of incense, refined gold by weight; and gold for the plans for the chariot, and the cherubim that spread out and cover the ark of the LORD’s covenant.'),
('1CH', 28, 19, '1CH.28.19', '“All this”, David said, “I have been made to understand in writing from the LORD’s hand, even all the works of this pattern.”'),
('1CH', 28, 20, '1CH.28.20', 'David said to Solomon his son, “Be strong and courageous, and do it. Don’t be afraid, nor be dismayed, for the LORD God, even my God, is with you. He will not fail you nor forsake you, until all the work for the service of the LORD’s house is finished.'),
('1CH', 28, 21, '1CH.28.21', 'Behold, there are the divisions of the priests and the Levites for all the service of God’s house. Every willing man who has skill for any kind of service shall be with you in all kinds of work. Also the captains and all the people will be entirely at your command.”'),
('1CH', 29, 1, '1CH.29.1', 'David the king said to all the assembly, “Solomon my son, whom alone God has chosen, is yet young and tender, and the work is great; for the palace is not for man, but for the LORD God.'),
('1CH', 29, 2, '1CH.29.2', 'Now I have prepared with all my might for the house of my God the gold for the things of gold, the silver for the things of silver, the bronze for the things of bronze, iron for the things of iron, and wood for the things of wood, also onyx stones, stones to be set, stones for inlaid work of various colors, all kinds of precious stones, and marble stones in abundance.'),
('1CH', 29, 3, '1CH.29.3', 'In addition, because I have set my affection on the house of my God, since I have a treasure of my own of gold and silver, I give it to the house of my God, over and above all that I have prepared for the holy house:'),
('1CH', 29, 4, '1CH.29.4', 'even three thousand talents of gold, of the gold of Ophir, and seven thousand talents of refined silver, with which to overlay the walls of the houses;'),
('1CH', 29, 5, '1CH.29.5', 'of gold for the things of gold, and of silver for the things of silver, and for all kinds of work to be made by the hands of artisans. Who then offers willingly to consecrate himself today to the LORD?”'),
('1CH', 29, 6, '1CH.29.6', 'Then the princes of the fathers’ households, and the princes of the tribes of Israel, and the captains of thousands and of hundreds, with the rulers over the king’s work, offered willingly;'),
('1CH', 29, 7, '1CH.29.7', 'and they gave for the service of God’s house of gold five thousand talents and ten thousand darics, of silver ten thousand talents, of bronze eighteen thousand talents, and of iron one hundred thousand talents.'),
('1CH', 29, 8, '1CH.29.8', 'People with whom precious stones were found gave them to the treasure of the LORD’s house, under the hand of Jehiel the Gershonite.'),
('1CH', 29, 9, '1CH.29.9', 'Then the people rejoiced, because they offered willingly, because with a perfect heart they offered willingly to the LORD; and David the king also rejoiced with great joy.'),
('1CH', 29, 10, '1CH.29.10', 'Therefore David blessed the LORD before all the assembly; and David said, “You are blessed, LORD, the God of Israel our father, forever and ever.'),
('1CH', 29, 11, '1CH.29.11', 'Yours, LORD, is the greatness, the power, the glory, the victory, and the majesty! For all that is in the heavens and on the earth is yours. Yours is the kingdom, LORD, and you are exalted as head above all.'),
('1CH', 29, 12, '1CH.29.12', 'Both riches and honor come from you, and you rule over all! In your hand is power and might! It is in your hand to make great, and to give strength to all!'),
('1CH', 29, 13, '1CH.29.13', 'Now therefore, our God, we thank you and praise your glorious name.'),
('1CH', 29, 14, '1CH.29.14', 'But who am I, and what is my people, that we should be able to offer so willingly as this? For all things come from you, and we have given you of your own.'),
('1CH', 29, 15, '1CH.29.15', 'For we are strangers before you and foreigners, as all our fathers were. Our days on the earth are as a shadow, and there is no remaining.'),
('1CH', 29, 16, '1CH.29.16', 'LORD our God, all this store that we have prepared to build you a house for your holy name comes from your hand, and is all your own.'),
('1CH', 29, 17, '1CH.29.17', 'I know also, my God, that you try the heart and have pleasure in uprightness. As for me, in the uprightness of my heart I have willingly offered all these things. Now I have seen with joy your people, who are present here, offer willingly to you.'),
('1CH', 29, 18, '1CH.29.18', 'LORD, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Israel, our fathers, keep this desire forever in the thoughts of the heart of your people, and prepare their heart for you;'),
('1CH', 29, 19, '1CH.29.19', 'and give to Solomon my son a perfect heart, to keep your commandments, your testimonies, and your statutes, and to do all these things, and to build the palace, for which I have made provision.”'),
('1CH', 29, 20, '1CH.29.20', 'Then David said to all the assembly, “Now bless the LORD your God!” All the assembly blessed the LORD, the God of their fathers, and bowed down their heads and prostrated themselves before the LORD and the king.'),
('1CH', 29, 21, '1CH.29.21', 'They sacrificed sacrifices to the LORD and offered burnt offerings to the LORD on the next day after that day, even one thousand bulls, one thousand rams, and one thousand lambs, with their drink offerings and sacrifices in abundance for all Israel,'),
('1CH', 29, 22, '1CH.29.22', 'and ate and drank before the LORD on that day with great gladness. They made Solomon the son of David king the second time, and anointed him before the LORD to be prince, and Zadok to be priest.'),
('1CH', 29, 23, '1CH.29.23', 'Then Solomon sat on the throne of the LORD as king instead of David his father, and prospered; and all Israel obeyed him.'),
('1CH', 29, 24, '1CH.29.24', 'All the princes, the mighty men, and also all of the sons of King David submitted themselves to Solomon the king.'),
('1CH', 29, 25, '1CH.29.25', 'The LORD magnified Solomon exceedingly in the sight of all Israel, and gave to him such royal majesty as had not been on any king before him in Israel.'),
('1CH', 29, 26, '1CH.29.26', 'Now David the son of Jesse reigned over all Israel.'),
('1CH', 29, 27, '1CH.29.27', 'The time that he reigned over Israel was forty years; he reigned seven years in Hebron, and he reigned thirty-three years in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 29, 28, '1CH.29.28', 'He died at a good old age, full of days, riches, and honor; and Solomon his son reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 29, 29, '1CH.29.29', 'Now the acts of David the king, first and last, behold, they are written in the history of Samuel the seer, and in the history of Nathan the prophet, and in the history of Gad the seer,'),
('1CH', 29, 30, '1CH.29.30', 'with all his reign and his might, and the events that involved him, Israel, and all the kingdoms of the lands.'),
('2CH', 1, 1, '2CH.1.1', 'Solomon the son of David was firmly established in his kingdom, and the LORD his God was with him, and made him exceedingly great.'),
('2CH', 1, 2, '2CH.1.2', 'Solomon spoke to all Israel, to the captains of thousands and of hundreds, to the judges, and to every prince in all Israel, the heads of the fathers’ households.'),
('2CH', 1, 3, '2CH.1.3', 'Then Solomon, and all the assembly with him, went to the high place that was at Gibeon; for God’s Tent of Meeting was there, which the LORD’s servant Moses had made in the wilderness.'),
('2CH', 1, 4, '2CH.1.4', 'But David had brought God’s ark up from Kiriath Jearim to the place that David had prepared for it; for he had pitched a tent for it at Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 1, 5, '2CH.1.5', 'Moreover the bronze altar that Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, had made was there before the LORD’s tabernacle; and Solomon and the assembly were seeking counsel there.'),
('2CH', 1, 6, '2CH.1.6', 'Solomon went up there to the bronze altar before the LORD, which was at the Tent of Meeting, and offered one thousand burnt offerings on it.'),
('2CH', 1, 7, '2CH.1.7', 'That night, God appeared to Solomon and said to him, “Ask for what you want me to give you.”'),
('2CH', 1, 8, '2CH.1.8', 'Solomon said to God, “You have shown great loving kindness to David my father, and have made me king in his place.'),
('2CH', 1, 9, '2CH.1.9', 'Now, LORD God, let your promise to David my father be established; for you have made me king over a people like the dust of the earth in multitude.'),
('2CH', 1, 10, '2CH.1.10', 'Now give me wisdom and knowledge, that I may go out and come in before this people; for who can judge this great people of yours?”'),
('2CH', 1, 11, '2CH.1.11', 'God said to Solomon, “Because this was in your heart, and you have not asked riches, wealth, honor, or the life of those who hate you, nor yet have you asked for long life; but have asked for wisdom and knowledge for yourself, that you may judge my people, over whom I have made you king,'),
('2CH', 1, 12, '2CH.1.12', 'therefore wisdom and knowledge is granted to you. I will give you riches, wealth, and honor, such as none of the kings have had who have been before you, and none after you will have.”'),
('2CH', 1, 13, '2CH.1.13', 'So Solomon came from the high place that was at Gibeon, from before the Tent of Meeting, to Jerusalem; and he reigned over Israel.'),
('2CH', 1, 14, '2CH.1.14', 'Solomon gathered chariots and horsemen. He had one thousand four hundred chariots and twelve thousand horsemen that he placed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 1, 15, '2CH.1.15', 'The king made silver and gold to be as common as stones in Jerusalem, and he made cedars to be as common as the sycamore trees that are in the lowland.'),
('2CH', 1, 16, '2CH.1.16', 'The horses which Solomon had were brought out of Egypt and from Kue. The king’s merchants purchased them from Kue.'),
('2CH', 1, 17, '2CH.1.17', 'They imported from Egypt then exported a chariot for six hundred pieces of silver and a horse for one hundred fifty. They also exported them to the Hittite kings and the Syrian kings.'),
('2CH', 2, 1, '2CH.2.1', 'Now Solomon decided to build a house for the LORD’s name, and a house for his kingdom.'),
('2CH', 2, 2, '2CH.2.2', 'Solomon counted out seventy thousand men to bear burdens, eighty thousand men who were stone cutters in the mountains, and three thousand six hundred to oversee them.'),
('2CH', 2, 3, '2CH.2.3', 'Solomon sent to Huram the king of Tyre, saying, “As you dealt with David my father, and sent him cedars to build him a house in which to dwell, so deal with me.'),
('2CH', 2, 4, '2CH.2.4', 'Behold, I am about to build a house for the name of the LORD my God, to dedicate it to him, to burn before him incense of sweet spices, for the continual show bread, and for the burnt offerings morning and evening, on the Sabbaths, on the new moons, and on the set feasts of the LORD our God. This is an ordinance forever to Israel.'),
('2CH', 2, 5, '2CH.2.5', '“The house which I am building will be great, for our God is greater than all gods.'),
('2CH', 2, 6, '2CH.2.6', 'But who is able to build him a house, since heaven and the heaven of heavens can’t contain him? Who am I then, that I should build him a house, except just to burn incense before him?'),
('2CH', 2, 7, '2CH.2.7', '“Now therefore send me a man skillful to work in gold, in silver, in bronze, in iron, and in purple, crimson, and blue, and who knows how to engrave engravings, to be with the skillful men who are with me in Judah and in Jerusalem, whom David my father provided.'),
('2CH', 2, 8, '2CH.2.8', '“Send me also cedar trees, cypress trees, and algum trees out of Lebanon, for I know that your servants know how to cut timber in Lebanon. Behold, my servants will be with your servants,'),
('2CH', 2, 9, '2CH.2.9', 'even to prepare timber in abundance for me; for the house which I am about to build will be great and wonderful.'),
('2CH', 2, 10, '2CH.2.10', 'Behold, I will give to your servants, the cutters who cut timber, twenty thousand cors of beaten wheat, twenty thousand baths of barley, twenty thousand baths of wine, and twenty thousand baths of oil.”'),
('2CH', 2, 11, '2CH.2.11', 'Then Huram the king of Tyre answered in writing, which he sent to Solomon, “Because the LORD loves his people, he has made you king over them.”'),
('2CH', 2, 12, '2CH.2.12', 'Huram continued, “Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who made heaven and earth, who has given to David the king a wise son, endowed with discretion and understanding, who would build a house for the LORD and a house for his kingdom.'),
('2CH', 2, 13, '2CH.2.13', 'Now I have sent a skillful man, endowed with understanding, Huram-abi,'),
('2CH', 2, 14, '2CH.2.14', 'the son of a woman of the daughters of Dan; and his father was a man of Tyre. He is skillful to work in gold, in silver, in bronze, in iron, in stone, in timber, in purple, in blue, in fine linen, and in crimson, also to engrave any kind of engraving and to devise any device, that there may be a place appointed to him with your skillful men, and with the skillful men of my lord David your father.'),
('2CH', 2, 15, '2CH.2.15', '“Now therefore, the wheat, the barley, the oil, and the wine which my lord has spoken of, let him send to his servants;'),
('2CH', 2, 16, '2CH.2.16', 'and we will cut wood out of Lebanon, as much as you need. We will bring it to you in rafts by sea to Joppa; then you shall carry it up to Jerusalem.”'),
('2CH', 2, 17, '2CH.2.17', 'Solomon counted all the foreigners who were in the land of Israel, after the census with which David his father had counted them; and they found one hundred fifty-three thousand six hundred.'),
('2CH', 2, 18, '2CH.2.18', 'He set seventy thousand of them to bear burdens, eighty thousand who were stone cutters in the mountains, and three thousand six hundred overseers to assign the people their work.'),
('2CH', 3, 1, '2CH.3.1', 'Then Solomon began to build the LORD’s house at Jerusalem on Mount Moriah, where the LORD appeared to David his father, which he prepared in the place that David had appointed, on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
('2CH', 3, 2, '2CH.3.2', 'He began to build in the second day of the second month, in the fourth year of his reign.'),
('2CH', 3, 3, '2CH.3.3', 'Now these are the foundations which Solomon laid for the building of God’s house: the length by cubits after the first measure was sixty cubits, and the width twenty cubits.'),
('2CH', 3, 4, '2CH.3.4', 'The porch that was in front, its length, across the width of the house, was twenty cubits, and the height one hundred twenty; and he overlaid it within with pure gold.'),
('2CH', 3, 5, '2CH.3.5', 'He made the larger room with a ceiling of cypress wood, which he overlaid with fine gold, and ornamented it with palm trees and chains.'),
('2CH', 3, 6, '2CH.3.6', 'He decorated the house with precious stones for beauty. The gold was gold from Parvaim.'),
('2CH', 3, 7, '2CH.3.7', 'He also overlaid the house, the beams, the thresholds, its walls, and its doors with gold, and engraved cherubim on the walls.'),
('2CH', 3, 8, '2CH.3.8', 'He made the most holy place. Its length, according to the width of the house, was twenty cubits, and its width twenty cubits; and he overlaid it with fine gold, amounting to six hundred talents.'),
('2CH', 3, 9, '2CH.3.9', 'The weight of the nails was fifty shekels of gold. He overlaid the upper rooms with gold.'),
('2CH', 3, 10, '2CH.3.10', 'In the most holy place he made two cherubim by carving, and they overlaid them with gold.'),
('2CH', 3, 11, '2CH.3.11', 'The wings of the cherubim were twenty cubits long: the wing of the one was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house; and the other wing was five cubits, reaching to the wing of the other cherub.'),
('2CH', 3, 12, '2CH.3.12', 'The wing of the other cherub was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house; and the other wing was five cubits, joining to the wing of the other cherub.'),
('2CH', 3, 13, '2CH.3.13', 'The wings of these cherubim spread themselves out twenty cubits. They stood on their feet, and their faces were toward the house.'),
('2CH', 3, 14, '2CH.3.14', 'He made the veil of blue, purple, crimson, and fine linen, and ornamented it with cherubim.'),
('2CH', 3, 15, '2CH.3.15', 'Also he made before the house two pillars thirty-five cubits high, and the capital that was on the top of each of them was five cubits.'),
('2CH', 3, 16, '2CH.3.16', 'He made chains in the inner sanctuary, and put them on the tops of the pillars; and he made one hundred pomegranates, and put them on the chains.'),
('2CH', 3, 17, '2CH.3.17', 'He set up the pillars before the temple, one on the right hand and the other on the left; and called the name of that on the right hand Jachin, and the name of that on the left Boaz.'),
('2CH', 4, 1, '2CH.4.1', 'Then he made an altar of bronze, twenty cubits long, twenty cubits wide, and ten cubits high.'),
('2CH', 4, 2, '2CH.4.2', 'Also he made the molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim. It was round, five cubits high, and thirty cubits in circumference.'),
('2CH', 4, 3, '2CH.4.3', 'Under it was the likeness of oxen, which encircled it, for ten cubits, encircling the sea. The oxen were in two rows, cast when it was cast.'),
('2CH', 4, 4, '2CH.4.4', 'It stood on twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, three looking toward the west, three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east; and the sea was set on them above, and all their hindquarters were inward.'),
('2CH', 4, 5, '2CH.4.5', 'It was a handbreadth thick. Its brim was made like the brim of a cup, like the flower of a lily. It received and held three thousand baths.'),
('2CH', 4, 6, '2CH.4.6', 'He also made ten basins, and put five on the right hand and five on the left, to wash in them. The things that belonged to the burnt offering were washed in them, but the sea was for the priests to wash in.'),
('2CH', 4, 7, '2CH.4.7', 'He made the ten lamp stands of gold according to the ordinance concerning them; and he set them in the temple, five on the right hand and five on the left.'),
('2CH', 4, 8, '2CH.4.8', 'He made also ten tables, and placed them in the temple, five on the right side and five on the left. He made one hundred basins of gold.'),
('2CH', 4, 9, '2CH.4.9', 'Furthermore he made the court of the priests, the great court, and doors for the court, and overlaid their doors with bronze.'),
('2CH', 4, 10, '2CH.4.10', 'He set the sea on the right side of the house eastward, toward the south.'),
('2CH', 4, 11, '2CH.4.11', 'Huram made the pots, the shovels, and the basins. So Huram finished doing the work that he did for King Solomon in God’s house:'),
('2CH', 4, 12, '2CH.4.12', 'the two pillars, the bowls, the two capitals which were on the top of the pillars, the two networks to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars,'),
('2CH', 4, 13, '2CH.4.13', 'and the four hundred pomegranates for the two networks—two rows of pomegranates for each network, to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the pillars.'),
('2CH', 4, 14, '2CH.4.14', 'He also made the bases, and he made the basins on the bases—'),
('2CH', 4, 15, '2CH.4.15', 'one sea, and the twelve oxen under it.'),
('2CH', 4, 16, '2CH.4.16', 'Huram-abi also made the pots, the shovels, the forks, and all its vessels for King Solomon, for the LORD’s house, of bright bronze.'),
('2CH', 4, 17, '2CH.4.17', 'The king cast them in the plain of the Jordan, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zeredah.'),
('2CH', 4, 18, '2CH.4.18', 'Thus Solomon made all these vessels in great abundance, so that the weight of the bronze could not be determined.'),
('2CH', 4, 19, '2CH.4.19', 'Solomon made all the vessels that were in God’s house: the golden altar, the tables with the show bread on them,'),
('2CH', 4, 20, '2CH.4.20', 'and the lamp stands with their lamps to burn according to the ordinance before the inner sanctuary, of pure gold;'),
('2CH', 4, 21, '2CH.4.21', 'and the flowers, the lamps, and the tongs of gold that was purest gold;'),
('2CH', 4, 22, '2CH.4.22', 'and the snuffers, the basins, the spoons, and the fire pans of pure gold. As for the entry of the house, its inner doors for the most holy place and the doors of the main hall of the temple were of gold.'),
('2CH', 5, 1, '2CH.5.1', 'Thus all the work that Solomon did for the LORD’s house was finished. Solomon brought in the things that David his father had dedicated, even the silver, the gold, and all the vessels, and put them in the treasuries of God’s house.'),
('2CH', 5, 2, '2CH.5.2', 'Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel and all the heads of the tribes, the princes of the fathers’ households of the children of Israel, to Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the LORD’s covenant out of David’s city, which is Zion.'),
('2CH', 5, 3, '2CH.5.3', 'So all the men of Israel assembled themselves to the king at the feast, which was in the seventh month.'),
('2CH', 5, 4, '2CH.5.4', 'All the elders of Israel came. The Levites took up the ark.'),
('2CH', 5, 5, '2CH.5.5', 'They brought up the ark, the Tent of Meeting, and all the holy vessels that were in the Tent. The Levitical priests brought these up.'),
('2CH', 5, 6, '2CH.5.6', 'King Solomon and all the congregation of Israel who were assembled to him were before the ark, sacrificing sheep and cattle that could not be counted or numbered for multitude.'),
('2CH', 5, 7, '2CH.5.7', 'The priests brought in the ark of the LORD’s covenant to its place, into the inner sanctuary of the house, to the most holy place, even under the wings of the cherubim.'),
('2CH', 5, 8, '2CH.5.8', 'For the cherubim spread out their wings over the place of the ark, and the cherubim covered the ark and its poles above.'),
('2CH', 5, 9, '2CH.5.9', 'The poles were so long that the ends of the poles were seen from the ark in front of the inner sanctuary, but they were not seen outside; and it is there to this day.'),
('2CH', 5, 10, '2CH.5.10', 'There was nothing in the ark except the two tablets which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of Egypt.'),
('2CH', 5, 11, '2CH.5.11', 'When the priests had come out of the holy place (for all the priests who were present had sanctified themselves, and didn’t keep their divisions;'),
('2CH', 5, 12, '2CH.5.12', 'also the Levites who were the singers, all of them, even Asaph, Heman, Jeduthun, and their sons and their brothers, arrayed in fine linen, with cymbals and stringed instruments and harps, stood at the east end of the altar, and with them one hundred twenty priests sounding with trumpets);'),
('2CH', 5, 13, '2CH.5.13', 'when the trumpeters and singers were as one, to make one sound to be heard in praising and thanking the LORD; and when they lifted up their voice with the trumpets and cymbals and instruments of music, and praised the LORD, saying, “For he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever!” then the house was filled with a cloud, even the LORD’s house,'),
('2CH', 5, 14, '2CH.5.14', 'so that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud; for the LORD’s glory filled God’s house.'),
('2CH', 6, 1, '2CH.6.1', 'Then Solomon said, “The LORD has said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.'),
('2CH', 6, 2, '2CH.6.2', 'But I have built you a house and home, a place for you to dwell in forever.”'),
('2CH', 6, 3, '2CH.6.3', 'The king turned his face, and blessed all the assembly of Israel; and all the assembly of Israel stood.'),
('2CH', 6, 4, '2CH.6.4', 'He said, “Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who spoke with his mouth to David my father, and has with his hands fulfilled it, saying,'),
('2CH', 6, 5, '2CH.6.5', '‘Since the day that I brought my people out of the land of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel to build a house in, that my name might be there, and I chose no man to be prince over my people Israel;'),
('2CH', 6, 6, '2CH.6.6', 'but now I have chosen Jerusalem, that my name might be there; and I have chosen David to be over my people Israel.’'),
('2CH', 6, 7, '2CH.6.7', 'Now it was in the heart of David my father to build a house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 6, 8, '2CH.6.8', 'But the LORD said to David my father, ‘Whereas it was in your heart to build a house for my name, you did well that it was in your heart;'),
('2CH', 6, 9, '2CH.6.9', 'nevertheless you shall not build the house, but your son who will come out of your body, he shall build the house for my name.’'),
('2CH', 6, 10, '2CH.6.10', '“The LORD has performed his word that he spoke; for I have risen up in the place of David my father, and sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised, and have built the house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 6, 11, '2CH.6.11', 'There I have set the ark, in which is the LORD’s covenant, which he made with the children of Israel.”'),
('2CH', 6, 12, '2CH.6.12', 'He stood before the LORD’s altar in the presence of all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands'),
('2CH', 6, 13, '2CH.6.13', '(for Solomon had made a bronze platform, five cubits long, five cubits wide, and three cubits high, and had set it in the middle of the court; and he stood on it, and knelt down on his knees before all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands toward heaven).'),
('2CH', 6, 14, '2CH.6.14', 'Then he said, “LORD, the God of Israel, there is no God like you in heaven or on earth—you who keep covenant and loving kindness with your servants who walk before you with all their heart;'),
('2CH', 6, 15, '2CH.6.15', 'who have kept with your servant David my father that which you promised him. Yes, you spoke with your mouth, and have fulfilled it with your hand, as it is today.'),
('2CH', 6, 16, '2CH.6.16', '“Now therefore, LORD, the God of Israel, keep with your servant David my father that which you have promised him, saying, ‘There shall not fail you a man in my sight to sit on the throne of Israel, if only your children take heed to their way, to walk in my law as you have walked before me.’'),
('2CH', 6, 17, '2CH.6.17', 'Now therefore, LORD, the God of Israel, let your word be verified, which you spoke to your servant David.'),
('2CH', 6, 18, '2CH.6.18', '“But will God indeed dwell with men on the earth? Behold, heaven and the heaven of heavens can’t contain you; how much less this house which I have built!'),
('2CH', 6, 19, '2CH.6.19', 'Yet have respect for the prayer of your servant and to his supplication, LORD my God, to listen to the cry and to the prayer which your servant prays before you;'),
('2CH', 6, 20, '2CH.6.20', 'that your eyes may be open toward this house day and night, even toward the place where you have said that you would put your name, to listen to the prayer which your servant will pray toward this place.'),
('2CH', 6, 21, '2CH.6.21', 'Listen to the petitions of your servant and of your people Israel, when they pray toward this place. Yes, hear from your dwelling place, even from heaven; and when you hear, forgive.'),
('2CH', 6, 22, '2CH.6.22', '“If a man sins against his neighbor, and an oath is laid on him to cause him to swear, and he comes and swears before your altar in this house,'),
('2CH', 6, 23, '2CH.6.23', 'then hear from heaven, act, and judge your servants, bringing retribution to the wicked, to bring his way on his own head; and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness.'),
('2CH', 6, 24, '2CH.6.24', '“If your people Israel are struck down before the enemy because they have sinned against you, and they turn again and confess your name, and pray and make supplication before you in this house,'),
('2CH', 6, 25, '2CH.6.25', 'then hear from heaven, and forgive the sin of your people Israel, and bring them again to the land which you gave to them and to their fathers.'),
('2CH', 6, 26, '2CH.6.26', '“When the sky is shut up and there is no rain because they have sinned against you, if they pray toward this place and confess your name, and turn from their sin when you afflict them,'),
('2CH', 6, 27, '2CH.6.27', 'then hear in heaven, and forgive the sin of your servants, your people Israel, when you teach them the good way in which they should walk, and send rain on your land, which you have given to your people for an inheritance.'),
('2CH', 6, 28, '2CH.6.28', '“If there is famine in the land, if there is pestilence, if there is blight or mildew, locust or caterpillar; if their enemies besiege them in the land of their cities; whatever plague or whatever sickness there is—'),
('2CH', 6, 29, '2CH.6.29', 'whatever prayer and supplication is made by any man, or by all your people Israel, who will each know his own plague and his own sorrow, and shall spread out his hands toward this house,'),
('2CH', 6, 30, '2CH.6.30', 'then hear from heaven your dwelling place and forgive, and give to every man according to all his ways, whose heart you know (for you, even you only, know the hearts of the children of men),'),
('2CH', 6, 31, '2CH.6.31', 'that they may fear you, to walk in your ways as long as they live in the land which you gave to our fathers.'),
('2CH', 6, 32, '2CH.6.32', '“Moreover, concerning the foreigner, who is not of your people Israel, when he comes from a far country for your great name’s sake and your mighty hand and your outstretched arm, when they come and pray toward this house,'),
('2CH', 6, 33, '2CH.6.33', 'then hear from heaven, even from your dwelling place, and do according to all that the foreigner calls to you for; that all the peoples of the earth may know your name and fear you, as do your people Israel, and that they may know that this house which I have built is called by your name.'),
('2CH', 6, 34, '2CH.6.34', '“If your people go out to battle against their enemies, by whatever way you send them, and they pray to you toward this city which you have chosen, and the house which I have built for your name;'),
('2CH', 6, 35, '2CH.6.35', 'then hear from heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.'),
('2CH', 6, 36, '2CH.6.36', '“If they sin against you (for there is no man who doesn’t sin), and you are angry with them and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captive to a land far off or near;'),
('2CH', 6, 37, '2CH.6.37', 'yet if they come to their senses in the land where they are carried captive, and turn again, and make supplication to you in the land of their captivity, saying, ‘We have sinned, we have done perversely, and have dealt wickedly;’'),
('2CH', 6, 38, '2CH.6.38', 'if they return to you with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their captivity, where they have been taken captive, and pray toward their land which you gave to their fathers, and the city which you have chosen, and toward the house which I have built for your name;'),
('2CH', 6, 39, '2CH.6.39', 'then hear from heaven, even from your dwelling place, their prayer and their petitions, and maintain their cause, and forgive your people who have sinned against you.'),
('2CH', 6, 40, '2CH.6.40', '“Now, my God, let, I beg you, your eyes be open, and let your ears be attentive to the prayer that is made in this place.'),
('2CH', 6, 41, '2CH.6.41', '“Now therefore arise, LORD God, into your resting place, you, and the ark of your strength. Let your priests, LORD God, be clothed with salvation, and let your saints rejoice in goodness.'),
('2CH', 6, 42, '2CH.6.42', '“LORD God, don’t turn away the face of your anointed. Remember your loving kindnesses to David your servant.”'),
('2CH', 7, 1, '2CH.7.1', 'Now when Solomon had finished praying, fire came down from heaven and consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices; and the LORD’s glory filled the house.'),
('2CH', 7, 2, '2CH.7.2', 'The priests could not enter into the LORD’s house, because the LORD’s glory filled the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 7, 3, '2CH.7.3', 'All the children of Israel looked on, when the fire came down, and the LORD’s glory was on the house. They bowed themselves with their faces to the ground on the pavement, worshiped, and gave thanks to the LORD, saying, “For he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever!”'),
('2CH', 7, 4, '2CH.7.4', 'Then the king and all the people offered sacrifices before the LORD.'),
('2CH', 7, 5, '2CH.7.5', 'King Solomon offered a sacrifice of twenty-two thousand head of cattle and a hundred twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the people dedicated God’s house.'),
('2CH', 7, 6, '2CH.7.6', 'The priests stood, according to their positions; the Levites also with instruments of music of the LORD, which David the king had made to give thanks to the LORD, when David praised by their ministry, saying “For his loving kindness endures forever.” The priests sounded trumpets before them; and all Israel stood.'),
('2CH', 7, 7, '2CH.7.7', 'Moreover Solomon made the middle of the court that was before the LORD’s house holy; for there he offered the burnt offerings and the fat of the peace offerings, because the bronze altar which Solomon had made was not able to receive the burnt offering, the meal offering, and the fat.'),
('2CH', 7, 8, '2CH.7.8', 'So Solomon held the feast at that time for seven days, and all Israel with him, a very great assembly, from the entrance of Hamath to the brook of Egypt.'),
('2CH', 7, 9, '2CH.7.9', 'On the eighth day, they held a solemn assembly; for they kept the dedication of the altar seven days, and the feast seven days.'),
('2CH', 7, 10, '2CH.7.10', 'On the twenty-third day of the seventh month, he sent the people away to their tents, joyful and glad of heart for the goodness that the LORD had shown to David, to Solomon, and to Israel his people.'),
('2CH', 7, 11, '2CH.7.11', 'Thus Solomon finished the LORD’s house and the king’s house; and he successfully completed all that came into Solomon’s heart to make in the LORD’s house and in his own house.'),
('2CH', 7, 12, '2CH.7.12', 'Then the LORD appeared to Solomon by night, and said to him, “I have heard your prayer, and have chosen this place for myself for a house of sacrifice.'),
('2CH', 7, 13, '2CH.7.13', '“If I shut up the sky so that there is no rain, or if I command the locust to devour the land, or if I send pestilence among my people,'),
('2CH', 7, 14, '2CH.7.14', 'if my people who are called by my name will humble themselves, pray, seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways, then I will hear from heaven, will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.'),
('2CH', 7, 15, '2CH.7.15', 'Now my eyes will be open and my ears attentive to prayer that is made in this place.'),
('2CH', 7, 16, '2CH.7.16', 'For now I have chosen and made this house holy, that my name may be there forever; and my eyes and my heart will be there perpetually.'),
('2CH', 7, 17, '2CH.7.17', '“As for you, if you will walk before me as David your father walked, and do according to all that I have commanded you, and will keep my statutes and my ordinances,'),
('2CH', 7, 18, '2CH.7.18', 'then I will establish the throne of your kingdom, according as I covenanted with David your father, saying, ‘There shall not fail you a man to be ruler in Israel.’'),
('2CH', 7, 19, '2CH.7.19', 'But if you turn away and forsake my statutes and my commandments which I have set before you, and go and serve other gods and worship them,'),
('2CH', 7, 20, '2CH.7.20', 'then I will pluck them up by the roots out of my land which I have given them; and this house, which I have made holy for my name, I will cast out of my sight, and I will make it a proverb and a byword among all peoples.'),
('2CH', 7, 21, '2CH.7.21', 'This house, which is so high, everyone who passes by it will be astonished and say, ‘Why has the LORD done this to this land and to this house?’'),
('2CH', 7, 22, '2CH.7.22', 'They shall answer, ‘Because they abandoned the LORD, the God of their fathers, who brought them out of the land of Egypt, and took other gods, worshiped them, and served them. Therefore he has brought all this evil on them.’”'),
('2CH', 8, 1, '2CH.8.1', 'At the end of twenty years, in which Solomon had built the LORD’s house and his own house,'),
('2CH', 8, 2, '2CH.8.2', 'Solomon built the cities which Huram had given to Solomon, and caused the children of Israel to dwell there.'),
('2CH', 8, 3, '2CH.8.3', 'Solomon went to Hamath Zobah, and prevailed against it.'),
('2CH', 8, 4, '2CH.8.4', 'He built Tadmor in the wilderness, and all the storage cities, which he built in Hamath.'),
('2CH', 8, 5, '2CH.8.5', 'Also he built Beth Horon the upper and Beth Horon the lower, fortified cities with walls, gates, and bars;'),
('2CH', 8, 6, '2CH.8.6', 'and Baalath, and all the storage cities that Solomon had, and all the cities for his chariots, the cities for his horsemen, and all that Solomon desired to build for his pleasure in Jerusalem, in Lebanon, and in all the land of his dominion.'),
('2CH', 8, 7, '2CH.8.7', 'As for all the people who were left of the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites, who were not of Israel—'),
('2CH', 8, 8, '2CH.8.8', 'of their children who were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel didn’t consume—of them Solomon conscripted forced labor to this day.'),
('2CH', 8, 9, '2CH.8.9', 'But of the children of Israel, Solomon made no servants for his work, but they were men of war, chief of his captains, and rulers of his chariots and of his horsemen.'),
('2CH', 8, 10, '2CH.8.10', 'These were the chief officers of King Solomon, even two-hundred fifty, who ruled over the people.'),
('2CH', 8, 11, '2CH.8.11', 'Solomon brought up Pharaoh’s daughter out of David’s city to the house that he had built for her; for he said, “My wife shall not dwell in the house of David king of Israel, because the places where the LORD’s ark has come are holy.”'),
('2CH', 8, 12, '2CH.8.12', 'Then Solomon offered burnt offerings to the LORD on the LORD’s altar which he had built before the porch,'),
('2CH', 8, 13, '2CH.8.13', 'even as the duty of every day required, offering according to the commandment of Moses on the Sabbaths, on the new moons, and on the set feasts, three times per year, during the feast of unleavened bread, during the feast of weeks, and during the feast of booths.'),
('2CH', 8, 14, '2CH.8.14', 'He appointed, according to the ordinance of David his father, the divisions of the priests to their service, and the Levites to their offices, to praise and to minister before the priests, as the duty of every day required, the doorkeepers also by their divisions at every gate, for David the man of God had so commanded.'),
('2CH', 8, 15, '2CH.8.15', 'They didn’t depart from the commandment of the king to the priests and Levites concerning any matter or concerning the treasures.'),
('2CH', 8, 16, '2CH.8.16', 'Now all the work of Solomon was accomplished from the day of the foundation of the LORD’s house until it was finished. So the LORD’s house was completed.'),
('2CH', 8, 17, '2CH.8.17', 'Then Solomon went to Ezion Geber and to Eloth, on the seashore in the land of Edom.'),
('2CH', 8, 18, '2CH.8.18', 'Huram sent him ships and servants who had knowledge of the sea by the hands of his servants; and they came with the servants of Solomon to Ophir, and brought from there four hundred fifty talents of gold, and brought them to King Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 1, '2CH.9.1', 'When the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon, she came to test Solomon with hard questions at Jerusalem, with a very great caravan, including camels that bore spices, gold in abundance, and precious stones. When she had come to Solomon, she talked with him about all that was in her heart.'),
('2CH', 9, 2, '2CH.9.2', 'Solomon answered all her questions. There wasn’t anything hidden from Solomon which he didn’t tell her.'),
('2CH', 9, 3, '2CH.9.3', 'When the queen of Sheba had seen the wisdom of Solomon, the house that he had built,'),
('2CH', 9, 4, '2CH.9.4', 'the food of his table, the seating of his servants, the attendance of his ministers, their clothing, his cup bearers and their clothing, and his ascent by which he went up to the LORD’s house, there was no more spirit in her.'),
('2CH', 9, 5, '2CH.9.5', 'She said to the king, “It was a true report that I heard in my own land of your acts and of your wisdom.'),
('2CH', 9, 6, '2CH.9.6', 'However I didn’t believe their words until I came, and my eyes had seen it; and behold half of the greatness of your wisdom wasn’t told me. You exceed the fame that I heard!'),
('2CH', 9, 7, '2CH.9.7', 'Happy are your men, and happy are these your servants, who stand continually before you and hear your wisdom.'),
('2CH', 9, 8, '2CH.9.8', 'Blessed be the LORD your God, who delighted in you and set you on his throne to be king for the LORD your God, because your God loved Israel, to establish them forever. Therefore he made you king over them, to do justice and righteousness.”'),
('2CH', 9, 9, '2CH.9.9', 'She gave the king one hundred and twenty talents of gold, spices in great abundance, and precious stones. There was never before such spice as the queen of Sheba gave to King Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 10, '2CH.9.10', 'The servants of Huram and the servants of Solomon, who brought gold from Ophir, also brought algum trees and precious stones.'),
('2CH', 9, 11, '2CH.9.11', 'The king used algum tree wood to make terraces for the LORD’s house and for the king’s house, and harps and stringed instruments for the singers. There were none like these seen before in the land of Judah.'),
('2CH', 9, 12, '2CH.9.12', 'King Solomon gave to the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatever she asked, more than that which she had brought to the king. So she turned and went to her own land, she and her servants.'),
('2CH', 9, 13, '2CH.9.13', 'Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred sixty-six talents of gold,'),
('2CH', 9, 14, '2CH.9.14', 'in addition to that which the traders and merchants brought. All the kings of Arabia and the governors of the country brought gold and silver to Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 15, '2CH.9.15', 'King Solomon made two hundred large shields of beaten gold. Six hundred shekels of beaten gold went to one large shield.'),
('2CH', 9, 16, '2CH.9.16', 'He made three hundred shields of beaten gold. Three hundred shekels of gold went to one shield. The king put them in the House of the Forest of Lebanon.'),
('2CH', 9, 17, '2CH.9.17', 'Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with pure gold.'),
('2CH', 9, 18, '2CH.9.18', 'There were six steps to the throne, with a footstool of gold, which were fastened to the throne, and armrests on either side by the place of the seat, and two lions standing beside the armrests.'),
('2CH', 9, 19, '2CH.9.19', 'Twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other on the six steps. There was nothing like it made in any other kingdom.'),
('2CH', 9, 20, '2CH.9.20', 'All King Solomon’s drinking vessels were of gold, and all the vessels of the House of the Forest of Lebanon were of pure gold. Silver was not considered valuable in the days of Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 21, '2CH.9.21', 'For the king had ships that went to Tarshish with Huram’s servants. Once every three years, the ships of Tarshish came bringing gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks.'),
('2CH', 9, 22, '2CH.9.22', 'So King Solomon exceeded all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom.'),
('2CH', 9, 23, '2CH.9.23', 'All the kings of the earth sought the presence of Solomon to hear his wisdom, which God had put in his heart.'),
('2CH', 9, 24, '2CH.9.24', 'They each brought tribute: vessels of silver, vessels of gold, clothing, armor, spices, horses, and mules every year.'),
('2CH', 9, 25, '2CH.9.25', 'Solomon had four thousand stalls for horses and chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen that he stationed in the chariot cities and with the king at Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 9, 26, '2CH.9.26', 'He ruled over all the kings from the River even to the land of the Philistines, and to the border of Egypt.'),
('2CH', 9, 27, '2CH.9.27', 'The king made silver as common in Jerusalem as stones, and he made cedars to be as abundant as the sycamore trees that are in the lowland.'),
('2CH', 9, 28, '2CH.9.28', 'They brought horses for Solomon out of Egypt and out of all lands.'),
('2CH', 9, 29, '2CH.9.29', 'Now the rest of the acts of Solomon, first and last, aren’t they written in the history of Nathan the prophet, and in the prophecy of Ahijah the Shilonite, and in the visions of Iddo the seer concerning Jeroboam the son of Nebat?'),
('2CH', 9, 30, '2CH.9.30', 'Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel forty years.'),
('2CH', 9, 31, '2CH.9.31', 'Solomon slept with his fathers, and he was buried in his father David’s city; and Rehoboam his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 10, 1, '2CH.10.1', 'Rehoboam went to Shechem, for all Israel had come to Shechem to make him king.'),
('2CH', 10, 2, '2CH.10.2', 'When Jeroboam the son of Nebat heard of it (for he was in Egypt, where he had fled from the presence of King Solomon), Jeroboam returned out of Egypt.'),
('2CH', 10, 3, '2CH.10.3', 'They sent and called him; and Jeroboam and all Israel came, and they spoke to Rehoboam, saying,'),
('2CH', 10, 4, '2CH.10.4', '“Your father made our yoke grievous. Now therefore make the grievous service of your father and his heavy yoke which he put on us, lighter, and we will serve you.”'),
('2CH', 10, 5, '2CH.10.5', 'He said to them, “Come again to me after three days.” So the people departed.'),
('2CH', 10, 6, '2CH.10.6', 'King Rehoboam took counsel with the old men, who had stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, saying, “What counsel do you give me about how to answer these people?”'),
('2CH', 10, 7, '2CH.10.7', 'They spoke to him, saying, “If you are kind to these people, please them, and speak good words to them, then they will be your servants forever.”'),
('2CH', 10, 8, '2CH.10.8', 'But he abandoned the counsel of the old men which they had given him, and took counsel with the young men who had grown up with him, who stood before him.'),
('2CH', 10, 9, '2CH.10.9', 'He said to them, “What counsel do you give, that we may give an answer to these people, who have spoken to me, saying, ‘Make the yoke that your father put on us lighter’?”'),
('2CH', 10, 10, '2CH.10.10', 'The young men who had grown up with him spoke to him, saying, “Thus you shall tell the people who spoke to you, saying, ‘Your father made our yoke heavy, but make it lighter on us;’ thus you shall say to them, ‘My little finger is thicker than my father’s waist.'),
('2CH', 10, 11, '2CH.10.11', 'Now whereas my father burdened you with a heavy yoke, I will add to your yoke. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.’”'),
('2CH', 10, 12, '2CH.10.12', 'So Jeroboam and all the people came to Rehoboam the third day, as the king asked, saying, “Come to me again the third day.”'),
('2CH', 10, 13, '2CH.10.13', 'The king answered them roughly; and King Rehoboam abandoned the counsel of the old men,'),
('2CH', 10, 14, '2CH.10.14', 'and spoke to them after the counsel of the young men, saying, “My father made your yoke heavy, but I will add to it. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.”'),
('2CH', 10, 15, '2CH.10.15', 'So the king didn’t listen to the people; for it was brought about by God, that the LORD might establish his word, which he spoke by Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam the son of Nebat.'),
('2CH', 10, 16, '2CH.10.16', 'When all Israel saw that the king didn’t listen to them, the people answered the king, saying, “What portion do we have in David? We don’t have an inheritance in the son of Jesse! Every man to your tents, Israel! Now see to your own house, David.” So all Israel departed to their tents.'),
('2CH', 10, 17, '2CH.10.17', 'But as for the children of Israel who lived in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them.'),
('2CH', 10, 18, '2CH.10.18', 'Then King Rehoboam sent Hadoram, who was over the men subject to forced labor; and the children of Israel stoned him to death with stones. King Rehoboam hurried to get himself up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 10, 19, '2CH.10.19', 'So Israel rebelled against David’s house to this day.'),
('2CH', 11, 1, '2CH.11.1', 'When Rehoboam had come to Jerusalem, he assembled the house of Judah and Benjamin, one hundred eighty thousand chosen men who were warriors, to fight against Israel, to bring the kingdom again to Rehoboam.'),
('2CH', 11, 2, '2CH.11.2', 'But the LORD’s word came to Shemaiah the man of God, saying,'),
('2CH', 11, 3, '2CH.11.3', '“Speak to Rehoboam the son of Solomon, king of Judah, and to all Israel in Judah and Benjamin, saying,'),
('2CH', 11, 4, '2CH.11.4', '‘The LORD says, “You shall not go up, nor fight against your brothers! Every man return to his house; for this thing is of me.”’” So they listened to the LORD’s words, and returned from going against Jeroboam.'),
('2CH', 11, 5, '2CH.11.5', 'Rehoboam lived in Jerusalem, and built cities for defense in Judah.'),
('2CH', 11, 6, '2CH.11.6', 'He built Bethlehem, Etam, Tekoa,'),
('2CH', 11, 7, '2CH.11.7', 'Beth Zur, Soco, Adullam,'),
('2CH', 11, 8, '2CH.11.8', 'Gath, Mareshah, Ziph,'),
('2CH', 11, 9, '2CH.11.9', 'Adoraim, Lachish, Azekah,'),
('2CH', 11, 10, '2CH.11.10', 'Zorah, Aijalon, and Hebron, which are fortified cities in Judah and in Benjamin.'),
('2CH', 11, 11, '2CH.11.11', 'He fortified the strongholds and put captains in them with stores of food, oil and wine.'),
('2CH', 11, 12, '2CH.11.12', 'He put shields and spears in every city, and made them exceedingly strong. Judah and Benjamin belonged to him.'),
('2CH', 11, 13, '2CH.11.13', 'The priests and the Levites who were in all Israel stood with him out of all their territory.'),
('2CH', 11, 14, '2CH.11.14', 'For the Levites left their pasture lands and their possessions, and came to Judah and Jerusalem; for Jeroboam and his sons cast them off, that they should not execute the priest’s office to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 11, 15, '2CH.11.15', 'He himself appointed priests for the high places, for the male goat and calf idols which he had made.'),
('2CH', 11, 16, '2CH.11.16', 'After them, out of all the tribes of Israel, those who set their hearts to seek the LORD, the God of Israel, came to Jerusalem to sacrifice to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 11, 17, '2CH.11.17', 'So they strengthened the kingdom of Judah and made Rehoboam the son of Solomon strong for three years, for they walked three years in the way of David and Solomon.'),
('2CH', 11, 18, '2CH.11.18', 'Rehoboam took a wife for himself, Mahalath the daughter of Jerimoth the son of David and of Abihail the daughter of Eliab the son of Jesse.'),
('2CH', 11, 19, '2CH.11.19', 'She bore him sons: Jeush, Shemariah, and Zaham.'),
('2CH', 11, 20, '2CH.11.20', 'After her, he took Maacah the granddaughter of Absalom; and she bore him Abijah, Attai, Ziza, and Shelomith.'),
('2CH', 11, 21, '2CH.11.21', 'Rehoboam loved Maacah the granddaughter of Absalom above all his wives and his concubines; for he took eighteen wives and sixty concubines, and became the father of twenty-eight sons and sixty daughters.'),
('2CH', 11, 22, '2CH.11.22', 'Rehoboam appointed Abijah the son of Maacah to be chief, the prince among his brothers, for he intended to make him king.'),
('2CH', 11, 23, '2CH.11.23', 'He dealt wisely, and dispersed some of his sons throughout all the lands of Judah and Benjamin, to every fortified city. He gave them food in abundance; and he sought many wives for them.'),
('2CH', 12, 1, '2CH.12.1', 'When the kingdom of Rehoboam was established and he was strong, he abandoned the LORD’s law, and all Israel with him.'),
('2CH', 12, 2, '2CH.12.2', 'In the fifth year of King Rehoboam, Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem, because they had trespassed against the LORD,'),
('2CH', 12, 3, '2CH.12.3', 'with twelve hundred chariots and sixty thousand horsemen. The people were without number who came with him out of Egypt: the Lubim, the Sukkiim, and the Ethiopians.'),
('2CH', 12, 4, '2CH.12.4', 'He took the fortified cities which belonged to Judah, and came to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 12, 5, '2CH.12.5', 'Now Shemaiah the prophet came to Rehoboam and to the princes of Judah, who were gathered together to Jerusalem because of Shishak, and said to them, “The LORD says, ‘You have forsaken me, therefore I have also left you in the hand of Shishak.’”'),
('2CH', 12, 6, '2CH.12.6', 'Then the princes of Israel and the king humbled themselves; and they said, “The LORD is righteous.”'),
('2CH', 12, 7, '2CH.12.7', 'When the LORD saw that they humbled themselves, the LORD’s word came to Shemaiah, saying, “They have humbled themselves. I will not destroy them, but I will grant them some deliverance, and my wrath won’t be poured out on Jerusalem by the hand of Shishak.'),
('2CH', 12, 8, '2CH.12.8', 'Nevertheless they will be his servants, that they may know my service, and the service of the kingdoms of the countries.”'),
('2CH', 12, 9, '2CH.12.9', 'So Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem and took away the treasures of the LORD’s house and the treasures of the king’s house. He took it all away. He also took away the shields of gold which Solomon had made.'),
('2CH', 12, 10, '2CH.12.10', 'King Rehoboam made shields of bronze in their place, and committed them to the hands of the captains of the guard, who kept the door of the king’s house.'),
('2CH', 12, 11, '2CH.12.11', 'As often as the king entered into the LORD’s house, the guard came and bore them, then brought them back into the guard room.'),
('2CH', 12, 12, '2CH.12.12', 'When he humbled himself, the LORD’s wrath turned from him, so as not to destroy him altogether. Moreover, there were good things found in Judah.'),
('2CH', 12, 13, '2CH.12.13', 'So King Rehoboam strengthened himself in Jerusalem and reigned; for Rehoboam was forty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city which the LORD had chosen out of all the tribes of Israel to put his name there. His mother’s name was Naamah the Ammonitess.'),
('2CH', 12, 14, '2CH.12.14', 'He did that which was evil, because he didn’t set his heart to seek the LORD.'),
('2CH', 12, 15, '2CH.12.15', 'Now the acts of Rehoboam, first and last, aren’t they written in the histories of Shemaiah the prophet and of Iddo the seer, in the genealogies? There were wars between Rehoboam and Jeroboam continually.'),
('2CH', 12, 16, '2CH.12.16', 'Rehoboam slept with his fathers, and was buried in David’s city; and Abijah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 13, 1, '2CH.13.1', 'In the eighteenth year of King Jeroboam, Abijah began to reign over Judah.'),
('2CH', 13, 2, '2CH.13.2', 'He reigned three years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Micaiah the daughter of Uriel of Gibeah. There was war between Abijah and Jeroboam.'),
('2CH', 13, 3, '2CH.13.3', 'Abijah joined battle with an army of valiant men of war, even four hundred thousand chosen men; and Jeroboam set the battle in array against him with eight hundred thousand chosen men, who were mighty men of valor.'),
('2CH', 13, 4, '2CH.13.4', 'Abijah stood up on Mount Zemaraim, which is in the hill country of Ephraim, and said, “Hear me, Jeroboam and all Israel:'),
('2CH', 13, 5, '2CH.13.5', 'Ought you not to know that the LORD, the God of Israel, gave the kingdom over Israel to David forever, even to him and to his sons by a covenant of salt?'),
('2CH', 13, 6, '2CH.13.6', 'Yet Jeroboam the son of Nebat, the servant of Solomon the son of David, rose up, and rebelled against his lord.'),
('2CH', 13, 7, '2CH.13.7', 'Worthless men were gathered to him, wicked fellows who strengthened themselves against Rehoboam the son of Solomon, when Rehoboam was young and tender hearted, and could not withstand them.'),
('2CH', 13, 8, '2CH.13.8', '“Now you intend to withstand the kingdom of the LORD in the hand of the sons of David. You are a great multitude, and the golden calves which Jeroboam made you for gods are with you.'),
('2CH', 13, 9, '2CH.13.9', 'Haven’t you driven out the priests of the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the Levites, and made priests for yourselves according to the ways of the peoples of other lands? Whoever comes to consecrate himself with a young bull and seven rams may be a priest of those who are no gods.'),
('2CH', 13, 10, '2CH.13.10', '“But as for us, the LORD is our God, and we have not forsaken him. We have priests serving the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the Levites in their work.'),
('2CH', 13, 11, '2CH.13.11', 'They burn to the LORD every morning and every evening burnt offerings and sweet incense. They also set the show bread in order on the pure table, and care for the gold lamp stand with its lamps, to burn every evening; for we keep the instruction of the LORD our God, but you have forsaken him.'),
('2CH', 13, 12, '2CH.13.12', 'Behold, God is with us at our head, and his priests with the trumpets of alarm to sound an alarm against you. Children of Israel, don’t fight against the LORD, the God of your fathers; for you will not prosper.”'),
('2CH', 13, 13, '2CH.13.13', 'But Jeroboam caused an ambush to come about behind them; so they were before Judah, and the ambush was behind them.'),
('2CH', 13, 14, '2CH.13.14', 'When Judah looked back, behold, the battle was before and behind them; and they cried to the LORD, and the priests sounded with the trumpets.'),
('2CH', 13, 15, '2CH.13.15', 'Then the men of Judah gave a shout. As the men of Judah shouted, God struck Jeroboam and all Israel before Abijah and Judah.'),
('2CH', 13, 16, '2CH.13.16', 'The children of Israel fled before Judah, and God delivered them into their hand.'),
('2CH', 13, 17, '2CH.13.17', 'Abijah and his people killed them with a great slaughter, so five hundred thousand chosen men of Israel fell down slain.'),
('2CH', 13, 18, '2CH.13.18', 'Thus the children of Israel were brought under at that time, and the children of Judah prevailed, because they relied on the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 13, 19, '2CH.13.19', 'Abijah pursued Jeroboam, and took cities from him: Bethel with its villages, Jeshanah with its villages, and Ephron with its villages.'),
('2CH', 13, 20, '2CH.13.20', 'Jeroboam didn’t recover strength again in the days of Abijah. The LORD struck him, and he died.'),
('2CH', 13, 21, '2CH.13.21', 'But Abijah grew mighty and took for himself fourteen wives, and became the father of twenty-two sons and sixteen daughters.'),
('2CH', 13, 22, '2CH.13.22', 'The rest of the acts of Abijah, his ways, and his sayings are written in the commentary of the prophet Iddo.'),
('2CH', 14, 1, '2CH.14.1', 'So Abijah slept with his fathers, and they buried him in David’s city; and Asa his son reigned in his place. In his days, the land was quiet ten years.'),
('2CH', 14, 2, '2CH.14.2', 'Asa did that which was good and right in the LORD his God’s eyes,'),
('2CH', 14, 3, '2CH.14.3', 'for he took away the foreign altars and the high places, broke down the pillars, cut down the Asherah poles,'),
('2CH', 14, 4, '2CH.14.4', 'and commanded Judah to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, and to obey his law and command.'),
('2CH', 14, 5, '2CH.14.5', 'Also he took away out of all the cities of Judah the high places and the sun images; and the kingdom was quiet before him.'),
('2CH', 14, 6, '2CH.14.6', 'He built fortified cities in Judah; for the land was quiet, and he had no war in those years, because the LORD had given him rest.'),
('2CH', 14, 7, '2CH.14.7', 'For he said to Judah, “Let’s build these cities and make walls around them, with towers, gates, and bars. The land is yet before us, because we have sought the LORD our God. We have sought him, and he has given us rest on every side.” So they built and prospered.'),
('2CH', 14, 8, '2CH.14.8', 'Asa had an army of three hundred thousand out of Judah who bore bucklers and spears, and two hundred eighty thousand out of Benjamin who bore shields and drew bows. All these were mighty men of valor.'),
('2CH', 14, 9, '2CH.14.9', 'Zerah the Ethiopian came out against them with an army of a million troops and three hundred chariots, and he came to Mareshah.'),
('2CH', 14, 10, '2CH.14.10', 'Then Asa went out to meet him, and they set the battle in array in the valley of Zephathah at Mareshah.'),
('2CH', 14, 11, '2CH.14.11', 'Asa cried to the LORD his God, and said, “LORD, there is no one besides you to help, between the mighty and him who has no strength. Help us, LORD our God; for we rely on you, and in your name we have come against this multitude. LORD, you are our God. Don’t let man prevail against you.”'),
('2CH', 14, 12, '2CH.14.12', 'So the LORD struck the Ethiopians before Asa and before Judah; and the Ethiopians fled.'),
('2CH', 14, 13, '2CH.14.13', 'Asa and the people who were with him pursued them to Gerar. So many of the Ethiopians fell that they could not recover themselves, for they were destroyed before the LORD and before his army. Judah’s army carried away very much booty.'),
('2CH', 14, 14, '2CH.14.14', 'They struck all the cities around Gerar, for the fear of the LORD came on them. They plundered all the cities, for there was much plunder in them.'),
('2CH', 14, 15, '2CH.14.15', 'They also struck the tents of those who had livestock, and carried away sheep and camels in abundance, then returned to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 15, 1, '2CH.15.1', 'The Spirit of God came on Azariah the son of Oded.'),
('2CH', 15, 2, '2CH.15.2', 'He went out to meet Asa, and said to him, “Hear me, Asa, and all Judah and Benjamin! The LORD is with you while you are with him; and if you seek him, he will be found by you; but if you forsake him, he will forsake you.'),
('2CH', 15, 3, '2CH.15.3', 'Now for a long time Israel was without the true God, without a teaching priest, and without law.'),
('2CH', 15, 4, '2CH.15.4', 'But when in their distress they turned to the LORD, the God of Israel, and sought him, he was found by them.'),
('2CH', 15, 5, '2CH.15.5', 'In those times there was no peace to him who went out, nor to him who came in; but great troubles were on all the inhabitants of the lands.'),
('2CH', 15, 6, '2CH.15.6', 'They were broken in pieces, nation against nation, and city against city; for God troubled them with all adversity.'),
('2CH', 15, 7, '2CH.15.7', 'But you be strong! Don’t let your hands be slack, for your work will be rewarded.”'),
('2CH', 15, 8, '2CH.15.8', 'When Asa heard these words and the prophecy of Oded the prophet, he took courage, and put away the abominations out of all the land of Judah and Benjamin, and out of the cities which he had taken from the hill country of Ephraim; and he renewed the LORD’s altar that was before the LORD’s porch.'),
('2CH', 15, 9, '2CH.15.9', 'He gathered all Judah and Benjamin, and those who lived with them out of Ephraim, Manasseh, and Simeon; for they came to him out of Israel in abundance when they saw that the LORD his God was with him.'),
('2CH', 15, 10, '2CH.15.10', 'So they gathered themselves together at Jerusalem in the third month, in the fifteenth year of Asa’s reign.'),
('2CH', 15, 11, '2CH.15.11', 'They sacrificed to the LORD in that day, from the plunder which they had brought, seven hundred head of cattle and seven thousand sheep.'),
('2CH', 15, 12, '2CH.15.12', 'They entered into the covenant to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, with all their heart and with all their soul;'),
('2CH', 15, 13, '2CH.15.13', 'and that whoever would not seek the LORD, the God of Israel, should be put to death, whether small or great, whether man or woman.'),
('2CH', 15, 14, '2CH.15.14', 'They swore to the LORD with a loud voice, with shouting, with trumpets, and with cornets.'),
('2CH', 15, 15, '2CH.15.15', 'All Judah rejoiced at the oath, for they had sworn with all their heart and sought him with their whole desire; and he was found by them. Then the LORD gave them rest all around.'),
('2CH', 15, 16, '2CH.15.16', 'Also Maacah, the mother of Asa the king, he removed from being queen mother, because she had made an abominable image for an Asherah; so Asa cut down her image, ground it into dust, and burned it at the brook Kidron.'),
('2CH', 15, 17, '2CH.15.17', 'But the high places were not taken away out of Israel; nevertheless the heart of Asa was perfect all his days.'),
('2CH', 15, 18, '2CH.15.18', 'He brought the things that his father had dedicated and that he himself had dedicated, silver, gold, and vessels into God’s house.'),
('2CH', 15, 19, '2CH.15.19', 'There was no more war to the thirty-fifth year of Asa’s reign.'),
('2CH', 16, 1, '2CH.16.1', 'In the thirty-sixth year of Asa’s reign, Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah, and built Ramah, that he might not allow anyone to go out or come in to Asa king of Judah.'),
('2CH', 16, 2, '2CH.16.2', 'Then Asa brought out silver and gold out of the treasures of the LORD’s house and of the king’s house, and sent to Ben Hadad king of Syria, who lived at Damascus, saying,'),
('2CH', 16, 3, '2CH.16.3', '“Let there be a treaty between me and you, as there was between my father and your father. Behold, I have sent you silver and gold. Go, break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.”'),
('2CH', 16, 4, '2CH.16.4', 'Ben Hadad listened to King Asa, and sent the captains of his armies against the cities of Israel; and they struck Ijon, Dan, Abel Maim, and all the storage cities of Naphtali.'),
('2CH', 16, 5, '2CH.16.5', 'When Baasha heard of it, he stopped building Ramah, and let his work cease.'),
('2CH', 16, 6, '2CH.16.6', 'Then Asa the king took all Judah, and they carried away the stones and timber of Ramah, with which Baasha had built; and he built Geba and Mizpah with them.'),
('2CH', 16, 7, '2CH.16.7', 'At that time Hanani the seer came to Asa king of Judah, and said to him, “Because you have relied on the king of Syria, and have not relied on the LORD your God, therefore the army of the king of Syria has escaped out of your hand.'),
('2CH', 16, 8, '2CH.16.8', 'Weren’t the Ethiopians and the Lubim a huge army, with chariots and exceedingly many horsemen? Yet, because you relied on the LORD, he delivered them into your hand.'),
('2CH', 16, 9, '2CH.16.9', 'For the LORD’s eyes run back and forth throughout the whole earth, to show himself strong in the behalf of them whose heart is perfect toward him. You have done foolishly in this; for from now on you will have wars.”'),
('2CH', 16, 10, '2CH.16.10', 'Then Asa was angry with the seer, and put him in the prison; for he was in a rage with him because of this thing. Asa oppressed some of the people at the same time.'),
('2CH', 16, 11, '2CH.16.11', 'Behold, the acts of Asa, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel.'),
('2CH', 16, 12, '2CH.16.12', 'In the thirty-ninth year of his reign, Asa was diseased in his feet. His disease was exceedingly great; yet in his disease he didn’t seek the LORD, but just the physicians.'),
('2CH', 16, 13, '2CH.16.13', 'Asa slept with his fathers, and died in the forty-first year of his reign.'),
('2CH', 16, 14, '2CH.16.14', 'They buried him in his own tomb, which he had dug out for himself in David’s city, and laid him in the bed which was filled with sweet odors and various kinds of spices prepared by the perfumers’ art; and they made a very great fire for him.'),
('2CH', 17, 1, '2CH.17.1', 'Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his place, and strengthened himself against Israel.'),
('2CH', 17, 2, '2CH.17.2', 'He placed forces in all the fortified cities of Judah, and set garrisons in the land of Judah and in the cities of Ephraim, which Asa his father had taken.'),
('2CH', 17, 3, '2CH.17.3', 'The LORD was with Jehoshaphat, because he walked in the first ways of his father David, and didn’t seek the Baals,'),
('2CH', 17, 4, '2CH.17.4', 'but sought the God of his father, and walked in his commandments, and not in the ways of Israel.'),
('2CH', 17, 5, '2CH.17.5', 'Therefore the LORD established the kingdom in his hand. All Judah brought tribute to Jehoshaphat, and he had riches and honor in abundance.'),
('2CH', 17, 6, '2CH.17.6', 'His heart was lifted up in the ways of the LORD. Furthermore, he took away the high places and the Asherah poles out of Judah.'),
('2CH', 17, 7, '2CH.17.7', 'Also in the third year of his reign he sent his princes, even Ben Hail, Obadiah, Zechariah, Nethanel, and Micaiah, to teach in the cities of Judah;'),
('2CH', 17, 8, '2CH.17.8', 'and with them Levites, even Shemaiah, Nethaniah, Zebadiah, Asahel, Shemiramoth, Jehonathan, Adonijah, Tobijah, and Tobadonijah, the Levites; and with them Elishama and Jehoram, the priests.'),
('2CH', 17, 9, '2CH.17.9', 'They taught in Judah, having the book of the LORD’s law with them. They went about throughout all the cities of Judah and taught among the people.'),
('2CH', 17, 10, '2CH.17.10', 'The fear of the LORD fell on all the kingdoms of the lands that were around Judah, so that they made no war against Jehoshaphat.'),
('2CH', 17, 11, '2CH.17.11', 'Some of the Philistines brought Jehoshaphat presents and silver for tribute. The Arabians also brought him flocks: seven thousand seven hundred rams and seven thousand seven hundred male goats.'),
('2CH', 17, 12, '2CH.17.12', 'Jehoshaphat grew great exceedingly; and he built fortresses and store cities in Judah.'),
('2CH', 17, 13, '2CH.17.13', 'He had many works in the cities of Judah; and men of war, mighty men of valor, in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 17, 14, '2CH.17.14', 'This was the numbering of them according to their fathers’ houses: From Judah, the captains of thousands: Adnah the captain, and with him three hundred thousand mighty men of valor;'),
('2CH', 17, 15, '2CH.17.15', 'and next to him Jehohanan the captain, and with him two hundred eighty thousand;'),
('2CH', 17, 16, '2CH.17.16', 'and next to him Amasiah the son of Zichri, who willingly offered himself to the LORD, and with him two hundred thousand mighty men of valor.'),
('2CH', 17, 17, '2CH.17.17', 'From Benjamin: Eliada, a mighty man of valor, and with him two hundred thousand armed with bow and shield;'),
('2CH', 17, 18, '2CH.17.18', 'and next to him Jehozabad, and with him one hundred eighty thousand ready and prepared for war.'),
('2CH', 17, 19, '2CH.17.19', 'These were those who waited on the king, in addition to those whom the king put in the fortified cities throughout all Judah.'),
('2CH', 18, 1, '2CH.18.1', 'Now Jehoshaphat had riches and honor in abundance; and he allied himself with Ahab.'),
('2CH', 18, 2, '2CH.18.2', 'After some years, he went down to Ahab to Samaria. Ahab killed sheep and cattle for him in abundance, and for the people who were with him, and moved him to go up with him to Ramoth Gilead.'),
('2CH', 18, 3, '2CH.18.3', 'Ahab king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat king of Judah, “Will you go with me to Ramoth Gilead?” He answered him, “I am as you are, and my people as your people. We will be with you in the war.”'),
('2CH', 18, 4, '2CH.18.4', 'Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, “Please inquire first for the LORD’s word.”'),
('2CH', 18, 5, '2CH.18.5', 'Then the king of Israel gathered the prophets together, four hundred men, and said to them, “Shall we go to Ramoth Gilead to battle, or shall I forbear?” They said, “Go up, for God will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('2CH', 18, 6, '2CH.18.6', 'But Jehoshaphat said, “Isn’t there here a prophet of the LORD besides, that we may inquire of him?”'),
('2CH', 18, 7, '2CH.18.7', 'The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “There is yet one man by whom we may inquire of the LORD; but I hate him, for he never prophesies good concerning me, but always evil. He is Micaiah the son of Imla.” Jehoshaphat said, “Don’t let the king say so.”'),
('2CH', 18, 8, '2CH.18.8', 'Then the king of Israel called an officer, and said, “Get Micaiah the son of Imla quickly.”'),
('2CH', 18, 9, '2CH.18.9', 'Now the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah each sat on his throne, arrayed in their robes, and they were sitting in an open place at the entrance of the gate of Samaria; and all the prophets were prophesying before them.'),
('2CH', 18, 10, '2CH.18.10', 'Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah made himself horns of iron and said, “The LORD says, ‘With these you shall push the Syrians, until they are consumed.’”'),
('2CH', 18, 11, '2CH.18.11', 'All the prophets prophesied so, saying, “Go up to Ramoth Gilead, and prosper; for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('2CH', 18, 12, '2CH.18.12', 'The messenger who went to call Micaiah spoke to him, saying, “Behold, the words of the prophets declare good to the king with one mouth. Let your word therefore, please be like one of theirs, and speak good.”'),
('2CH', 18, 13, '2CH.18.13', 'Micaiah said, “As the LORD lives, I will say what my God says.”'),
('2CH', 18, 14, '2CH.18.14', 'When he had come to the king, the king said to him, “Micaiah, shall we go to Ramoth Gilead to battle, or shall I forbear?” He said, “Go up, and prosper. They shall be delivered into your hand.”'),
('2CH', 18, 15, '2CH.18.15', 'The king said to him, “How many times shall I adjure you that you speak to me nothing but the truth in the LORD’s name?”'),
('2CH', 18, 16, '2CH.18.16', 'He said, “I saw all Israel scattered on the mountains, as sheep that have no shepherd. The LORD said, ‘These have no master. Let them each return to his house in peace.’”'),
('2CH', 18, 17, '2CH.18.17', 'The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “Didn’t I tell you that he would not prophesy good concerning me, but evil?”'),
('2CH', 18, 18, '2CH.18.18', 'Micaiah said, “Therefore hear the LORD’s word: I saw the LORD sitting on his throne, and all the army of heaven standing on his right hand and on his left.'),
('2CH', 18, 19, '2CH.18.19', 'The LORD said, ‘Who will entice Ahab king of Israel, that he may go up and fall at Ramoth Gilead?’ One spoke saying in this way, and another saying in that way.'),
('2CH', 18, 20, '2CH.18.20', 'A spirit came out, stood before the LORD, and said, ‘I will entice him.’ “The LORD said to him, ‘How?’'),
('2CH', 18, 21, '2CH.18.21', '“He said, ‘I will go, and will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets.’ “He said, ‘You will entice him, and will prevail also. Go and do so.’'),
('2CH', 18, 22, '2CH.18.22', '“Now therefore, behold, the LORD has put a lying spirit in the mouth of these your prophets; and the LORD has spoken evil concerning you.”'),
('2CH', 18, 23, '2CH.18.23', 'Then Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah came near, and struck Micaiah on the cheek, and said, “Which way did the LORD’s Spirit go from me to speak to you?”'),
('2CH', 18, 24, '2CH.18.24', 'Micaiah said, “Behold, you shall see on that day, when you go into an inner room to hide yourself.”'),
('2CH', 18, 25, '2CH.18.25', 'The king of Israel said, “Take Micaiah, and carry him back to Amon the governor of the city, and to Joash the king’s son;'),
('2CH', 18, 26, '2CH.18.26', 'and say, ‘The king says, “Put this fellow in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I return in peace.”’”'),
('2CH', 18, 27, '2CH.18.27', 'Micaiah said, “If you return at all in peace, the LORD has not spoken by me.” He said, “Listen, you people, all of you!”'),
('2CH', 18, 28, '2CH.18.28', 'So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went up to Ramoth Gilead.'),
('2CH', 18, 29, '2CH.18.29', 'The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “I will disguise myself, and go into the battle; but you put on your robes.” So the king of Israel disguised himself; and they went into the battle.'),
('2CH', 18, 30, '2CH.18.30', 'Now the king of Syria had commanded the captains of his chariots, saying, “Don’t fight with small nor great, except only with the king of Israel.”'),
('2CH', 18, 31, '2CH.18.31', 'When the captains of the chariots saw Jehoshaphat, they said, “It is the king of Israel!” Therefore they turned around to fight against him. But Jehoshaphat cried out, and the LORD helped him; and God moved them to depart from him.'),
('2CH', 18, 32, '2CH.18.32', 'When the captains of the chariots saw that it was not the king of Israel, they turned back from pursuing him.'),
('2CH', 18, 33, '2CH.18.33', 'A certain man drew his bow at random, and struck the king of Israel between the joints of the armor. Therefore he said to the driver of the chariot, “Turn around and carry me out of the battle, for I am severely wounded.”'),
('2CH', 18, 34, '2CH.18.34', 'The battle increased that day. However, the king of Israel propped himself up in his chariot against the Syrians until the evening; and at about sunset, he died.'),
('2CH', 19, 1, '2CH.19.1', 'Jehoshaphat the king of Judah returned to his house in peace to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 19, 2, '2CH.19.2', 'Jehu the son of Hanani the seer went out to meet him, and said to King Jehoshaphat, “Should you help the wicked, and love those who hate the LORD? Because of this, wrath is on you from before the LORD.'),
('2CH', 19, 3, '2CH.19.3', 'Nevertheless there are good things found in you, in that you have put away the Asheroth out of the land, and have set your heart to seek God.”'),
('2CH', 19, 4, '2CH.19.4', 'Jehoshaphat lived at Jerusalem; and he went out again among the people from Beersheba to the hill country of Ephraim, and brought them back to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 19, 5, '2CH.19.5', 'He set judges in the land throughout all the fortified cities of Judah, city by city,'),
('2CH', 19, 6, '2CH.19.6', 'and said to the judges, “Consider what you do, for you don’t judge for man, but for the LORD; and he is with you in the judgment.'),
('2CH', 19, 7, '2CH.19.7', 'Now therefore let the fear of the LORD be on you. Take heed and do it; for there is no iniquity with the LORD our God, nor respect of persons, nor taking of bribes.”'),
('2CH', 19, 8, '2CH.19.8', 'Moreover in Jerusalem Jehoshaphat appointed certain Levites, priests, and heads of the fathers’ households of Israel to give judgment for the LORD and for controversies. They returned to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 19, 9, '2CH.19.9', 'He commanded them, saying, “You shall do this in the fear of the LORD, faithfully, and with a perfect heart.'),
('2CH', 19, 10, '2CH.19.10', 'Whenever any controversy comes to you from your brothers who dwell in their cities, between blood and blood, between law and commandment, statutes and ordinances, you must warn them, that they not be guilty toward the LORD, and so wrath come on you and on your brothers. Do this, and you will not be guilty.'),
('2CH', 19, 11, '2CH.19.11', 'Behold, Amariah the chief priest is over you in all matters of the LORD; and Zebadiah the son of Ishmael, the ruler of the house of Judah, in all the king’s matters. Also the Levites shall be officers before you. Deal courageously, and may the LORD be with the good.”'),
('2CH', 20, 1, '2CH.20.1', 'After this, the children of Moab, the children of Ammon, and with them some of the Meunites, came against Jehoshaphat to battle.'),
('2CH', 20, 2, '2CH.20.2', 'Then some came who told Jehoshaphat, saying, “A great multitude is coming against you from beyond the sea from Syria. Behold, they are in Hazazon Tamar” (that is, En Gedi).'),
('2CH', 20, 3, '2CH.20.3', 'Jehoshaphat was alarmed, and set himself to seek the LORD. He proclaimed a fast throughout all Judah.'),
('2CH', 20, 4, '2CH.20.4', 'Judah gathered themselves together to seek help from the LORD. They came out of all the cities of Judah to seek the LORD.'),
('2CH', 20, 5, '2CH.20.5', 'Jehoshaphat stood in the assembly of Judah and Jerusalem, in the LORD’s house, before the new court;'),
('2CH', 20, 6, '2CH.20.6', 'and he said, “LORD, the God of our fathers, aren’t you God in heaven? Aren’t you ruler over all the kingdoms of the nations? Power and might are in your hand, so that no one is able to withstand you.'),
('2CH', 20, 7, '2CH.20.7', 'Didn’t you, our God, drive out the inhabitants of this land before your people Israel, and give it to the offspring of Abraham your friend forever?'),
('2CH', 20, 8, '2CH.20.8', 'They lived in it, and have built you a sanctuary in it for your name, saying,'),
('2CH', 20, 9, '2CH.20.9', '‘If evil comes on us—the sword, judgment, pestilence, or famine—we will stand before this house, and before you (for your name is in this house), and cry to you in our affliction, and you will hear and save.’'),
('2CH', 20, 10, '2CH.20.10', 'Now, behold, the children of Ammon and Moab and Mount Seir, whom you would not let Israel invade when they came out of the land of Egypt, but they turned away from them, and didn’t destroy them;'),
('2CH', 20, 11, '2CH.20.11', 'behold, how they reward us, to come to cast us out of your possession, which you have given us to inherit.'),
('2CH', 20, 12, '2CH.20.12', 'Our God, will you not judge them? For we have no might against this great company that comes against us. We don’t know what to do, but our eyes are on you.”'),
('2CH', 20, 13, '2CH.20.13', 'All Judah stood before the LORD, with their little ones, their wives, and their children.'),
('2CH', 20, 14, '2CH.20.14', 'Then the LORD’s Spirit came on Jahaziel the son of Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, the Levite, of the sons of Asaph, in the middle of the assembly;'),
('2CH', 20, 15, '2CH.20.15', 'and he said, “Listen, all Judah, and you inhabitants of Jerusalem, and you, King Jehoshaphat. The LORD says to you, ‘Don’t be afraid, and don’t be dismayed because of this great multitude; for the battle is not yours, but God’s.'),
('2CH', 20, 16, '2CH.20.16', 'Tomorrow, go down against them. Behold, they are coming up by the ascent of Ziz. You will find them at the end of the valley, before the wilderness of Jeruel.'),
('2CH', 20, 17, '2CH.20.17', 'You will not need to fight this battle. Set yourselves, stand still, and see the salvation of the LORD with you, O Judah and Jerusalem. Don’t be afraid, nor be dismayed. Go out against them tomorrow, for the LORD is with you.’”'),
('2CH', 20, 18, '2CH.20.18', 'Jehoshaphat bowed his head with his face to the ground; and all Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem fell down before the LORD, worshiping the LORD.'),
('2CH', 20, 19, '2CH.20.19', 'The Levites, of the children of the Kohathites and of the children of the Korahites, stood up to praise the LORD, the God of Israel, with an exceedingly loud voice.'),
('2CH', 20, 20, '2CH.20.20', 'They rose early in the morning and went out into the wilderness of Tekoa. As they went out, Jehoshaphat stood and said, “Listen to me, Judah and you inhabitants of Jerusalem! Believe in the LORD your God, so you will be established! Believe his prophets, so you will prosper.”'),
('2CH', 20, 21, '2CH.20.21', 'When he had taken counsel with the people, he appointed those who were to sing to the LORD and give praise in holy array as they go out before the army, and say, “Give thanks to the LORD, for his loving kindness endures forever.”'),
('2CH', 20, 22, '2CH.20.22', 'When they began to sing and to praise, the LORD set ambushers against the children of Ammon, Moab, and Mount Seir, who had come against Judah; and they were struck.'),
('2CH', 20, 23, '2CH.20.23', 'For the children of Ammon and Moab stood up against the inhabitants of Mount Seir to utterly kill and destroy them. When they had finished the inhabitants of Seir, everyone helped to destroy each other.'),
('2CH', 20, 24, '2CH.20.24', 'When Judah came to the place overlooking the wilderness, they looked at the multitude; and behold, they were dead bodies fallen to the earth, and there were none who escaped.'),
('2CH', 20, 25, '2CH.20.25', 'When Jehoshaphat and his people came to take their plunder, they found among them in abundance both riches and dead bodies with precious jewels, which they stripped off for themselves, more than they could carry away. They took plunder for three days, it was so much.'),
('2CH', 20, 26, '2CH.20.26', 'On the fourth day, they assembled themselves in Beracah Valley, for there they blessed the LORD. Therefore the name of that place was called “Beracah Valley” to this day.'),
('2CH', 20, 27, '2CH.20.27', 'Then they returned, every man of Judah and Jerusalem, with Jehoshaphat in front of them, to go again to Jerusalem with joy; for the LORD had made them to rejoice over their enemies.'),
('2CH', 20, 28, '2CH.20.28', 'They came to Jerusalem with stringed instruments, harps, and trumpets to the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 20, 29, '2CH.20.29', 'The fear of God was on all the kingdoms of the countries when they heard that the LORD fought against the enemies of Israel.'),
('2CH', 20, 30, '2CH.20.30', 'So the realm of Jehoshaphat was quiet, for his God gave him rest all around.'),
('2CH', 20, 31, '2CH.20.31', 'So Jehoshaphat reigned over Judah. He was thirty-five years old when he began to reign. He reigned twenty-five years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Azubah the daughter of Shilhi.'),
('2CH', 20, 32, '2CH.20.32', 'He walked in the way of Asa his father, and didn’t turn away from it, doing that which was right in the LORD’s eyes.'),
('2CH', 20, 33, '2CH.20.33', 'However the high places were not taken away, and the people had still not set their hearts on the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 20, 34, '2CH.20.34', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, first and last, behold, they are written in the history of Jehu the son of Hanani, which is included in the book of the kings of Israel.'),
('2CH', 20, 35, '2CH.20.35', 'After this, Jehoshaphat king of Judah joined himself with Ahaziah king of Israel. The same did very wickedly.'),
('2CH', 20, 36, '2CH.20.36', 'He joined himself with him to make ships to go to Tarshish. They made the ships in Ezion Geber.'),
('2CH', 20, 37, '2CH.20.37', 'Then Eliezer the son of Dodavahu of Mareshah prophesied against Jehoshaphat, saying, “Because you have joined yourself with Ahaziah, the LORD has destroyed your works.” The ships were wrecked, so that they were not able to go to Tarshish.'),
('2CH', 21, 1, '2CH.21.1', 'Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David’s city; and Jehoram his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 21, 2, '2CH.21.2', 'He had brothers, the sons of Jehoshaphat: Azariah, Jehiel, Zechariah, Azariah, Michael, and Shephatiah. All these were the sons of Jehoshaphat king of Israel.'),
('2CH', 21, 3, '2CH.21.3', 'Their father gave them great gifts of silver, of gold, and of precious things, with fortified cities in Judah; but he gave the kingdom to Jehoram, because he was the firstborn.'),
('2CH', 21, 4, '2CH.21.4', 'Now when Jehoram had risen up over the kingdom of his father, and had strengthened himself, he killed all his brothers with the sword, and also some of the princes of Israel.'),
('2CH', 21, 5, '2CH.21.5', 'Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 21, 6, '2CH.21.6', 'He walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did Ahab’s house, for he had Ahab’s daughter as his wife. He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight.'),
('2CH', 21, 7, '2CH.21.7', 'However the LORD would not destroy David’s house, because of the covenant that he had made with David, and as he promised to give a lamp to him and to his children always.'),
('2CH', 21, 8, '2CH.21.8', 'In his days Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah, and made a king over themselves.'),
('2CH', 21, 9, '2CH.21.9', 'Then Jehoram went there with his captains and all his chariots with him. He rose up by night and struck the Edomites who surrounded him, along with the captains of the chariots.'),
('2CH', 21, 10, '2CH.21.10', 'So Edom has been in revolt from under the hand of Judah to this day. Then Libnah revolted at the same time from under his hand, because he had forsaken the LORD, the God of his fathers.'),
('2CH', 21, 11, '2CH.21.11', 'Moreover he made high places in the mountains of Judah, and made the inhabitants of Jerusalem play the prostitute, and led Judah astray.'),
('2CH', 21, 12, '2CH.21.12', 'A letter came to him from Elijah the prophet, saying, “the LORD, the God of David your father, says, ‘Because you have not walked in the ways of Jehoshaphat your father, nor in the ways of Asa king of Judah,'),
('2CH', 21, 13, '2CH.21.13', 'but have walked in the way of the kings of Israel, and have made Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem to play the prostitute like Ahab’s house did, and also have slain your brothers of your father’s house, who were better than yourself,'),
('2CH', 21, 14, '2CH.21.14', 'behold, the LORD will strike your people with a great plague, including your children, your wives, and all your possessions;'),
('2CH', 21, 15, '2CH.21.15', 'and you will have great sickness with a disease of your bowels, until your bowels fall out by reason of the sickness, day by day.’”'),
('2CH', 21, 16, '2CH.21.16', 'The LORD stirred up against Jehoram the spirit of the Philistines and of the Arabians who are beside the Ethiopians;'),
('2CH', 21, 17, '2CH.21.17', 'and they came up against Judah, broke into it, and carried away all the possessions that were found in the king’s house, including his sons and his wives, so that there was no son left to him except Jehoahaz, the youngest of his sons.'),
('2CH', 21, 18, '2CH.21.18', 'After all this the LORD struck him in his bowels with an incurable disease.'),
('2CH', 21, 19, '2CH.21.19', 'In process of time, at the end of two years, his bowels fell out by reason of his sickness, and he died of severe diseases. His people made no burning for him, like the burning of his fathers.'),
('2CH', 21, 20, '2CH.21.20', 'He was thirty-two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years. He departed with no one’s regret. They buried him in David’s city, but not in the tombs of the kings.'),
('2CH', 22, 1, '2CH.22.1', 'The inhabitants of Jerusalem made Ahaziah his youngest son king in his place, because the band of men who came with the Arabians to the camp had slain all the oldest. So Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah reigned.'),
('2CH', 22, 2, '2CH.22.2', 'Ahaziah was forty-two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Athaliah the daughter of Omri.'),
('2CH', 22, 3, '2CH.22.3', 'He also walked in the ways of Ahab’s house, because his mother was his counselor in acting wickedly.'),
('2CH', 22, 4, '2CH.22.4', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, as did Ahab’s house, for they were his counselors after the death of his father, to his destruction.'),
('2CH', 22, 5, '2CH.22.5', 'He also followed their counsel, and went with Jehoram the son of Ahab king of Israel to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth Gilead; and the Syrians wounded Joram.'),
('2CH', 22, 6, '2CH.22.6', 'He returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which they had given him at Ramah, when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. Azariah the son of Jehoram, king of Judah, went down to see Jehoram the son of Ahab in Jezreel, because he was sick.'),
('2CH', 22, 7, '2CH.22.7', 'Now the destruction of Ahaziah was of God, in that he went to Joram; for when he had come, he went out with Jehoram against Jehu the son of Nimshi, whom the LORD had anointed to cut off Ahab’s house.'),
('2CH', 22, 8, '2CH.22.8', 'When Jehu was executing judgment on Ahab’s house, he found the princes of Judah and the sons of the brothers of Ahaziah serving Ahaziah, and killed them.'),
('2CH', 22, 9, '2CH.22.9', 'He sought Ahaziah, and they caught him (now he was hiding in Samaria), and they brought him to Jehu and killed him; and they buried him, for they said, “He is the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart.” The house of Ahaziah had no power to hold the kingdom.'),
('2CH', 22, 10, '2CH.22.10', 'Now when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the royal offspring of the house of Judah.'),
('2CH', 22, 11, '2CH.22.11', 'But Jehoshabeath, the king’s daughter, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stealthily rescued him from among the king’s sons who were slain, and put him and his nurse in the bedroom. So Jehoshabeath, the daughter of King Jehoram, the wife of Jehoiada the priest (for she was the sister of Ahaziah), hid him from Athaliah, so that she didn’t kill him.'),
('2CH', 22, 12, '2CH.22.12', 'He was with them hidden in God’s house six years while Athaliah reigned over the land.'),
('2CH', 23, 1, '2CH.23.1', 'In the seventh year, Jehoiada strengthened himself, and took the captains of hundreds—Azariah the son of Jeroham, Ishmael the son of Jehohanan, Azariah the son of Obed, Maaseiah the son of Adaiah, and Elishaphat the son of Zichri—into a covenant with him.'),
('2CH', 23, 2, '2CH.23.2', 'They went around in Judah and gathered the Levites out of all the cities of Judah, and the heads of fathers’ households of Israel, and they came to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 23, 3, '2CH.23.3', 'All the assembly made a covenant with the king in God’s house. Jehoiada said to them, “Behold, the king’s son must reign, as the LORD has spoken concerning the sons of David.'),
('2CH', 23, 4, '2CH.23.4', 'This is the thing that you must do: a third part of you, who come in on the Sabbath, of the priests and of the Levites, shall be gatekeepers of the thresholds.'),
('2CH', 23, 5, '2CH.23.5', 'A third part shall be at the king’s house; and a third part at the gate of the foundation. All the people will be in the courts of the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 23, 6, '2CH.23.6', 'But let no one come into the LORD’s house except the priests and those who minister of the Levites. They shall come in, for they are holy, but all the people shall follow the LORD’s instructions.'),
('2CH', 23, 7, '2CH.23.7', 'The Levites shall surround the king, every man with his weapons in his hand. Whoever comes into the house, let him be slain. Be with the king when he comes in and when he goes out.”'),
('2CH', 23, 8, '2CH.23.8', 'So the Levites and all Judah did according to all that Jehoiada the priest commanded. They each took his men, those who were to come in on the Sabbath, with those who were to go out on the Sabbath, for Jehoiada the priest didn’t dismiss the shift.'),
('2CH', 23, 9, '2CH.23.9', 'Jehoiada the priest delivered to the captains of hundreds the spears, bucklers, and shields that had been king David’s, which were in God’s house.'),
('2CH', 23, 10, '2CH.23.10', 'He set all the people, every man with his weapon in his hand, from the right side of the house to the left side of the house, near the altar and the house, around the king.'),
('2CH', 23, 11, '2CH.23.11', 'Then they brought out the king’s son, put the crown on him, gave him the covenant, and made him king. Jehoiada and his sons anointed him, and they said, “Long live the king!”'),
('2CH', 23, 12, '2CH.23.12', 'When Athaliah heard the noise of the people running and praising the king, she came to the people into the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 23, 13, '2CH.23.13', 'Then she looked, and behold, the king stood by his pillar at the entrance, with the captains and the trumpeters by the king. All the people of the land rejoiced and blew trumpets. The singers also played musical instruments, and led the singing of praise. Then Athaliah tore her clothes, and said, “Treason! treason!”'),
('2CH', 23, 14, '2CH.23.14', 'Jehoiada the priest brought out the captains of hundreds who were set over the army, and said to them, “Bring her out between the ranks; and whoever follows her, let him be slain with the sword.” For the priest said, “Don’t kill her in the LORD’s house.”'),
('2CH', 23, 15, '2CH.23.15', 'So they made way for her. She went to the entrance of the horse gate to the king’s house; and they killed her there.'),
('2CH', 23, 16, '2CH.23.16', 'Jehoiada made a covenant between himself, all the people, and the king, that they should be the LORD’s people.'),
('2CH', 23, 17, '2CH.23.17', 'All the people went to the house of Baal, broke it down, broke his altars and his images in pieces, and killed Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars.'),
('2CH', 23, 18, '2CH.23.18', 'Jehoiada appointed the officers of the LORD’s house under the hand of the Levitical priests, whom David had distributed in the LORD’s house, to offer the burnt offerings of the LORD, as it is written in the law of Moses, with rejoicing and with singing, as David had ordered.'),
('2CH', 23, 19, '2CH.23.19', 'He set the gatekeepers at the gates of the LORD’s house, that no one who was unclean in anything should enter in.'),
('2CH', 23, 20, '2CH.23.20', 'He took the captains of hundreds, the nobles, the governors of the people, and all the people of the land, and brought the king down from the LORD’s house. They came through the upper gate to the king’s house, and set the king on the throne of the kingdom.'),
('2CH', 23, 21, '2CH.23.21', 'So all the people of the land rejoiced, and the city was quiet. They had slain Athaliah with the sword.'),
('2CH', 24, 1, '2CH.24.1', 'Joash was seven years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Zibiah, of Beersheba.'),
('2CH', 24, 2, '2CH.24.2', 'Joash did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes all the days of Jehoiada the priest.'),
('2CH', 24, 3, '2CH.24.3', 'Jehoiada took for him two wives, and he became the father of sons and daughters.'),
('2CH', 24, 4, '2CH.24.4', 'After this, Joash intended to restore the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 24, 5, '2CH.24.5', 'He gathered together the priests and the Levites, and said to them, “Go out to the cities of Judah, and gather money to repair the house of your God from all Israel from year to year. See that you expedite this matter.” However the Levites didn’t do it right away.'),
('2CH', 24, 6, '2CH.24.6', 'The king called for Jehoiada the chief, and said to him, “Why haven’t you required of the Levites to bring in the tax of Moses the servant of the LORD, and of the assembly of Israel, out of Judah and out of Jerusalem, for the Tent of the Testimony?”'),
('2CH', 24, 7, '2CH.24.7', 'For the sons of Athaliah, that wicked woman, had broken up God’s house; and they also gave all the dedicated things of the LORD’s house to the Baals.'),
('2CH', 24, 8, '2CH.24.8', 'So the king commanded, and they made a chest, and set it outside at the gate of the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 24, 9, '2CH.24.9', 'They made a proclamation through Judah and Jerusalem, to bring in for the LORD the tax that Moses the servant of God laid on Israel in the wilderness.'),
('2CH', 24, 10, '2CH.24.10', 'All the princes and all the people rejoiced, and brought in, and cast into the chest, until they had filled it.'),
('2CH', 24, 11, '2CH.24.11', 'Whenever the chest was brought to the king’s officers by the hand of the Levites, and when they saw that there was much money, the king’s scribe and the chief priest’s officer came and emptied the chest, and took it, and carried it to its place again. Thus they did day by day, and gathered money in abundance.'),
('2CH', 24, 12, '2CH.24.12', 'The king and Jehoiada gave it to those who did the work of the service of the LORD’s house. They hired masons and carpenters to restore the LORD’s house, and also those who worked iron and bronze to repair the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 24, 13, '2CH.24.13', 'So the workmen worked, and the work of repairing went forward in their hands. They set up God’s house as it was designed, and strengthened it.'),
('2CH', 24, 14, '2CH.24.14', 'When they had finished, they brought the rest of the money before the king and Jehoiada, from which were made vessels for the LORD’s house, even vessels with which to minister and to offer, including spoons and vessels of gold and silver. They offered burnt offerings in the LORD’s house continually all the days of Jehoiada.'),
('2CH', 24, 15, '2CH.24.15', 'But Jehoiada grew old and was full of days, and he died. He was one hundred thirty years old when he died.'),
('2CH', 24, 16, '2CH.24.16', 'They buried him in David’s city among the kings, because he had done good in Israel, and toward God and his house.'),
('2CH', 24, 17, '2CH.24.17', 'Now after the death of Jehoiada, the princes of Judah came and bowed down to the king. Then the king listened to them.'),
('2CH', 24, 18, '2CH.24.18', 'They abandoned the house of the LORD, the God of their fathers, and served the Asherah poles and the idols, so wrath came on Judah and Jerusalem for this their guiltiness.'),
('2CH', 24, 19, '2CH.24.19', 'Yet he sent prophets to them to bring them again to the LORD, and they testified against them; but they would not listen.'),
('2CH', 24, 20, '2CH.24.20', 'The Spirit of God came on Zechariah the son of Jehoiada the priest; and he stood above the people, and said to them, “God says, ‘Why do you disobey the LORD’s commandments, so that you can’t prosper? Because you have forsaken the LORD, he has also forsaken you.’”'),
('2CH', 24, 21, '2CH.24.21', 'They conspired against him, and stoned him with stones at the commandment of the king in the court of the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 24, 22, '2CH.24.22', 'Thus Joash the king didn’t remember the kindness which Jehoiada his father had done to him, but killed his son. When he died, he said, “May the LORD look at it, and repay it.”'),
('2CH', 24, 23, '2CH.24.23', 'At the end of the year, the army of the Syrians came up against him. They came to Judah and Jerusalem, and destroyed all the princes of the people from among the people, and sent all their plunder to the king of Damascus.'),
('2CH', 24, 24, '2CH.24.24', 'For the army of the Syrians came with a small company of men; and the LORD delivered a very great army into their hand, because they had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers. So they executed judgment on Joash.'),
('2CH', 24, 25, '2CH.24.25', 'When they had departed from him (for they left him seriously wounded), his own servants conspired against him for the blood of the sons of Jehoiada the priest, and killed him on his bed, and he died. They buried him in David’s city, but they didn’t bury him in the tombs of the kings.'),
('2CH', 24, 26, '2CH.24.26', 'These are those who conspired against him: Zabad the son of Shimeath the Ammonitess and Jehozabad the son of Shimrith the Moabitess.'),
('2CH', 24, 27, '2CH.24.27', 'Now concerning his sons, the greatness of the burdens laid on him, and the rebuilding of God’s house, behold, they are written in the commentary of the book of the kings. Amaziah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 25, 1, '2CH.25.1', 'Amaziah was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Jehoaddan, of Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 25, 2, '2CH.25.2', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, but not with a perfect heart.'),
('2CH', 25, 3, '2CH.25.3', 'Now when the kingdom was established to him, he killed his servants who had killed his father the king.'),
('2CH', 25, 4, '2CH.25.4', 'But he didn’t put their children to death, but did according to that which is written in the law in the book of Moses, as the LORD commanded, saying, “The fathers shall not die for the children, neither shall the children die for the fathers; but every man shall die for his own sin.”'),
('2CH', 25, 5, '2CH.25.5', 'Moreover Amaziah gathered Judah together and ordered them according to their fathers’ houses, under captains of thousands and captains of hundreds, even all Judah and Benjamin. He counted them from twenty years old and upward, and found that there were three hundred thousand chosen men, able to go out to war, who could handle spear and shield.'),
('2CH', 25, 6, '2CH.25.6', 'He also hired one hundred thousand mighty men of valor out of Israel for one hundred talents of silver.'),
('2CH', 25, 7, '2CH.25.7', 'A man of God came to him, saying, “O king, don’t let the army of Israel go with you, for the LORD is not with Israel, with all the children of Ephraim.'),
('2CH', 25, 8, '2CH.25.8', 'But if you will go, take action, and be strong for the battle. God will overthrow you before the enemy; for God has power to help, and to overthrow.”'),
('2CH', 25, 9, '2CH.25.9', 'Amaziah said to the man of God, “But what shall we do for the hundred talents which I have given to the army of Israel?” The man of God answered, “The LORD is able to give you much more than this.”'),
('2CH', 25, 10, '2CH.25.10', 'Then Amaziah separated them, the army that had come to him out of Ephraim, to go home again. Therefore their anger was greatly kindled against Judah, and they returned home in fierce anger.'),
('2CH', 25, 11, '2CH.25.11', 'Amaziah took courage, and led his people out and went to the Valley of Salt, and struck ten thousand of the children of Seir.'),
('2CH', 25, 12, '2CH.25.12', 'The children of Judah carried away ten thousand alive, and brought them to the top of the rock, and threw them down from the top of the rock, so that they all were broken in pieces.'),
('2CH', 25, 13, '2CH.25.13', 'But the men of the army whom Amaziah sent back, that they should not go with him to battle, fell on the cities of Judah from Samaria even to Beth Horon, and struck of them three thousand, and took much plunder.'),
('2CH', 25, 14, '2CH.25.14', 'Now after Amaziah had come from the slaughter of the Edomites, he brought the gods of the children of Seir, and set them up to be his gods, and bowed down himself before them and burned incense to them.'),
('2CH', 25, 15, '2CH.25.15', 'Therefore the LORD’s anger burned against Amaziah, and he sent to him a prophet who said to him, “Why have you sought after the gods of the people, which have not delivered their own people out of your hand?”'),
('2CH', 25, 16, '2CH.25.16', 'As he talked with him, the king said to him, “Have we made you one of the king’s counselors? Stop! Why should you be struck down?” Then the prophet stopped, and said, “I know that God has determined to destroy you, because you have done this and have not listened to my counsel.”'),
('2CH', 25, 17, '2CH.25.17', 'Then Amaziah king of Judah consulted his advisers, and sent to Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, “Come! Let’s look one another in the face.”'),
('2CH', 25, 18, '2CH.25.18', 'Joash king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, “The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, ‘Give your daughter to my son as his wife. Then a wild animal that was in Lebanon passed by and trampled down the thistle.'),
('2CH', 25, 19, '2CH.25.19', 'You say to yourself that you have struck Edom; and your heart lifts you up to boast. Now stay at home. Why should you meddle with trouble, that you should fall, even you and Judah with you?’”'),
('2CH', 25, 20, '2CH.25.20', 'But Amaziah would not listen; for it was of God, that he might deliver them into the hand of their enemies, because they had sought after the gods of Edom.'),
('2CH', 25, 21, '2CH.25.21', 'So Joash king of Israel went up, and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Beth Shemesh, which belongs to Judah.'),
('2CH', 25, 22, '2CH.25.22', 'Judah was defeated by Israel; so every man fled to his tent.'),
('2CH', 25, 23, '2CH.25.23', 'Joash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Joash the son of Jehoahaz, at Beth Shemesh and brought him to Jerusalem, and broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate, four hundred cubits.'),
('2CH', 25, 24, '2CH.25.24', 'He took all the gold and silver, and all the vessels that were found in God’s house with Obed-Edom, and the treasures of the king’s house, and the hostages, and returned to Samaria.'),
('2CH', 25, 25, '2CH.25.25', 'Amaziah the son of Joash, king of Judah, lived for fifteen years after the death of Joash, son of Jehoahaz, king of Israel.'),
('2CH', 25, 26, '2CH.25.26', 'Now the rest of the acts of Amaziah, first and last, behold, aren’t they written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel?'),
('2CH', 25, 27, '2CH.25.27', 'Now from the time that Amaziah turned away from following the LORD, they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem. He fled to Lachish, but they sent after him to Lachish and killed him there.'),
('2CH', 25, 28, '2CH.25.28', 'They brought him on horses and buried him with his fathers in the City of Judah.'),
('2CH', 26, 1, '2CH.26.1', 'All the people of Judah took Uzziah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in the place of his father Amaziah.'),
('2CH', 26, 2, '2CH.26.2', 'He built Eloth and restored it to Judah. After that the king slept with his fathers.'),
('2CH', 26, 3, '2CH.26.3', 'Uzziah was sixteen years old when he began to reign; and he reigned fifty-two years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Jechiliah, of Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 26, 4, '2CH.26.4', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, according to all that his father Amaziah had done.'),
('2CH', 26, 5, '2CH.26.5', 'He set himself to seek God in the days of Zechariah, who had understanding in the vision of God; and as long as he sought the LORD, God made him prosper.'),
('2CH', 26, 6, '2CH.26.6', 'He went out and fought against the Philistines, and broke down the wall of Gath, the wall of Jabneh, and the wall of Ashdod; and he built cities in the country of Ashdod, and among the Philistines.'),
('2CH', 26, 7, '2CH.26.7', 'God helped him against the Philistines, and against the Arabians who lived in Gur Baal, and the Meunim.'),
('2CH', 26, 8, '2CH.26.8', 'The Ammonites gave tribute to Uzziah. His name spread abroad even to the entrance of Egypt, for he grew exceedingly strong.'),
('2CH', 26, 9, '2CH.26.9', 'Moreover Uzziah built towers in Jerusalem at the corner gate, at the valley gate, and at the turning of the wall, and fortified them.'),
('2CH', 26, 10, '2CH.26.10', 'He built towers in the wilderness, and dug out many cisterns, for he had much livestock, both in the lowlands and in the plains. He had farmers and vineyard keepers in the mountains and in the fruitful fields, for he loved farming.'),
('2CH', 26, 11, '2CH.26.11', 'Moreover Uzziah had an army of fighting men who went out to war by bands, according to the number of their reckoning made by Jeiel the scribe and Maaseiah the officer, under the hand of Hananiah, one of the king’s captains.'),
('2CH', 26, 12, '2CH.26.12', 'The whole number of the heads of fathers’ households, even the mighty men of valor, was two thousand six hundred.'),
('2CH', 26, 13, '2CH.26.13', 'Under their hand was an army, three hundred seven thousand five hundred, who made war with mighty power, to help the king against the enemy.'),
('2CH', 26, 14, '2CH.26.14', 'Uzziah prepared for them, even for all the army, shields, spears, helmets, coats of mail, bows, and stones for slinging.'),
('2CH', 26, 15, '2CH.26.15', 'In Jerusalem, he made devices, invented by skillful men, to be on the towers and on the battlements, with which to shoot arrows and great stones. His name spread far abroad, because he was marvelously helped until he was strong.'),
('2CH', 26, 16, '2CH.26.16', 'But when he was strong, his heart was lifted up, so that he did corruptly and he trespassed against the LORD his God, for he went into the LORD’s temple to burn incense on the altar of incense.'),
('2CH', 26, 17, '2CH.26.17', 'Azariah the priest went in after him, and with him eighty priests of the LORD, who were valiant men.'),
('2CH', 26, 18, '2CH.26.18', 'They resisted Uzziah the king, and said to him, “It isn’t for you, Uzziah, to burn incense to the LORD, but for the priests the sons of Aaron, who are consecrated to burn incense. Go out of the sanctuary, for you have trespassed. It will not be for your honor from the LORD God.”'),
('2CH', 26, 19, '2CH.26.19', 'Then Uzziah was angry. He had a censer in his hand to burn incense, and while he was angry with the priests, the leprosy broke out on his forehead before the priests in the LORD’s house, beside the altar of incense.'),
('2CH', 26, 20, '2CH.26.20', 'Azariah the chief priest and all the priests looked at him, and behold, he was leprous in his forehead; and they thrust him out quickly from there. Indeed, he himself also hurried to go out, because the LORD had struck him.'),
('2CH', 26, 21, '2CH.26.21', 'Uzziah the king was a leper to the day of his death, and lived in a separate house, being a leper; for he was cut off from the LORD’s house. Jotham his son was over the king’s house, judging the people of the land.'),
('2CH', 26, 22, '2CH.26.22', 'Now the rest of the acts of Uzziah, first and last, Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, wrote.'),
('2CH', 26, 23, '2CH.26.23', 'So Uzziah slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in the field of burial which belonged to the kings, for they said, “He is a leper.” Jotham his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 27, 1, '2CH.27.1', 'Jotham was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Jerushah the daughter of Zadok.'),
('2CH', 27, 2, '2CH.27.2', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, according to all that his father Uzziah had done. However he didn’t enter into the LORD’s temple. The people still acted corruptly.'),
('2CH', 27, 3, '2CH.27.3', 'He built the upper gate of the LORD’s house, and he built much on the wall of Ophel.'),
('2CH', 27, 4, '2CH.27.4', 'Moreover he built cities in the hill country of Judah, and in the forests he built fortresses and towers.'),
('2CH', 27, 5, '2CH.27.5', 'He also fought with the king of the children of Ammon, and prevailed against them. The children of Ammon gave him the same year one hundred talents of silver, ten thousand cors of wheat, and ten thousand cors of barley. The children of Ammon also gave that much to him in the second year, and in the third.'),
('2CH', 27, 6, '2CH.27.6', 'So Jotham became mighty, because he ordered his ways before the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 27, 7, '2CH.27.7', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jotham, and all his wars and his ways, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah.'),
('2CH', 27, 8, '2CH.27.8', 'He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 27, 9, '2CH.27.9', 'Jotham slept with his fathers, and they buried him in David’s city; and Ahaz his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 28, 1, '2CH.28.1', 'Ahaz was twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. He didn’t do that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, like David his father,'),
('2CH', 28, 2, '2CH.28.2', 'but he walked in the ways of the kings of Israel, and also made molten images for the Baals.'),
('2CH', 28, 3, '2CH.28.3', 'Moreover he burned incense in the valley of the son of Hinnom, and burned his children in the fire, according to the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.'),
('2CH', 28, 4, '2CH.28.4', 'He sacrificed and burned incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree.'),
('2CH', 28, 5, '2CH.28.5', 'Therefore the LORD his God delivered him into the hand of the king of Syria. They struck him, and carried away from him a great multitude of captives, and brought them to Damascus. He was also delivered into the hand of the king of Israel, who struck him with a great slaughter.'),
('2CH', 28, 6, '2CH.28.6', 'For Pekah the son of Remaliah killed in Judah one hundred twenty thousand in one day, all of them valiant men, because they had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 28, 7, '2CH.28.7', 'Zichri, a mighty man of Ephraim, killed Maaseiah the king’s son, Azrikam the ruler of the house, and Elkanah who was next to the king.'),
('2CH', 28, 8, '2CH.28.8', 'The children of Israel carried away captive of their brothers two hundred thousand women, sons, and daughters, and also took away much plunder from them, and brought the plunder to Samaria.'),
('2CH', 28, 9, '2CH.28.9', 'But a prophet of the LORD was there, whose name was Oded; and he went out to meet the army that came to Samaria, and said to them, “Behold, because the LORD, the God of your fathers, was angry with Judah, he has delivered them into your hand, and you have slain them in a rage which has reached up to heaven.'),
('2CH', 28, 10, '2CH.28.10', 'Now you intend to degrade the children of Judah and Jerusalem as male and female slaves for yourselves. Aren’t there even with you trespasses of your own against the LORD your God?'),
('2CH', 28, 11, '2CH.28.11', 'Now hear me therefore, and send back the captives that you have taken captive from your brothers, for the fierce wrath of the LORD is on you.”'),
('2CH', 28, 12, '2CH.28.12', 'Then some of the heads of the children of Ephraim, Azariah the son of Johanan, Berechiah the son of Meshillemoth, Jehizkiah the son of Shallum, and Amasa the son of Hadlai, stood up against those who came from the war,'),
('2CH', 28, 13, '2CH.28.13', 'and said to them, “You must not bring in the captives here, for you intend that which will bring on us a trespass against the LORD, to add to our sins and to our guilt; for our guilt is great, and there is fierce wrath against Israel.”'),
('2CH', 28, 14, '2CH.28.14', 'So the armed men left the captives and the plunder before the princes and all the assembly.'),
('2CH', 28, 15, '2CH.28.15', 'The men who have been mentioned by name rose up and took the captives, and with the plunder clothed all who were naked among them, dressed them, gave them sandals, gave them something to eat and to drink, anointed them, carried all the feeble of them on donkeys, and brought them to Jericho, the city of palm trees, to their brothers. Then they returned to Samaria.'),
('2CH', 28, 16, '2CH.28.16', 'At that time King Ahaz sent to the kings of Assyria to help him.'),
('2CH', 28, 17, '2CH.28.17', 'For again the Edomites had come and struck Judah, and carried away captives.'),
('2CH', 28, 18, '2CH.28.18', 'The Philistines also had invaded the cities of the lowland and of the South of Judah, and had taken Beth Shemesh, Aijalon, Gederoth, Soco with its villages, Timnah with its villages, and also Gimzo and its villages; and they lived there.'),
('2CH', 28, 19, '2CH.28.19', 'For the LORD brought Judah low because of Ahaz king of Israel, because he acted without restraint in Judah and trespassed severely against the LORD.'),
('2CH', 28, 20, '2CH.28.20', 'Tilgath-pilneser king of Assyria came to him and gave him trouble, but didn’t strengthen him.'),
('2CH', 28, 21, '2CH.28.21', 'For Ahaz took away a portion out of the LORD’s house, and out of the house of the king and of the princes, and gave it to the king of Assyria; but it didn’t help him.'),
('2CH', 28, 22, '2CH.28.22', 'In the time of his distress, he trespassed yet more against the LORD, this same King Ahaz.'),
('2CH', 28, 23, '2CH.28.23', 'For he sacrificed to the gods of Damascus which had defeated him. He said, “Because the gods of the kings of Syria helped them, I will sacrifice to them, that they may help me.” But they were the ruin of him and of all Israel.'),
('2CH', 28, 24, '2CH.28.24', 'Ahaz gathered together the vessels of God’s house, cut the vessels of God’s house in pieces, and shut up the doors of the LORD’s house; and he made himself altars in every corner of Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 28, 25, '2CH.28.25', 'In every city of Judah he made high places to burn incense to other gods, and provoked the LORD, the God of his fathers, to anger.'),
('2CH', 28, 26, '2CH.28.26', 'Now the rest of his acts, and all his ways, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel.'),
('2CH', 28, 27, '2CH.28.27', 'Ahaz slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city, even in Jerusalem, because they didn’t bring him into the tombs of the kings of Israel; and Hezekiah his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 29, 1, '2CH.29.1', 'Hezekiah began to reign when he was twenty-five years old, and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name was Abijah, the daughter of Zechariah.'),
('2CH', 29, 2, '2CH.29.2', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, according to all that David his father had done.'),
('2CH', 29, 3, '2CH.29.3', 'In the first year of his reign, in the first month, he opened the doors of the LORD’s house and repaired them.'),
('2CH', 29, 4, '2CH.29.4', 'He brought in the priests and the Levites and gathered them together into the wide place on the east,'),
('2CH', 29, 5, '2CH.29.5', 'and said to them, “Listen to me, you Levites! Now sanctify yourselves, and sanctify the house of the LORD, the God of your fathers, and carry the filthiness out of the holy place.'),
('2CH', 29, 6, '2CH.29.6', 'For our fathers were unfaithful, and have done that which was evil in the LORD our God’s sight, and have forsaken him, and have turned away their faces from the habitation of the LORD, and turned their backs.'),
('2CH', 29, 7, '2CH.29.7', 'Also they have shut up the doors of the porch, and put out the lamps, and have not burned incense nor offered burnt offerings in the holy place to the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 29, 8, '2CH.29.8', 'Therefore the LORD’s wrath was on Judah and Jerusalem, and he has delivered them to be tossed back and forth, to be an astonishment and a hissing, as you see with your eyes.'),
('2CH', 29, 9, '2CH.29.9', 'For behold, our fathers have fallen by the sword, and our sons and our daughters and our wives are in captivity for this.'),
('2CH', 29, 10, '2CH.29.10', 'Now it is in my heart to make a covenant with the LORD, the God of Israel, that his fierce anger may turn away from us.'),
('2CH', 29, 11, '2CH.29.11', 'My sons, don’t be negligent now; for the LORD has chosen you to stand before him, to minister to him, and that you should be his ministers and burn incense.”'),
('2CH', 29, 12, '2CH.29.12', 'Then the Levites arose: Mahath, the son of Amasai, and Joel the son of Azariah, of the sons of the Kohathites; and of the sons of Merari, Kish the son of Abdi, and Azariah the son of Jehallelel; and of the Gershonites, Joah the son of Zimmah, and Eden the son of Joah;'),
('2CH', 29, 13, '2CH.29.13', 'and of the sons of Elizaphan, Shimri and Jeuel; and of the sons of Asaph, Zechariah and Mattaniah;'),
('2CH', 29, 14, '2CH.29.14', 'and of the sons of Heman, Jehuel and Shimei; and of the sons of Jeduthun, Shemaiah and Uzziel.'),
('2CH', 29, 15, '2CH.29.15', 'They gathered their brothers, sanctified themselves, and went in, according to the commandment of the king by the LORD’s words, to cleanse the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 29, 16, '2CH.29.16', 'The priests went into the inner part of the LORD’s house to cleanse it, and brought out all the uncleanness that they found in the LORD’s temple into the court of the LORD’s house. The Levites took it from there to carry it out to the brook Kidron.'),
('2CH', 29, 17, '2CH.29.17', 'Now they began on the first day of the first month to sanctify, and on the eighth day of the month they came to the LORD’s porch. They sanctified the LORD’s house in eight days, and on the sixteenth day of the first month they finished.'),
('2CH', 29, 18, '2CH.29.18', 'Then they went in to Hezekiah the king within the palace and said, “We have cleansed all the LORD’s house, including the altar of burnt offering with all its vessels, and the table of show bread with all its vessels.'),
('2CH', 29, 19, '2CH.29.19', 'Moreover, we have prepared and sanctified all the vessels which King Ahaz threw away in his reign when he was unfaithful. Behold, they are before the LORD’s altar.”'),
('2CH', 29, 20, '2CH.29.20', 'Then Hezekiah the king arose early, gathered the princes of the city, and went up to the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 29, 21, '2CH.29.21', 'They brought seven bulls, seven rams, seven lambs, and seven male goats, for a sin offering for the kingdom, for the sanctuary, and for Judah. He commanded the priests the sons of Aaron to offer them on the LORD’s altar.'),
('2CH', 29, 22, '2CH.29.22', 'So they killed the bulls, and the priests received the blood and sprinkled it on the altar. They killed the rams and sprinkled the blood on the altar. They also killed the lambs and sprinkled the blood on the altar.'),
('2CH', 29, 23, '2CH.29.23', 'They brought near the male goats for the sin offering before the king and the assembly; and they laid their hands on them.'),
('2CH', 29, 24, '2CH.29.24', 'Then the priests killed them, and they made a sin offering with their blood on the altar, to make atonement for all Israel; for the king commanded that the burnt offering and the sin offering should be made for all Israel.'),
('2CH', 29, 25, '2CH.29.25', 'He set the Levites in the LORD’s house with cymbals, with stringed instruments, and with harps, according to the commandment of David, of Gad the king’s seer, and Nathan the prophet; for the commandment was from the LORD by his prophets.'),
('2CH', 29, 26, '2CH.29.26', 'The Levites stood with David’s instruments, and the priests with the trumpets.'),
('2CH', 29, 27, '2CH.29.27', 'Hezekiah commanded them to offer the burnt offering on the altar. When the burnt offering began, the LORD’s song also began, along with the trumpets and instruments of David king of Israel.'),
('2CH', 29, 28, '2CH.29.28', 'All the assembly worshiped, the singers sang, and the trumpeters sounded. All this continued until the burnt offering was finished.'),
('2CH', 29, 29, '2CH.29.29', 'When they had finished offering, the king and all who were present with him bowed themselves and worshiped.'),
('2CH', 29, 30, '2CH.29.30', 'Moreover Hezekiah the king and the princes commanded the Levites to sing praises to the LORD with the words of David, and of Asaph the seer. They sang praises with gladness, and they bowed their heads and worshiped.'),
('2CH', 29, 31, '2CH.29.31', 'Then Hezekiah answered, “Now you have consecrated yourselves to the LORD. Come near and bring sacrifices and thank offerings into the LORD’s house.” The assembly brought in sacrifices and thank offerings, and as many as were of a willing heart brought burnt offerings.'),
('2CH', 29, 32, '2CH.29.32', 'The number of the burnt offerings which the assembly brought was seventy bulls, one hundred rams, and two hundred lambs. All these were for a burnt offering to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 29, 33, '2CH.29.33', 'The consecrated things were six hundred head of cattle and three thousand sheep.'),
('2CH', 29, 34, '2CH.29.34', 'But the priests were too few, so that they could not skin all the burnt offerings. Therefore their brothers the Levites helped them until the work was ended, and until the priests had sanctified themselves, for the Levites were more upright in heart to sanctify themselves than the priests.'),
('2CH', 29, 35, '2CH.29.35', 'Also the burnt offerings were in abundance, with the fat of the peace offerings and with the drink offerings for every burnt offering. So the service of the LORD’s house was set in order.'),
('2CH', 29, 36, '2CH.29.36', 'Hezekiah and all the people rejoiced because of that which God had prepared for the people; for the thing was done suddenly.'),
('2CH', 30, 1, '2CH.30.1', 'Hezekiah sent to all Israel and Judah, and wrote letters also to Ephraim and Manasseh, that they should come to the LORD’s house at Jerusalem, to keep the Passover to the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 30, 2, '2CH.30.2', 'For the king had taken counsel with his princes and all the assembly in Jerusalem to keep the Passover in the second month.'),
('2CH', 30, 3, '2CH.30.3', 'For they could not keep it at that time, because the priests had not sanctified themselves in sufficient number, and the people had not gathered themselves together to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 30, 4, '2CH.30.4', 'The thing was right in the eyes of the king and of all the assembly.'),
('2CH', 30, 5, '2CH.30.5', 'So they established a decree to make proclamation throughout all Israel, from Beersheba even to Dan, that they should come to keep the Passover to the LORD, the God of Israel, at Jerusalem, for they had not kept it in great numbers in the way it is written.'),
('2CH', 30, 6, '2CH.30.6', 'So the couriers went with the letters from the king and his princes throughout all Israel and Judah, according to the commandment of the king, saying, “You children of Israel, turn again to the LORD, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, that he may return to the remnant of you that have escaped out of the hand of the kings of Assyria.'),
('2CH', 30, 7, '2CH.30.7', 'Don’t be like your fathers and like your brothers, who trespassed against the LORD, the God of their fathers, so that he gave them up to desolation, as you see.'),
('2CH', 30, 8, '2CH.30.8', 'Now don’t be stiff-necked, as your fathers were, but yield yourselves to the LORD, and enter into his sanctuary, which he has sanctified forever, and serve the LORD your God, that his fierce anger may turn away from you.'),
('2CH', 30, 9, '2CH.30.9', 'For if you turn again to the LORD, your brothers and your children will find compassion with those who led them captive, and will come again into this land, because the LORD your God is gracious and merciful, and will not turn away his face from you if you return to him.”'),
('2CH', 30, 10, '2CH.30.10', 'So the couriers passed from city to city through the country of Ephraim and Manasseh, even to Zebulun, but people ridiculed them and mocked them.'),
('2CH', 30, 11, '2CH.30.11', 'Nevertheless some men of Asher, Manasseh, and Zebulun humbled themselves and came to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 30, 12, '2CH.30.12', 'Also the hand of God came on Judah to give them one heart, to do the commandment of the king and of the princes by the LORD’s word.'),
('2CH', 30, 13, '2CH.30.13', 'Many people assembled at Jerusalem to keep the feast of unleavened bread in the second month, a very great assembly.'),
('2CH', 30, 14, '2CH.30.14', 'They arose and took away the altars that were in Jerusalem, and they took away all the altars for incense and threw them into the brook Kidron.'),
('2CH', 30, 15, '2CH.30.15', 'Then they killed the Passover on the fourteenth day of the second month. The priests and the Levites were ashamed, and sanctified themselves, and brought burnt offerings into the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 30, 16, '2CH.30.16', 'They stood in their place after their order, according to the law of Moses the man of God. The priests sprinkled the blood which they received of the hand of the Levites.'),
('2CH', 30, 17, '2CH.30.17', 'For there were many in the assembly who had not sanctified themselves; therefore the Levites were in charge of killing the Passovers for everyone who was not clean, to sanctify them to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 30, 18, '2CH.30.18', 'For a multitude of the people, even many of Ephraim, Manasseh, Issachar, and Zebulun, had not cleansed themselves, yet they ate the Passover other than the way it is written. For Hezekiah had prayed for them, saying, “May the good LORD pardon everyone'),
('2CH', 30, 19, '2CH.30.19', 'who sets his heart to seek God, the LORD, the God of his fathers, even if they aren’t clean according to the purification of the sanctuary.”'),
('2CH', 30, 20, '2CH.30.20', 'The LORD listened to Hezekiah, and healed the people.'),
('2CH', 30, 21, '2CH.30.21', 'The children of Israel who were present at Jerusalem kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with great gladness. The Levites and the priests praised the LORD day by day, singing with loud instruments to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 30, 22, '2CH.30.22', 'Hezekiah spoke encouragingly to all the Levites who had good understanding in the service of the LORD. So they ate throughout the feast for the seven days, offering sacrifices of peace offerings and making confession to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 30, 23, '2CH.30.23', 'The whole assembly took counsel to keep another seven days, and they kept another seven days with gladness.'),
('2CH', 30, 24, '2CH.30.24', 'For Hezekiah king of Judah gave to the assembly for offerings one thousand bulls and seven thousand sheep; and the princes gave to the assembly a thousand bulls and ten thousand sheep; and a great number of priests sanctified themselves.'),
('2CH', 30, 25, '2CH.30.25', 'All the assembly of Judah, with the priests and the Levites, and all the assembly who came out of Israel, and the foreigners who came out of the land of Israel and who lived in Judah, rejoiced.'),
('2CH', 30, 26, '2CH.30.26', 'So there was great joy in Jerusalem; for since the time of Solomon the son of David king of Israel there was nothing like this in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 30, 27, '2CH.30.27', 'Then the Levitical priests arose and blessed the people. Their voice was heard, and their prayer came up to his holy habitation, even to heaven.'),
('2CH', 31, 1, '2CH.31.1', 'Now when all this was finished, all Israel who were present went out to the cities of Judah and broke the pillars in pieces, cut down the Asherah poles, and broke down the high places and the altars out of all Judah and Benjamin, also in Ephraim and Manasseh, until they had destroyed them all. Then all the children of Israel returned, every man to his possession, into their own cities.'),
('2CH', 31, 2, '2CH.31.2', 'Hezekiah appointed the divisions of the priests and the Levites after their divisions, every man according to his service, both the priests and the Levites, for burnt offerings and for peace offerings, to minister, to give thanks, and to praise in the gates of the LORD’s camp.'),
('2CH', 31, 3, '2CH.31.3', 'He also appointed the king’s portion of his possessions for the burnt offerings: for the morning and evening burnt offerings, and the burnt offerings for the Sabbaths, for the new moons, and for the set feasts, as it is written in the LORD’s law.'),
('2CH', 31, 4, '2CH.31.4', 'Moreover he commanded the people who lived in Jerusalem to give the portion of the priests and the Levites, that they might give themselves to the LORD’s law.'),
('2CH', 31, 5, '2CH.31.5', 'As soon as the commandment went out, the children of Israel gave in abundance the first fruits of grain, new wine, oil, honey, and of all the increase of the field; and they brought in the tithe of all things abundantly.'),
('2CH', 31, 6, '2CH.31.6', 'The children of Israel and Judah, who lived in the cities of Judah, also brought in the tithe of cattle and sheep, and the tithe of dedicated things which were consecrated to the LORD their God, and laid them in heaps.'),
('2CH', 31, 7, '2CH.31.7', 'In the third month, they began to lay the foundation of the heaps, and finished them in the seventh month.'),
('2CH', 31, 8, '2CH.31.8', 'When Hezekiah and the princes came and saw the heaps, they blessed the LORD and his people Israel.'),
('2CH', 31, 9, '2CH.31.9', 'Then Hezekiah questioned the priests and the Levites about the heaps.'),
('2CH', 31, 10, '2CH.31.10', 'Azariah the chief priest, of the house of Zadok, answered him and said, “Since people began to bring the offerings into the LORD’s house, we have eaten and had enough, and have plenty left over, for the LORD has blessed his people; and that which is left is this great store.”'),
('2CH', 31, 11, '2CH.31.11', 'Then Hezekiah commanded them to prepare rooms in the LORD’s house, and they prepared them.'),
('2CH', 31, 12, '2CH.31.12', 'They brought in the offerings, the tithes, and the dedicated things faithfully. Conaniah the Levite was ruler over them, and Shimei his brother was second.'),
('2CH', 31, 13, '2CH.31.13', 'Jehiel, Azaziah, Nahath, Asahel, Jerimoth, Jozabad, Eliel, Ismachiah, Mahath, and Benaiah were overseers under the hand of Conaniah and Shimei his brother, by the appointment of Hezekiah the king and Azariah the ruler of God’s house.'),
('2CH', 31, 14, '2CH.31.14', 'Kore the son of Imnah the Levite, the gatekeeper at the east gate, was over the free will offerings of God, to distribute the LORD’s offerings and the most holy things.'),
('2CH', 31, 15, '2CH.31.15', 'Under him were Eden, Miniamin, Jeshua, Shemaiah, Amariah, and Shecaniah, in the cities of the priests, in their office of trust, to give to their brothers by divisions, to the great as well as to the small;'),
('2CH', 31, 16, '2CH.31.16', 'in addition to those who were listed by genealogy of males, from three years old and upward, even everyone who entered into the LORD’s house, as the duty of every day required, for their service in their offices according to their divisions;'),
('2CH', 31, 17, '2CH.31.17', 'and those who were listed by genealogy of the priests by their fathers’ houses, and the Levites from twenty years old and upward, in their offices by their divisions;'),
('2CH', 31, 18, '2CH.31.18', 'and those who were listed by genealogy of all their little ones, their wives, their sons, and their daughters, through all the congregation; for in their office of trust they sanctified themselves in holiness.'),
('2CH', 31, 19, '2CH.31.19', 'Also for the sons of Aaron the priests, who were in the fields of the pasture lands of their cities, in every city, there were men who were mentioned by name to give portions to all the males among the priests and to all who were listed by genealogy among the Levites.'),
('2CH', 31, 20, '2CH.31.20', 'Hezekiah did so throughout all Judah; and he did that which was good, right, and faithful before the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 31, 21, '2CH.31.21', 'In every work that he began in the service of God’s house, in the law, and in the commandments, to seek his God, he did it with all his heart and prospered.'),
('2CH', 32, 1, '2CH.32.1', 'After these things and this faithfulness, Sennacherib king of Assyria came, entered into Judah, encamped against the fortified cities, and intended to win them for himself.'),
('2CH', 32, 2, '2CH.32.2', 'When Hezekiah saw that Sennacherib had come, and that he was planning to fight against Jerusalem,'),
('2CH', 32, 3, '2CH.32.3', 'he took counsel with his princes and his mighty men to stop the waters of the springs which were outside of the city, and they helped him.'),
('2CH', 32, 4, '2CH.32.4', 'Then many people gathered together and they stopped all the springs and the brook that flowed through the middle of the land, saying, “Why should the kings of Assyria come, and find abundant water?”'),
('2CH', 32, 5, '2CH.32.5', 'He took courage, built up all the wall that was broken down, and raised it up to the towers, with the other wall outside, and strengthened Millo in David’s city, and made weapons and shields in abundance.'),
('2CH', 32, 6, '2CH.32.6', 'He set captains of war over the people, gathered them together to him in the wide place at the gate of the city, and spoke encouragingly to them, saying,'),
('2CH', 32, 7, '2CH.32.7', '“Be strong and courageous. Don’t be afraid or dismayed because of the king of Assyria, nor for all the multitude who is with him; for there is a greater one with us than with him.'),
('2CH', 32, 8, '2CH.32.8', 'An arm of flesh is with him, but the LORD our God is with us to help us and to fight our battles.” The people rested themselves on the words of Hezekiah king of Judah.'),
('2CH', 32, 9, '2CH.32.9', 'After this, Sennacherib king of Assyria sent his servants to Jerusalem, (now he was attacking Lachish, and all his forces were with him), to Hezekiah king of Judah, and to all Judah who were at Jerusalem, saying,'),
('2CH', 32, 10, '2CH.32.10', 'Sennacherib king of Assyria says, “In whom do you trust, that you remain under siege in Jerusalem?'),
('2CH', 32, 11, '2CH.32.11', 'Doesn’t Hezekiah persuade you to give you over to die by famine and by thirst, saying, ‘The LORD our God will deliver us out of the hand of the king of Assyria’?'),
('2CH', 32, 12, '2CH.32.12', 'Hasn’t the same Hezekiah taken away his high places and his altars, and commanded Judah and Jerusalem, saying, ‘You shall worship before one altar, and you shall burn incense on it’?'),
('2CH', 32, 13, '2CH.32.13', 'Don’t you know what I and my fathers have done to all the peoples of the lands? Were the gods of the nations of those lands in any way able to deliver their land out of my hand?'),
('2CH', 32, 14, '2CH.32.14', 'Who was there among all the gods of those nations which my fathers utterly destroyed that could deliver his people out of my hand, that your God should be able to deliver you out of my hand?'),
('2CH', 32, 15, '2CH.32.15', 'Now therefore don’t let Hezekiah deceive you nor persuade you in this way. Don’t believe him, for no god of any nation or kingdom was able to deliver his people out of my hand, and out of the hand of my fathers. How much less will your God deliver you out of my hand?”'),
('2CH', 32, 16, '2CH.32.16', 'His servants spoke yet more against the LORD God and against his servant Hezekiah.'),
('2CH', 32, 17, '2CH.32.17', 'He also wrote letters insulting the LORD, the God of Israel, and speaking against him, saying, “As the gods of the nations of the lands, which have not delivered their people out of my hand, so shall the God of Hezekiah not deliver his people out of my hand.”'),
('2CH', 32, 18, '2CH.32.18', 'They called out with a loud voice in the Jews’ language to the people of Jerusalem who were on the wall, to frighten them and to trouble them, that they might take the city.'),
('2CH', 32, 19, '2CH.32.19', 'They spoke of the God of Jerusalem as of the gods of the peoples of the earth, which are the work of men’s hands.'),
('2CH', 32, 20, '2CH.32.20', 'Hezekiah the king and Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, prayed because of this, and cried to heaven.'),
('2CH', 32, 21, '2CH.32.21', 'The LORD sent an angel, who cut off all the mighty men of valor, the leaders, and captains in the camp of the king of Assyria. So he returned with shame of face to his own land. When he had come into the house of his god, those who came out of his own body killed him there with the sword.'),
('2CH', 32, 22, '2CH.32.22', 'Thus the LORD saved Hezekiah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem from the hand of Sennacherib the king of Assyria and from the hand of all others, and guided them on every side.'),
('2CH', 32, 23, '2CH.32.23', 'Many brought gifts to the LORD to Jerusalem, and precious things to Hezekiah king of Judah, so that he was exalted in the sight of all nations from then on.'),
('2CH', 32, 24, '2CH.32.24', 'In those days Hezekiah was terminally ill, and he prayed to the LORD; and he spoke to him, and gave him a sign.'),
('2CH', 32, 25, '2CH.32.25', 'But Hezekiah didn’t reciprocate appropriate to the benefit done for him, because his heart was lifted up. Therefore there was wrath on him, Judah, and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 32, 26, '2CH.32.26', 'However, Hezekiah humbled himself for the pride of his heart, both he and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so that the LORD’s wrath didn’t come on them in the days of Hezekiah.'),
('2CH', 32, 27, '2CH.32.27', 'Hezekiah had exceedingly great riches and honor. He provided himself with treasuries for silver, for gold, for precious stones, for spices, for shields, and for all kinds of valuable vessels;'),
('2CH', 32, 28, '2CH.32.28', 'also storehouses for the increase of grain, new wine, and oil; and stalls for all kinds of animals, and flocks in folds.'),
('2CH', 32, 29, '2CH.32.29', 'Moreover he provided for himself cities, and possessions of flocks and herds in abundance; for God had given him abundant possessions.'),
('2CH', 32, 30, '2CH.32.30', 'This same Hezekiah also stopped the upper spring of the waters of Gihon, and brought them straight down on the west side of David’s city. Hezekiah prospered in all his works.'),
('2CH', 32, 31, '2CH.32.31', 'However, concerning the ambassadors of the princes of Babylon, who sent to him to inquire of the wonder that was done in the land, God left him to test him, that he might know all that was in his heart.'),
('2CH', 32, 32, '2CH.32.32', 'Now the rest of the acts of Hezekiah and his good deeds, behold, they are written in the vision of Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel.'),
('2CH', 32, 33, '2CH.32.33', 'Hezekiah slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the ascent to the tombs of the sons of David. All Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem honored him at his death. Manasseh his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 33, 1, '2CH.33.1', 'Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-five years in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 33, 2, '2CH.33.2', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, after the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.'),
('2CH', 33, 3, '2CH.33.3', 'For he built again the high places which Hezekiah his father had broken down; and he raised up altars for the Baals, made Asheroth, and worshiped all the army of the sky, and served them.'),
('2CH', 33, 4, '2CH.33.4', 'He built altars in the LORD’s house, of which the LORD said, “My name shall be in Jerusalem forever.”'),
('2CH', 33, 5, '2CH.33.5', 'He built altars for all the army of the sky in the two courts of the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 33, 6, '2CH.33.6', 'He also made his children to pass through the fire in the valley of the son of Hinnom. He practiced sorcery, divination, and witchcraft, and dealt with those who had familiar spirits and with wizards. He did much evil in the LORD’s sight, to provoke him to anger.'),
('2CH', 33, 7, '2CH.33.7', 'He set the engraved image of the idol, which he had made, in God’s house, of which God said to David and to Solomon his son, “In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will put my name forever.'),
('2CH', 33, 8, '2CH.33.8', 'I will not any more remove the foot of Israel from off the land which I have appointed for your fathers, if only they will observe to do all that I have commanded them, even all the law, the statutes, and the ordinances given by Moses.”'),
('2CH', 33, 9, '2CH.33.9', 'Manasseh seduced Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so that they did more evil than did the nations whom the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel.'),
('2CH', 33, 10, '2CH.33.10', 'The LORD spoke to Manasseh and to his people, but they didn’t listen.'),
('2CH', 33, 11, '2CH.33.11', 'Therefore the LORD brought on them the captains of the army of the king of Assyria, who took Manasseh in chains, bound him with fetters, and carried him to Babylon.'),
('2CH', 33, 12, '2CH.33.12', 'When he was in distress, he begged the LORD his God, and humbled himself greatly before the God of his fathers.'),
('2CH', 33, 13, '2CH.33.13', 'He prayed to him; and he was entreated by him, and heard his supplication, and brought him again to Jerusalem into his kingdom. Then Manasseh knew that the LORD was God.'),
('2CH', 33, 14, '2CH.33.14', 'Now after this, he built an outer wall to David’s city on the west side of Gihon, in the valley, even to the entrance at the fish gate. He encircled Ophel with it, and raised it up to a very great height; and he put valiant captains in all the fortified cities of Judah.'),
('2CH', 33, 15, '2CH.33.15', 'He took away the foreign gods and the idol out of the LORD’s house, and all the altars that he had built in the mountain of the LORD’s house and in Jerusalem, and cast them out of the city.'),
('2CH', 33, 16, '2CH.33.16', 'He built up the LORD’s altar, and offered sacrifices of peace offerings and of thanksgiving on it, and commanded Judah to serve the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 33, 17, '2CH.33.17', 'Nevertheless the people still sacrificed in the high places, but only to the LORD their God.'),
('2CH', 33, 18, '2CH.33.18', 'Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and his prayer to his God, and the words of the seers who spoke to him in the name of the LORD, the God of Israel, behold, they are written among the acts of the kings of Israel.'),
('2CH', 33, 19, '2CH.33.19', 'His prayer also, and how God listened to his request, and all his sin and his trespass, and the places in which he built high places and set up the Asherah poles and the engraved images before he humbled himself: behold, they are written in the history of Hozai.'),
('2CH', 33, 20, '2CH.33.20', 'So Manasseh slept with his fathers, and they buried him in his own house; and Amon his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 33, 21, '2CH.33.21', 'Amon was twenty-two years old when he began to reign; and he reigned two years in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 33, 22, '2CH.33.22', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, as did Manasseh his father; and Amon sacrificed to all the engraved images which Manasseh his father had made, and served them.'),
('2CH', 33, 23, '2CH.33.23', 'He didn’t humble himself before the LORD, as Manasseh his father had humbled himself; but this same Amon trespassed more and more.'),
('2CH', 33, 24, '2CH.33.24', 'His servants conspired against him, and put him to death in his own house.'),
('2CH', 33, 25, '2CH.33.25', 'But the people of the land killed all those who had conspired against King Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his place.'),
('2CH', 34, 1, '2CH.34.1', 'Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty-one years in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 2, '2CH.34.2', 'He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, and walked in the ways of David his father, and didn’t turn away to the right hand or to the left.'),
('2CH', 34, 3, '2CH.34.3', 'For in the eighth year of his reign, while he was yet young, he began to seek after the God of David his father; and in the twelfth year he began to purge Judah and Jerusalem from the high places, the Asherah poles, the engraved images, and the molten images.'),
('2CH', 34, 4, '2CH.34.4', 'They broke down the altars of the Baals in his presence; and he cut down the incense altars that were on high above them. He broke the Asherah poles, the engraved images, and the molten images in pieces, made dust of them, and scattered it on the graves of those who had sacrificed to them.'),
('2CH', 34, 5, '2CH.34.5', 'He burned the bones of the priests on their altars, and purged Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 6, '2CH.34.6', 'He did this in the cities of Manasseh, Ephraim, and Simeon, even to Naphtali, around in their ruins.'),
('2CH', 34, 7, '2CH.34.7', 'He broke down the altars, beat the Asherah poles and the engraved images into powder, and cut down all the incense altars throughout all the land of Israel, then returned to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 8, '2CH.34.8', 'Now in the eighteenth year of his reign, when he had purged the land and the house, he sent Shaphan the son of Azaliah, Maaseiah the governor of the city, and Joah the son of Joahaz the recorder to repair the house of the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 34, 9, '2CH.34.9', 'They came to Hilkiah the high priest and delivered the money that was brought into God’s house, which the Levites, the keepers of the threshold, had gathered from the hands of Manasseh, Ephraim, of all the remnant of Israel, of all Judah and Benjamin, and of the inhabitants of Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 10, '2CH.34.10', 'They delivered it into the hands of the workmen who had the oversight of the LORD’s house; and the workmen who labored in the LORD’s house gave it to mend and repair the house.'),
('2CH', 34, 11, '2CH.34.11', 'They gave it to the carpenters and to the builders to buy cut stone and timber for couplings, and to make beams for the houses which the kings of Judah had destroyed.'),
('2CH', 34, 12, '2CH.34.12', 'The men did the work faithfully. Their overseers were Jahath and Obadiah the Levites, of the sons of Merari; and Zechariah and Meshullam, of the sons of the Kohathites, to give direction; and others of the Levites, who were all skillful with musical instruments.'),
('2CH', 34, 13, '2CH.34.13', 'Also they were over the bearers of burdens, and directed all who did the work in every kind of service. Of the Levites, there were scribes, officials, and gatekeepers.'),
('2CH', 34, 14, '2CH.34.14', 'When they brought out the money that was brought into the LORD’s house, Hilkiah the priest found the book of the LORD’s law given by Moses.'),
('2CH', 34, 15, '2CH.34.15', 'Hilkiah answered Shaphan the scribe, “I have found the book of the law in the LORD’s house.” So Hilkiah delivered the book to Shaphan.'),
('2CH', 34, 16, '2CH.34.16', 'Shaphan carried the book to the king, and moreover brought back word to the king, saying, “All that was committed to your servants, they are doing.'),
('2CH', 34, 17, '2CH.34.17', 'They have emptied out the money that was found in the LORD’s house, and have delivered it into the hand of the overseers and into the hand of the workmen.”'),
('2CH', 34, 18, '2CH.34.18', 'Shaphan the scribe told the king, saying, “Hilkiah the priest has delivered me a book.” Shaphan read from it to the king.'),
('2CH', 34, 19, '2CH.34.19', 'When the king had heard the words of the law, he tore his clothes.'),
('2CH', 34, 20, '2CH.34.20', 'The king commanded Hilkiah, Ahikam the son of Shaphan, Abdon the son of Micah, Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah the king’s servant, saying,'),
('2CH', 34, 21, '2CH.34.21', '“Go inquire of the LORD for me, and for those who are left in Israel and in Judah, concerning the words of the book that is found; for great is the LORD’s wrath that is poured out on us, because our fathers have not kept the LORD’s word, to do according to all that is written in this book.”'),
('2CH', 34, 22, '2CH.34.22', 'So Hilkiah and those whom the king had commanded went to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tokhath, the son of Hasrah, keeper of the wardrobe (now she lived in Jerusalem in the second quarter), and they spoke to her to that effect.'),
('2CH', 34, 23, '2CH.34.23', 'She said to them, “The LORD, the God of Israel says: ‘Tell the man who sent you to me,'),
('2CH', 34, 24, '2CH.34.24', '“The LORD says, ‘Behold, I will bring evil on this place and on its inhabitants, even all the curses that are written in the book which they have read before the king of Judah.'),
('2CH', 34, 25, '2CH.34.25', 'Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense to other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands, therefore my wrath is poured out on this place, and it will not be quenched.’”’'),
('2CH', 34, 26, '2CH.34.26', 'But to the king of Judah, who sent you to inquire of the LORD, you shall tell him this, ‘The LORD, the God of Israel says: “About the words which you have heard,'),
('2CH', 34, 27, '2CH.34.27', 'because your heart was tender, and you humbled yourself before God when you heard his words against this place and against its inhabitants, and have humbled yourself before me, and have torn your clothes and wept before me, I also have heard you,” says the LORD.'),
('2CH', 34, 28, '2CH.34.28', '“Behold, I will gather you to your fathers, and you will be gathered to your grave in peace. Your eyes won’t see all the evil that I will bring on this place and on its inhabitants.”’” They brought back this message to the king.'),
('2CH', 34, 29, '2CH.34.29', 'Then the king sent and gathered together all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 30, '2CH.34.30', 'The king went up to the LORD’s house with all the men of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem—the priests, the Levites, and all the people, both great and small—and he read in their hearing all the words of the book of the covenant that was found in the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 34, 31, '2CH.34.31', 'The king stood in his place and made a covenant before the LORD, to walk after the LORD, and to keep his commandments, his testimonies, and his statutes with all his heart and with all his soul, to perform the words of the covenant that were written in this book.'),
('2CH', 34, 32, '2CH.34.32', 'He caused all who were found in Jerusalem and Benjamin to stand. The inhabitants of Jerusalem did according to the covenant of God, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 34, 33, '2CH.34.33', 'Josiah took away all the abominations out of all the countries that belonged to the children of Israel, and made all who were found in Israel to serve, even to serve the LORD their God. All his days they didn’t depart from following the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 35, 1, '2CH.35.1', 'Josiah kept a Passover to the LORD in Jerusalem. They killed the Passover on the fourteenth day of the first month.'),
('2CH', 35, 2, '2CH.35.2', 'He set the priests in their offices and encouraged them in the service of the LORD’s house.'),
('2CH', 35, 3, '2CH.35.3', 'He said to the Levites who taught all Israel, who were holy to the LORD, “Put the holy ark in the house which Solomon the son of David king of Israel built. It will no longer be a burden on your shoulders. Now serve the LORD your God and his people Israel.'),
('2CH', 35, 4, '2CH.35.4', 'Prepare yourselves after your fathers’ houses by your divisions, according to the writing of David king of Israel, and according to the writing of Solomon his son.'),
('2CH', 35, 5, '2CH.35.5', 'Stand in the holy place according to the divisions of the fathers’ houses of your brothers the children of the people, and let there be for each a portion of a fathers’ house of the Levites.'),
('2CH', 35, 6, '2CH.35.6', 'Kill the Passover lamb, sanctify yourselves, and prepare for your brothers, to do according to the LORD’s word by Moses.”'),
('2CH', 35, 7, '2CH.35.7', 'Josiah gave to the children of the people, of the flock, lambs and young goats, all of them for the Passover offerings, to all who were present, to the number of thirty thousand, and three thousand bulls. These were of the king’s substance.'),
('2CH', 35, 8, '2CH.35.8', 'His princes gave a free will offering to the people, to the priests, and to the Levites. Hilkiah, Zechariah, and Jehiel, the rulers of God’s house, gave to the priests for the Passover offerings two thousand six hundred small livestock, and three hundred head of cattle.'),
('2CH', 35, 9, '2CH.35.9', 'Conaniah also, and Shemaiah and Nethanel, his brothers, and Hashabiah, Jeiel, and Jozabad, the chiefs of the Levites, gave to the Levites for the Passover offerings five thousand small livestock and five hundred head of cattle.'),
('2CH', 35, 10, '2CH.35.10', 'So the service was prepared, and the priests stood in their place, and the Levites by their divisions, according to the king’s commandment.'),
('2CH', 35, 11, '2CH.35.11', 'They killed the Passover lambs, and the priests sprinkled the blood which they received from their hands, and the Levites skinned them.'),
('2CH', 35, 12, '2CH.35.12', 'They removed the burnt offerings, that they might give them according to the divisions of the fathers’ houses of the children of the people, to offer to the LORD, as it is written in the book of Moses. They did the same with the cattle.'),
('2CH', 35, 13, '2CH.35.13', 'They roasted the Passover with fire according to the ordinance. They boiled the holy offerings in pots, in cauldrons, and in pans, and carried them quickly to all the children of the people.'),
('2CH', 35, 14, '2CH.35.14', 'Afterward they prepared for themselves and for the priests, because the priests the sons of Aaron were busy with offering the burnt offerings and the fat until night. Therefore the Levites prepared for themselves and for the priests the sons of Aaron.'),
('2CH', 35, 15, '2CH.35.15', 'The singers, the sons of Asaph, were in their place, according to the commandment of David, Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun the king’s seer; and the gatekeepers were at every gate. They didn’t need to depart from their service, because their brothers the Levites prepared for them.'),
('2CH', 35, 16, '2CH.35.16', 'So all the service of the LORD was prepared the same day, to keep the Passover, and to offer burnt offerings on the LORD’s altar, according to the commandment of King Josiah.'),
('2CH', 35, 17, '2CH.35.17', 'The children of Israel who were present kept the Passover at that time, and the feast of unleavened bread seven days.'),
('2CH', 35, 18, '2CH.35.18', 'There was no Passover like that kept in Israel from the days of Samuel the prophet, nor did any of the kings of Israel keep such a Passover as Josiah kept—with the priests, the Levites, and all Judah and Israel who were present, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 35, 19, '2CH.35.19', 'This Passover was kept in the eighteenth year of the reign of Josiah.'),
('2CH', 35, 20, '2CH.35.20', 'After all this, when Josiah had prepared the temple, Neco king of Egypt went up to fight against Carchemish by the Euphrates, and Josiah went out against him.'),
('2CH', 35, 21, '2CH.35.21', 'But he sent ambassadors to him, saying, “What have I to do with you, you king of Judah? I come not against you today, but against the house with which I have war. God has commanded me to make haste. Beware that it is God who is with me, that he not destroy you.”'),
('2CH', 35, 22, '2CH.35.22', 'Nevertheless Josiah would not turn his face from him, but disguised himself, that he might fight with him, and didn’t listen to the words of Neco from the mouth of God, and came to fight in the valley of Megiddo.'),
('2CH', 35, 23, '2CH.35.23', 'The archers shot at King Josiah; and the king said to his servants, “Take me away, because I am seriously wounded!”'),
('2CH', 35, 24, '2CH.35.24', 'So his servants took him out of the chariot, and put him in the second chariot that he had, and brought him to Jerusalem; and he died, and was buried in the tombs of his fathers. All Judah and Jerusalem mourned for Josiah.'),
('2CH', 35, 25, '2CH.35.25', 'Jeremiah lamented for Josiah, and all the singing men and singing women spoke of Josiah in their lamentations to this day; and they made them an ordinance in Israel. Behold, they are written in the lamentations.'),
('2CH', 35, 26, '2CH.35.26', 'Now the rest of the acts of Josiah and his good deeds, according to that which is written in the LORD’s law,'),
('2CH', 35, 27, '2CH.35.27', 'and his acts, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah.'),
('2CH', 36, 1, '2CH.36.1', 'Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz the son of Josiah, and made him king in his father’s place in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 36, 2, '2CH.36.2', 'Joahaz was twenty-three years old when he began to reign; and he reigned three months in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 36, 3, '2CH.36.3', 'The king of Egypt removed him from office at Jerusalem, and fined the land one hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold.'),
('2CH', 36, 4, '2CH.36.4', 'The king of Egypt made Eliakim his brother king over Judah and Jerusalem, and changed his name to Jehoiakim. Neco took Joahaz his brother, and carried him to Egypt.'),
('2CH', 36, 5, '2CH.36.5', 'Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. He did that which was evil in the LORD his God’s sight.'),
('2CH', 36, 6, '2CH.36.6', 'Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up against him, and bound him in fetters to carry him to Babylon.'),
('2CH', 36, 7, '2CH.36.7', 'Nebuchadnezzar also carried some of the vessels of the LORD’s house to Babylon, and put them in his temple at Babylon.'),
('2CH', 36, 8, '2CH.36.8', 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, and his abominations which he did, and that which was found in him, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah; and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 36, 9, '2CH.36.9', 'Jehoiachin was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months and ten days in Jerusalem. He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight.'),
('2CH', 36, 10, '2CH.36.10', 'At the return of the year, King Nebuchadnezzar sent and brought him to Babylon, with the valuable vessels of the LORD’s house, and made Zedekiah his brother king over Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 36, 11, '2CH.36.11', 'Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 36, 12, '2CH.36.12', 'He did that which was evil in the LORD his God’s sight. He didn’t humble himself before Jeremiah the prophet speaking from the LORD’s mouth.'),
('2CH', 36, 13, '2CH.36.13', 'He also rebelled against King Nebuchadnezzar, who had made him swear by God; but he stiffened his neck, and hardened his heart against turning to the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 36, 14, '2CH.36.14', 'Moreover all the chiefs of the priests and the people trespassed very greatly after all the abominations of the nations; and they polluted the LORD’s house which he had made holy in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 36, 15, '2CH.36.15', 'The LORD, the God of their fathers, sent to them by his messengers, rising up early and sending, because he had compassion on his people and on his dwelling place;'),
('2CH', 36, 16, '2CH.36.16', 'but they mocked the messengers of God, despised his words, and scoffed at his prophets, until the LORD’s wrath arose against his people, until there was no remedy.'),
('2CH', 36, 17, '2CH.36.17', 'Therefore he brought on them the king of the Chaldeans, who killed their young men with the sword in the house of their sanctuary, and had no compassion on young man or virgin, old man or infirm. He gave them all into his hand.'),
('2CH', 36, 18, '2CH.36.18', 'All the vessels of God’s house, great and small, and the treasures of the LORD’s house, and the treasures of the king and of his princes, all these he brought to Babylon.'),
('2CH', 36, 19, '2CH.36.19', 'They burned God’s house, broke down the wall of Jerusalem, burned all its palaces with fire, and destroyed all of its valuable vessels.'),
('2CH', 36, 20, '2CH.36.20', 'He carried those who had escaped from the sword away to Babylon, and they were servants to him and his sons until the reign of the kingdom of Persia,'),
('2CH', 36, 21, '2CH.36.21', 'to fulfill the LORD’s word by Jeremiah’s mouth, until the land had enjoyed its Sabbaths. As long as it lay desolate, it kept Sabbath, to fulfill seventy years.'),
('2CH', 36, 22, '2CH.36.22', 'Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the LORD’s word by the mouth of Jeremiah might be accomplished, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, so that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,'),
('2CH', 36, 23, '2CH.36.23', '“Cyrus king of Persia says, ‘The LORD, the God of heaven, has given all the kingdoms of the earth to me; and he has commanded me to build him a house in Jerusalem, which is in Judah. Whoever there is among you of all his people, the LORD his God be with him, and let him go up.’”'),
('EZR', 1, 1, 'EZR.1.1', 'Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the LORD’s word by Jeremiah’s mouth might be accomplished, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, so that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,'),
('EZR', 1, 2, 'EZR.1.2', '“Cyrus king of Persia says, ‘The LORD, the God of heaven, has given me all the kingdoms of the earth; and he has commanded me to build him a house in Jerusalem, which is in Judah.'),
('EZR', 1, 3, 'EZR.1.3', 'Whoever there is among you of all his people, may his God be with him, and let him go up to Jerusalem, which is in Judah, and build the house of the LORD, the God of Israel (he is God), which is in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 1, 4, 'EZR.1.4', 'Whoever is left, in any place where he lives, let the men of his place help him with silver, with gold, with goods, and with animals, in addition to the free will offering for God’s house which is in Jerusalem.’”'),
('EZR', 1, 5, 'EZR.1.5', 'Then the heads of fathers’ households of Judah and Benjamin, the priests and the Levites, all whose spirit God had stirred to go up, rose up to build the LORD’s house which is in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 1, 6, 'EZR.1.6', 'All those who were around them strengthened their hands with vessels of silver, with gold, with goods, with animals, and with precious things, in addition to all that was willingly offered.'),
('EZR', 1, 7, 'EZR.1.7', 'Also Cyrus the king brought out the vessels of the LORD’s house, which Nebuchadnezzar had brought out of Jerusalem, and had put in the house of his gods;'),
('EZR', 1, 8, 'EZR.1.8', 'even those, Cyrus king of Persia brought out by the hand of Mithredath the treasurer, and counted them out to Sheshbazzar the prince of Judah.'),
('EZR', 1, 9, 'EZR.1.9', 'This is the number of them: thirty platters of gold, one thousand platters of silver, twenty-nine knives,'),
('EZR', 1, 10, 'EZR.1.10', 'thirty bowls of gold, four hundred ten silver bowls of a second kind, and one thousand other vessels.'),
('EZR', 1, 11, 'EZR.1.11', 'All the vessels of gold and of silver were five thousand four hundred. Sheshbazzar brought all these up when the captives were brought up from Babylon to Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 2, 1, 'EZR.2.1', 'Now these are the children of the province who went up out of the captivity of those who had been carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away to Babylon, and who returned to Jerusalem and Judah, everyone to his city;'),
('EZR', 2, 2, 'EZR.2.2', 'who came with Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum, and Baanah. The number of the men of the people of Israel:'),
('EZR', 2, 3, 'EZR.2.3', 'The children of Parosh, two thousand one hundred seventy-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 4, 'EZR.2.4', 'The children of Shephatiah, three hundred seventy-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 5, 'EZR.2.5', 'The children of Arah, seven hundred seventy-five.'),
('EZR', 2, 6, 'EZR.2.6', 'The children of Pahathmoab, of the children of Jeshua and Joab, two thousand eight hundred twelve.'),
('EZR', 2, 7, 'EZR.2.7', 'The children of Elam, one thousand two hundred fifty-four.'),
('EZR', 2, 8, 'EZR.2.8', 'The children of Zattu, nine hundred forty-five.'),
('EZR', 2, 9, 'EZR.2.9', 'The children of Zaccai, seven hundred sixty.'),
('EZR', 2, 10, 'EZR.2.10', 'The children of Bani, six hundred forty-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 11, 'EZR.2.11', 'The children of Bebai, six hundred twenty-three.'),
('EZR', 2, 12, 'EZR.2.12', 'The children of Azgad, one thousand two hundred twenty-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 13, 'EZR.2.13', 'The children of Adonikam, six hundred sixty-six.'),
('EZR', 2, 14, 'EZR.2.14', 'The children of Bigvai, two thousand fifty-six.'),
('EZR', 2, 15, 'EZR.2.15', 'The children of Adin, four hundred fifty-four.'),
('EZR', 2, 16, 'EZR.2.16', 'The children of Ater, of Hezekiah, ninety-eight.'),
('EZR', 2, 17, 'EZR.2.17', 'The children of Bezai, three hundred twenty-three.'),
('EZR', 2, 18, 'EZR.2.18', 'The children of Jorah, one hundred twelve.'),
('EZR', 2, 19, 'EZR.2.19', 'The children of Hashum, two hundred twenty-three.'),
('EZR', 2, 20, 'EZR.2.20', 'The children of Gibbar, ninety-five.'),
('EZR', 2, 21, 'EZR.2.21', 'The children of Bethlehem, one hundred twenty-three.'),
('EZR', 2, 22, 'EZR.2.22', 'The men of Netophah, fifty-six.'),
('EZR', 2, 23, 'EZR.2.23', 'The men of Anathoth, one hundred twenty-eight.'),
('EZR', 2, 24, 'EZR.2.24', 'The children of Azmaveth, forty-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 25, 'EZR.2.25', 'The children of Kiriath Arim, Chephirah, and Beeroth, seven hundred forty-three.'),
('EZR', 2, 26, 'EZR.2.26', 'The children of Ramah and Geba, six hundred twenty-one.'),
('EZR', 2, 27, 'EZR.2.27', 'The men of Michmas, one hundred twenty-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 28, 'EZR.2.28', 'The men of Bethel and Ai, two hundred twenty-three.'),
('EZR', 2, 29, 'EZR.2.29', 'The children of Nebo, fifty-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 30, 'EZR.2.30', 'The children of Magbish, one hundred fifty-six.'),
('EZR', 2, 31, 'EZR.2.31', 'The children of the other Elam, one thousand two hundred fifty-four.'),
('EZR', 2, 32, 'EZR.2.32', 'The children of Harim, three hundred twenty.'),
('EZR', 2, 33, 'EZR.2.33', 'The children of Lod, Hadid, and Ono, seven hundred twenty-five.'),
('EZR', 2, 34, 'EZR.2.34', 'The children of Jericho, three hundred forty-five.'),
('EZR', 2, 35, 'EZR.2.35', 'The children of Senaah, three thousand six hundred thirty.'),
('EZR', 2, 36, 'EZR.2.36', 'The priests: the children of Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua, nine hundred seventy-three.'),
('EZR', 2, 37, 'EZR.2.37', 'The children of Immer, one thousand fifty-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 38, 'EZR.2.38', 'The children of Pashhur, one thousand two hundred forty-seven.'),
('EZR', 2, 39, 'EZR.2.39', 'The children of Harim, one thousand seventeen.'),
('EZR', 2, 40, 'EZR.2.40', 'The Levites: the children of Jeshua and Kadmiel, of the children of Hodaviah, seventy-four.'),
('EZR', 2, 41, 'EZR.2.41', 'The singers: the children of Asaph, one hundred twenty-eight.'),
('EZR', 2, 42, 'EZR.2.42', 'The children of the gatekeepers: the children of Shallum, the children of Ater, the children of Talmon, the children of Akkub, the children of Hatita, the children of Shobai, in all one hundred thirty-nine.'),
('EZR', 2, 43, 'EZR.2.43', 'The temple servants: the children of Ziha, the children of Hasupha, the children of Tabbaoth,'),
('EZR', 2, 44, 'EZR.2.44', 'the children of Keros, the children of Siaha, the children of Padon,'),
('EZR', 2, 45, 'EZR.2.45', 'the children of Lebanah, the children of Hagabah, the children of Akkub,'),
('EZR', 2, 46, 'EZR.2.46', 'the children of Hagab, the children of Shamlai, the children of Hanan,'),
('EZR', 2, 47, 'EZR.2.47', 'the children of Giddel, the children of Gahar, the children of Reaiah,'),
('EZR', 2, 48, 'EZR.2.48', 'the children of Rezin, the children of Nekoda, the children of Gazzam,'),
('EZR', 2, 49, 'EZR.2.49', 'the children of Uzza, the children of Paseah, the children of Besai,'),
('EZR', 2, 50, 'EZR.2.50', 'the children of Asnah, the children of Meunim, the children of Nephisim,'),
('EZR', 2, 51, 'EZR.2.51', 'the children of Bakbuk, the children of Hakupha, the children of Harhur,'),
('EZR', 2, 52, 'EZR.2.52', 'the children of Bazluth, the children of Mehida, the children of Harsha,'),
('EZR', 2, 53, 'EZR.2.53', 'the children of Barkos, the children of Sisera, the children of Temah,'),
('EZR', 2, 54, 'EZR.2.54', 'the children of Neziah, the children of Hatipha.'),
('EZR', 2, 55, 'EZR.2.55', 'The children of Solomon’s servants: the children of Sotai, the children of Hassophereth, the children of Peruda,'),
('EZR', 2, 56, 'EZR.2.56', 'the children of Jaalah, the children of Darkon, the children of Giddel,'),
('EZR', 2, 57, 'EZR.2.57', 'the children of Shephatiah, the children of Hattil, the children of Pochereth Hazzebaim, the children of Ami.'),
('EZR', 2, 58, 'EZR.2.58', 'All the temple servants, and the children of Solomon’s servants, were three hundred ninety-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 59, 'EZR.2.59', 'These were those who went up from Tel Melah, Tel Harsha, Cherub, Addan, and Immer; but they could not show their fathers’ houses and their offspring, whether they were of Israel:'),
('EZR', 2, 60, 'EZR.2.60', 'the children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda, six hundred fifty-two.'),
('EZR', 2, 61, 'EZR.2.61', 'Of the children of the priests: the children of Habaiah, the children of Hakkoz, and the children of Barzillai, who took a wife of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite, and was called after their name.'),
('EZR', 2, 62, 'EZR.2.62', 'These sought their place among those who were registered by genealogy, but they were not found; therefore they were deemed disqualified and removed from the priesthood.'),
('EZR', 2, 63, 'EZR.2.63', 'The governor told them that they should not eat of the most holy things until a priest stood up to serve with Urim and with Thummim.'),
('EZR', 2, 64, 'EZR.2.64', 'The whole assembly together was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,'),
('EZR', 2, 65, 'EZR.2.65', 'in addition to their male servants and their female servants, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred thirty-seven; and they had two hundred singing men and singing women.'),
('EZR', 2, 66, 'EZR.2.66', 'Their horses were seven hundred thirty-six; their mules, two hundred forty-five;'),
('EZR', 2, 67, 'EZR.2.67', 'their camels, four hundred thirty-five; their donkeys, six thousand seven hundred twenty.'),
('EZR', 2, 68, 'EZR.2.68', 'Some of the heads of fathers’ households, when they came to the LORD’s house which is in Jerusalem, offered willingly for God’s house to set it up in its place.'),
('EZR', 2, 69, 'EZR.2.69', 'They gave according to their ability into the treasury of the work sixty-one thousand darics of gold, five thousand minas of silver, and one hundred priests’ garments.'),
('EZR', 2, 70, 'EZR.2.70', 'So the priests and the Levites, with some of the people, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants, lived in their cities, and all Israel in their cities.'),
('EZR', 3, 1, 'EZR.3.1', 'When the seventh month had come, and the children of Israel were in the cities, the people gathered themselves together as one man to Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 3, 2, 'EZR.3.2', 'Then Jeshua the son of Jozadak stood up with his brothers the priests and Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel and his relatives, and built the altar of the God of Israel, to offer burnt offerings on it, as it is written in the law of Moses the man of God.'),
('EZR', 3, 3, 'EZR.3.3', 'In spite of their fear because of the peoples of the surrounding lands, they set the altar on its base; and they offered burnt offerings on it to the LORD, even burnt offerings morning and evening.'),
('EZR', 3, 4, 'EZR.3.4', 'They kept the feast of booths, as it is written, and offered the daily burnt offerings by number, according to the ordinance, as the duty of every day required;'),
('EZR', 3, 5, 'EZR.3.5', 'and afterward the continual burnt offering, the offerings of the new moons, of all the set feasts of the LORD that were consecrated, and of everyone who willingly offered a free will offering to the LORD.'),
('EZR', 3, 6, 'EZR.3.6', 'From the first day of the seventh month, they began to offer burnt offerings to the LORD; but the foundation of the LORD’s temple was not yet laid.'),
('EZR', 3, 7, 'EZR.3.7', 'They also gave money to the masons and to the carpenters. They also gave food, drink, and oil to the people of Sidon and Tyre to bring cedar trees from Lebanon to the sea, to Joppa, according to the grant that they had from Cyrus King of Persia.'),
('EZR', 3, 8, 'EZR.3.8', 'Now in the second year of their coming to God’s house at Jerusalem, in the second month, Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and the rest of their brothers the priests and the Levites, and all those who had come out of the captivity to Jerusalem, began the work and appointed the Levites, from twenty years old and upward, to have the oversight of the work of the LORD’s house.'),
('EZR', 3, 9, 'EZR.3.9', 'Then Jeshua stood with his sons and his brothers, Kadmiel and his sons, the sons of Judah, together to have the oversight of the workmen in God’s house: the sons of Henadad, with their sons and their brothers the Levites.'),
('EZR', 3, 10, 'EZR.3.10', 'When the builders laid the foundation of the LORD’s temple, they set the priests in their vestments with trumpets, with the Levites the sons of Asaph with cymbals, to praise the LORD, according to the directions of David king of Israel.'),
('EZR', 3, 11, 'EZR.3.11', 'They sang to one another in praising and giving thanks to the LORD, “For he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever toward Israel.” All the people shouted with a great shout, when they praised the LORD, because the foundation of the LORD’s house had been laid.'),
('EZR', 3, 12, 'EZR.3.12', 'But many of the priests and Levites and heads of fathers’ households, the old men who had seen the first house, when the foundation of this house was laid before their eyes, wept with a loud voice. Many also shouted aloud for joy,'),
('EZR', 3, 13, 'EZR.3.13', 'so that the people could not discern the noise of the shout of joy from the noise of the weeping of the people; for the people shouted with a loud shout, and the noise was heard far away.'),
('EZR', 4, 1, 'EZR.4.1', 'Now when the adversaries of Judah and Benjamin heard that the children of the captivity were building a temple to the LORD, the God of Israel,'),
('EZR', 4, 2, 'EZR.4.2', 'they came near to Zerubbabel, and to the heads of fathers’ households, and said to them, “Let us build with you, for we seek your God as you do; and we have been sacrificing to him since the days of Esar Haddon king of Assyria, who brought us up here.”'),
('EZR', 4, 3, 'EZR.4.3', 'But Zerubbabel, Jeshua, and the rest of the heads of fathers’ households of Israel said to them, “You have nothing to do with us in building a house to our God; but we ourselves together will build to the LORD, the God of Israel, as King Cyrus the king of Persia has commanded us.”'),
('EZR', 4, 4, 'EZR.4.4', 'Then the people of the land weakened the hands of the people of Judah, and troubled them in building.'),
('EZR', 4, 5, 'EZR.4.5', 'They hired counselors against them to frustrate their purpose all the days of Cyrus king of Persia, even until the reign of Darius king of Persia.'),
('EZR', 4, 6, 'EZR.4.6', 'In the reign of Ahasuerus, in the beginning of his reign, they wrote an accusation against the inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 4, 7, 'EZR.4.7', 'In the days of Artaxerxes, Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of his companions wrote to Artaxerxes king of Persia; and the writing of the letter was written in Syrian and delivered in the Syrian language.'),
('EZR', 4, 8, 'EZR.4.8', 'Rehum the chancellor and Shimshai the scribe wrote a letter against Jerusalem to Artaxerxes the king as follows.'),
('EZR', 4, 9, 'EZR.4.9', 'Then Rehum the chancellor, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of their companions, the Dinaites, and the Apharsathchites, the Tarpelites, the Apharsites, the Archevites, the Babylonians, the Shushanchites, the Dehaites, the Elamites,'),
('EZR', 4, 10, 'EZR.4.10', 'and the rest of the nations whom the great and noble Osnappar brought over and settled in the city of Samaria, and in the rest of the country beyond the River, and so forth, wrote.'),
('EZR', 4, 11, 'EZR.4.11', 'This is the copy of the letter that they sent: To King Artaxerxes, from your servants, the people beyond the River.'),
('EZR', 4, 12, 'EZR.4.12', 'Be it known to the king that the Jews who came up from you have come to us to Jerusalem. They are building the rebellious and bad city, and have finished the walls and repaired the foundations.'),
('EZR', 4, 13, 'EZR.4.13', 'Be it known now to the king that if this city is built and the walls finished, they will not pay tribute, custom, or toll, and in the end it will be hurtful to the kings.'),
('EZR', 4, 14, 'EZR.4.14', 'Now because we eat the salt of the palace and it is not appropriate for us to see the king’s dishonor, therefore we have sent and informed the king,'),
('EZR', 4, 15, 'EZR.4.15', 'that search may be made in the book of the records of your fathers. You will see in the book of the records, and know that this city is a rebellious city, and hurtful to kings and provinces, and that they have started rebellions within it in the past. That is why this city was destroyed.'),
('EZR', 4, 16, 'EZR.4.16', 'We inform the king that if this city is built and the walls finished, then you will have no possession beyond the River.'),
('EZR', 4, 17, 'EZR.4.17', 'Then the king sent an answer to Rehum the chancellor, and to Shimshai the scribe, and to the rest of their companions who live in Samaria, and in the rest of the country beyond the River: Peace.'),
('EZR', 4, 18, 'EZR.4.18', 'The letter which you sent to us has been plainly read before me.'),
('EZR', 4, 19, 'EZR.4.19', 'I decreed, and search has been made, and it was found that this city has made insurrection against kings in the past, and that rebellion and revolts have been made in it.'),
('EZR', 4, 20, 'EZR.4.20', 'There have also been mighty kings over Jerusalem who have ruled over all the country beyond the River; and tribute, custom, and toll was paid to them.'),
('EZR', 4, 21, 'EZR.4.21', 'Make a decree now to cause these men to cease, and that this city not be built until a decree is made by me.'),
('EZR', 4, 22, 'EZR.4.22', 'Be careful that you not be slack doing so. Why should damage grow to the hurt of the kings?'),
('EZR', 4, 23, 'EZR.4.23', 'Then when the copy of King Artaxerxes’ letter was read before Rehum, Shimshai the scribe, and their companions, they went in haste to Jerusalem to the Jews, and made them to cease by force of arms.'),
('EZR', 4, 24, 'EZR.4.24', 'Then work stopped on God’s house which is at Jerusalem. It stopped until the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia.'),
('EZR', 5, 1, 'EZR.5.1', 'Now the prophets, Haggai the prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo, prophesied to the Jews who were in Judah and Jerusalem. They prophesied to them in the name of the God of Israel.'),
('EZR', 5, 2, 'EZR.5.2', 'Then Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak rose up and began to build God’s house which is at Jerusalem; and with them were the prophets of God, helping them.'),
('EZR', 5, 3, 'EZR.5.3', 'At the same time Tattenai, the governor beyond the River, came to them, with Shetharbozenai and their companions, and asked them, “Who gave you a decree to build this house and to finish this wall?”'),
('EZR', 5, 4, 'EZR.5.4', 'They also asked for the names of the men who were making this building.'),
('EZR', 5, 5, 'EZR.5.5', 'But the eye of their God was on the elders of the Jews, and they didn’t make them cease until the matter should come to Darius, and an answer should be returned by letter concerning it.'),
('EZR', 5, 6, 'EZR.5.6', 'The copy of the letter that Tattenai, the governor beyond the River, and Shetharbozenai, and his companions the Apharsachites who were beyond the River, sent to Darius the king follows.'),
('EZR', 5, 7, 'EZR.5.7', 'They sent a letter to him, in which was written: To Darius the king, all peace.'),
('EZR', 5, 8, 'EZR.5.8', 'Be it known to the king that we went into the province of Judah, to the house of the great God, which is being built with great stones and timber is laid in the walls. This work goes on with diligence and prospers in their hands.'),
('EZR', 5, 9, 'EZR.5.9', 'Then we asked those elders, and said to them thus, “Who gave you a decree to build this house, and to finish this wall?”'),
('EZR', 5, 10, 'EZR.5.10', 'We asked them their names also, to inform you that we might write the names of the men who were at their head.'),
('EZR', 5, 11, 'EZR.5.11', 'Thus they returned us answer, saying, “We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth and are building the house that was built these many years ago, which a great king of Israel built and finished.'),
('EZR', 5, 12, 'EZR.5.12', 'But after our fathers had provoked the God of heaven to wrath, he gave them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, the Chaldean, who destroyed this house and carried the people away into Babylon.'),
('EZR', 5, 13, 'EZR.5.13', 'But in the first year of Cyrus king of Babylon, Cyrus the king made a decree to build this house of God.'),
('EZR', 5, 14, 'EZR.5.14', 'The gold and silver vessels of God’s house, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple that was in Jerusalem and brought into the temple of Babylon, those Cyrus the king also took out of the temple of Babylon, and they were delivered to one whose name was Sheshbazzar, whom he had made governor.'),
('EZR', 5, 15, 'EZR.5.15', 'He said to him, ‘Take these vessels, go, put them in the temple that is in Jerusalem, and let God’s house be built in its place.’'),
('EZR', 5, 16, 'EZR.5.16', 'Then the same Sheshbazzar came and laid the foundations of God’s house which is in Jerusalem. Since that time even until now it has been being built, and yet it is not completed.'),
('EZR', 5, 17, 'EZR.5.17', 'Now therefore, if it seems good to the king, let a search be made in the king’s treasure house, which is there at Babylon, whether it is so that a decree was made by Cyrus the king to build this house of God at Jerusalem; and let the king send his pleasure to us concerning this matter.”'),
('EZR', 6, 1, 'EZR.6.1', 'Then Darius the king made a decree, and the house of the archives, where the treasures were laid up in Babylon, was searched.'),
('EZR', 6, 2, 'EZR.6.2', 'A scroll was found at Achmetha, in the palace that is in the province of Media, and in it this was written for a record:'),
('EZR', 6, 3, 'EZR.6.3', 'In the first year of Cyrus the king, Cyrus the king made a decree: Concerning God’s house at Jerusalem, let the house be built, the place where they offer sacrifices, and let its foundations be strongly laid, with its height sixty cubits and its width sixty cubits;'),
('EZR', 6, 4, 'EZR.6.4', 'with three courses of great stones and a course of new timber. Let the expenses be given out of the king’s house.'),
('EZR', 6, 5, 'EZR.6.5', 'Also let the gold and silver vessels of God’s house, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple which is at Jerusalem and brought to Babylon, be restored and brought again to the temple which is at Jerusalem, everything to its place. You shall put them in God’s house.'),
('EZR', 6, 6, 'EZR.6.6', 'Now therefore, Tattenai, governor beyond the River, Shetharbozenai, and your companions the Apharsachites, who are beyond the River, you must stay far from there.'),
('EZR', 6, 7, 'EZR.6.7', 'Leave the work of this house of God alone; let the governor of the Jews and the elders of the Jews build this house of God in its place.'),
('EZR', 6, 8, 'EZR.6.8', 'Moreover I make a decree regarding what you shall do for these elders of the Jews for the building of this house of God: that of the king’s goods, even of the tribute beyond the River, expenses must be given with all diligence to these men, that they not be hindered.'),
('EZR', 6, 9, 'EZR.6.9', 'That which they have need of, including young bulls, rams, and lambs, for burnt offerings to the God of heaven; also wheat, salt, wine, and oil, according to the word of the priests who are at Jerusalem, let it be given them day by day without fail,'),
('EZR', 6, 10, 'EZR.6.10', 'that they may offer sacrifices of pleasant aroma to the God of heaven, and pray for the life of the king and of his sons.'),
('EZR', 6, 11, 'EZR.6.11', 'I have also made a decree that whoever alters this message, let a beam be pulled out from his house, and let him be lifted up and fastened on it; and let his house be made a dunghill for this.'),
('EZR', 6, 12, 'EZR.6.12', 'May the God who has caused his name to dwell there overthrow all kings and peoples who stretch out their hand to alter this, to destroy this house of God which is at Jerusalem. I Darius have made a decree. Let it be done with all diligence.'),
('EZR', 6, 13, 'EZR.6.13', 'Then Tattenai, the governor beyond the River, Shetharbozenai, and their companions did accordingly with all diligence, because Darius the king had sent a decree.'),
('EZR', 6, 14, 'EZR.6.14', 'The elders of the Jews built and prospered, through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo. They built and finished it, according to the commandment of the God of Israel, and according to the decree of Cyrus, Darius, and Artaxerxes king of Persia.'),
('EZR', 6, 15, 'EZR.6.15', 'This house was finished on the third day of the month Adar, which was in the sixth year of the reign of Darius the king.'),
('EZR', 6, 16, 'EZR.6.16', 'The children of Israel, the priests, the Levites, and the rest of the children of the captivity, kept the dedication of this house of God with joy.'),
('EZR', 6, 17, 'EZR.6.17', 'They offered at the dedication of this house of God one hundred bulls, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs; and for a sin offering for all Israel, twelve male goats, according to the number of the tribes of Israel.'),
('EZR', 6, 18, 'EZR.6.18', 'They set the priests in their divisions and the Levites in their courses, for the service of God which is at Jerusalem, as it is written in the book of Moses.'),
('EZR', 6, 19, 'EZR.6.19', 'The children of the captivity kept the Passover on the fourteenth day of the first month.'),
('EZR', 6, 20, 'EZR.6.20', 'Because the priests and the Levites had purified themselves together, all of them were pure. They killed the Passover for all the children of the captivity, for their brothers the priests, and for themselves.'),
('EZR', 6, 21, 'EZR.6.21', 'The children of Israel who had returned out of the captivity, and all who had separated themselves to them from the filthiness of the nations of the land to seek the LORD, the God of Israel, ate,'),
('EZR', 6, 22, 'EZR.6.22', 'and kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with joy; because the LORD had made them joyful, and had turned the heart of the king of Assyria to them, to strengthen their hands in the work of God, the God of Israel’s house.'),
('EZR', 7, 1, 'EZR.7.1', 'Now after these things, in the reign of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Ezra the son of Seraiah, the son of Azariah, the son of Hilkiah,'),
('EZR', 7, 2, 'EZR.7.2', 'the son of Shallum, the son of Zadok, the son of Ahitub,'),
('EZR', 7, 3, 'EZR.7.3', 'the son of Amariah, the son of Azariah, the son of Meraioth,'),
('EZR', 7, 4, 'EZR.7.4', 'the son of Zerahiah, the son of Uzzi, the son of Bukki,'),
('EZR', 7, 5, 'EZR.7.5', 'the son of Abishua, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the chief priest—'),
('EZR', 7, 6, 'EZR.7.6', 'this Ezra went up from Babylon. He was a skilled scribe in the law of Moses, which the LORD, the God of Israel, had given; and the king granted him all his request, according to the LORD his God’s hand on him.'),
('EZR', 7, 7, 'EZR.7.7', 'Some of the children of Israel, including some of the priests, the Levites, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants went up to Jerusalem in the seventh year of Artaxerxes the king.'),
('EZR', 7, 8, 'EZR.7.8', 'He came to Jerusalem in the fifth month, which was in the seventh year of the king.'),
('EZR', 7, 9, 'EZR.7.9', 'For on the first day of the first month he began to go up from Babylon; and on the first day of the fifth month he came to Jerusalem, according to the good hand of his God on him.'),
('EZR', 7, 10, 'EZR.7.10', 'For Ezra had set his heart to seek the LORD’s law, and to do it, and to teach statutes and ordinances in Israel.'),
('EZR', 7, 11, 'EZR.7.11', 'Now this is the copy of the letter that King Artaxerxes gave to Ezra the priest, the scribe, even the scribe of the words of the LORD’s commandments, and of his statutes to Israel:'),
('EZR', 7, 12, 'EZR.7.12', 'Artaxerxes, king of kings, To Ezra the priest, the scribe of the law of the perfect God of heaven. Now'),
('EZR', 7, 13, 'EZR.7.13', 'I make a decree that all those of the people of Israel and their priests and the Levites in my realm, who intend of their own free will to go to Jerusalem, go with you.'),
('EZR', 7, 14, 'EZR.7.14', 'Because you are sent by the king and his seven counselors to inquire concerning Judah and Jerusalem, according to the law of your God which is in your hand,'),
('EZR', 7, 15, 'EZR.7.15', 'and to carry the silver and gold, which the king and his counselors have freely offered to the God of Israel, whose habitation is in Jerusalem,'),
('EZR', 7, 16, 'EZR.7.16', 'and all the silver and gold that you will find in all the province of Babylon, with the free will offering of the people and of the priests, offering willingly for the house of their God which is in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 7, 17, 'EZR.7.17', 'Therefore you shall with all diligence buy with this money bulls, rams, and lambs with their meal offerings and their drink offerings, and shall offer them on the altar of the house of your God which is in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 7, 18, 'EZR.7.18', 'Whatever seems good to you and to your brothers to do with the rest of the silver and the gold, do that according to the will of your God.'),
('EZR', 7, 19, 'EZR.7.19', 'The vessels that are given to you for the service of the house of your God, deliver before the God of Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 7, 20, 'EZR.7.20', 'Whatever more will be needed for the house of your God, which you may have occasion to give, give it out of the king’s treasure house.'),
('EZR', 7, 21, 'EZR.7.21', 'I, even I, Artaxerxes the king, make a decree to all the treasurers who are beyond the River, that whatever Ezra the priest, the scribe of the law of the God of heaven, requires of you, it shall be done with all diligence,'),
('EZR', 7, 22, 'EZR.7.22', 'up to one hundred talents of silver, and to one hundred cors of wheat, and to one hundred baths of wine, and to one hundred baths of oil, and salt without prescribing how much.'),
('EZR', 7, 23, 'EZR.7.23', 'Whatever is commanded by the God of heaven, let it be done exactly for the house of the God of heaven; for why should there be wrath against the realm of the king and his sons?'),
('EZR', 7, 24, 'EZR.7.24', 'Also we inform you that it shall not be lawful to impose tribute, custom, or toll on any of the priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, temple servants, or laborers of this house of God.'),
('EZR', 7, 25, 'EZR.7.25', 'You, Ezra, according to the wisdom of your God that is in your hand, appoint magistrates and judges who may judge all the people who are beyond the River, who all know the laws of your God; and teach him who doesn’t know them.'),
('EZR', 7, 26, 'EZR.7.26', 'Whoever will not do the law of your God and the law of the king, let judgment be executed on him with all diligence, whether it is to death, or to banishment, or to confiscation of goods, or to imprisonment.'),
('EZR', 7, 27, 'EZR.7.27', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of our fathers, who has put such a thing as this in the king’s heart, to beautify the LORD’s house which is in Jerusalem;'),
('EZR', 7, 28, 'EZR.7.28', 'and has extended loving kindness to me before the king and his counselors, and before all the king’s mighty princes. I was strengthened according to the LORD my God’s hand on me, and I gathered together chief men out of Israel to go up with me.'),
('EZR', 8, 1, 'EZR.8.1', 'Now these are the heads of their fathers’ households, and this is the genealogy of those who went up with me from Babylon, in the reign of Artaxerxes the king:'),
('EZR', 8, 2, 'EZR.8.2', 'Of the sons of Phinehas, Gershom. Of the sons of Ithamar, Daniel. Of the sons of David, Hattush.'),
('EZR', 8, 3, 'EZR.8.3', 'Of the sons of Shecaniah, of the sons of Parosh, Zechariah; and with him were listed by genealogy of the males one hundred fifty.'),
('EZR', 8, 4, 'EZR.8.4', 'Of the sons of Pahathmoab, Eliehoenai the son of Zerahiah; and with him two hundred males.'),
('EZR', 8, 5, 'EZR.8.5', 'Of the sons of Shecaniah, the son of Jahaziel; and with him three hundred males.'),
('EZR', 8, 6, 'EZR.8.6', 'Of the sons of Adin, Ebed the son of Jonathan; and with him fifty males.'),
('EZR', 8, 7, 'EZR.8.7', 'Of the sons of Elam, Jeshaiah the son of Athaliah; and with him seventy males.'),
('EZR', 8, 8, 'EZR.8.8', 'Of the sons of Shephatiah, Zebadiah the son of Michael; and with him eighty males.'),
('EZR', 8, 9, 'EZR.8.9', 'Of the sons of Joab, Obadiah the son of Jehiel; and with him two hundred eighteen males.'),
('EZR', 8, 10, 'EZR.8.10', 'Of the sons of Shelomith, the son of Josiphiah; and with him one hundred sixty males.'),
('EZR', 8, 11, 'EZR.8.11', 'Of the sons of Bebai, Zechariah the son of Bebai; and with him twenty-eight males.'),
('EZR', 8, 12, 'EZR.8.12', 'Of the sons of Azgad, Johanan the son of Hakkatan; and with him one hundred ten males.'),
('EZR', 8, 13, 'EZR.8.13', 'Of the sons of Adonikam, who were the last, their names are: Eliphelet, Jeuel, and Shemaiah; and with them sixty males.'),
('EZR', 8, 14, 'EZR.8.14', 'Of the sons of Bigvai, Uthai and Zabbud; and with them seventy males.'),
('EZR', 8, 15, 'EZR.8.15', 'I gathered them together to the river that runs to Ahava; and there we encamped three days. Then I looked around at the people and the priests, and found there were none of the sons of Levi.'),
('EZR', 8, 16, 'EZR.8.16', 'Then I sent for Eliezer, for Ariel, for Shemaiah, for Elnathan, for Jarib, for Elnathan, for Nathan, for Zechariah, and for Meshullam, chief men; also for Joiarib and for Elnathan, who were teachers.'),
('EZR', 8, 17, 'EZR.8.17', 'I sent them out to Iddo the chief at the place Casiphia; and I told them what they should tell Iddo and his brothers the temple servants at the place Casiphia, that they should bring to us ministers for the house of our God.'),
('EZR', 8, 18, 'EZR.8.18', 'According to the good hand of our God on us they brought us a man of discretion, of the sons of Mahli, the son of Levi, the son of Israel, namely Sherebiah, with his sons and his brothers, eighteen;'),
('EZR', 8, 19, 'EZR.8.19', 'and Hashabiah, and with him Jeshaiah of the sons of Merari, his brothers and their sons, twenty;'),
('EZR', 8, 20, 'EZR.8.20', 'and of the temple servants, whom David and the princes had given for the service of the Levites, two hundred twenty temple servants. All of them were mentioned by name.'),
('EZR', 8, 21, 'EZR.8.21', 'Then I proclaimed a fast there at the river Ahava, that we might humble ourselves before our God, to seek from him a straight way for us, for our little ones, and for all our possessions.'),
('EZR', 8, 22, 'EZR.8.22', 'For I was ashamed to ask of the king a band of soldiers and horsemen to help us against the enemy on the way, because we had spoken to the king, saying, “The hand of our God is on all those who seek him, for good; but his power and his wrath is against all those who forsake him.”'),
('EZR', 8, 23, 'EZR.8.23', 'So we fasted and begged our God for this, and he granted our request.'),
('EZR', 8, 24, 'EZR.8.24', 'Then I set apart twelve of the chiefs of the priests, even Sherebiah, Hashabiah, and ten of their brothers with them,'),
('EZR', 8, 25, 'EZR.8.25', 'and weighed to them the silver, the gold, and the vessels, even the offering for the house of our God, which the king, his counselors, his princes, and all Israel there present, had offered.'),
('EZR', 8, 26, 'EZR.8.26', 'I weighed into their hand six hundred fifty talents of silver, one hundred talents of silver vessels, one hundred talents of gold,'),
('EZR', 8, 27, 'EZR.8.27', 'twenty bowls of gold weighing one thousand darics, and two vessels of fine bright bronze, precious as gold.'),
('EZR', 8, 28, 'EZR.8.28', 'I said to them, “You are holy to the LORD, and the vessels are holy. The silver and the gold are a free will offering to the LORD, the God of your fathers.'),
('EZR', 8, 29, 'EZR.8.29', 'Watch and keep them until you weigh them before the chiefs of the priests, the Levites, and the princes of the fathers’ households of Israel at Jerusalem, in the rooms of the LORD’s house.”'),
('EZR', 8, 30, 'EZR.8.30', 'So the priests and the Levites received the weight of the silver, the gold, and the vessels, to bring them to Jerusalem to the house of our God.'),
('EZR', 8, 31, 'EZR.8.31', 'Then we departed from the river Ahava on the twelfth day of the first month, to go to Jerusalem. The hand of our God was on us, and he delivered us from the hand of the enemy and the bandits by the way.'),
('EZR', 8, 32, 'EZR.8.32', 'We came to Jerusalem, and stayed there three days.'),
('EZR', 8, 33, 'EZR.8.33', 'On the fourth day the silver and the gold and the vessels were weighed in the house of our God into the hand of Meremoth the son of Uriah the priest; and with him was Eleazar the son of Phinehas; and with them were Jozabad the son of Jeshua, and Noadiah the son of Binnui, the Levites.'),
('EZR', 8, 34, 'EZR.8.34', 'Everything was counted and weighed; and all the weight was written at that time.'),
('EZR', 8, 35, 'EZR.8.35', 'The children of the captivity, who had come out of exile, offered burnt offerings to the God of Israel: twelve bulls for all Israel, ninety-six rams, seventy-seven lambs, and twelve male goats for a sin offering. All this was a burnt offering to the LORD.'),
('EZR', 8, 36, 'EZR.8.36', 'They delivered the king’s commissions to the king’s local governors and to the governors beyond the River. So they supported the people and God’s house.'),
('EZR', 9, 1, 'EZR.9.1', 'Now when these things were done, the princes came near to me, saying, “The people of Israel, the priests, and the Levites have not separated themselves from the peoples of the lands, following their abominations, even those of the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Jebusites, the Ammonites, the Moabites, the Egyptians, and the Amorites.'),
('EZR', 9, 2, 'EZR.9.2', 'For they have taken of their daughters for themselves and for their sons, so that the holy offspring have mixed themselves with the peoples of the lands. Yes, the hand of the princes and rulers has been chief in this trespass.”'),
('EZR', 9, 3, 'EZR.9.3', 'When I heard this thing, I tore my garment and my robe, and pulled the hair out of my head and of my beard, and sat down confounded.'),
('EZR', 9, 4, 'EZR.9.4', 'Then everyone who trembled at the words of the God of Israel were assembled to me because of the trespass of the exiles; and I sat confounded until the evening offering.'),
('EZR', 9, 5, 'EZR.9.5', 'At the evening offering I rose up from my humiliation, even with my garment and my robe torn; and I fell on my knees, and spread out my hands to the LORD my God;'),
('EZR', 9, 6, 'EZR.9.6', 'and I said, “My God, I am ashamed and blush to lift up my face to you, my God, for our iniquities have increased over our head, and our guiltiness has grown up to the heavens.'),
('EZR', 9, 7, 'EZR.9.7', 'Since the days of our fathers we have been exceedingly guilty to this day; and for our iniquities we, our kings, and our priests have been delivered into the hand of the kings of the lands, to the sword, to captivity, to plunder, and to confusion of face, as it is this day.'),
('EZR', 9, 8, 'EZR.9.8', 'Now for a little moment grace has been shown from the LORD our God, to leave us a remnant to escape, and to give us a stake in his holy place, that our God may lighten our eyes, and revive us a little in our bondage.'),
('EZR', 9, 9, 'EZR.9.9', 'For we are bondservants; yet our God has not forsaken us in our bondage, but has extended loving kindness to us in the sight of the kings of Persia, to revive us, to set up the house of our God, and to repair its ruins, and to give us a wall in Judah and in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 9, 10, 'EZR.9.10', '“Now, our God, what shall we say after this? For we have forsaken your commandments,'),
('EZR', 9, 11, 'EZR.9.11', 'which you have commanded by your servants the prophets, saying, ‘The land to which you go to possess is an unclean land through the uncleanness of the peoples of the lands, through their abominations, which have filled it from one end to another with their filthiness.'),
('EZR', 9, 12, 'EZR.9.12', 'Now therefore don’t give your daughters to their sons. Don’t take their daughters to your sons, nor seek their peace or their prosperity forever, that you may be strong and eat the good of the land, and leave it for an inheritance to your children forever.’'),
('EZR', 9, 13, 'EZR.9.13', '“After all that has come on us for our evil deeds and for our great guilt, since you, our God, have punished us less than our iniquities deserve, and have given us such a remnant,'),
('EZR', 9, 14, 'EZR.9.14', 'shall we again break your commandments, and join ourselves with the peoples that do these abominations? Wouldn’t you be angry with us until you had consumed us, so that there would be no remnant, nor any to escape?'),
('EZR', 9, 15, 'EZR.9.15', 'LORD, the God of Israel, you are righteous; for we are left a remnant that has escaped, as it is today. Behold, we are before you in our guiltiness; for no one can stand before you because of this.”'),
('EZR', 10, 1, 'EZR.10.1', 'Now while Ezra prayed and made confession, weeping and casting himself down before God’s house, there was gathered together to him out of Israel a very great assembly of men and women and children; for the people wept very bitterly.'),
('EZR', 10, 2, 'EZR.10.2', 'Shecaniah the son of Jehiel, one of the sons of Elam, answered Ezra, “We have trespassed against our God, and have married foreign women of the peoples of the land. Yet now there is hope for Israel concerning this thing.'),
('EZR', 10, 3, 'EZR.10.3', 'Now therefore let’s make a covenant with our God to put away all the wives and those who are born of them, according to the counsel of my lord and of those who tremble at the commandment of our God. Let it be done according to the law.'),
('EZR', 10, 4, 'EZR.10.4', 'Arise, for the matter belongs to you and we are with you. Be courageous, and do it.”'),
('EZR', 10, 5, 'EZR.10.5', 'Then Ezra arose, and made the chiefs of the priests, the Levites, and all Israel to swear that they would do according to this word. So they swore.'),
('EZR', 10, 6, 'EZR.10.6', 'Then Ezra rose up from before God’s house, and went into the room of Jehohanan the son of Eliashib. When he came there, he didn’t eat bread or drink water, for he mourned because of the trespass of the exiles.'),
('EZR', 10, 7, 'EZR.10.7', 'They made a proclamation throughout Judah and Jerusalem to all the children of the captivity, that they should gather themselves together to Jerusalem;'),
('EZR', 10, 8, 'EZR.10.8', 'and that whoever didn’t come within three days, according to the counsel of the princes and the elders, all his possessions should be forfeited, and he himself separated from the assembly of the captivity.'),
('EZR', 10, 9, 'EZR.10.9', 'Then all the men of Judah and Benjamin gathered themselves together to Jerusalem within the three days. It was the ninth month, on the twentieth day of the month; and all the people sat in the wide place in front of God’s house, trembling because of this matter, and because of the great rain.'),
('EZR', 10, 10, 'EZR.10.10', 'Ezra the priest stood up and said to them, “You have trespassed, and have married foreign women, increasing the guilt of Israel.'),
('EZR', 10, 11, 'EZR.10.11', 'Now therefore make confession to the LORD, the God of your fathers and do his pleasure. Separate yourselves from the peoples of the land and from the foreign women.”'),
('EZR', 10, 12, 'EZR.10.12', 'Then all the assembly answered with a loud voice, “We must do as you have said concerning us.'),
('EZR', 10, 13, 'EZR.10.13', 'But the people are many, and it is a time of much rain, and we are not able to stand outside. This is not a work of one day or two, for we have greatly transgressed in this matter.'),
('EZR', 10, 14, 'EZR.10.14', 'Now let our princes be appointed for all the assembly, and let all those who are in our cities who have married foreign women come at appointed times, and with them the elders of every city and its judges, until the fierce wrath of our God is turned from us, until this matter is resolved.”'),
('EZR', 10, 15, 'EZR.10.15', 'Only Jonathan the son of Asahel and Jahzeiah the son of Tikvah stood up against this; and Meshullam and Shabbethai the Levite helped them.'),
('EZR', 10, 16, 'EZR.10.16', 'The children of the captivity did so. Ezra the priest, with certain heads of fathers’ households, after their fathers’ houses, and all of them by their names, were set apart; and they sat down in the first day of the tenth month to examine the matter.'),
('EZR', 10, 17, 'EZR.10.17', 'They finished with all the men who had married foreign women by the first day of the first month.'),
('EZR', 10, 18, 'EZR.10.18', 'Among the sons of the priests there were found who had married foreign women: of the sons of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and his brothers: Maaseiah, Eliezer, Jarib, and Gedaliah.'),
('EZR', 10, 19, 'EZR.10.19', 'They gave their hand that they would put away their wives; and being guilty, they offered a ram of the flock for their guilt.'),
('EZR', 10, 20, 'EZR.10.20', 'Of the sons of Immer: Hanani and Zebadiah.'),
('EZR', 10, 21, 'EZR.10.21', 'Of the sons of Harim: Maaseiah, Elijah, Shemaiah, Jehiel, and Uzziah.'),
('EZR', 10, 22, 'EZR.10.22', 'Of the sons of Pashhur: Elioenai, Maaseiah, Ishmael, Nethanel, Jozabad, and Elasah.'),
('EZR', 10, 23, 'EZR.10.23', 'Of the Levites: Jozabad, Shimei, Kelaiah (also called Kelita), Pethahiah, Judah, and Eliezer.'),
('EZR', 10, 24, 'EZR.10.24', 'Of the singers: Eliashib. Of the gatekeepers: Shallum, Telem, and Uri.'),
('EZR', 10, 25, 'EZR.10.25', 'Of Israel: Of the sons of Parosh: Ramiah, Izziah, Malchijah, Mijamin, Eleazar, Malchijah, and Benaiah.'),
('EZR', 10, 26, 'EZR.10.26', 'Of the sons of Elam: Mattaniah, Zechariah, Jehiel, Abdi, Jeremoth, and Elijah.'),
('EZR', 10, 27, 'EZR.10.27', 'Of the sons of Zattu: Elioenai, Eliashib, Mattaniah, Jeremoth, Zabad, and Aziza.'),
('EZR', 10, 28, 'EZR.10.28', 'Of the sons of Bebai: Jehohanan, Hananiah, Zabbai, and Athlai.'),
('EZR', 10, 29, 'EZR.10.29', 'Of the sons of Bani: Meshullam, Malluch, Adaiah, Jashub, Sheal, and Jeremoth.'),
('EZR', 10, 30, 'EZR.10.30', 'Of the sons of Pahathmoab: Adna, Chelal, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattaniah, Bezalel, Binnui, and Manasseh.'),
('EZR', 10, 31, 'EZR.10.31', 'Of the sons of Harim: Eliezer, Isshijah, Malchijah, Shemaiah, Shimeon,'),
('EZR', 10, 32, 'EZR.10.32', 'Benjamin, Malluch, and Shemariah.'),
('EZR', 10, 33, 'EZR.10.33', 'Of the sons of Hashum: Mattenai, Mattattah, Zabad, Eliphelet, Jeremai, Manasseh, and Shimei.'),
('EZR', 10, 34, 'EZR.10.34', 'Of the sons of Bani: Maadai, Amram, Uel,'),
('EZR', 10, 35, 'EZR.10.35', 'Benaiah, Bedeiah, Cheluhi,'),
('EZR', 10, 36, 'EZR.10.36', 'Vaniah, Meremoth, Eliashib,'),
('EZR', 10, 37, 'EZR.10.37', 'Mattaniah, Mattenai, Jaasu,'),
('EZR', 10, 38, 'EZR.10.38', 'Bani, Binnui, Shimei,'),
('EZR', 10, 39, 'EZR.10.39', 'Shelemiah, Nathan, Adaiah,'),
('EZR', 10, 40, 'EZR.10.40', 'Machnadebai, Shashai, Sharai,'),
('EZR', 10, 41, 'EZR.10.41', 'Azarel, Shelemiah, Shemariah,'),
('EZR', 10, 42, 'EZR.10.42', 'Shallum, Amariah, and Joseph.'),
('EZR', 10, 43, 'EZR.10.43', 'Of the sons of Nebo: Jeiel, Mattithiah, Zabad, Zebina, Iddo, Joel, and Benaiah.'),
('EZR', 10, 44, 'EZR.10.44', 'All these had taken foreign wives. Some of them had wives by whom they had children.'),
('NEH', 1, 1, 'NEH.1.1', 'The words of Nehemiah the son of Hacaliah. Now in the month Chislev, in the twentieth year, as I was in Susa the palace,'),
('NEH', 1, 2, 'NEH.1.2', 'Hanani, one of my brothers, came, he and certain men out of Judah; and I asked them about the Jews who had escaped, who were left of the captivity, and concerning Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 1, 3, 'NEH.1.3', 'They said to me, “The remnant who are left of the captivity there in the province are in great affliction and reproach. The wall of Jerusalem is also broken down, and its gates are burned with fire.”'),
('NEH', 1, 4, 'NEH.1.4', 'When I heard these words, I sat down and wept, and mourned several days; and I fasted and prayed before the God of heaven,'),
('NEH', 1, 5, 'NEH.1.5', 'and said, “I beg you, LORD, the God of heaven, the great and awesome God who keeps covenant and loving kindness with those who love him and keep his commandments,'),
('NEH', 1, 6, 'NEH.1.6', 'let your ear now be attentive and your eyes open, that you may listen to the prayer of your servant which I pray before you at this time, day and night, for the children of Israel your servants, while I confess the sins of the children of Israel which we have sinned against you. Yes, I and my father’s house have sinned.'),
('NEH', 1, 7, 'NEH.1.7', 'We have dealt very corruptly against you, and have not kept the commandments, nor the statutes, nor the ordinances, which you commanded your servant Moses.'),
('NEH', 1, 8, 'NEH.1.8', '“Remember, I beg you, the word that you commanded your servant Moses, saying, ‘If you trespass, I will scatter you among the peoples;'),
('NEH', 1, 9, 'NEH.1.9', 'but if you return to me, and keep my commandments and do them, though your outcasts were in the uttermost part of the heavens, yet I will gather them from there, and will bring them to the place that I have chosen, to cause my name to dwell there.’'),
('NEH', 1, 10, 'NEH.1.10', '“Now these are your servants and your people, whom you have redeemed by your great power and by your strong hand.'),
('NEH', 1, 11, 'NEH.1.11', 'Lord, I beg you, let your ear be attentive now to the prayer of your servant, and to the prayer of your servants who delight to fear your name; and please prosper your servant today, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man.” Now I was cup bearer to the king.'),
('NEH', 2, 1, 'NEH.2.1', 'In the month Nisan, in the twentieth year of Artaxerxes the king, when wine was before him, I picked up the wine, and gave it to the king. Now I had not been sad before in his presence.'),
('NEH', 2, 2, 'NEH.2.2', 'The king said to me, “Why is your face sad, since you are not sick? This is nothing else but sorrow of heart.” Then I was very much afraid.'),
('NEH', 2, 3, 'NEH.2.3', 'I said to the king, “Let the king live forever! Why shouldn’t my face be sad, when the city, the place of my fathers’ tombs, lies waste, and its gates have been consumed with fire?”'),
('NEH', 2, 4, 'NEH.2.4', 'Then the king said to me, “What is your request?” So I prayed to the God of heaven.'),
('NEH', 2, 5, 'NEH.2.5', 'I said to the king, “If it pleases the king, and if your servant has found favor in your sight, I ask that you would send me to Judah, to the city of my fathers’ tombs, that I may build it.”'),
('NEH', 2, 6, 'NEH.2.6', 'The king said to me (the queen was also sitting by him), “How long will your journey be? When will you return?” So it pleased the king to send me, and I set a time for him.'),
('NEH', 2, 7, 'NEH.2.7', 'Moreover I said to the king, “If it pleases the king, let letters be given me to the governors beyond the River, that they may let me pass through until I come to Judah;'),
('NEH', 2, 8, 'NEH.2.8', 'and a letter to Asaph the keeper of the king’s forest, that he may give me timber to make beams for the gates of the citadel by the temple, for the wall of the city, and for the house that I will occupy.” The king granted my requests, because of the good hand of my God on me.'),
('NEH', 2, 9, 'NEH.2.9', 'Then I came to the governors beyond the River, and gave them the king’s letters. Now the king had sent captains of the army and horsemen with me.'),
('NEH', 2, 10, 'NEH.2.10', 'When Sanballat the Horonite and Tobiah the Ammonite servant heard of it, it grieved them exceedingly, because a man had come to seek the welfare of the children of Israel.'),
('NEH', 2, 11, 'NEH.2.11', 'So I came to Jerusalem, and was there three days.'),
('NEH', 2, 12, 'NEH.2.12', 'I arose in the night, I and a few men with me. I didn’t tell anyone what my God put into my heart to do for Jerusalem. There wasn’t any animal with me except the animal that I rode on.'),
('NEH', 2, 13, 'NEH.2.13', 'I went out by night by the valley gate toward the jackal’s well, then to the dung gate; and I inspected the walls of Jerusalem, which were broken down, and its gates were consumed with fire.'),
('NEH', 2, 14, 'NEH.2.14', 'Then I went on to the spring gate and to the king’s pool, but there was no place for the animal that was under me to pass.'),
('NEH', 2, 15, 'NEH.2.15', 'Then I went up in the night by the brook and inspected the wall; and I turned back, and entered by the valley gate, and so returned.'),
('NEH', 2, 16, 'NEH.2.16', 'The rulers didn’t know where I went, or what I did. I had not as yet told it to the Jews, nor to the priests, nor to the nobles, nor to the rulers, nor to the rest who did the work.'),
('NEH', 2, 17, 'NEH.2.17', 'Then I said to them, “You see the bad situation that we are in, how Jerusalem lies waste, and its gates are burned with fire. Come, let’s build up the wall of Jerusalem, that we won’t be disgraced.”'),
('NEH', 2, 18, 'NEH.2.18', 'I told them about the hand of my God which was good on me, and also about the king’s words that he had spoken to me. They said, “Let’s rise up and build.” So they strengthened their hands for the good work.'),
('NEH', 2, 19, 'NEH.2.19', 'But when Sanballat the Horonite, Tobiah the Ammonite servant, and Geshem the Arabian, heard it, they ridiculed us and despised us, and said, “What is this thing that you are doing? Will you rebel against the king?”'),
('NEH', 2, 20, 'NEH.2.20', 'Then I answered them, and said to them, “The God of heaven will prosper us. Therefore we, his servants, will arise and build; but you have no portion, nor right, nor memorial in Jerusalem.”'),
('NEH', 3, 1, 'NEH.3.1', 'Then Eliashib the high priest rose up with his brothers the priests, and they built the sheep gate. They sanctified it, and set up its doors. They sanctified it even to the tower of Hammeah, to the tower of Hananel.'),
('NEH', 3, 2, 'NEH.3.2', 'Next to him the men of Jericho built. Next to them Zaccur the son of Imri built.'),
('NEH', 3, 3, 'NEH.3.3', 'The sons of Hassenaah built the fish gate. They laid its beams, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars.'),
('NEH', 3, 4, 'NEH.3.4', 'Next to them, Meremoth the son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz made repairs. Next to them, Meshullam the son of Berechiah, the son of Meshezabel made repairs. Next to them, Zadok the son of Baana made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 5, 'NEH.3.5', 'Next to them, the Tekoites made repairs; but their nobles didn’t put their necks to the Lord’s work.'),
('NEH', 3, 6, 'NEH.3.6', 'Joiada the son of Paseah and Meshullam the son of Besodeiah repaired the old gate. They laid its beams and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars.'),
('NEH', 3, 7, 'NEH.3.7', 'Next to them, Melatiah the Gibeonite and Jadon the Meronothite, the men of Gibeon and of Mizpah, repaired the residence of the governor beyond the River.'),
('NEH', 3, 8, 'NEH.3.8', 'Next to him, Uzziel the son of Harhaiah, goldsmiths, made repairs. Next to him, Hananiah, one of the perfumers, made repairs, and they fortified Jerusalem even to the wide wall.'),
('NEH', 3, 9, 'NEH.3.9', 'Next to them, Rephaiah the son of Hur, the ruler of half the district of Jerusalem, made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 10, 'NEH.3.10', 'Next to them, Jedaiah the son of Harumaph made repairs across from his house. Next to him, Hattush the son of Hashabneiah made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 11, 'NEH.3.11', 'Malchijah the son of Harim and Hasshub the son of Pahathmoab repaired another portion and the tower of the furnaces.'),
('NEH', 3, 12, 'NEH.3.12', 'Next to him, Shallum the son of Hallohesh, the ruler of half the district of Jerusalem, he and his daughters made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 13, 'NEH.3.13', 'Hanun and the inhabitants of Zanoah repaired the valley gate. They built it, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars, and one thousand cubits of the wall to the dung gate.'),
('NEH', 3, 14, 'NEH.3.14', 'Malchijah the son of Rechab, the ruler of the district of Beth Haccherem, repaired the dung gate. He built it, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars.'),
('NEH', 3, 15, 'NEH.3.15', 'Shallun the son of Colhozeh, the ruler of the district of Mizpah, repaired the spring gate. He built it, covered it, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars; and he repaired the wall of the pool of Shelah by the king’s garden, even to the stairs that go down from David’s city.'),
('NEH', 3, 16, 'NEH.3.16', 'After him, Nehemiah the son of Azbuk, the ruler of half the district of Beth Zur, made repairs to the place opposite the tombs of David, and to the pool that was made, and to the house of the mighty men.'),
('NEH', 3, 17, 'NEH.3.17', 'After him, the Levites—Rehum the son of Bani made repairs. Next to him, Hashabiah, the ruler of half the district of Keilah, made repairs for his district.'),
('NEH', 3, 18, 'NEH.3.18', 'After him, their brothers, Bavvai the son of Henadad, the ruler of half the district of Keilah made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 19, 'NEH.3.19', 'Next to him, Ezer the son of Jeshua, the ruler of Mizpah, repaired another portion across from the ascent to the armory at the turning of the wall.'),
('NEH', 3, 20, 'NEH.3.20', 'After him, Baruch the son of Zabbai earnestly repaired another portion, from the turning of the wall to the door of the house of Eliashib the high priest.'),
('NEH', 3, 21, 'NEH.3.21', 'After him, Meremoth the son of Uriah the son of Hakkoz repaired another portion, from the door of the house of Eliashib even to the end of the house of Eliashib.'),
('NEH', 3, 22, 'NEH.3.22', 'After him, the priests, the men of the surrounding area made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 23, 'NEH.3.23', 'After them, Benjamin and Hasshub made repairs across from their house. After them, Azariah the son of Maaseiah the son of Ananiah made repairs beside his own house.'),
('NEH', 3, 24, 'NEH.3.24', 'After him, Binnui the son of Henadad repaired another portion, from the house of Azariah to the turning of the wall, and to the corner.'),
('NEH', 3, 25, 'NEH.3.25', 'Palal the son of Uzai made repairs opposite the turning of the wall, and the tower that stands out from the upper house of the king, which is by the court of the guard. After him Pedaiah the son of Parosh made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 26, 'NEH.3.26', '(Now the temple servants lived in Ophel, to the place opposite the water gate toward the east, and the tower that stands out.)'),
('NEH', 3, 27, 'NEH.3.27', 'After him the Tekoites repaired another portion, opposite the great tower that stands out, and to the wall of Ophel.'),
('NEH', 3, 28, 'NEH.3.28', 'Above the horse gate, the priests made repairs, everyone across from his own house.'),
('NEH', 3, 29, 'NEH.3.29', 'After them, Zadok the son of Immer made repairs across from his own house. After him, Shemaiah the son of Shecaniah, the keeper of the east gate, made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 30, 'NEH.3.30', 'After him, Hananiah the son of Shelemiah, and Hanun, the sixth son of Zalaph, repaired another portion. After him, Meshullam the son of Berechiah made repairs across from his room.'),
('NEH', 3, 31, 'NEH.3.31', 'After him, Malchijah, one of the goldsmiths to the house of the temple servants, and of the merchants, made repairs opposite the gate of Hammiphkad and to the ascent of the corner.'),
('NEH', 3, 32, 'NEH.3.32', 'Between the ascent of the corner and the sheep gate, the goldsmiths and the merchants made repairs.'),
('NEH', 4, 1, 'NEH.4.1', 'But when Sanballat heard that we were building the wall, he was angry, and was very indignant, and mocked the Jews.'),
('NEH', 4, 2, 'NEH.4.2', 'He spoke before his brothers and the army of Samaria, and said, “What are these feeble Jews doing? Will they fortify themselves? Will they sacrifice? Will they finish in a day? Will they revive the stones out of the heaps of rubbish, since they are burned?”'),
('NEH', 4, 3, 'NEH.4.3', 'Now Tobiah the Ammonite was by him, and he said, “What they are building, if a fox climbed up it, he would break down their stone wall.”'),
('NEH', 4, 4, 'NEH.4.4', '“Hear, our God, for we are despised. Turn back their reproach on their own head. Give them up for a plunder in a land of captivity.'),
('NEH', 4, 5, 'NEH.4.5', 'Don’t cover their iniquity. Don’t let their sin be blotted out from before you; for they have insulted the builders.”'),
('NEH', 4, 6, 'NEH.4.6', 'So we built the wall; and all the wall was joined together to half its height, for the people had a mind to work.'),
('NEH', 4, 7, 'NEH.4.7', 'But when Sanballat, Tobiah, the Arabians, the Ammonites, and the Ashdodites heard that the repairing of the walls of Jerusalem went forward, and that the breaches began to be filled, they were very angry;'),
('NEH', 4, 8, 'NEH.4.8', 'and they all conspired together to come and fight against Jerusalem, and to cause confusion among us.'),
('NEH', 4, 9, 'NEH.4.9', 'But we made our prayer to our God, and set a watch against them day and night because of them.'),
('NEH', 4, 10, 'NEH.4.10', 'Judah said, “The strength of the bearers of burdens is fading and there is much rubble, so that we are not able to build the wall.”'),
('NEH', 4, 11, 'NEH.4.11', 'Our adversaries said, “They will not know or see, until we come in among them and kill them, and cause the work to cease.”'),
('NEH', 4, 12, 'NEH.4.12', 'When the Jews who lived by them came, they said to us ten times from all places, “Wherever you turn, they will attack us.”'),
('NEH', 4, 13, 'NEH.4.13', 'Therefore I set guards in the lowest parts of the space behind the wall, in the open places. I set the people by family groups with their swords, their spears, and their bows.'),
('NEH', 4, 14, 'NEH.4.14', 'I looked, and rose up, and said to the nobles, to the rulers, and to the rest of the people, “Don’t be afraid of them! Remember the Lord, who is great and awesome, and fight for your brothers, your sons, your daughters, your wives, and your houses.”'),
('NEH', 4, 15, 'NEH.4.15', 'When our enemies heard that it was known to us, and God had brought their counsel to nothing, all of us returned to the wall, everyone to his work.'),
('NEH', 4, 16, 'NEH.4.16', 'From that time forth, half of my servants did the work, and half of them held the spears, the shields, the bows, and the coats of mail; and the rulers were behind all the house of Judah.'),
('NEH', 4, 17, 'NEH.4.17', 'Those who built the wall, and those who bore burdens loaded themselves; everyone with one of his hands did the work, and with the other held his weapon.'),
('NEH', 4, 18, 'NEH.4.18', 'Among the builders, everyone wore his sword at his side, and so built. He who sounded the trumpet was by me.'),
('NEH', 4, 19, 'NEH.4.19', 'I said to the nobles, and to the rulers and to the rest of the people, “The work is great and widely spread out, and we are separated on the wall, far from one another.'),
('NEH', 4, 20, 'NEH.4.20', 'Wherever you hear the sound of the trumpet, rally there to us. Our God will fight for us.”'),
('NEH', 4, 21, 'NEH.4.21', 'So we did the work. Half of the people held the spears from the rising of the morning until the stars appeared.'),
('NEH', 4, 22, 'NEH.4.22', 'Likewise at the same time I said to the people, “Let everyone with his servant lodge within Jerusalem, that in the night they may be a guard to us, and may labor in the day.”'),
('NEH', 4, 23, 'NEH.4.23', 'So neither I, nor my brothers, nor my servants, nor the men of the guard who followed me took off our clothes. Everyone took his weapon to the water.'),
('NEH', 5, 1, 'NEH.5.1', 'Then there arose a great cry of the people and of their wives against their brothers the Jews.'),
('NEH', 5, 2, 'NEH.5.2', 'For there were some who said, “We, our sons and our daughters, are many. Let us get grain, that we may eat and live.”'),
('NEH', 5, 3, 'NEH.5.3', 'There were also some who said, “We are mortgaging our fields, our vineyards, and our houses. Let us get grain, because of the famine.”'),
('NEH', 5, 4, 'NEH.5.4', 'There were also some who said, “We have borrowed money for the king’s tribute using our fields and our vineyards as collateral.'),
('NEH', 5, 5, 'NEH.5.5', 'Yet now our flesh is as the flesh of our brothers, our children as their children. Behold, we bring our sons and our daughters into bondage to be servants, and some of our daughters have been brought into bondage. It is also not in our power to help it, because other men have our fields and our vineyards.”'),
('NEH', 5, 6, 'NEH.5.6', 'I was very angry when I heard their cry and these words.'),
('NEH', 5, 7, 'NEH.5.7', 'Then I consulted with myself, and contended with the nobles and the rulers, and said to them, “You exact usury, everyone of his brother.” I held a great assembly against them.'),
('NEH', 5, 8, 'NEH.5.8', 'I said to them, “We, after our ability, have redeemed our brothers the Jews that were sold to the nations; and would you even sell your brothers, and should they be sold to us?” Then they held their peace, and found not a word to say.'),
('NEH', 5, 9, 'NEH.5.9', 'Also I said, “The thing that you do is not good. Shouldn’t you walk in the fear of our God because of the reproach of the nations, our enemies?'),
('NEH', 5, 10, 'NEH.5.10', 'I likewise, my brothers and my servants, lend them money and grain. Please let us stop this usury.'),
('NEH', 5, 11, 'NEH.5.11', 'Please restore to them, even today, their fields, their vineyards, their olive groves, and their houses, also the hundredth part of the money, and of the grain, the new wine, and the oil, that you are charging them.”'),
('NEH', 5, 12, 'NEH.5.12', 'Then they said, “We will restore them, and will require nothing of them. We will do so, even as you say.” Then I called the priests, and took an oath of them, that they would do according to this promise.'),
('NEH', 5, 13, 'NEH.5.13', 'Also I shook out my lap, and said, “So may God shake out every man from his house, and from his labor, that doesn’t perform this promise; even may he be shaken out and emptied like this.” All the assembly said, “Amen,” and praised the LORD. The people did according to this promise.'),
('NEH', 5, 14, 'NEH.5.14', 'Moreover from the time that I was appointed to be their governor in the land of Judah, from the twentieth year even to the thirty-second year of Artaxerxes the king, that is, twelve years, I and my brothers have not eaten the bread of the governor.'),
('NEH', 5, 15, 'NEH.5.15', 'But the former governors who were before me were supported by the people, and took bread and wine from them, plus forty shekels of silver; yes, even their servants ruled over the people, but I didn’t do so, because of the fear of God.'),
('NEH', 5, 16, 'NEH.5.16', 'Yes, I also continued in the work of this wall. We didn’t buy any land. All my servants were gathered there to the work.'),
('NEH', 5, 17, 'NEH.5.17', 'Moreover there were at my table, of the Jews and the rulers, one hundred fifty men, in addition to those who came to us from among the nations that were around us.'),
('NEH', 5, 18, 'NEH.5.18', 'Now that which was prepared for one day was one ox and six choice sheep. Also fowls were prepared for me, and once in ten days a store of all sorts of wine. Yet for all this, I didn’t demand the governor’s pay, because the bondage was heavy on this people.'),
('NEH', 5, 19, 'NEH.5.19', 'Remember me, my God, for all the good that I have done for this people.'),
('NEH', 6, 1, 'NEH.6.1', 'Now when it was reported to Sanballat, Tobiah, Geshem the Arabian, and to the rest of our enemies that I had built the wall, and that there was no breach left in it (though even to that time I had not set up the doors in the gates),'),
('NEH', 6, 2, 'NEH.6.2', 'Sanballat and Geshem sent to me, saying, “Come! Let’s meet together in the villages in the plain of Ono.” But they intended to harm me.'),
('NEH', 6, 3, 'NEH.6.3', 'I sent messengers to them, saying, “I am doing a great work, so that I can’t come down. Why should the work cease while I leave it and come down to you?”'),
('NEH', 6, 4, 'NEH.6.4', 'They sent to me four times like this; and I answered them the same way.'),
('NEH', 6, 5, 'NEH.6.5', 'Then Sanballat sent his servant to me the same way the fifth time with an open letter in his hand,'),
('NEH', 6, 6, 'NEH.6.6', 'in which was written, “It is reported among the nations, and Gashmu says it, that you and the Jews intend to rebel. Because of that, you are building the wall. You would be their king, according to these words.'),
('NEH', 6, 7, 'NEH.6.7', 'You have also appointed prophets to proclaim of you at Jerusalem, saying, ‘There is a king in Judah!’ Now it will be reported to the king according to these words. Come now therefore, and let’s take counsel together.”'),
('NEH', 6, 8, 'NEH.6.8', 'Then I sent to him, saying, “There are no such things done as you say, but you imagine them out of your own heart.”'),
('NEH', 6, 9, 'NEH.6.9', 'For they all would have made us afraid, saying, “Their hands will be weakened from the work, that it not be done.” But now, strengthen my hands.'),
('NEH', 6, 10, 'NEH.6.10', 'I went to the house of Shemaiah the son of Delaiah the son of Mehetabel, who was shut in at his home; and he said, “Let us meet together in God’s house, within the temple, and let’s shut the doors of the temple; for they will come to kill you. Yes, in the night they will come to kill you.”'),
('NEH', 6, 11, 'NEH.6.11', 'I said, “Should a man like me flee? Who is there that, being such as I, would go into the temple to save his life? I will not go in.”'),
('NEH', 6, 12, 'NEH.6.12', 'I discerned, and behold, God had not sent him, but he pronounced this prophecy against me. Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him.'),
('NEH', 6, 13, 'NEH.6.13', 'He was hired so that I would be afraid, do so, and sin, and that they might have material for an evil report, that they might reproach me.'),
('NEH', 6, 14, 'NEH.6.14', '“Remember, my God, Tobiah and Sanballat according to these their works, and also the prophetess Noadiah and the rest of the prophets that would have put me in fear.”'),
('NEH', 6, 15, 'NEH.6.15', 'So the wall was finished in the twenty-fifth day of Elul, in fifty-two days.'),
('NEH', 6, 16, 'NEH.6.16', 'When all our enemies heard of it, all the nations that were around us were afraid, and they lost their confidence; for they perceived that this work was done by our God.'),
('NEH', 6, 17, 'NEH.6.17', 'Moreover in those days the nobles of Judah sent many letters to Tobiah, and Tobiah’s letters came to them.'),
('NEH', 6, 18, 'NEH.6.18', 'For there were many in Judah sworn to him because he was the son-in-law of Shecaniah the son of Arah; and his son Jehohanan had taken the daughter of Meshullam the son of Berechiah as wife.'),
('NEH', 6, 19, 'NEH.6.19', 'Also they spoke of his good deeds before me, and reported my words to him. Tobiah sent letters to put me in fear.'),
('NEH', 7, 1, 'NEH.7.1', 'Now when the wall was built and I had set up the doors, and the gatekeepers and the singers and the Levites were appointed,'),
('NEH', 7, 2, 'NEH.7.2', 'I put my brother Hanani, and Hananiah the governor of the fortress, in charge of Jerusalem; for he was a faithful man and feared God above many.'),
('NEH', 7, 3, 'NEH.7.3', 'I said to them, “Don’t let the gates of Jerusalem be opened until the sun is hot; and while they stand guard, let them shut the doors, and you bar them; and appoint watches of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, everyone in his watch, with everyone near his house.”'),
('NEH', 7, 4, 'NEH.7.4', 'Now the city was wide and large; but the people were few therein, and the houses were not built.'),
('NEH', 7, 5, 'NEH.7.5', 'My God put into my heart to gather together the nobles, and the rulers, and the people, that they might be listed by genealogy. I found the book of the genealogy of those who came up at the first, and I found this written in it:'),
('NEH', 7, 6, 'NEH.7.6', 'These are the children of the province who went up out of the captivity of those who had been carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away, and who returned to Jerusalem and to Judah, everyone to his city,'),
('NEH', 7, 7, 'NEH.7.7', 'who came with Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah, Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, and Baanah. The number of the men of the people of Israel:'),
('NEH', 7, 8, 'NEH.7.8', 'The children of Parosh: two thousand one hundred seventy-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 9, 'NEH.7.9', 'The children of Shephatiah: three hundred seventy-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 10, 'NEH.7.10', 'The children of Arah: six hundred fifty-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 11, 'NEH.7.11', 'The children of Pahathmoab, of the children of Jeshua and Joab: two thousand eight hundred eighteen.'),
('NEH', 7, 12, 'NEH.7.12', 'The children of Elam: one thousand two hundred fifty-four.'),
('NEH', 7, 13, 'NEH.7.13', 'The children of Zattu: eight hundred forty-five.'),
('NEH', 7, 14, 'NEH.7.14', 'The children of Zaccai: seven hundred sixty.'),
('NEH', 7, 15, 'NEH.7.15', 'The children of Binnui: six hundred forty-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 16, 'NEH.7.16', 'The children of Bebai: six hundred twenty-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 17, 'NEH.7.17', 'The children of Azgad: two thousand three hundred twenty-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 18, 'NEH.7.18', 'The children of Adonikam: six hundred sixty-seven.'),
('NEH', 7, 19, 'NEH.7.19', 'The children of Bigvai: two thousand sixty-seven.'),
('NEH', 7, 20, 'NEH.7.20', 'The children of Adin: six hundred fifty-five.'),
('NEH', 7, 21, 'NEH.7.21', 'The children of Ater: of Hezekiah, ninety-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 22, 'NEH.7.22', 'The children of Hashum: three hundred twenty-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 23, 'NEH.7.23', 'The children of Bezai: three hundred twenty-four.'),
('NEH', 7, 24, 'NEH.7.24', 'The children of Hariph: one hundred twelve.'),
('NEH', 7, 25, 'NEH.7.25', 'The children of Gibeon: ninety-five.'),
('NEH', 7, 26, 'NEH.7.26', 'The men of Bethlehem and Netophah: one hundred eighty-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 27, 'NEH.7.27', 'The men of Anathoth: one hundred twenty-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 28, 'NEH.7.28', 'The men of Beth Azmaveth: forty-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 29, 'NEH.7.29', 'The men of Kiriath Jearim, Chephirah, and Beeroth: seven hundred forty-three.'),
('NEH', 7, 30, 'NEH.7.30', 'The men of Ramah and Geba: six hundred twenty-one.'),
('NEH', 7, 31, 'NEH.7.31', 'The men of Michmas: one hundred twenty-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 32, 'NEH.7.32', 'The men of Bethel and Ai: one hundred twenty-three.'),
('NEH', 7, 33, 'NEH.7.33', 'The men of the other Nebo: fifty-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 34, 'NEH.7.34', 'The children of the other Elam: one thousand two hundred fifty-four.'),
('NEH', 7, 35, 'NEH.7.35', 'The children of Harim: three hundred twenty.'),
('NEH', 7, 36, 'NEH.7.36', 'The children of Jericho: three hundred forty-five.'),
('NEH', 7, 37, 'NEH.7.37', 'The children of Lod, Hadid, and Ono: seven hundred twenty-one.'),
('NEH', 7, 38, 'NEH.7.38', 'The children of Senaah: three thousand nine hundred thirty.'),
('NEH', 7, 39, 'NEH.7.39', 'The priests: The children of Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua: nine hundred seventy-three.'),
('NEH', 7, 40, 'NEH.7.40', 'The children of Immer: one thousand fifty-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 41, 'NEH.7.41', 'The children of Pashhur: one thousand two hundred forty-seven.'),
('NEH', 7, 42, 'NEH.7.42', 'The children of Harim: one thousand seventeen.'),
('NEH', 7, 43, 'NEH.7.43', 'The Levites: the children of Jeshua, of Kadmiel, of the children of Hodevah: seventy-four.'),
('NEH', 7, 44, 'NEH.7.44', 'The singers: the children of Asaph: one hundred forty-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 45, 'NEH.7.45', 'The gatekeepers: the children of Shallum, the children of Ater, the children of Talmon, the children of Akkub, the children of Hatita, the children of Shobai: one hundred thirty-eight.'),
('NEH', 7, 46, 'NEH.7.46', 'The temple servants: the children of Ziha, the children of Hasupha, the children of Tabbaoth,'),
('NEH', 7, 47, 'NEH.7.47', 'the children of Keros, the children of Sia, the children of Padon,'),
('NEH', 7, 48, 'NEH.7.48', 'the children of Lebana, the children of Hagaba, the children of Salmai,'),
('NEH', 7, 49, 'NEH.7.49', 'the children of Hanan, the children of Giddel, the children of Gahar,'),
('NEH', 7, 50, 'NEH.7.50', 'the children of Reaiah, the children of Rezin, the children of Nekoda,'),
('NEH', 7, 51, 'NEH.7.51', 'the children of Gazzam, the children of Uzza, the children of Paseah,'),
('NEH', 7, 52, 'NEH.7.52', 'the children of Besai, the children of Meunim, the children of Nephushesim,'),
('NEH', 7, 53, 'NEH.7.53', 'the children of Bakbuk, the children of Hakupha, the children of Harhur,'),
('NEH', 7, 54, 'NEH.7.54', 'the children of Bazlith, the children of Mehida, the children of Harsha,'),
('NEH', 7, 55, 'NEH.7.55', 'the children of Barkos, the children of Sisera, the children of Temah,'),
('NEH', 7, 56, 'NEH.7.56', 'the children of Neziah, and the children of Hatipha.'),
('NEH', 7, 57, 'NEH.7.57', 'The children of Solomon’s servants: the children of Sotai, the children of Sophereth, the children of Perida,'),
('NEH', 7, 58, 'NEH.7.58', 'the children of Jaala, the children of Darkon, the children of Giddel,'),
('NEH', 7, 59, 'NEH.7.59', 'the children of Shephatiah, the children of Hattil, the children of Pochereth Hazzebaim, and the children of Amon.'),
('NEH', 7, 60, 'NEH.7.60', 'All the temple servants and the children of Solomon’s servants were three hundred ninety-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 61, 'NEH.7.61', 'These were those who went up from Tel Melah, Tel Harsha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer; but they could not show their fathers’ houses, nor their offspring, whether they were of Israel:'),
('NEH', 7, 62, 'NEH.7.62', 'The children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda: six hundred forty-two.'),
('NEH', 7, 63, 'NEH.7.63', 'Of the priests: the children of Hobaiah, the children of Hakkoz, the children of Barzillai, who took a wife of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite, and was called after their name.'),
('NEH', 7, 64, 'NEH.7.64', 'These searched for their genealogical records, but couldn’t find them. Therefore they were deemed disqualified and removed from the priesthood.'),
('NEH', 7, 65, 'NEH.7.65', 'The governor told them not to eat of the most holy things until a priest stood up to minister with Urim and Thummim.'),
('NEH', 7, 66, 'NEH.7.66', 'The whole assembly together was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,'),
('NEH', 7, 67, 'NEH.7.67', 'in addition to their male servants and their female servants, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred thirty-seven. They had two hundred forty-five singing men and singing women.'),
('NEH', 7, 68, 'NEH.7.68', 'Their horses were seven hundred thirty-six; their mules, two hundred forty-five;'),
('NEH', 7, 69, 'NEH.7.69', 'their camels, four hundred thirty-five; their donkeys, six thousand seven hundred twenty.'),
('NEH', 7, 70, 'NEH.7.70', 'Some from among the heads of fathers’ households gave to the work. The governor gave to the treasury one thousand darics of gold, fifty basins, and five hundred thirty priests’ garments.'),
('NEH', 7, 71, 'NEH.7.71', 'Some of the heads of fathers’ households gave into the treasury of the work twenty thousand darics of gold, and two thousand two hundred minas of silver.'),
('NEH', 7, 72, 'NEH.7.72', 'That which the rest of the people gave was twenty thousand darics of gold, plus two thousand minas of silver, and sixty-seven priests’ garments.'),
('NEH', 7, 73, 'NEH.7.73', 'So the priests, the Levites, the gatekeepers, the singers, some of the people, the temple servants, and all Israel lived in their cities. When the seventh month had come, the children of Israel were in their cities.'),
('NEH', 8, 1, 'NEH.8.1', 'All the people gathered themselves together as one man into the wide place that was in front of the water gate; and they spoke to Ezra the scribe to bring the book of the law of Moses, which the LORD had commanded to Israel.'),
('NEH', 8, 2, 'NEH.8.2', 'Ezra the priest brought the law before the assembly, both men and women, and all who could hear with understanding, on the first day of the seventh month.'),
('NEH', 8, 3, 'NEH.8.3', 'He read from it before the wide place that was in front of the water gate from early morning until midday, in the presence of the men and the women, and of those who could understand. The ears of all the people were attentive to the book of the law.'),
('NEH', 8, 4, 'NEH.8.4', 'Ezra the scribe stood on a pulpit of wood, which they had made for the purpose; and beside him stood Mattithiah, Shema, Anaiah, Uriah, Hilkiah, and Maaseiah, on his right hand; and on his left hand, Pedaiah, Mishael, Malchijah, Hashum, Hashbaddanah, Zechariah, and Meshullam.'),
('NEH', 8, 5, 'NEH.8.5', 'Ezra opened the book in the sight of all the people (for he was above all the people), and when he opened it, all the people stood up.'),
('NEH', 8, 6, 'NEH.8.6', 'Then Ezra blessed the LORD, the great God. All the people answered, “Amen, Amen,” with the lifting up of their hands. They bowed their heads, and worshiped the LORD with their faces to the ground.'),
('NEH', 8, 7, 'NEH.8.7', 'Also Jeshua, Bani, Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai, Hodiah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah, Jozabad, Hanan, Pelaiah, and the Levites, caused the people to understand the law; and the people stayed in their place.'),
('NEH', 8, 8, 'NEH.8.8', 'They read in the book, in the law of God, distinctly; and they gave the sense, so that they understood the reading.'),
('NEH', 8, 9, 'NEH.8.9', 'Nehemiah, who was the governor, Ezra the priest and scribe, and the Levites who taught the people said to all the people, “Today is holy to the LORD your God. Don’t mourn, nor weep.” For all the people wept when they heard the words of the law.'),
('NEH', 8, 10, 'NEH.8.10', 'Then he said to them, “Go your way. Eat the fat, drink the sweet, and send portions to him for whom nothing is prepared, for today is holy to our Lord. Don’t be grieved, for the joy of the LORD is your strength.”'),
('NEH', 8, 11, 'NEH.8.11', 'So the Levites calmed all the people, saying, “Hold your peace, for the day is holy. Don’t be grieved.”'),
('NEH', 8, 12, 'NEH.8.12', 'All the people went their way to eat, to drink, to send portions, and to celebrate, because they had understood the words that were declared to them.'),
('NEH', 8, 13, 'NEH.8.13', 'On the second day, the heads of fathers’ households of all the people, the priests, and the Levites were gathered together to Ezra the scribe, to study the words of the law.'),
('NEH', 8, 14, 'NEH.8.14', 'They found written in the law how the LORD had commanded by Moses that the children of Israel should dwell in booths in the feast of the seventh month;'),
('NEH', 8, 15, 'NEH.8.15', 'and that they should publish and proclaim in all their cities and in Jerusalem, saying, “Go out to the mountain, and get olive branches, branches of wild olive, myrtle branches, palm branches, and branches of thick trees, to make temporary shelters, as it is written.”'),
('NEH', 8, 16, 'NEH.8.16', 'So the people went out and brought them, and made themselves temporary shelters, everyone on the roof of his house, in their courts, in the courts of God’s house, in the wide place of the water gate, and in the wide place of Ephraim’s gate.'),
('NEH', 8, 17, 'NEH.8.17', 'All the assembly of those who had come back out of the captivity made temporary shelters and lived in the temporary shelters, for since the days of Joshua the son of Nun to that day the children of Israel had not done so. There was very great gladness.'),
('NEH', 8, 18, 'NEH.8.18', 'Also day by day, from the first day to the last day, he read in the book of the law of God. They kept the feast seven days; and on the eighth day was a solemn assembly, according to the ordinance.'),
('NEH', 9, 1, 'NEH.9.1', 'Now in the twenty-fourth day of this month the children of Israel were assembled with fasting, with sackcloth, and dirt on them.'),
('NEH', 9, 2, 'NEH.9.2', 'The offspring of Israel separated themselves from all foreigners and stood and confessed their sins and the iniquities of their fathers.'),
('NEH', 9, 3, 'NEH.9.3', 'They stood up in their place, and read in the book of the law of the LORD their God a fourth part of the day; and a fourth part they confessed and worshiped the LORD their God.'),
('NEH', 9, 4, 'NEH.9.4', 'Then Jeshua, Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani of the Levites stood up on the stairs, and cried with a loud voice to the LORD their God.'),
('NEH', 9, 5, 'NEH.9.5', 'Then the Levites, Jeshua, and Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabneiah, Sherebiah, Hodiah, Shebaniah, and Pethahiah, said, “Stand up and bless the LORD your God from everlasting to everlasting! Blessed be your glorious name, which is exalted above all blessing and praise!'),
('NEH', 9, 6, 'NEH.9.6', 'You are the LORD, even you alone. You have made heaven, the heaven of heavens, with all their army, the earth and all things that are on it, the seas and all that is in them, and you preserve them all. The army of heaven worships you.'),
('NEH', 9, 7, 'NEH.9.7', 'You are the LORD, the God who chose Abram, brought him out of Ur of the Chaldees, gave him the name of Abraham,'),
('NEH', 9, 8, 'NEH.9.8', 'found his heart faithful before you, and made a covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Amorite, the Perizzite, the Jebusite, and the Girgashite, to give it to his offspring, and have performed your words, for you are righteous.'),
('NEH', 9, 9, 'NEH.9.9', '“You saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt, and heard their cry by the Red Sea,'),
('NEH', 9, 10, 'NEH.9.10', 'and showed signs and wonders against Pharaoh, against all his servants, and against all the people of his land, for you knew that they dealt proudly against them, and made a name for yourself, as it is today.'),
('NEH', 9, 11, 'NEH.9.11', 'You divided the sea before them, so that they went through the middle of the sea on the dry land; and you cast their pursuers into the depths, as a stone into the mighty waters.'),
('NEH', 9, 12, 'NEH.9.12', 'Moreover, in a pillar of cloud you led them by day; and in a pillar of fire by night, to give them light in the way in which they should go.'),
('NEH', 9, 13, 'NEH.9.13', '“You also came down on Mount Sinai, and spoke with them from heaven, and gave them right ordinances and true laws, good statutes and commandments,'),
('NEH', 9, 14, 'NEH.9.14', 'and made known to them your holy Sabbath, and commanded them commandments, statutes, and a law, by Moses your servant,'),
('NEH', 9, 15, 'NEH.9.15', 'and gave them bread from the sky for their hunger, and brought water out of the rock for them for their thirst, and commanded them that they should go in to possess the land which you had sworn to give them.'),
('NEH', 9, 16, 'NEH.9.16', '“But they and our fathers behaved proudly, hardened their neck, didn’t listen to your commandments,'),
('NEH', 9, 17, 'NEH.9.17', 'and refused to obey. They weren’t mindful of your wonders that you did among them, but hardened their neck, and in their rebellion appointed a captain to return to their bondage. But you are a God ready to pardon, gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness, and didn’t forsake them.'),
('NEH', 9, 18, 'NEH.9.18', 'Yes, when they had made themselves a molded calf, and said, ‘This is your God who brought you up out of Egypt,’ and had committed awful blasphemies,'),
('NEH', 9, 19, 'NEH.9.19', 'yet you in your manifold mercies didn’t forsake them in the wilderness. The pillar of cloud didn’t depart from over them by day, to lead them in the way; neither did the pillar of fire by night, to show them light, and the way in which they should go.'),
('NEH', 9, 20, 'NEH.9.20', 'You gave also your good Spirit to instruct them, and didn’t withhold your manna from their mouth, and gave them water for their thirst.'),
('NEH', 9, 21, 'NEH.9.21', '“Yes, forty years you sustained them in the wilderness. They lacked nothing. Their clothes didn’t grow old, and their feet didn’t swell.'),
('NEH', 9, 22, 'NEH.9.22', 'Moreover you gave them kingdoms and peoples, which you allotted according to their portions. So they possessed the land of Sihon, even the land of the king of Heshbon, and the land of Og king of Bashan.'),
('NEH', 9, 23, 'NEH.9.23', 'You also multiplied their children as the stars of the sky, and brought them into the land concerning which you said to their fathers that they should go in to possess it.'),
('NEH', 9, 24, 'NEH.9.24', '“So the children went in and possessed the land; and you subdued before them the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, and gave them into their hands, with their kings and the peoples of the land, that they might do with them as they pleased.'),
('NEH', 9, 25, 'NEH.9.25', 'They took fortified cities and a rich land, and possessed houses full of all good things, cisterns dug out, vineyards, olive groves, and fruit trees in abundance. So they ate, were filled, became fat, and delighted themselves in your great goodness.'),
('NEH', 9, 26, 'NEH.9.26', '“Nevertheless they were disobedient and rebelled against you, cast your law behind their back, killed your prophets that testified against them to turn them again to you, and they committed awful blasphemies.'),
('NEH', 9, 27, 'NEH.9.27', 'Therefore you delivered them into the hand of their adversaries, who distressed them. In the time of their trouble, when they cried to you, you heard from heaven; and according to your manifold mercies you gave them saviors who saved them out of the hands of their adversaries.'),
('NEH', 9, 28, 'NEH.9.28', 'But after they had rest, they did evil again before you; therefore you left them in the hands of their enemies, so that they had the dominion over them; yet when they returned and cried to you, you heard from heaven; and many times you delivered them according to your mercies,'),
('NEH', 9, 29, 'NEH.9.29', 'and testified against them, that you might bring them again to your law. Yet they were arrogant, and didn’t listen to your commandments, but sinned against your ordinances (which if a man does, he shall live in them), turned their backs, stiffened their neck, and would not hear.'),
('NEH', 9, 30, 'NEH.9.30', 'Yet many years you put up with them, and testified against them by your Spirit through your prophets. Yet they would not listen. Therefore you gave them into the hand of the peoples of the lands.'),
('NEH', 9, 31, 'NEH.9.31', '“Nevertheless in your manifold mercies you didn’t make a full end of them, nor forsake them; for you are a gracious and merciful God.'),
('NEH', 9, 32, 'NEH.9.32', 'Now therefore, our God, the great, the mighty, and the awesome God, who keeps covenant and loving kindness, don’t let all the travail seem little before you that has come on us, on our kings, on our princes, on our priests, on our prophets, on our fathers, and on all your people, since the time of the kings of Assyria to this day.'),
('NEH', 9, 33, 'NEH.9.33', 'However you are just in all that has come on us; for you have dealt truly, but we have done wickedly.'),
('NEH', 9, 34, 'NEH.9.34', 'Also our kings, our princes, our priests, and our fathers have not kept your law, nor listened to your commandments and your testimonies with which you testified against them.'),
('NEH', 9, 35, 'NEH.9.35', 'For they have not served you in their kingdom, and in your great goodness that you gave them, and in the large and rich land which you gave before them. They didn’t turn from their wicked works.'),
('NEH', 9, 36, 'NEH.9.36', '“Behold, we are servants today, and as for the land that you gave to our fathers to eat its fruit and its good, behold, we are servants in it.'),
('NEH', 9, 37, 'NEH.9.37', 'It yields much increase to the kings whom you have set over us because of our sins. Also they have power over our bodies and over our livestock, at their pleasure, and we are in great distress.'),
('NEH', 9, 38, 'NEH.9.38', 'Yet for all this, we make a sure covenant, and write it; and our princes, our Levites, and our priests, seal it.”'),
('NEH', 10, 1, 'NEH.10.1', 'Now those who sealed were: Nehemiah the governor, the son of Hacaliah, and Zedekiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 2, 'NEH.10.2', 'Seraiah, Azariah, Jeremiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 3, 'NEH.10.3', 'Pashhur, Amariah, Malchijah,'),
('NEH', 10, 4, 'NEH.10.4', 'Hattush, Shebaniah, Malluch,'),
('NEH', 10, 5, 'NEH.10.5', 'Harim, Meremoth, Obadiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 6, 'NEH.10.6', 'Daniel, Ginnethon, Baruch,'),
('NEH', 10, 7, 'NEH.10.7', 'Meshullam, Abijah, Mijamin,'),
('NEH', 10, 8, 'NEH.10.8', 'Maaziah, Bilgai, and Shemaiah. These were the priests.'),
('NEH', 10, 9, 'NEH.10.9', 'The Levites: Jeshua the son of Azaniah, Binnui of the sons of Henadad, Kadmiel;'),
('NEH', 10, 10, 'NEH.10.10', 'and their brothers, Shebaniah, Hodiah, Kelita, Pelaiah, Hanan,'),
('NEH', 10, 11, 'NEH.10.11', 'Mica, Rehob, Hashabiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 12, 'NEH.10.12', 'Zaccur, Sherebiah, Shebaniah,'),
('NEH', 10, 13, 'NEH.10.13', 'Hodiah, Bani, and Beninu.'),
('NEH', 10, 14, 'NEH.10.14', 'The chiefs of the people: Parosh, Pahathmoab, Elam, Zattu, Bani,'),
('NEH', 10, 15, 'NEH.10.15', 'Bunni, Azgad, Bebai,'),
('NEH', 10, 16, 'NEH.10.16', 'Adonijah, Bigvai, Adin,'),
('NEH', 10, 17, 'NEH.10.17', 'Ater, Hezekiah, Azzur,'),
('NEH', 10, 18, 'NEH.10.18', 'Hodiah, Hashum, Bezai,'),
('NEH', 10, 19, 'NEH.10.19', 'Hariph, Anathoth, Nobai,'),
('NEH', 10, 20, 'NEH.10.20', 'Magpiash, Meshullam, Hezir,'),
('NEH', 10, 21, 'NEH.10.21', 'Meshezabel, Zadok, Jaddua,'),
('NEH', 10, 22, 'NEH.10.22', 'Pelatiah, Hanan, Anaiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 23, 'NEH.10.23', 'Hoshea, Hananiah, Hasshub,'),
('NEH', 10, 24, 'NEH.10.24', 'Hallohesh, Pilha, Shobek,'),
('NEH', 10, 25, 'NEH.10.25', 'Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 26, 'NEH.10.26', 'Ahiah, Hanan, Anan,'),
('NEH', 10, 27, 'NEH.10.27', 'Malluch, Harim, and Baanah.'),
('NEH', 10, 28, 'NEH.10.28', 'The rest of the people, the priests, the Levites, the gatekeepers, the singers, the temple servants, and all those who had separated themselves from the peoples of the lands to the law of God, their wives, their sons, and their daughters—everyone who had knowledge and understanding—'),
('NEH', 10, 29, 'NEH.10.29', 'joined with their brothers, their nobles, and entered into a curse and into an oath, to walk in God’s law, which was given by Moses the servant of God, and to observe and do all the commandments of the LORD our Lord, and his ordinances and his statutes;'),
('NEH', 10, 30, 'NEH.10.30', 'and that we would not give our daughters to the peoples of the land, nor take their daughters for our sons;'),
('NEH', 10, 31, 'NEH.10.31', 'and if the peoples of the land bring wares or any grain on the Sabbath day to sell, that we would not buy from them on the Sabbath, or on a holy day; and that we would forego the seventh year crops and the exaction of every debt.'),
('NEH', 10, 32, 'NEH.10.32', 'Also we made ordinances for ourselves, to charge ourselves yearly with the third part of a shekel for the service of the house of our God:'),
('NEH', 10, 33, 'NEH.10.33', 'for the show bread, for the continual meal offering, for the continual burnt offering, for the Sabbaths, for the new moons, for the set feasts, for the holy things, for the sin offerings to make atonement for Israel, and for all the work of the house of our God.'),
('NEH', 10, 34, 'NEH.10.34', 'We, the priests, the Levites, and the people, cast lots for the wood offering, to bring it into the house of our God, according to our fathers’ houses, at times appointed year by year, to burn on the LORD our God’s altar, as it is written in the law;'),
('NEH', 10, 35, 'NEH.10.35', 'and to bring the first fruits of our ground and the first fruits of all fruit of all kinds of trees, year by year, to the LORD’s house;'),
('NEH', 10, 36, 'NEH.10.36', 'also the firstborn of our sons and of our livestock, as it is written in the law, and the firstborn of our herds and of our flocks, to bring to the house of our God, to the priests who minister in the house of our God;'),
('NEH', 10, 37, 'NEH.10.37', 'and that we should bring the first fruits of our dough, our wave offerings, the fruit of all kinds of trees, and the new wine and the oil, to the priests, to the rooms of the house of our God; and the tithes of our ground to the Levites; for they, the Levites, take the tithes in all our farming villages.'),
('NEH', 10, 38, 'NEH.10.38', 'The priest, the descendent of Aaron, shall be with the Levites when the Levites take tithes. The Levites shall bring up the tithe of the tithes to the house of our God, to the rooms, into the treasure house.'),
('NEH', 10, 39, 'NEH.10.39', 'For the children of Israel and the children of Levi shall bring the wave offering of the grain, of the new wine, and of the oil, to the rooms where the vessels of the sanctuary are, and the priests who minister, with the gatekeepers and the singers. We will not forsake the house of our God.'),
('NEH', 11, 1, 'NEH.11.1', 'The princes of the people lived in Jerusalem. The rest of the people also cast lots to bring one of ten to dwell in Jerusalem, the holy city, and nine parts in the other cities.'),
('NEH', 11, 2, 'NEH.11.2', 'The people blessed all the men who willingly offered themselves to dwell in Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 11, 3, 'NEH.11.3', 'Now these are the chiefs of the province who lived in Jerusalem; but in the cities of Judah, everyone lived in his possession in their cities—Israel, the priests, the Levites, the temple servants, and the children of Solomon’s servants.'),
('NEH', 11, 4, 'NEH.11.4', 'Some of the children of Judah and of the children of Benjamin lived in Jerusalem. Of the children of Judah: Athaiah the son of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the son of Amariah, the son of Shephatiah, the son of Mahalalel, of the children of Perez;'),
('NEH', 11, 5, 'NEH.11.5', 'and Maaseiah the son of Baruch, the son of Colhozeh, the son of Hazaiah, the son of Adaiah, the son of Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, the son of the Shilonite.'),
('NEH', 11, 6, 'NEH.11.6', 'All the sons of Perez who lived in Jerusalem were four hundred sixty-eight valiant men.'),
('NEH', 11, 7, 'NEH.11.7', 'These are the sons of Benjamin: Sallu the son of Meshullam, the son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ithiel, the son of Jeshaiah.'),
('NEH', 11, 8, 'NEH.11.8', 'After him Gabbai and Sallai, nine hundred twenty-eight.'),
('NEH', 11, 9, 'NEH.11.9', 'Joel the son of Zichri was their overseer; and Judah the son of Hassenuah was second over the city.'),
('NEH', 11, 10, 'NEH.11.10', 'Of the priests: Jedaiah the son of Joiarib, Jachin,'),
('NEH', 11, 11, 'NEH.11.11', 'Seraiah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the ruler of God’s house,'),
('NEH', 11, 12, 'NEH.11.12', 'and their brothers who did the work of the house, eight hundred twenty-two; and Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah,'),
('NEH', 11, 13, 'NEH.11.13', 'and his brothers, chiefs of fathers’ households, two hundred forty-two; and Amashsai the son of Azarel, the son of Ahzai, the son of Meshillemoth, the son of Immer,'),
('NEH', 11, 14, 'NEH.11.14', 'and their brothers, mighty men of valor, one hundred twenty-eight; and their overseer was Zabdiel, the son of Haggedolim.'),
('NEH', 11, 15, 'NEH.11.15', 'Of the Levites: Shemaiah the son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Bunni;'),
('NEH', 11, 16, 'NEH.11.16', 'and Shabbethai and Jozabad, of the chiefs of the Levites, who had the oversight of the outward business of God’s house;'),
('NEH', 11, 17, 'NEH.11.17', 'and Mattaniah the son of Mica, the son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, who was the chief to begin the thanksgiving in prayer, and Bakbukiah, the second among his brothers; and Abda the son of Shammua, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun.'),
('NEH', 11, 18, 'NEH.11.18', 'All the Levites in the holy city were two hundred eighty-four.'),
('NEH', 11, 19, 'NEH.11.19', 'Moreover the gatekeepers, Akkub, Talmon, and their brothers, who kept watch at the gates, were one hundred seventy-two.'),
('NEH', 11, 20, 'NEH.11.20', 'The residue of Israel, of the priests, and the Levites were in all the cities of Judah, everyone in his inheritance.'),
('NEH', 11, 21, 'NEH.11.21', 'But the temple servants lived in Ophel; and Ziha and Gishpa were over the temple servants.'),
('NEH', 11, 22, 'NEH.11.22', 'The overseer also of the Levites at Jerusalem was Uzzi the son of Bani, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Mica, of the sons of Asaph, the singers responsible for the service of God’s house.'),
('NEH', 11, 23, 'NEH.11.23', 'For there was a commandment from the king concerning them, and a settled provision for the singers, as every day required.'),
('NEH', 11, 24, 'NEH.11.24', 'Pethahiah the son of Meshezabel, of the children of Zerah the son of Judah, was at the king’s hand in all matters concerning the people.'),
('NEH', 11, 25, 'NEH.11.25', 'As for the villages with their fields, some of the children of Judah lived in Kiriath Arba and its towns, in Dibon and its towns, in Jekabzeel and its villages,'),
('NEH', 11, 26, 'NEH.11.26', 'in Jeshua, in Moladah, Beth Pelet,'),
('NEH', 11, 27, 'NEH.11.27', 'in Hazar Shual, in Beersheba and its towns,'),
('NEH', 11, 28, 'NEH.11.28', 'in Ziklag, in Meconah and in its towns,'),
('NEH', 11, 29, 'NEH.11.29', 'in En Rimmon, in Zorah, in Jarmuth,'),
('NEH', 11, 30, 'NEH.11.30', 'Zanoah, Adullam, and their villages, Lachish and its fields, and Azekah and its towns. So they encamped from Beersheba to the valley of Hinnom.'),
('NEH', 11, 31, 'NEH.11.31', 'The children of Benjamin also lived from Geba onward, at Michmash and Aija, and at Bethel and its towns,'),
('NEH', 11, 32, 'NEH.11.32', 'at Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,'),
('NEH', 11, 33, 'NEH.11.33', 'Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,'),
('NEH', 11, 34, 'NEH.11.34', 'Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,'),
('NEH', 11, 35, 'NEH.11.35', 'Lod, and Ono, the valley of craftsmen.'),
('NEH', 11, 36, 'NEH.11.36', 'Of the Levites, certain divisions in Judah settled in Benjamin’s territory.'),
('NEH', 12, 1, 'NEH.12.1', 'Now these are the priests and the Levites who went up with Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,'),
('NEH', 12, 2, 'NEH.12.2', 'Amariah, Malluch, Hattush,'),
('NEH', 12, 3, 'NEH.12.3', 'Shecaniah, Rehum, Meremoth,'),
('NEH', 12, 4, 'NEH.12.4', 'Iddo, Ginnethoi, Abijah,'),
('NEH', 12, 5, 'NEH.12.5', 'Mijamin, Maadiah, Bilgah,'),
('NEH', 12, 6, 'NEH.12.6', 'Shemaiah, Joiarib, Jedaiah,'),
('NEH', 12, 7, 'NEH.12.7', 'Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, and Jedaiah. These were the chiefs of the priests and of their brothers in the days of Jeshua.'),
('NEH', 12, 8, 'NEH.12.8', 'Moreover the Levites were Jeshua, Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah, and Mattaniah, who was over the thanksgiving songs, he and his brothers.'),
('NEH', 12, 9, 'NEH.12.9', 'Also Bakbukiah and Unno, their brothers, were close to them according to their offices.'),
('NEH', 12, 10, 'NEH.12.10', 'Jeshua became the father of Joiakim, and Joiakim became the father of Eliashib, and Eliashib became the father of Joiada,'),
('NEH', 12, 11, 'NEH.12.11', 'and Joiada became the father of Jonathan, and Jonathan became the father of Jaddua.'),
('NEH', 12, 12, 'NEH.12.12', 'In the days of Joiakim were priests, heads of fathers’ households: of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;'),
('NEH', 12, 13, 'NEH.12.13', 'of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;'),
('NEH', 12, 14, 'NEH.12.14', 'of Malluchi, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;'),
('NEH', 12, 15, 'NEH.12.15', 'of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;'),
('NEH', 12, 16, 'NEH.12.16', 'of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;'),
('NEH', 12, 17, 'NEH.12.17', 'of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin, of Moadiah, Piltai;'),
('NEH', 12, 18, 'NEH.12.18', 'of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jehonathan;'),
('NEH', 12, 19, 'NEH.12.19', 'of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;'),
('NEH', 12, 20, 'NEH.12.20', 'of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;'),
('NEH', 12, 21, 'NEH.12.21', 'of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; of Jedaiah, Nethanel.'),
('NEH', 12, 22, 'NEH.12.22', 'As for the Levites, in the days of Eliashib, Joiada, Johanan, and Jaddua, there were recorded the heads of fathers’ households; also the priests, in the reign of Darius the Persian.'),
('NEH', 12, 23, 'NEH.12.23', 'The sons of Levi, heads of fathers’ households, were written in the book of the chronicles, even until the days of Johanan the son of Eliashib.'),
('NEH', 12, 24, 'NEH.12.24', 'The chiefs of the Levites: Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua the son of Kadmiel, with their brothers close to them, to praise and give thanks according to the commandment of David the man of God, section next to section.'),
('NEH', 12, 25, 'NEH.12.25', 'Mattaniah, Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, and Akkub were gatekeepers keeping the watch at the storehouses of the gates.'),
('NEH', 12, 26, 'NEH.12.26', 'These were in the days of Joiakim the son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor, and of Ezra the priest and scribe.'),
('NEH', 12, 27, 'NEH.12.27', 'At the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, they sought the Levites out of all their places, to bring them to Jerusalem to keep the dedication with gladness, both with giving thanks and with singing, with cymbals, stringed instruments, and with harps.'),
('NEH', 12, 28, 'NEH.12.28', 'The sons of the singers gathered themselves together, both out of the plain around Jerusalem and from the villages of the Netophathites;'),
('NEH', 12, 29, 'NEH.12.29', 'also from Beth Gilgal and out of the fields of Geba and Azmaveth, for the singers had built themselves villages around Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 12, 30, 'NEH.12.30', 'The priests and the Levites purified themselves; and they purified the people, the gates, and the wall.'),
('NEH', 12, 31, 'NEH.12.31', 'Then I brought the princes of Judah up on the wall, and appointed two great companies who gave thanks and went in procession. One went on the right hand on the wall toward the dung gate;'),
('NEH', 12, 32, 'NEH.12.32', 'and after them went Hoshaiah, with half of the princes of Judah,'),
('NEH', 12, 33, 'NEH.12.33', 'and Azariah, Ezra, and Meshullam,'),
('NEH', 12, 34, 'NEH.12.34', 'Judah, Benjamin, Shemaiah, Jeremiah,'),
('NEH', 12, 35, 'NEH.12.35', 'and some of the priests’ sons with trumpets: Zechariah the son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Micaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph;'),
('NEH', 12, 36, 'NEH.12.36', 'and his brothers, Shemaiah, Azarel, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethanel, Judah, and Hanani, with the musical instruments of David the man of God; and Ezra the scribe was before them.'),
('NEH', 12, 37, 'NEH.12.37', 'By the spring gate, and straight before them, they went up by the stairs of David’s city, at the ascent of the wall, above David’s house, even to the water gate eastward.'),
('NEH', 12, 38, 'NEH.12.38', 'The other company of those who gave thanks went to meet them, and I after them, with the half of the people on the wall above the tower of the furnaces, even to the wide wall,'),
('NEH', 12, 39, 'NEH.12.39', 'and above the gate of Ephraim, and by the old gate, and by the fish gate, the tower of Hananel, and the tower of Hammeah, even to the sheep gate; and they stood still in the gate of the guard.'),
('NEH', 12, 40, 'NEH.12.40', 'So the two companies of those who gave thanks in God’s house stood, and I and the half of the rulers with me;'),
('NEH', 12, 41, 'NEH.12.41', 'and the priests, Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Micaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, and Hananiah, with trumpets;'),
('NEH', 12, 42, 'NEH.12.42', 'and Maaseiah, Shemaiah, Eleazar, Uzzi, Jehohanan, Malchijah, Elam, and Ezer. The singers sang loud, with Jezrahiah their overseer.'),
('NEH', 12, 43, 'NEH.12.43', 'They offered great sacrifices that day, and rejoiced, for God had made them rejoice with great joy; and the women and the children also rejoiced, so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard even far away.'),
('NEH', 12, 44, 'NEH.12.44', 'On that day, men were appointed over the rooms for the treasures, for the wave offerings, for the first fruits, and for the tithes, to gather into them according to the fields of the cities the portions appointed by the law for the priests and Levites; for Judah rejoiced for the priests and for the Levites who served.'),
('NEH', 12, 45, 'NEH.12.45', 'They performed the duty of their God and the duty of the purification, and so did the singers and the gatekeepers, according to the commandment of David and of Solomon his son.'),
('NEH', 12, 46, 'NEH.12.46', 'For in the days of David and Asaph of old there was a chief of the singers, and songs of praise and thanksgiving to God.'),
('NEH', 12, 47, 'NEH.12.47', 'All Israel in the days of Zerubbabel and in the days of Nehemiah gave the portions of the singers and the gatekeepers, as every day required; and they set apart that which was for the Levites; and the Levites set apart that which was for the sons of Aaron.'),
('NEH', 13, 1, 'NEH.13.1', 'On that day they read in the book of Moses in the hearing of the people; and it was found written in it that an Ammonite and a Moabite should not enter into the assembly of God forever,'),
('NEH', 13, 2, 'NEH.13.2', 'because they didn’t meet the children of Israel with bread and with water, but hired Balaam against them to curse them; however, our God turned the curse into a blessing.'),
('NEH', 13, 3, 'NEH.13.3', 'It came to pass, when they had heard the law, that they separated all the mixed multitude from Israel.'),
('NEH', 13, 4, 'NEH.13.4', 'Now before this, Eliashib the priest, who was appointed over the rooms of the house of our God, being allied to Tobiah,'),
('NEH', 13, 5, 'NEH.13.5', 'had prepared for him a great room, where previously they laid the meal offerings, the frankincense, the vessels, and the tithes of the grain, the new wine, and the oil, which were given by commandment to the Levites, the singers, and the gatekeepers; and the wave offerings for the priests.'),
('NEH', 13, 6, 'NEH.13.6', 'But in all this, I was not at Jerusalem; for in the thirty-second year of Artaxerxes king of Babylon I went to the king; and after some days I asked leave of the king,'),
('NEH', 13, 7, 'NEH.13.7', 'and I came to Jerusalem, and understood the evil that Eliashib had done for Tobiah, in preparing him a room in the courts of God’s house.'),
('NEH', 13, 8, 'NEH.13.8', 'It grieved me severely. Therefore I threw all Tobiah’s household stuff out of the room.'),
('NEH', 13, 9, 'NEH.13.9', 'Then I commanded, and they cleansed the rooms. I brought into them the vessels of God’s house, with the meal offerings and the frankincense again.'),
('NEH', 13, 10, 'NEH.13.10', 'I perceived that the portions of the Levites had not been given them, so that the Levites and the singers, who did the work, had each fled to his field.'),
('NEH', 13, 11, 'NEH.13.11', 'Then I contended with the rulers, and said, “Why is God’s house forsaken?” I gathered them together, and set them in their place.'),
('NEH', 13, 12, 'NEH.13.12', 'Then all Judah brought the tithe of the grain, the new wine, and the oil to the treasuries.'),
('NEH', 13, 13, 'NEH.13.13', 'I made treasurers over the treasuries, Shelemiah the priest, and Zadok the scribe, and of the Levites, Pedaiah: and next to them was Hanan the son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah; for they were counted faithful, and their business was to distribute to their brothers.'),
('NEH', 13, 14, 'NEH.13.14', 'Remember me, my God, concerning this, and don’t wipe out my good deeds that I have done for the house of my God, and for its observances.'),
('NEH', 13, 15, 'NEH.13.15', 'In those days I saw some men treading wine presses on the Sabbath in Judah, bringing in sheaves, and loading donkeys with wine, grapes, figs, and all kinds of burdens which they brought into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day; and I testified against them in the day in which they sold food.'),
('NEH', 13, 16, 'NEH.13.16', 'Some men of Tyre also lived there, who brought in fish and all kinds of wares, and sold on the Sabbath to the children of Judah, and in Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 13, 17, 'NEH.13.17', 'Then I contended with the nobles of Judah, and said to them, “What evil thing is this that you do, and profane the Sabbath day?'),
('NEH', 13, 18, 'NEH.13.18', 'Didn’t your fathers do this, and didn’t our God bring all this evil on us and on this city? Yet you bring more wrath on Israel by profaning the Sabbath.”'),
('NEH', 13, 19, 'NEH.13.19', 'It came to pass that when the gates of Jerusalem began to be dark before the Sabbath, I commanded that the doors should be shut, and commanded that they should not be opened until after the Sabbath. I set some of my servants over the gates, so that no burden should be brought in on the Sabbath day.'),
('NEH', 13, 20, 'NEH.13.20', 'So the merchants and sellers of all kinds of wares camped outside of Jerusalem once or twice.'),
('NEH', 13, 21, 'NEH.13.21', 'Then I testified against them, and said to them, “Why do you stay around the wall? If you do so again, I will lay hands on you.” From that time on, they didn’t come on the Sabbath.'),
('NEH', 13, 22, 'NEH.13.22', 'I commanded the Levites that they should purify themselves, and that they should come and keep the gates, to sanctify the Sabbath day. Remember me for this also, my God, and spare me according to the greatness of your loving kindness.'),
('NEH', 13, 23, 'NEH.13.23', 'In those days I also saw the Jews who had married women of Ashdod, of Ammon, and of Moab;'),
('NEH', 13, 24, 'NEH.13.24', 'and their children spoke half in the speech of Ashdod, and could not speak in the Jews’ language, but according to the language of each people.'),
('NEH', 13, 25, 'NEH.13.25', 'I contended with them, cursed them, struck certain of them, plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God, “You shall not give your daughters to their sons, nor take their daughters for your sons, or for yourselves.'),
('NEH', 13, 26, 'NEH.13.26', 'Didn’t Solomon king of Israel sin by these things? Yet among many nations there was no king like him, and he was loved by his God, and God made him king over all Israel. Nevertheless foreign women caused even him to sin.'),
('NEH', 13, 27, 'NEH.13.27', 'Shall we then listen to you to do all this great evil, to trespass against our God in marrying foreign women?”'),
('NEH', 13, 28, 'NEH.13.28', 'One of the sons of Joiada, the son of Eliashib the high priest, was son-in-law to Sanballat the Horonite; therefore I chased him from me.'),
('NEH', 13, 29, 'NEH.13.29', 'Remember them, my God, because they have defiled the priesthood and the covenant of the priesthood and of the Levites.'),
('NEH', 13, 30, 'NEH.13.30', 'Thus I cleansed them from all foreigners and appointed duties for the priests and for the Levites, everyone in his work;'),
('NEH', 13, 31, 'NEH.13.31', 'and for the wood offering, at appointed times, and for the first fruits. Remember me, my God, for good.'),
('EST', 1, 1, 'EST.1.1', 'Now in the days of Ahasuerus (this is Ahasuerus who reigned from India even to Ethiopia, over one hundred twenty-seven provinces),'),
('EST', 1, 2, 'EST.1.2', 'in those days, when the King Ahasuerus sat on the throne of his kingdom, which was in Susa the palace,'),
('EST', 1, 3, 'EST.1.3', 'in the third year of his reign, he made a feast for all his princes and his servants; the army of Persia and Media, the nobles and princes of the provinces being before him.'),
('EST', 1, 4, 'EST.1.4', 'He displayed the riches of his glorious kingdom and the honor of his excellent majesty many days, even one hundred eighty days.'),
('EST', 1, 5, 'EST.1.5', 'When these days were fulfilled, the king made a seven day feast for all the people who were present in Susa the palace, both great and small, in the court of the garden of the king’s palace.'),
('EST', 1, 6, 'EST.1.6', 'There were hangings of white and blue material, fastened with cords of fine linen and purple to silver rings and marble pillars. The couches were of gold and silver, on a pavement of red, white, yellow, and black marble.'),
('EST', 1, 7, 'EST.1.7', 'They gave them drinks in golden vessels of various kinds, including royal wine in abundance, according to the bounty of the king.'),
('EST', 1, 8, 'EST.1.8', 'In accordance with the law, the drinking was not compulsory; for so the king had instructed all the officials of his house, that they should do according to every man’s pleasure.'),
('EST', 1, 9, 'EST.1.9', 'Also Vashti the queen made a feast for the women in the royal house which belonged to King Ahasuerus.'),
('EST', 1, 10, 'EST.1.10', 'On the seventh day, when the heart of the king was merry with wine, he commanded Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, and Abagtha, Zethar, and Carcass, the seven eunuchs who served in the presence of Ahasuerus the king,'),
('EST', 1, 11, 'EST.1.11', 'to bring Vashti the queen before the king wearing the royal crown, to show the people and the princes her beauty; for she was beautiful.'),
('EST', 1, 12, 'EST.1.12', 'But the queen Vashti refused to come at the king’s commandment by the eunuchs. Therefore the king was very angry, and his anger burned in him.'),
('EST', 1, 13, 'EST.1.13', 'Then the king said to the wise men, who knew the times (for it was the king’s custom to consult those who knew law and judgment;'),
('EST', 1, 14, 'EST.1.14', 'and next to him were Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media, who saw the king’s face, and sat first in the kingdom),'),
('EST', 1, 15, 'EST.1.15', '“What shall we do to Queen Vashti according to law, because she has not done the bidding of the King Ahasuerus by the eunuchs?”'),
('EST', 1, 16, 'EST.1.16', 'Memucan answered before the king and the princes, “Vashti the queen has not done wrong to just the king, but also to all the princes, and to all the people who are in all the provinces of the King Ahasuerus.'),
('EST', 1, 17, 'EST.1.17', 'For this deed of the queen will become known to all women, causing them to show contempt for their husbands when it is reported, ‘King Ahasuerus commanded Vashti the queen to be brought in before him, but she didn’t come.’'),
('EST', 1, 18, 'EST.1.18', 'Today, the princesses of Persia and Media who have heard of the queen’s deed will tell all the king’s princes. This will cause much contempt and wrath.'),
('EST', 1, 19, 'EST.1.19', '“If it pleases the king, let a royal commandment go from him, and let it be written among the laws of the Persians and the Medes, so that it cannot be altered, that Vashti may never again come before King Ahasuerus; and let the king give her royal estate to another who is better than she.'),
('EST', 1, 20, 'EST.1.20', 'When the king’s decree which he shall make is published throughout all his kingdom (for it is great), all the wives will give their husbands honor, both great and small.”'),
('EST', 1, 21, 'EST.1.21', 'This advice pleased the king and the princes, and the king did according to the word of Memucan:'),
('EST', 1, 22, 'EST.1.22', 'for he sent letters into all the king’s provinces, into every province according to its writing, and to every people in their language, that every man should rule his own house, speaking in the language of his own people.'),
('EST', 2, 1, 'EST.2.1', 'After these things, when the wrath of King Ahasuerus was pacified, he remembered Vashti, and what she had done, and what was decreed against her.'),
('EST', 2, 2, 'EST.2.2', 'Then the king’s servants who served him said, “Let beautiful young virgins be sought for the king.'),
('EST', 2, 3, 'EST.2.3', 'Let the king appoint officers in all the provinces of his kingdom, that they may gather together all the beautiful young virgins to the citadel of Susa, to the women’s house, to the custody of Hegai the king’s eunuch, keeper of the women. Let cosmetics be given them;'),
('EST', 2, 4, 'EST.2.4', 'and let the maiden who pleases the king be queen instead of Vashti.” The thing pleased the king, and he did so.'),
('EST', 2, 5, 'EST.2.5', 'There was a certain Jew in the citadel of Susa whose name was Mordecai, the son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish, a Benjamite,'),
('EST', 2, 6, 'EST.2.6', 'who had been carried away from Jerusalem with the captives who had been carried away with Jeconiah king of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away.'),
('EST', 2, 7, 'EST.2.7', 'He brought up Hadassah, that is, Esther, his uncle’s daughter; for she had neither father nor mother. The maiden was fair and beautiful; and when her father and mother were dead, Mordecai took her for his own daughter.'),
('EST', 2, 8, 'EST.2.8', 'So, when the king’s commandment and his decree was heard, and when many maidens were gathered together to the citadel of Susa, to the custody of Hegai, Esther was taken into the king’s house, to the custody of Hegai, keeper of the women.'),
('EST', 2, 9, 'EST.2.9', 'The maiden pleased him, and she obtained kindness from him. He quickly gave her cosmetics and her portions of food, and the seven choice maidens who were to be given her out of the king’s house. He moved her and her maidens to the best place in the women’s house.'),
('EST', 2, 10, 'EST.2.10', 'Esther had not made known her people nor her relatives, because Mordecai had instructed her that she should not make it known.'),
('EST', 2, 11, 'EST.2.11', 'Mordecai walked every day in front of the court of the women’s house, to find out how Esther was doing, and what would become of her.'),
('EST', 2, 12, 'EST.2.12', 'Each young woman’s turn came to go in to King Ahasuerus after her purification for twelve months (for so were the days of their purification accomplished, six months with oil of myrrh, and six months with sweet fragrances and with preparations for beautifying women).'),
('EST', 2, 13, 'EST.2.13', 'The young woman then came to the king like this: whatever she desired was given her to go with her out of the women’s house to the king’s house.'),
('EST', 2, 14, 'EST.2.14', 'In the evening she went, and on the next day she returned into the second women’s house, to the custody of Shaashgaz, the king’s eunuch, who kept the concubines. She came in to the king no more, unless the king delighted in her, and she was called by name.'),
('EST', 2, 15, 'EST.2.15', 'Now when the turn of Esther, the daughter of Abihail the uncle of Mordecai, who had taken her for his daughter, came to go in to the king, she required nothing but what Hegai the king’s eunuch, the keeper of the women, advised. Esther obtained favor in the sight of all those who looked at her.'),
('EST', 2, 16, 'EST.2.16', 'So Esther was taken to King Ahasuerus into his royal house in the tenth month, which is the month Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.'),
('EST', 2, 17, 'EST.2.17', 'The king loved Esther more than all the women, and she obtained favor and kindness in his sight more than all the virgins; so that he set the royal crown on her head, and made her queen instead of Vashti.'),
('EST', 2, 18, 'EST.2.18', 'Then the king made a great feast for all his princes and his servants, even Esther’s feast; and he proclaimed a holiday in the provinces, and gave gifts according to the king’s bounty.'),
('EST', 2, 19, 'EST.2.19', 'When the virgins were gathered together the second time, Mordecai was sitting in the king’s gate.'),
('EST', 2, 20, 'EST.2.20', 'Esther had not yet made known her relatives nor her people, as Mordecai had commanded her; for Esther obeyed Mordecai, like she did when she was brought up by him.'),
('EST', 2, 21, 'EST.2.21', 'In those days, while Mordecai was sitting in the king’s gate, two of the king’s eunuchs, Bigthan and Teresh, who were doorkeepers, were angry, and sought to lay hands on the King Ahasuerus.'),
('EST', 2, 22, 'EST.2.22', 'This thing became known to Mordecai, who informed Esther the queen; and Esther informed the king in Mordecai’s name.'),
('EST', 2, 23, 'EST.2.23', 'When this matter was investigated, and it was found to be so, they were both hanged on a gallows; and it was written in the book of the chronicles in the king’s presence.'),
('EST', 3, 1, 'EST.3.1', 'After these things King Ahasuerus promoted Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes who were with him.'),
('EST', 3, 2, 'EST.3.2', 'All the king’s servants who were in the king’s gate bowed down and paid homage to Haman, for the king had so commanded concerning him. But Mordecai didn’t bow down or pay him homage.'),
('EST', 3, 3, 'EST.3.3', 'Then the king’s servants who were in the king’s gate said to Mordecai, “Why do you disobey the king’s commandment?”'),
('EST', 3, 4, 'EST.3.4', 'Now it came to pass, when they spoke daily to him, and he didn’t listen to them, that they told Haman, to see whether Mordecai’s reason would stand; for he had told them that he was a Jew.'),
('EST', 3, 5, 'EST.3.5', 'When Haman saw that Mordecai didn’t bow down nor pay him homage, Haman was full of wrath.'),
('EST', 3, 6, 'EST.3.6', 'But he scorned the thought of laying hands on Mordecai alone, for they had made known to him Mordecai’s people. Therefore Haman sought to destroy all the Jews who were throughout the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, even Mordecai’s people.'),
('EST', 3, 7, 'EST.3.7', 'In the first month, which is the month Nisan, in the twelfth year of King Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that is, the lot, before Haman from day to day, and from month to month, and chose the twelfth month, which is the month Adar.'),
('EST', 3, 8, 'EST.3.8', 'Haman said to King Ahasuerus, “There is a certain people scattered abroad and dispersed among the peoples in all the provinces of your kingdom, and their laws are different from other people’s. They don’t keep the king’s laws. Therefore it is not for the king’s profit to allow them to remain.'),
('EST', 3, 9, 'EST.3.9', 'If it pleases the king, let it be written that they be destroyed; and I will pay ten thousand talents of silver into the hands of those who are in charge of the king’s business, to bring it into the king’s treasuries.”'),
('EST', 3, 10, 'EST.3.10', 'The king took his ring from his hand, and gave it to Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, the Jews’ enemy.'),
('EST', 3, 11, 'EST.3.11', 'The king said to Haman, “The silver is given to you, the people also, to do with them as it seems good to you.”'),
('EST', 3, 12, 'EST.3.12', 'Then the king’s scribes were called in on the first month, on the thirteenth day of the month; and all that Haman commanded was written to the king’s local governors, and to the governors who were over every province, and to the princes of every people, to every province according to its writing, and to every people in their language. It was written in the name of King Ahasuerus, and it was sealed with the king’s ring.'),
('EST', 3, 13, 'EST.3.13', 'Letters were sent by couriers into all the king’s provinces, to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, both young and old, little children and women, in one day, even on the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, and to plunder their possessions.'),
('EST', 3, 14, 'EST.3.14', 'A copy of the letter, that the decree should be given out in every province, was published to all the peoples, that they should be ready against that day.'),
('EST', 3, 15, 'EST.3.15', 'The couriers went out in haste by the king’s commandment, and the decree was given out in the citadel of Susa. The king and Haman sat down to drink; but the city of Susa was perplexed.'),
('EST', 4, 1, 'EST.4.1', 'Now when Mordecai found out all that was done, Mordecai tore his clothes and put on sackcloth with ashes, and went out into the middle of the city, and wailed loudly and bitterly.'),
('EST', 4, 2, 'EST.4.2', 'He came even before the king’s gate, for no one is allowed inside the king’s gate clothed with sackcloth.'),
('EST', 4, 3, 'EST.4.3', 'In every province, wherever the king’s commandment and his decree came, there was great mourning among the Jews, and fasting, and weeping, and wailing; and many lay in sackcloth and ashes.'),
('EST', 4, 4, 'EST.4.4', 'Esther’s maidens and her eunuchs came and told her this, and the queen was exceedingly grieved. She sent clothing to Mordecai, to replace his sackcloth, but he didn’t receive it.'),
('EST', 4, 5, 'EST.4.5', 'Then Esther called for Hathach, one of the king’s eunuchs, whom he had appointed to attend her, and commanded him to go to Mordecai, to find out what this was, and why it was.'),
('EST', 4, 6, 'EST.4.6', 'So Hathach went out to Mordecai, to the city square which was before the king’s gate.'),
('EST', 4, 7, 'EST.4.7', 'Mordecai told him of all that had happened to him, and the exact sum of the money that Haman had promised to pay to the king’s treasuries for the destruction of the Jews.'),
('EST', 4, 8, 'EST.4.8', 'He also gave him the copy of the writing of the decree that was given out in Susa to destroy them, to show it to Esther, and to declare it to her, and to urge her to go in to the king to make supplication to him, and to make request before him for her people.'),
('EST', 4, 9, 'EST.4.9', 'Hathach came and told Esther the words of Mordecai.'),
('EST', 4, 10, 'EST.4.10', 'Then Esther spoke to Hathach, and gave him a message to Mordecai:'),
('EST', 4, 11, 'EST.4.11', '“All the king’s servants and the people of the king’s provinces know that whoever, whether man or woman, comes to the king into the inner court without being called, there is one law for him, that he be put to death, except those to whom the king might hold out the golden scepter, that he may live. I have not been called to come in to the king these thirty days.”'),
('EST', 4, 12, 'EST.4.12', 'They told Esther’s words to Mordecai.'),
('EST', 4, 13, 'EST.4.13', 'Then Mordecai asked them to return this answer to Esther: “Don’t think to yourself that you will escape in the king’s house any more than all the Jews.'),
('EST', 4, 14, 'EST.4.14', 'For if you remain silent now, then relief and deliverance will come to the Jews from another place, but you and your father’s house will perish. Who knows if you haven’t come to the kingdom for such a time as this?”'),
('EST', 4, 15, 'EST.4.15', 'Then Esther asked them to answer Mordecai,'),
('EST', 4, 16, 'EST.4.16', '“Go, gather together all the Jews who are present in Susa, and fast for me, and neither eat nor drink three days, night or day. I and my maidens will also fast the same way. Then I will go in to the king, which is against the law; and if I perish, I perish.”'),
('EST', 4, 17, 'EST.4.17', 'So Mordecai went his way, and did according to all that Esther had commanded him.'),
('EST', 5, 1, 'EST.5.1', 'Now on the third day, Esther put on her royal clothing and stood in the inner court of the king’s house, next to the king’s house. The king sat on his royal throne in the royal house, next to the entrance of the house.'),
('EST', 5, 2, 'EST.5.2', 'When the king saw Esther the queen standing in the court, she obtained favor in his sight; and the king held out to Esther the golden scepter that was in his hand. So Esther came near and touched the top of the scepter.'),
('EST', 5, 3, 'EST.5.3', 'Then the king asked her, “What would you like, queen Esther? What is your request? It shall be given you even to the half of the kingdom.”'),
('EST', 5, 4, 'EST.5.4', 'Esther said, “If it seems good to the king, let the king and Haman come today to the banquet that I have prepared for him.”'),
('EST', 5, 5, 'EST.5.5', 'Then the king said, “Bring Haman quickly, so that it may be done as Esther has said.” So the king and Haman came to the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
('EST', 5, 6, 'EST.5.6', 'The king said to Esther at the banquet of wine, “What is your petition? It shall be granted you. What is your request? Even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.”'),
('EST', 5, 7, 'EST.5.7', 'Then Esther answered and said, “My petition and my request is this.'),
('EST', 5, 8, 'EST.5.8', 'If I have found favor in the sight of the king, and if it pleases the king to grant my petition and to perform my request, let the king and Haman come to the banquet that I will prepare for them, and I will do tomorrow as the king has said.”'),
('EST', 5, 9, 'EST.5.9', 'Then Haman went out that day joyful and glad of heart, but when Haman saw Mordecai in the king’s gate, that he didn’t stand up nor move for him, he was filled with wrath against Mordecai.'),
('EST', 5, 10, 'EST.5.10', 'Nevertheless Haman restrained himself, and went home. There, he sent and called for his friends and Zeresh his wife.'),
('EST', 5, 11, 'EST.5.11', 'Haman recounted to them the glory of his riches, the multitude of his children, all the things in which the king had promoted him, and how he had advanced him above the princes and servants of the king.'),
('EST', 5, 12, 'EST.5.12', 'Haman also said, “Yes, Esther the queen let no man come in with the king to the banquet that she had prepared but myself; and tomorrow I am also invited by her together with the king.'),
('EST', 5, 13, 'EST.5.13', 'Yet all this avails me nothing, so long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king’s gate.”'),
('EST', 5, 14, 'EST.5.14', 'Then Zeresh his wife and all his friends said to him, “Let a gallows be made fifty cubits high, and in the morning speak to the king about hanging Mordecai on it. Then go in merrily with the king to the banquet.” This pleased Haman, so he had the gallows made.'),
('EST', 6, 1, 'EST.6.1', 'On that night, the king couldn’t sleep. He commanded the book of records of the chronicles to be brought, and they were read to the king.'),
('EST', 6, 2, 'EST.6.2', 'It was found written that Mordecai had told of Bigthana and Teresh, two of the king’s eunuchs, who were doorkeepers, who had tried to lay hands on the King Ahasuerus.'),
('EST', 6, 3, 'EST.6.3', 'The king said, “What honor and dignity has been given to Mordecai for this?” Then the king’s servants who attended him said, “Nothing has been done for him.”'),
('EST', 6, 4, 'EST.6.4', 'The king said, “Who is in the court?” Now Haman had come into the outer court of the king’s house, to speak to the king about hanging Mordecai on the gallows that he had prepared for him.'),
('EST', 6, 5, 'EST.6.5', 'The king’s servants said to him, “Behold, Haman stands in the court.” The king said, “Let him come in.”'),
('EST', 6, 6, 'EST.6.6', 'So Haman came in. The king said to him, “What shall be done to the man whom the king delights to honor?” Now Haman said in his heart, “Who would the king delight to honor more than myself?”'),
('EST', 6, 7, 'EST.6.7', 'Haman said to the king, “For the man whom the king delights to honor,'),
('EST', 6, 8, 'EST.6.8', 'let royal clothing be brought which the king uses to wear, and the horse that the king rides on, and on the head of which a royal crown is set.'),
('EST', 6, 9, 'EST.6.9', 'Let the clothing and the horse be delivered to the hand of one of the king’s most noble princes, that they may array the man whom the king delights to honor with them, and have him ride on horseback through the city square, and proclaim before him, ‘Thus it shall be done to the man whom the king delights to honor!’”'),
('EST', 6, 10, 'EST.6.10', 'Then the king said to Haman, “Hurry and take the clothing and the horse, as you have said, and do this for Mordecai the Jew, who sits at the king’s gate. Let nothing fail of all that you have spoken.”'),
('EST', 6, 11, 'EST.6.11', 'Then Haman took the clothing and the horse, and arrayed Mordecai, and had him ride through the city square, and proclaimed before him, “Thus it shall be done to the man whom the king delights to honor!”'),
('EST', 6, 12, 'EST.6.12', 'Mordecai came back to the king’s gate, but Haman hurried to his house, mourning and having his head covered.'),
('EST', 6, 13, 'EST.6.13', 'Haman recounted to Zeresh his wife and all his friends everything that had happened to him. Then his wise men and Zeresh his wife said to him, “If Mordecai, before whom you have begun to fall, is of Jewish descent, you will not prevail against him, but you will surely fall before him.”'),
('EST', 6, 14, 'EST.6.14', 'While they were yet talking with him, the king’s eunuchs came, and hurried to bring Haman to the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
('EST', 7, 1, 'EST.7.1', 'So the king and Haman came to banquet with Esther the queen.'),
('EST', 7, 2, 'EST.7.2', 'The king said again to Esther on the second day at the banquet of wine, “What is your petition, queen Esther? It shall be granted you. What is your request? Even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.”'),
('EST', 7, 3, 'EST.7.3', 'Then Esther the queen answered, “If I have found favor in your sight, O king, and if it pleases the king, let my life be given me at my petition, and my people at my request.'),
('EST', 7, 4, 'EST.7.4', 'For we are sold, I and my people, to be destroyed, to be slain, and to perish. But if we had been sold for male and female slaves, I would have held my peace, although the adversary could not have compensated for the king’s loss.”'),
('EST', 7, 5, 'EST.7.5', 'Then King Ahasuerus said to Esther the queen, “Who is he, and where is he who dared presume in his heart to do so?”'),
('EST', 7, 6, 'EST.7.6', 'Esther said, “An adversary and an enemy, even this wicked Haman!” Then Haman was afraid before the king and the queen.'),
('EST', 7, 7, 'EST.7.7', 'The king arose in his wrath from the banquet of wine and went into the palace garden. Haman stood up to make request for his life to Esther the queen, for he saw that there was evil determined against him by the king.'),
('EST', 7, 8, 'EST.7.8', 'Then the king returned out of the palace garden into the place of the banquet of wine; and Haman had fallen on the couch where Esther was. Then the king said, “Will he even assault the queen in front of me in the house?” As the word went out of the king’s mouth, they covered Haman’s face.'),
('EST', 7, 9, 'EST.7.9', 'Then Harbonah, one of the eunuchs who were with the king, said, “Behold, the gallows fifty cubits high, which Haman has made for Mordecai, who spoke good for the king, is standing at Haman’s house.” The king said, “Hang him on it!”'),
('EST', 7, 10, 'EST.7.10', 'So they hanged Haman on the gallows that he had prepared for Mordecai. Then the king’s wrath was pacified.'),
('EST', 8, 1, 'EST.8.1', 'On that day, King Ahasuerus gave the house of Haman, the Jews’ enemy, to Esther the queen. Mordecai came before the king; for Esther had told what he was to her.'),
('EST', 8, 2, 'EST.8.2', 'The king took off his ring, which he had taken from Haman, and gave it to Mordecai. Esther set Mordecai over the house of Haman.'),
('EST', 8, 3, 'EST.8.3', 'Esther spoke yet again before the king, and fell down at his feet and begged him with tears to put away the mischief of Haman the Agagite, and his plan that he had planned against the Jews.'),
('EST', 8, 4, 'EST.8.4', 'Then the king held out to Esther the golden scepter. So Esther arose, and stood before the king.'),
('EST', 8, 5, 'EST.8.5', 'She said, “If it pleases the king, and if I have found favor in his sight, and the thing seems right to the king, and I am pleasing in his eyes, let it be written to reverse the letters devised by Haman, the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, which he wrote to destroy the Jews who are in all the king’s provinces.'),
('EST', 8, 6, 'EST.8.6', 'For how can I endure to see the evil that would come to my people? How can I endure to see the destruction of my relatives?”'),
('EST', 8, 7, 'EST.8.7', 'Then King Ahasuerus said to Esther the queen and to Mordecai the Jew, “See, I have given Esther the house of Haman, and they have hanged him on the gallows because he laid his hand on the Jews.'),
('EST', 8, 8, 'EST.8.8', 'Write also to the Jews as it pleases you, in the king’s name, and seal it with the king’s ring; for the writing which is written in the king’s name, and sealed with the king’s ring, may not be reversed by any man.”'),
('EST', 8, 9, 'EST.8.9', 'Then the king’s scribes were called at that time, in the third month, which is the month Sivan, on the twenty-third day of the month; and it was written according to all that Mordecai commanded to the Jews, and to the local governors, and the governors and princes of the provinces which are from India to Ethiopia, one hundred twenty-seven provinces, to every province according to its writing, and to every people in their language, and to the Jews in their writing, and in their language.'),
('EST', 8, 10, 'EST.8.10', 'He wrote in the name of King Ahasuerus, and sealed it with the king’s ring, and sent letters by courier on horseback, riding on royal horses that were bred from swift steeds.'),
('EST', 8, 11, 'EST.8.11', 'In those letters, the king granted the Jews who were in every city to gather themselves together and to defend their lives—to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish all the power of the people and province that would assault them, their little ones and women, and to plunder their possessions,'),
('EST', 8, 12, 'EST.8.12', 'on one day in all the provinces of King Ahasuerus, on the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar.'),
('EST', 8, 13, 'EST.8.13', 'A copy of the letter, that the decree should be given out in every province, was published to all the peoples, that the Jews should be ready for that day to avenge themselves on their enemies.'),
('EST', 8, 14, 'EST.8.14', 'So the couriers who rode on royal horses went out, hastened and pressed on by the king’s commandment. The decree was given out in the citadel of Susa.'),
('EST', 8, 15, 'EST.8.15', 'Mordecai went out of the presence of the king in royal clothing of blue and white, and with a great crown of gold, and with a robe of fine linen and purple; and the city of Susa shouted and was glad.'),
('EST', 8, 16, 'EST.8.16', 'The Jews had light, gladness, joy, and honor.'),
('EST', 8, 17, 'EST.8.17', 'In every province and in every city, wherever the king’s commandment and his decree came, the Jews had gladness, joy, a feast and a holiday. Many from among the peoples of the land became Jews, for the fear of the Jews had fallen on them.'),
('EST', 9, 1, 'EST.9.1', 'Now in the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, on the thirteenth day of the month, when the king’s commandment and his decree came near to be put in execution, on the day that the enemies of the Jews hoped to conquer them, (but it turned out that the opposite happened, that the Jews conquered those who hated them),'),
('EST', 9, 2, 'EST.9.2', 'the Jews gathered themselves together in their cities throughout all the provinces of the King Ahasuerus, to lay hands on those who wanted to harm them. No one could withstand them, because the fear of them had fallen on all the people.'),
('EST', 9, 3, 'EST.9.3', 'All the princes of the provinces, the local governors, the governors, and those who did the king’s business helped the Jews, because the fear of Mordecai had fallen on them.'),
('EST', 9, 4, 'EST.9.4', 'For Mordecai was great in the king’s house, and his fame went out throughout all the provinces, for the man Mordecai grew greater and greater.'),
('EST', 9, 5, 'EST.9.5', 'The Jews struck all their enemies with the stroke of the sword, and with slaughter and destruction, and did what they wanted to those who hated them.'),
('EST', 9, 6, 'EST.9.6', 'In the citadel of Susa, the Jews killed and destroyed five hundred men.'),
('EST', 9, 7, 'EST.9.7', 'They killed Parshandatha, Dalphon, Aspatha,'),
('EST', 9, 8, 'EST.9.8', 'Poratha, Adalia, Aridatha,'),
('EST', 9, 9, 'EST.9.9', 'Parmashta, Arisai, Aridai, and Vaizatha,'),
('EST', 9, 10, 'EST.9.10', 'the ten sons of Haman the son of Hammedatha, the Jews’ enemy, but they didn’t lay their hand on the plunder.'),
('EST', 9, 11, 'EST.9.11', 'On that day, the number of those who were slain in the citadel of Susa was brought before the king.'),
('EST', 9, 12, 'EST.9.12', 'The king said to Esther the queen, “The Jews have slain and destroyed five hundred men in the citadel of Susa, including the ten sons of Haman; what then have they done in the rest of the king’s provinces! Now what is your petition? It shall be granted you. What is your further request? It shall be done.”'),
('EST', 9, 13, 'EST.9.13', 'Then Esther said, “If it pleases the king, let it be granted to the Jews who are in Susa to do tomorrow also according to today’s decree, and let Haman’s ten sons be hanged on the gallows.”'),
('EST', 9, 14, 'EST.9.14', 'The king commanded this to be done. A decree was given out in Susa; and they hanged Haman’s ten sons.'),
('EST', 9, 15, 'EST.9.15', 'The Jews who were in Susa gathered themselves together on the fourteenth day also of the month Adar, and killed three hundred men in Susa; but they didn’t lay their hand on the plunder.'),
('EST', 9, 16, 'EST.9.16', 'The other Jews who were in the king’s provinces gathered themselves together, defended their lives, had rest from their enemies, and killed seventy-five thousand of those who hated them; but they didn’t lay their hand on the plunder.'),
('EST', 9, 17, 'EST.9.17', 'This was done on the thirteenth day of the month Adar; and on the fourteenth day of that month they rested and made it a day of feasting and gladness.'),
('EST', 9, 18, 'EST.9.18', 'But the Jews who were in Susa assembled together on the thirteenth and on the fourteenth days of the month; and on the fifteenth day of that month, they rested, and made it a day of feasting and gladness.'),
('EST', 9, 19, 'EST.9.19', 'Therefore the Jews of the villages, who live in the unwalled towns, make the fourteenth day of the month Adar a day of gladness and feasting, a holiday, and a day of sending presents of food to one another.'),
('EST', 9, 20, 'EST.9.20', 'Mordecai wrote these things, and sent letters to all the Jews who were in all the provinces of the King Ahasuerus, both near and far,'),
('EST', 9, 21, 'EST.9.21', 'to enjoin them that they should keep the fourteenth and fifteenth days of the month Adar yearly,'),
('EST', 9, 22, 'EST.9.22', 'as the days in which the Jews had rest from their enemies, and the month which was turned to them from sorrow to gladness, and from mourning into a holiday; that they should make them days of feasting and gladness, and of sending presents of food to one another, and gifts to the needy.'),
('EST', 9, 23, 'EST.9.23', 'The Jews accepted the custom that they had begun, as Mordecai had written to them,'),
('EST', 9, 24, 'EST.9.24', 'because Haman the son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had plotted against the Jews to destroy them, and had cast “Pur”, that is the lot, to consume them and to destroy them;'),
('EST', 9, 25, 'EST.9.25', 'but when this became known to the king, he commanded by letters that his wicked plan, which he had planned against the Jews, should return on his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the gallows.'),
('EST', 9, 26, 'EST.9.26', 'Therefore they called these days “Purim”, from the word “Pur.” Therefore because of all the words of this letter, and of that which they had seen concerning this matter, and that which had come to them,'),
('EST', 9, 27, 'EST.9.27', 'the Jews established and imposed on themselves, on their descendants, and on all those who joined themselves to them, so that it should not fail that they would keep these two days according to what was written and according to its appointed time every year;'),
('EST', 9, 28, 'EST.9.28', 'and that these days should be remembered and kept throughout every generation, every family, every province, and every city; and that these days of Purim should not fail from among the Jews, nor their memory perish from their offspring.'),
('EST', 9, 29, 'EST.9.29', 'Then Esther the queen, the daughter of Abihail, and Mordecai the Jew wrote with all authority to confirm this second letter of Purim.'),
('EST', 9, 30, 'EST.9.30', 'He sent letters to all the Jews in the hundred twenty-seven provinces of the kingdom of Ahasuerus with words of peace and truth,'),
('EST', 9, 31, 'EST.9.31', 'to confirm these days of Purim in their appointed times, as Mordecai the Jew and Esther the queen had decreed, and as they had imposed upon themselves and their descendants in the matter of the fastings and their mourning.'),
('EST', 9, 32, 'EST.9.32', 'The commandment of Esther confirmed these matters of Purim; and it was written in the book.'),
('EST', 10, 1, 'EST.10.1', 'King Ahasuerus laid a tribute on the land and on the islands of the sea.'),
('EST', 10, 2, 'EST.10.2', 'Aren’t all the acts of his power and of his might, and the full account of the greatness of Mordecai, to which the king advanced him, written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Media and Persia?'),
('EST', 10, 3, 'EST.10.3', 'For Mordecai the Jew was next to King Ahasuerus, and great among the Jews and accepted by the multitude of his brothers, seeking the good of his people and speaking peace to all his descendants.'),
('JOB', 1, 1, 'JOB.1.1', 'There was a man in the land of Uz, whose name was Job. That man was blameless and upright, and one who feared God, and turned away from evil.'),
('JOB', 1, 2, 'JOB.1.2', 'There were born to him seven sons and three daughters.'),
('JOB', 1, 3, 'JOB.1.3', 'His possessions also were seven thousand sheep, three thousand camels, five hundred yoke of oxen, five hundred female donkeys, and a very great household; so that this man was the greatest of all the children of the east.'),
('JOB', 1, 4, 'JOB.1.4', 'His sons went and held a feast in the house of each one on his birthday; and they sent and called for their three sisters to eat and to drink with them.'),
('JOB', 1, 5, 'JOB.1.5', 'It was so, when the days of their feasting had run their course, that Job sent and sanctified them, and rose up early in the morning, and offered burnt offerings according to the number of them all. For Job said, “It may be that my sons have sinned, and renounced God in their hearts.” Job did so continually.'),
('JOB', 1, 6, 'JOB.1.6', 'Now on the day when God’s sons came to present themselves before the LORD, Satan also came among them.'),
('JOB', 1, 7, 'JOB.1.7', 'The LORD said to Satan, “Where have you come from?” Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, “From going back and forth on the earth, and from walking up and down in it.”'),
('JOB', 1, 8, 'JOB.1.8', 'The LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered my servant, Job? For there is no one like him on the earth, a blameless and an upright man, one who fears God, and turns away from evil.”'),
('JOB', 1, 9, 'JOB.1.9', 'Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, “Does Job fear God for nothing?'),
('JOB', 1, 10, 'JOB.1.10', 'Haven’t you made a hedge around him, and around his house, and around all that he has, on every side? You have blessed the work of his hands, and his substance is increased in the land.'),
('JOB', 1, 11, 'JOB.1.11', 'But stretch out your hand now, and touch all that he has, and he will renounce you to your face.”'),
('JOB', 1, 12, 'JOB.1.12', 'The LORD said to Satan, “Behold, all that he has is in your power. Only on himself don’t stretch out your hand.” So Satan went out from the presence of the LORD.'),
('JOB', 1, 13, 'JOB.1.13', 'It fell on a day when his sons and his daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,'),
('JOB', 1, 14, 'JOB.1.14', 'that a messenger came to Job, and said, “The oxen were plowing, and the donkeys feeding beside them,'),
('JOB', 1, 15, 'JOB.1.15', 'and the Sabeans attacked, and took them away. Yes, they have killed the servants with the edge of the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you.”'),
('JOB', 1, 16, 'JOB.1.16', 'While he was still speaking, another also came and said, “The fire of God has fallen from the sky, and has burned up the sheep and the servants, and consumed them, and I alone have escaped to tell you.”'),
('JOB', 1, 17, 'JOB.1.17', 'While he was still speaking, another also came and said, “The Chaldeans made three bands, and swept down on the camels, and have taken them away, yes, and killed the servants with the edge of the sword; and I alone have escaped to tell you.”'),
('JOB', 1, 18, 'JOB.1.18', 'While he was still speaking, there came also another, and said, “Your sons and your daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,'),
('JOB', 1, 19, 'JOB.1.19', 'and behold, there came a great wind from the wilderness, and struck the four corners of the house, and it fell on the young men, and they are dead. I alone have escaped to tell you.”'),
('JOB', 1, 20, 'JOB.1.20', 'Then Job arose, and tore his robe, and shaved his head, and fell down on the ground, and worshiped.'),
('JOB', 1, 21, 'JOB.1.21', 'He said, “Naked I came out of my mother’s womb, and naked will I return there. The LORD gave, and the LORD has taken away. Blessed be the LORD’s name.”'),
('JOB', 1, 22, 'JOB.1.22', 'In all this, Job didn’t sin, nor charge God with wrongdoing.'),
('JOB', 2, 1, 'JOB.2.1', 'Again, on the day when God’s sons came to present themselves before the LORD, Satan came also among them to present himself before the LORD.'),
('JOB', 2, 2, 'JOB.2.2', 'The LORD said to Satan, “Where have you come from?” Satan answered the LORD, and said, “From going back and forth on the earth, and from walking up and down in it.”'),
('JOB', 2, 3, 'JOB.2.3', 'The LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered my servant Job? For there is no one like him on the earth, a blameless and an upright man, one who fears God, and turns away from evil. He still maintains his integrity, although you incited me against him, to ruin him without cause.”'),
('JOB', 2, 4, 'JOB.2.4', 'Satan answered the LORD, and said, “Skin for skin. Yes, all that a man has he will give for his life.'),
('JOB', 2, 5, 'JOB.2.5', 'But stretch out your hand now, and touch his bone and his flesh, and he will renounce you to your face.”'),
('JOB', 2, 6, 'JOB.2.6', 'The LORD said to Satan, “Behold, he is in your hand. Only spare his life.”'),
('JOB', 2, 7, 'JOB.2.7', 'So Satan went out from the presence of the LORD, and struck Job with painful sores from the sole of his foot to his head.'),
('JOB', 2, 8, 'JOB.2.8', 'He took for himself a potsherd to scrape himself with, and he sat among the ashes.'),
('JOB', 2, 9, 'JOB.2.9', 'Then his wife said to him, “Do you still maintain your integrity? Renounce God, and die.”'),
('JOB', 2, 10, 'JOB.2.10', 'But he said to her, “You speak as one of the foolish women would speak. What? Shall we receive good at the hand of God, and shall we not receive evil?” In all this Job didn’t sin with his lips.'),
('JOB', 2, 11, 'JOB.2.11', 'Now when Job’s three friends heard of all this evil that had come on him, they each came from his own place: Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite; and they made an appointment together to come to sympathize with him and to comfort him.'),
('JOB', 2, 12, 'JOB.2.12', 'When they lifted up their eyes from a distance, and didn’t recognize him, they raised their voices, and wept; and they each tore his robe, and sprinkled dust on their heads toward the sky.'),
('JOB', 2, 13, 'JOB.2.13', 'So they sat down with him on the ground seven days and seven nights, and no one spoke a word to him, for they saw that his grief was very great.'),
('JOB', 3, 1, 'JOB.3.1', 'After this Job opened his mouth, and cursed the day of his birth.'),
('JOB', 3, 2, 'JOB.3.2', 'Job answered:'),
('JOB', 3, 3, 'JOB.3.3', '“Let the day perish in which I was born, the night which said, ‘There is a boy conceived.’'),
('JOB', 3, 4, 'JOB.3.4', 'Let that day be darkness. Don’t let God from above seek for it, neither let the light shine on it.'),
('JOB', 3, 5, 'JOB.3.5', 'Let darkness and the shadow of death claim it for their own. Let a cloud dwell on it. Let all that makes the day black terrify it.'),
('JOB', 3, 6, 'JOB.3.6', 'As for that night, let thick darkness seize on it. Let it not rejoice among the days of the year. Let it not come into the number of the months.'),
('JOB', 3, 7, 'JOB.3.7', 'Behold, let that night be barren. Let no joyful voice come therein.'),
('JOB', 3, 8, 'JOB.3.8', 'Let them curse it who curse the day, who are ready to rouse up leviathan.'),
('JOB', 3, 9, 'JOB.3.9', 'Let the stars of its twilight be dark. Let it look for light, but have none, neither let it see the eyelids of the morning,'),
('JOB', 3, 10, 'JOB.3.10', 'because it didn’t shut up the doors of my mother’s womb, nor did it hide trouble from my eyes.'),
('JOB', 3, 11, 'JOB.3.11', '“Why didn’t I die from the womb? Why didn’t I give up the spirit when my mother bore me?'),
('JOB', 3, 12, 'JOB.3.12', 'Why did the knees receive me? Or why the breast, that I should nurse?'),
('JOB', 3, 13, 'JOB.3.13', 'For now I should have lain down and been quiet. I should have slept, then I would have been at rest,'),
('JOB', 3, 14, 'JOB.3.14', 'with kings and counselors of the earth, who built up waste places for themselves;'),
('JOB', 3, 15, 'JOB.3.15', 'or with princes who had gold, who filled their houses with silver;'),
('JOB', 3, 16, 'JOB.3.16', 'or as a hidden untimely birth I had not been, as infants who never saw light.'),
('JOB', 3, 17, 'JOB.3.17', 'There the wicked cease from troubling. There the weary are at rest.'),
('JOB', 3, 18, 'JOB.3.18', 'There the prisoners are at ease together. They don’t hear the voice of the taskmaster.'),
('JOB', 3, 19, 'JOB.3.19', 'The small and the great are there. The servant is free from his master.'),
('JOB', 3, 20, 'JOB.3.20', '“Why is light given to him who is in misery, life to the bitter in soul,'),
('JOB', 3, 21, 'JOB.3.21', 'who long for death, but it doesn’t come; and dig for it more than for hidden treasures,'),
('JOB', 3, 22, 'JOB.3.22', 'who rejoice exceedingly, and are glad, when they can find the grave?'),
('JOB', 3, 23, 'JOB.3.23', 'Why is light given to a man whose way is hidden, whom God has hedged in?'),
('JOB', 3, 24, 'JOB.3.24', 'For my sighing comes before I eat. My groanings are poured out like water.'),
('JOB', 3, 25, 'JOB.3.25', 'For the thing which I fear comes on me, that which I am afraid of comes to me.'),
('JOB', 3, 26, 'JOB.3.26', 'I am not at ease, neither am I quiet, neither do I have rest; but trouble comes.”'),
('JOB', 4, 1, 'JOB.4.1', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered,'),
('JOB', 4, 2, 'JOB.4.2', '“If someone ventures to talk with you, will you be grieved? But who can withhold himself from speaking?'),
('JOB', 4, 3, 'JOB.4.3', 'Behold, you have instructed many, you have strengthened the weak hands.'),
('JOB', 4, 4, 'JOB.4.4', 'Your words have supported him who was falling, you have made the feeble knees firm.'),
('JOB', 4, 5, 'JOB.4.5', 'But now it has come to you, and you faint. It touches you, and you are troubled.'),
('JOB', 4, 6, 'JOB.4.6', 'Isn’t your piety your confidence? Isn’t the integrity of your ways your hope?'),
('JOB', 4, 7, 'JOB.4.7', '“Remember, now, who ever perished, being innocent? Or where were the upright cut off?'),
('JOB', 4, 8, 'JOB.4.8', 'According to what I have seen, those who plow iniquity and sow trouble, reap the same.'),
('JOB', 4, 9, 'JOB.4.9', 'By the breath of God they perish. By the blast of his anger are they consumed.'),
('JOB', 4, 10, 'JOB.4.10', 'The roaring of the lion, and the voice of the fierce lion, the teeth of the young lions, are broken.'),
('JOB', 4, 11, 'JOB.4.11', 'The old lion perishes for lack of prey. The cubs of the lioness are scattered abroad.'),
('JOB', 4, 12, 'JOB.4.12', '“Now a thing was secretly brought to me. My ear received a whisper of it.'),
('JOB', 4, 13, 'JOB.4.13', 'In thoughts from the visions of the night, when deep sleep falls on men,'),
('JOB', 4, 14, 'JOB.4.14', 'fear came on me, and trembling, which made all my bones shake.'),
('JOB', 4, 15, 'JOB.4.15', 'Then a spirit passed before my face. The hair of my flesh stood up.'),
('JOB', 4, 16, 'JOB.4.16', 'It stood still, but I couldn’t discern its appearance. A form was before my eyes. Silence, then I heard a voice, saying,'),
('JOB', 4, 17, 'JOB.4.17', '‘Shall mortal man be more just than God? Shall a man be more pure than his Maker?'),
('JOB', 4, 18, 'JOB.4.18', 'Behold, he puts no trust in his servants. He charges his angels with error.'),
('JOB', 4, 19, 'JOB.4.19', 'How much more those who dwell in houses of clay, whose foundation is in the dust, who are crushed before the moth!'),
('JOB', 4, 20, 'JOB.4.20', 'Between morning and evening they are destroyed. They perish forever without any regarding it.'),
('JOB', 4, 21, 'JOB.4.21', 'Isn’t their tent cord plucked up within them? They die, and that without wisdom.’'),
('JOB', 5, 1, 'JOB.5.1', '“Call now; is there any who will answer you? To which of the holy ones will you turn?'),
('JOB', 5, 2, 'JOB.5.2', 'For resentment kills the foolish man, and jealousy kills the simple.'),
('JOB', 5, 3, 'JOB.5.3', 'I have seen the foolish taking root, but suddenly I cursed his habitation.'),
('JOB', 5, 4, 'JOB.5.4', 'His children are far from safety. They are crushed in the gate. Neither is there any to deliver them,'),
('JOB', 5, 5, 'JOB.5.5', 'whose harvest the hungry eat up, and take it even out of the thorns. The snare gapes for their substance.'),
('JOB', 5, 6, 'JOB.5.6', 'For affliction doesn’t come out of the dust, neither does trouble spring out of the ground;'),
('JOB', 5, 7, 'JOB.5.7', 'but man is born to trouble, as the sparks fly upward.'),
('JOB', 5, 8, 'JOB.5.8', '“But as for me, I would seek God. I would commit my cause to God,'),
('JOB', 5, 9, 'JOB.5.9', 'who does great things that can’t be fathomed, marvelous things without number;'),
('JOB', 5, 10, 'JOB.5.10', 'who gives rain on the earth, and sends waters on the fields;'),
('JOB', 5, 11, 'JOB.5.11', 'so that he sets up on high those who are low, those who mourn are exalted to safety.'),
('JOB', 5, 12, 'JOB.5.12', 'He frustrates the plans of the crafty, so that their hands can’t perform their enterprise.'),
('JOB', 5, 13, 'JOB.5.13', 'He takes the wise in their own craftiness; the counsel of the cunning is carried headlong.'),
('JOB', 5, 14, 'JOB.5.14', 'They meet with darkness in the day time, and grope at noonday as in the night.'),
('JOB', 5, 15, 'JOB.5.15', 'But he saves from the sword of their mouth, even the needy from the hand of the mighty.'),
('JOB', 5, 16, 'JOB.5.16', 'So the poor has hope, and injustice shuts her mouth.'),
('JOB', 5, 17, 'JOB.5.17', '“Behold, happy is the man whom God corrects. Therefore do not despise the chastening of the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 5, 18, 'JOB.5.18', 'For he wounds and binds up. He injures and his hands make whole.'),
('JOB', 5, 19, 'JOB.5.19', 'He will deliver you in six troubles; yes, in seven no evil will touch you.'),
('JOB', 5, 20, 'JOB.5.20', 'In famine he will redeem you from death; in war, from the power of the sword.'),
('JOB', 5, 21, 'JOB.5.21', 'You will be hidden from the scourge of the tongue, neither will you be afraid of destruction when it comes.'),
('JOB', 5, 22, 'JOB.5.22', 'You will laugh at destruction and famine, neither will you be afraid of the animals of the earth.'),
('JOB', 5, 23, 'JOB.5.23', 'For you will be allied with the stones of the field. The animals of the field will be at peace with you.'),
('JOB', 5, 24, 'JOB.5.24', 'You will know that your tent is in peace. You will visit your fold, and will miss nothing.'),
('JOB', 5, 25, 'JOB.5.25', 'You will know also that your offspring will be great, your offspring as the grass of the earth.'),
('JOB', 5, 26, 'JOB.5.26', 'You will come to your grave in a full age, like a shock of grain comes in its season.'),
('JOB', 5, 27, 'JOB.5.27', 'Behold, we have researched it. It is so. Hear it, and know it for your good.”'),
('JOB', 6, 1, 'JOB.6.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 6, 2, 'JOB.6.2', '“Oh that my anguish were weighed, and all my calamity laid in the balances!'),
('JOB', 6, 3, 'JOB.6.3', 'For now it would be heavier than the sand of the seas, therefore my words have been rash.'),
('JOB', 6, 4, 'JOB.6.4', 'For the arrows of the Almighty are within me. My spirit drinks up their poison. The terrors of God set themselves in array against me.'),
('JOB', 6, 5, 'JOB.6.5', 'Does the wild donkey bray when he has grass? Or does the ox low over his fodder?'),
('JOB', 6, 6, 'JOB.6.6', 'Can that which has no flavor be eaten without salt? Or is there any taste in the white of an egg?'),
('JOB', 6, 7, 'JOB.6.7', 'My soul refuses to touch them. They are as loathsome food to me.'),
('JOB', 6, 8, 'JOB.6.8', '“Oh that I might have my request, that God would grant the thing that I long for,'),
('JOB', 6, 9, 'JOB.6.9', 'even that it would please God to crush me; that he would let loose his hand, and cut me off!'),
('JOB', 6, 10, 'JOB.6.10', 'Let it still be my consolation, yes, let me exult in pain that doesn’t spare, that I have not denied the words of the Holy One.'),
('JOB', 6, 11, 'JOB.6.11', 'What is my strength, that I should wait? What is my end, that I should be patient?'),
('JOB', 6, 12, 'JOB.6.12', 'Is my strength the strength of stones? Or is my flesh of bronze?'),
('JOB', 6, 13, 'JOB.6.13', 'Isn’t it that I have no help in me, that wisdom is driven away from me?'),
('JOB', 6, 14, 'JOB.6.14', '“To him who is ready to faint, kindness should be shown from his friend; even to him who forsakes the fear of the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 6, 15, 'JOB.6.15', 'My brothers have dealt deceitfully as a brook, as the channel of brooks that pass away;'),
('JOB', 6, 16, 'JOB.6.16', 'which are black by reason of the ice, in which the snow hides itself.'),
('JOB', 6, 17, 'JOB.6.17', 'In the dry season, they vanish. When it is hot, they are consumed out of their place.'),
('JOB', 6, 18, 'JOB.6.18', 'The caravans that travel beside them turn away. They go up into the waste, and perish.'),
('JOB', 6, 19, 'JOB.6.19', 'The caravans of Tema looked. The companies of Sheba waited for them.'),
('JOB', 6, 20, 'JOB.6.20', 'They were distressed because they were confident. They came there, and were confounded.'),
('JOB', 6, 21, 'JOB.6.21', 'For now you are nothing. You see a terror, and are afraid.'),
('JOB', 6, 22, 'JOB.6.22', 'Did I ever say, ‘Give to me’? or, ‘Offer a present for me from your substance’?'),
('JOB', 6, 23, 'JOB.6.23', 'or, ‘Deliver me from the adversary’s hand’? or, ‘Redeem me from the hand of the oppressors’?'),
('JOB', 6, 24, 'JOB.6.24', '“Teach me, and I will hold my peace. Cause me to understand my error.'),
('JOB', 6, 25, 'JOB.6.25', 'How forcible are words of uprightness! But your reproof, what does it reprove?'),
('JOB', 6, 26, 'JOB.6.26', 'Do you intend to reprove words, since the speeches of one who is desperate are as wind?'),
('JOB', 6, 27, 'JOB.6.27', 'Yes, you would even cast lots for the fatherless, and make merchandise of your friend.'),
('JOB', 6, 28, 'JOB.6.28', 'Now therefore be pleased to look at me, for surely I will not lie to your face.'),
('JOB', 6, 29, 'JOB.6.29', 'Please return. Let there be no injustice. Yes, return again. My cause is righteous.'),
('JOB', 6, 30, 'JOB.6.30', 'Is there injustice on my tongue? Can’t my taste discern mischievous things?'),
('JOB', 7, 1, 'JOB.7.1', '“Isn’t a man forced to labor on earth? Aren’t his days like the days of a hired hand?'),
('JOB', 7, 2, 'JOB.7.2', 'As a servant who earnestly desires the shadow, as a hireling who looks for his wages,'),
('JOB', 7, 3, 'JOB.7.3', 'so I am made to possess months of misery, wearisome nights are appointed to me.'),
('JOB', 7, 4, 'JOB.7.4', 'When I lie down, I say, ‘When will I arise, and the night be gone?’ I toss and turn until the dawning of the day.'),
('JOB', 7, 5, 'JOB.7.5', 'My flesh is clothed with worms and clods of dust. My skin closes up, and breaks out afresh.'),
('JOB', 7, 6, 'JOB.7.6', 'My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle, and are spent without hope.'),
('JOB', 7, 7, 'JOB.7.7', 'Oh remember that my life is a breath. My eye will no more see good.'),
('JOB', 7, 8, 'JOB.7.8', 'The eye of him who sees me will see me no more. Your eyes will be on me, but I will not be.'),
('JOB', 7, 9, 'JOB.7.9', 'As the cloud is consumed and vanishes away, so he who goes down to Sheol will come up no more.'),
('JOB', 7, 10, 'JOB.7.10', 'He will return no more to his house, neither will his place know him any more.'),
('JOB', 7, 11, 'JOB.7.11', '“Therefore I will not keep silent. I will speak in the anguish of my spirit. I will complain in the bitterness of my soul.'),
('JOB', 7, 12, 'JOB.7.12', 'Am I a sea, or a sea monster, that you put a guard over me?'),
('JOB', 7, 13, 'JOB.7.13', 'When I say, ‘My bed will comfort me. My couch will ease my complaint,’'),
('JOB', 7, 14, 'JOB.7.14', 'then you scare me with dreams and terrify me through visions,'),
('JOB', 7, 15, 'JOB.7.15', 'so that my soul chooses strangling, death rather than my bones.'),
('JOB', 7, 16, 'JOB.7.16', 'I loathe my life. I don’t want to live forever. Leave me alone, for my days are but a breath.'),
('JOB', 7, 17, 'JOB.7.17', 'What is man, that you should magnify him, that you should set your mind on him,'),
('JOB', 7, 18, 'JOB.7.18', 'that you should visit him every morning, and test him every moment?'),
('JOB', 7, 19, 'JOB.7.19', 'How long will you not look away from me, nor leave me alone until I swallow down my spittle?'),
('JOB', 7, 20, 'JOB.7.20', 'If I have sinned, what do I do to you, you watcher of men? Why have you set me as a mark for you, so that I am a burden to myself?'),
('JOB', 7, 21, 'JOB.7.21', 'Why do you not pardon my disobedience, and take away my iniquity? For now will I lie down in the dust. You will seek me diligently, but I will not be.”'),
('JOB', 8, 1, 'JOB.8.1', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,'),
('JOB', 8, 2, 'JOB.8.2', '“How long will you speak these things? Shall the words of your mouth be a mighty wind?'),
('JOB', 8, 3, 'JOB.8.3', 'Does God pervert justice? Or does the Almighty pervert righteousness?'),
('JOB', 8, 4, 'JOB.8.4', 'If your children have sinned against him, he has delivered them into the hand of their disobedience.'),
('JOB', 8, 5, 'JOB.8.5', 'If you want to seek God diligently, make your supplication to the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 8, 6, 'JOB.8.6', 'If you were pure and upright, surely now he would awaken for you, and make the habitation of your righteousness prosperous.'),
('JOB', 8, 7, 'JOB.8.7', 'Though your beginning was small, yet your latter end would greatly increase.'),
('JOB', 8, 8, 'JOB.8.8', '“Please inquire of past generations. Find out about the learning of their fathers.'),
('JOB', 8, 9, 'JOB.8.9', '(For we are but of yesterday, and know nothing, because our days on earth are a shadow.)'),
('JOB', 8, 10, 'JOB.8.10', 'Shall they not teach you, tell you, and utter words out of their heart?'),
('JOB', 8, 11, 'JOB.8.11', '“Can the papyrus grow up without mire? Can the rushes grow without water?'),
('JOB', 8, 12, 'JOB.8.12', 'While it is yet in its greenness, not cut down, it withers before any other reed.'),
('JOB', 8, 13, 'JOB.8.13', 'So are the paths of all who forget God. The hope of the godless man will perish,'),
('JOB', 8, 14, 'JOB.8.14', 'whose confidence will break apart, whose trust is a spider’s web.'),
('JOB', 8, 15, 'JOB.8.15', 'He will lean on his house, but it will not stand. He will cling to it, but it will not endure.'),
('JOB', 8, 16, 'JOB.8.16', 'He is green before the sun. His shoots go out along his garden.'),
('JOB', 8, 17, 'JOB.8.17', 'His roots are wrapped around the rock pile. He sees the place of stones.'),
('JOB', 8, 18, 'JOB.8.18', 'If he is destroyed from his place, then it will deny him, saying, ‘I have not seen you.’'),
('JOB', 8, 19, 'JOB.8.19', 'Behold, this is the joy of his way. Out of the earth, others will spring.'),
('JOB', 8, 20, 'JOB.8.20', '“Behold, God will not cast away a blameless man, neither will he uphold the evildoers.'),
('JOB', 8, 21, 'JOB.8.21', 'He will still fill your mouth with laughter, your lips with shouting.'),
('JOB', 8, 22, 'JOB.8.22', 'Those who hate you will be clothed with shame. The tent of the wicked will be no more.”'),
('JOB', 9, 1, 'JOB.9.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 9, 2, 'JOB.9.2', '“Truly I know that it is so, but how can man be just with God?'),
('JOB', 9, 3, 'JOB.9.3', 'If he is pleased to contend with him, he can’t answer him one time in a thousand.'),
('JOB', 9, 4, 'JOB.9.4', 'God is wise in heart, and mighty in strength. Who has hardened himself against him and prospered?'),
('JOB', 9, 5, 'JOB.9.5', 'He removes the mountains, and they don’t know it, when he overturns them in his anger.'),
('JOB', 9, 6, 'JOB.9.6', 'He shakes the earth out of its place. Its pillars tremble.'),
('JOB', 9, 7, 'JOB.9.7', 'He commands the sun and it doesn’t rise, and seals up the stars.'),
('JOB', 9, 8, 'JOB.9.8', 'He alone stretches out the heavens, and treads on the waves of the sea.'),
('JOB', 9, 9, 'JOB.9.9', 'He makes the Bear, Orion, and the Pleiades, and the rooms of the south.'),
('JOB', 9, 10, 'JOB.9.10', 'He does great things past finding out; yes, marvelous things without number.'),
('JOB', 9, 11, 'JOB.9.11', 'Behold, he goes by me, and I don’t see him. He passes on also, but I don’t perceive him.'),
('JOB', 9, 12, 'JOB.9.12', 'Behold, he snatches away. Who can hinder him? Who will ask him, ‘What are you doing?’'),
('JOB', 9, 13, 'JOB.9.13', '“God will not withdraw his anger. The helpers of Rahab stoop under him.'),
('JOB', 9, 14, 'JOB.9.14', 'How much less will I answer him, and choose my words to argue with him?'),
('JOB', 9, 15, 'JOB.9.15', 'Though I were righteous, yet I wouldn’t answer him. I would make supplication to my judge.'),
('JOB', 9, 16, 'JOB.9.16', 'If I had called, and he had answered me, yet I wouldn’t believe that he listened to my voice.'),
('JOB', 9, 17, 'JOB.9.17', 'For he breaks me with a storm, and multiplies my wounds without cause.'),
('JOB', 9, 18, 'JOB.9.18', 'He will not allow me to catch my breath, but fills me with bitterness.'),
('JOB', 9, 19, 'JOB.9.19', 'If it is a matter of strength, behold, he is mighty! If of justice, ‘Who,’ says he, ‘will summon me?’'),
('JOB', 9, 20, 'JOB.9.20', 'Though I am righteous, my own mouth will condemn me. Though I am blameless, it will prove me perverse.'),
('JOB', 9, 21, 'JOB.9.21', 'I am blameless. I don’t respect myself. I despise my life.'),
('JOB', 9, 22, 'JOB.9.22', '“It is all the same. Therefore I say he destroys the blameless and the wicked.'),
('JOB', 9, 23, 'JOB.9.23', 'If the scourge kills suddenly, he will mock at the trial of the innocent.'),
('JOB', 9, 24, 'JOB.9.24', 'The earth is given into the hand of the wicked. He covers the faces of its judges. If not he, then who is it?'),
('JOB', 9, 25, 'JOB.9.25', '“Now my days are swifter than a runner. They flee away. They see no good.'),
('JOB', 9, 26, 'JOB.9.26', 'They have passed away as the swift ships, as the eagle that swoops on the prey.'),
('JOB', 9, 27, 'JOB.9.27', 'If I say, ‘I will forget my complaint, I will put off my sad face, and cheer up,’'),
('JOB', 9, 28, 'JOB.9.28', 'I am afraid of all my sorrows. I know that you will not hold me innocent.'),
('JOB', 9, 29, 'JOB.9.29', 'I will be condemned. Why then do I labor in vain?'),
('JOB', 9, 30, 'JOB.9.30', 'If I wash myself with snow, and cleanse my hands with lye,'),
('JOB', 9, 31, 'JOB.9.31', 'yet you will plunge me in the ditch. My own clothes will abhor me.'),
('JOB', 9, 32, 'JOB.9.32', 'For he is not a man, as I am, that I should answer him, that we should come together in judgment.'),
('JOB', 9, 33, 'JOB.9.33', 'There is no umpire between us, that might lay his hand on us both.'),
('JOB', 9, 34, 'JOB.9.34', 'Let him take his rod away from me. Let his terror not make me afraid;'),
('JOB', 9, 35, 'JOB.9.35', 'then I would speak, and not fear him, for I am not so in myself.'),
('JOB', 10, 1, 'JOB.10.1', '“My soul is weary of my life. I will give free course to my complaint. I will speak in the bitterness of my soul.'),
('JOB', 10, 2, 'JOB.10.2', 'I will tell God, ‘Do not condemn me. Show me why you contend with me.'),
('JOB', 10, 3, 'JOB.10.3', 'Is it good to you that you should oppress, that you should despise the work of your hands, and smile on the counsel of the wicked?'),
('JOB', 10, 4, 'JOB.10.4', 'Do you have eyes of flesh? Or do you see as man sees?'),
('JOB', 10, 5, 'JOB.10.5', 'Are your days as the days of mortals, or your years as man’s years,'),
('JOB', 10, 6, 'JOB.10.6', 'that you inquire after my iniquity, and search after my sin?'),
('JOB', 10, 7, 'JOB.10.7', 'Although you know that I am not wicked, there is no one who can deliver out of your hand.'),
('JOB', 10, 8, 'JOB.10.8', '“‘Your hands have framed me and fashioned me altogether, yet you destroy me.'),
('JOB', 10, 9, 'JOB.10.9', 'Remember, I beg you, that you have fashioned me as clay. Will you bring me into dust again?'),
('JOB', 10, 10, 'JOB.10.10', 'Haven’t you poured me out like milk, and curdled me like cheese?'),
('JOB', 10, 11, 'JOB.10.11', 'You have clothed me with skin and flesh, and knit me together with bones and sinews.'),
('JOB', 10, 12, 'JOB.10.12', 'You have granted me life and loving kindness. Your visitation has preserved my spirit.'),
('JOB', 10, 13, 'JOB.10.13', 'Yet you hid these things in your heart. I know that this is with you:'),
('JOB', 10, 14, 'JOB.10.14', 'if I sin, then you mark me. You will not acquit me from my iniquity.'),
('JOB', 10, 15, 'JOB.10.15', 'If I am wicked, woe to me. If I am righteous, I still will not lift up my head, being filled with disgrace, and conscious of my affliction.'),
('JOB', 10, 16, 'JOB.10.16', 'If my head is held high, you hunt me like a lion. Again you show yourself powerful to me.'),
('JOB', 10, 17, 'JOB.10.17', 'You renew your witnesses against me, and increase your indignation on me. Changes and warfare are with me.'),
('JOB', 10, 18, 'JOB.10.18', '“‘Why, then, have you brought me out of the womb? I wish I had given up the spirit, and no eye had seen me.'),
('JOB', 10, 19, 'JOB.10.19', 'I should have been as though I had not been. I should have been carried from the womb to the grave.'),
('JOB', 10, 20, 'JOB.10.20', 'Aren’t my days few? Stop! Leave me alone, that I may find a little comfort,'),
('JOB', 10, 21, 'JOB.10.21', 'before I go where I will not return from, to the land of darkness and of the shadow of death;'),
('JOB', 10, 22, 'JOB.10.22', 'the land dark as midnight, of the shadow of death, without any order, where the light is as midnight.’”'),
('JOB', 11, 1, 'JOB.11.1', 'Then Zophar, the Naamathite, answered,'),
('JOB', 11, 2, 'JOB.11.2', '“Shouldn’t the multitude of words be answered? Should a man full of talk be justified?'),
('JOB', 11, 3, 'JOB.11.3', 'Should your boastings make men hold their peace? When you mock, will no man make you ashamed?'),
('JOB', 11, 4, 'JOB.11.4', 'For you say, ‘My doctrine is pure. I am clean in your eyes.’'),
('JOB', 11, 5, 'JOB.11.5', 'But oh that God would speak, and open his lips against you,'),
('JOB', 11, 6, 'JOB.11.6', 'that he would show you the secrets of wisdom! For true wisdom has two sides. Know therefore that God exacts of you less than your iniquity deserves.'),
('JOB', 11, 7, 'JOB.11.7', '“Can you fathom the mystery of God? Or can you probe the limits of the Almighty?'),
('JOB', 11, 8, 'JOB.11.8', 'They are high as heaven. What can you do? They are deeper than Sheol. What can you know?'),
('JOB', 11, 9, 'JOB.11.9', 'Its measure is longer than the earth, and broader than the sea.'),
('JOB', 11, 10, 'JOB.11.10', 'If he passes by, or confines, or convenes a court, then who can oppose him?'),
('JOB', 11, 11, 'JOB.11.11', 'For he knows false men. He sees iniquity also, even though he doesn’t consider it.'),
('JOB', 11, 12, 'JOB.11.12', 'An empty-headed man becomes wise when a man is born as a wild donkey’s colt.'),
('JOB', 11, 13, 'JOB.11.13', '“If you set your heart aright, stretch out your hands toward him.'),
('JOB', 11, 14, 'JOB.11.14', 'If iniquity is in your hand, put it far away. Don’t let unrighteousness dwell in your tents.'),
('JOB', 11, 15, 'JOB.11.15', 'Surely then you will lift up your face without spot. Yes, you will be steadfast, and will not fear,'),
('JOB', 11, 16, 'JOB.11.16', 'for you will forget your misery. You will remember it like waters that have passed away.'),
('JOB', 11, 17, 'JOB.11.17', 'Life will be clearer than the noonday. Though there is darkness, it will be as the morning.'),
('JOB', 11, 18, 'JOB.11.18', 'You will be secure, because there is hope. Yes, you will search, and will take your rest in safety.'),
('JOB', 11, 19, 'JOB.11.19', 'Also you will lie down, and no one will make you afraid. Yes, many will court your favor.'),
('JOB', 11, 20, 'JOB.11.20', 'But the eyes of the wicked will fail. They will have no way to flee. Their hope will be the giving up of the spirit.”'),
('JOB', 12, 1, 'JOB.12.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 12, 2, 'JOB.12.2', '“No doubt, but you are the people, and wisdom will die with you.'),
('JOB', 12, 3, 'JOB.12.3', 'But I have understanding as well as you; I am not inferior to you. Yes, who doesn’t know such things as these?'),
('JOB', 12, 4, 'JOB.12.4', 'I am like one who is a joke to his neighbor, I, who called on God, and he answered. The just, the blameless man is a joke.'),
('JOB', 12, 5, 'JOB.12.5', 'In the thought of him who is at ease there is contempt for misfortune. It is ready for them whose foot slips.'),
('JOB', 12, 6, 'JOB.12.6', 'The tents of robbers prosper. Those who provoke God are secure, who carry their god in their hands.'),
('JOB', 12, 7, 'JOB.12.7', '“But ask the animals now, and they will teach you; the birds of the sky, and they will tell you.'),
('JOB', 12, 8, 'JOB.12.8', 'Or speak to the earth, and it will teach you. The fish of the sea will declare to you.'),
('JOB', 12, 9, 'JOB.12.9', 'Who doesn’t know that in all these, the LORD’s hand has done this,'),
('JOB', 12, 10, 'JOB.12.10', 'in whose hand is the life of every living thing, and the breath of all mankind?'),
('JOB', 12, 11, 'JOB.12.11', 'Doesn’t the ear try words, even as the palate tastes its food?'),
('JOB', 12, 12, 'JOB.12.12', 'With aged men is wisdom, in length of days understanding.'),
('JOB', 12, 13, 'JOB.12.13', '“With God is wisdom and might. He has counsel and understanding.'),
('JOB', 12, 14, 'JOB.12.14', 'Behold, he breaks down, and it can’t be built again. He imprisons a man, and there can be no release.'),
('JOB', 12, 15, 'JOB.12.15', 'Behold, he withholds the waters, and they dry up. Again, he sends them out, and they overturn the earth.'),
('JOB', 12, 16, 'JOB.12.16', 'With him is strength and wisdom. The deceived and the deceiver are his.'),
('JOB', 12, 17, 'JOB.12.17', 'He leads counselors away stripped. He makes judges fools.'),
('JOB', 12, 18, 'JOB.12.18', 'He loosens the bond of kings. He binds their waist with a belt.'),
('JOB', 12, 19, 'JOB.12.19', 'He leads priests away stripped, and overthrows the mighty.'),
('JOB', 12, 20, 'JOB.12.20', 'He removes the speech of those who are trusted, and takes away the understanding of the elders.'),
('JOB', 12, 21, 'JOB.12.21', 'He pours contempt on princes, and loosens the belt of the strong.'),
('JOB', 12, 22, 'JOB.12.22', 'He uncovers deep things out of darkness, and brings out to light the shadow of death.'),
('JOB', 12, 23, 'JOB.12.23', 'He increases the nations, and he destroys them. He enlarges the nations, and he leads them captive.'),
('JOB', 12, 24, 'JOB.12.24', 'He takes away understanding from the chiefs of the people of the earth, and causes them to wander in a wilderness where there is no way.'),
('JOB', 12, 25, 'JOB.12.25', 'They grope in the dark without light. He makes them stagger like a drunken man.'),
('JOB', 13, 1, 'JOB.13.1', '“Behold, my eye has seen all this. My ear has heard and understood it.'),
('JOB', 13, 2, 'JOB.13.2', 'What you know, I know also. I am not inferior to you.'),
('JOB', 13, 3, 'JOB.13.3', '“Surely I would speak to the Almighty. I desire to reason with God.'),
('JOB', 13, 4, 'JOB.13.4', 'But you are forgers of lies. You are all physicians of no value.'),
('JOB', 13, 5, 'JOB.13.5', 'Oh that you would be completely silent! Then you would be wise.'),
('JOB', 13, 6, 'JOB.13.6', 'Hear now my reasoning. Listen to the pleadings of my lips.'),
('JOB', 13, 7, 'JOB.13.7', 'Will you speak unrighteously for God, and talk deceitfully for him?'),
('JOB', 13, 8, 'JOB.13.8', 'Will you show partiality to him? Will you contend for God?'),
('JOB', 13, 9, 'JOB.13.9', 'Is it good that he should search you out? Or as one deceives a man, will you deceive him?'),
('JOB', 13, 10, 'JOB.13.10', 'He will surely reprove you if you secretly show partiality.'),
('JOB', 13, 11, 'JOB.13.11', 'Won’t his majesty make you afraid and his dread fall on you?'),
('JOB', 13, 12, 'JOB.13.12', 'Your memorable sayings are proverbs of ashes. Your defenses are defenses of clay.'),
('JOB', 13, 13, 'JOB.13.13', '“Be silent! Leave me alone, that I may speak. Let come on me what will.'),
('JOB', 13, 14, 'JOB.13.14', 'Why should I take my flesh in my teeth, and put my life in my hand?'),
('JOB', 13, 15, 'JOB.13.15', 'Behold, he will kill me. I have no hope. Nevertheless, I will maintain my ways before him.'),
('JOB', 13, 16, 'JOB.13.16', 'This also will be my salvation, that a godless man will not come before him.'),
('JOB', 13, 17, 'JOB.13.17', 'Listen carefully to my speech. Let my declaration be in your ears.'),
('JOB', 13, 18, 'JOB.13.18', 'See now, I have set my cause in order. I know that I am righteous.'),
('JOB', 13, 19, 'JOB.13.19', 'Who is he who will contend with me? For then I would hold my peace and give up the spirit.'),
('JOB', 13, 20, 'JOB.13.20', '“Only don’t do two things to me, then I will not hide myself from your face:'),
('JOB', 13, 21, 'JOB.13.21', 'withdraw your hand far from me, and don’t let your terror make me afraid.'),
('JOB', 13, 22, 'JOB.13.22', 'Then call, and I will answer, or let me speak, and you answer me.'),
('JOB', 13, 23, 'JOB.13.23', 'How many are my iniquities and sins? Make me know my disobedience and my sin.'),
('JOB', 13, 24, 'JOB.13.24', 'Why do you hide your face, and consider me your enemy?'),
('JOB', 13, 25, 'JOB.13.25', 'Will you harass a driven leaf? Will you pursue the dry stubble?'),
('JOB', 13, 26, 'JOB.13.26', 'For you write bitter things against me, and make me inherit the iniquities of my youth.'),
('JOB', 13, 27, 'JOB.13.27', 'You also put my feet in the stocks, and mark all my paths. You set a bound to the soles of my feet,'),
('JOB', 13, 28, 'JOB.13.28', 'though I am decaying like a rotten thing, like a garment that is moth-eaten.'),
('JOB', 14, 1, 'JOB.14.1', '“Man, who is born of a woman, is of few days, and full of trouble.'),
('JOB', 14, 2, 'JOB.14.2', 'He grows up like a flower, and is cut down. He also flees like a shadow, and doesn’t continue.'),
('JOB', 14, 3, 'JOB.14.3', 'Do you open your eyes on such a one, and bring me into judgment with you?'),
('JOB', 14, 4, 'JOB.14.4', 'Who can bring a clean thing out of an unclean? Not one.'),
('JOB', 14, 5, 'JOB.14.5', 'Seeing his days are determined, the number of his months is with you, and you have appointed his bounds that he can’t pass.'),
('JOB', 14, 6, 'JOB.14.6', 'Look away from him, that he may rest, until he accomplishes, as a hireling, his day.'),
('JOB', 14, 7, 'JOB.14.7', '“For there is hope for a tree if it is cut down, that it will sprout again, that the tender branch of it will not cease.'),
('JOB', 14, 8, 'JOB.14.8', 'Though its root grows old in the earth, and its stock dies in the ground,'),
('JOB', 14, 9, 'JOB.14.9', 'yet through the scent of water it will bud, and sprout boughs like a plant.'),
('JOB', 14, 10, 'JOB.14.10', 'But man dies, and is laid low. Yes, man gives up the spirit, and where is he?'),
('JOB', 14, 11, 'JOB.14.11', 'As the waters fail from the sea, and the river wastes and dries up,'),
('JOB', 14, 12, 'JOB.14.12', 'so man lies down and doesn’t rise. Until the heavens are no more, they will not awake, nor be roused out of their sleep.'),
('JOB', 14, 13, 'JOB.14.13', '“Oh that you would hide me in Sheol, that you would keep me secret until your wrath is past, that you would appoint me a set time and remember me!'),
('JOB', 14, 14, 'JOB.14.14', 'If a man dies, will he live again? I would wait all the days of my warfare, until my release should come.'),
('JOB', 14, 15, 'JOB.14.15', 'You would call, and I would answer you. You would have a desire for the work of your hands.'),
('JOB', 14, 16, 'JOB.14.16', 'But now you count my steps. Don’t you watch over my sin?'),
('JOB', 14, 17, 'JOB.14.17', 'My disobedience is sealed up in a bag. You fasten up my iniquity.'),
('JOB', 14, 18, 'JOB.14.18', '“But the mountain falling comes to nothing. The rock is removed out of its place.'),
('JOB', 14, 19, 'JOB.14.19', 'The waters wear the stones. The torrents of it wash away the dust of the earth. So you destroy the hope of man.'),
('JOB', 14, 20, 'JOB.14.20', 'You forever prevail against him, and he departs. You change his face, and send him away.'),
('JOB', 14, 21, 'JOB.14.21', 'His sons come to honor, and he doesn’t know it. They are brought low, but he doesn’t perceive it of them.'),
('JOB', 14, 22, 'JOB.14.22', 'But his flesh on him has pain, and his soul within him mourns.”'),
('JOB', 15, 1, 'JOB.15.1', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered,'),
('JOB', 15, 2, 'JOB.15.2', '“Should a wise man answer with vain knowledge, and fill himself with the east wind?'),
('JOB', 15, 3, 'JOB.15.3', 'Should he reason with unprofitable talk, or with speeches with which he can do no good?'),
('JOB', 15, 4, 'JOB.15.4', 'Yes, you do away with fear, and hinder devotion before God.'),
('JOB', 15, 5, 'JOB.15.5', 'For your iniquity teaches your mouth, and you choose the language of the crafty.'),
('JOB', 15, 6, 'JOB.15.6', 'Your own mouth condemns you, and not I. Yes, your own lips testify against you.'),
('JOB', 15, 7, 'JOB.15.7', '“Are you the first man who was born? Or were you brought out before the hills?'),
('JOB', 15, 8, 'JOB.15.8', 'Have you heard the secret counsel of God? Do you limit wisdom to yourself?'),
('JOB', 15, 9, 'JOB.15.9', 'What do you know that we don’t know? What do you understand which is not in us?'),
('JOB', 15, 10, 'JOB.15.10', 'With us are both the gray-headed and the very aged men, much older than your father.'),
('JOB', 15, 11, 'JOB.15.11', 'Are the consolations of God too small for you, even the word that is gentle toward you?'),
('JOB', 15, 12, 'JOB.15.12', 'Why does your heart carry you away? Why do your eyes flash,'),
('JOB', 15, 13, 'JOB.15.13', 'that you turn your spirit against God, and let such words go out of your mouth?'),
('JOB', 15, 14, 'JOB.15.14', 'What is man, that he should be clean? What is he who is born of a woman, that he should be righteous?'),
('JOB', 15, 15, 'JOB.15.15', 'Behold, he puts no trust in his holy ones. Yes, the heavens are not clean in his sight;'),
('JOB', 15, 16, 'JOB.15.16', 'how much less one who is abominable and corrupt, a man who drinks iniquity like water!'),
('JOB', 15, 17, 'JOB.15.17', '“I will show you, listen to me; that which I have seen I will declare'),
('JOB', 15, 18, 'JOB.15.18', '(which wise men have told by their fathers, and have not hidden it;'),
('JOB', 15, 19, 'JOB.15.19', 'to whom alone the land was given, and no stranger passed among them):'),
('JOB', 15, 20, 'JOB.15.20', 'the wicked man writhes in pain all his days, even the number of years that are laid up for the oppressor.'),
('JOB', 15, 21, 'JOB.15.21', 'A sound of terrors is in his ears. In prosperity the destroyer will come on him.'),
('JOB', 15, 22, 'JOB.15.22', 'He doesn’t believe that he will return out of darkness. He is waited for by the sword.'),
('JOB', 15, 23, 'JOB.15.23', 'He wanders abroad for bread, saying, ‘Where is it?’ He knows that the day of darkness is ready at his hand.'),
('JOB', 15, 24, 'JOB.15.24', 'Distress and anguish make him afraid. They prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle.'),
('JOB', 15, 25, 'JOB.15.25', 'Because he has stretched out his hand against God, and behaves himself proudly against the Almighty,'),
('JOB', 15, 26, 'JOB.15.26', 'he runs at him with a stiff neck, with the thick shields of his bucklers,'),
('JOB', 15, 27, 'JOB.15.27', 'because he has covered his face with his fatness, and gathered fat on his thighs.'),
('JOB', 15, 28, 'JOB.15.28', 'He has lived in desolate cities, in houses which no one inhabited, which were ready to become heaps.'),
('JOB', 15, 29, 'JOB.15.29', 'He will not be rich, neither will his substance continue, neither will their possessions be extended on the earth.'),
('JOB', 15, 30, 'JOB.15.30', 'He will not depart out of darkness. The flame will dry up his branches. He will go away by the breath of God’s mouth.'),
('JOB', 15, 31, 'JOB.15.31', 'Let him not trust in emptiness, deceiving himself, for emptiness will be his reward.'),
('JOB', 15, 32, 'JOB.15.32', 'It will be accomplished before his time. His branch will not be green.'),
('JOB', 15, 33, 'JOB.15.33', 'He will shake off his unripe grape as the vine, and will cast off his flower as the olive tree.'),
('JOB', 15, 34, 'JOB.15.34', 'For the company of the godless will be barren, and fire will consume the tents of bribery.'),
('JOB', 15, 35, 'JOB.15.35', 'They conceive mischief and produce iniquity. Their heart prepares deceit.”'),
('JOB', 16, 1, 'JOB.16.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 16, 2, 'JOB.16.2', '“I have heard many such things. You are all miserable comforters!'),
('JOB', 16, 3, 'JOB.16.3', 'Shall vain words have an end? Or what provokes you that you answer?'),
('JOB', 16, 4, 'JOB.16.4', 'I also could speak as you do. If your soul were in my soul’s place, I could join words together against you, and shake my head at you,'),
('JOB', 16, 5, 'JOB.16.5', 'but I would strengthen you with my mouth. The solace of my lips would relieve you.'),
('JOB', 16, 6, 'JOB.16.6', '“Though I speak, my grief is not subsided. Though I forbear, what am I eased?'),
('JOB', 16, 7, 'JOB.16.7', 'But now, God, you have surely worn me out. You have made all my company desolate.'),
('JOB', 16, 8, 'JOB.16.8', 'You have shriveled me up. This is a witness against me. My leanness rises up against me. It testifies to my face.'),
('JOB', 16, 9, 'JOB.16.9', 'He has torn me in his wrath and persecuted me. He has gnashed on me with his teeth. My adversary sharpens his eyes on me.'),
('JOB', 16, 10, 'JOB.16.10', 'They have gaped on me with their mouth. They have struck me on the cheek reproachfully. They gather themselves together against me.'),
('JOB', 16, 11, 'JOB.16.11', 'God delivers me to the ungodly, and casts me into the hands of the wicked.'),
('JOB', 16, 12, 'JOB.16.12', 'I was at ease, and he broke me apart. Yes, he has taken me by the neck, and dashed me to pieces. He has also set me up for his target.'),
('JOB', 16, 13, 'JOB.16.13', 'His archers surround me. He splits my kidneys apart, and does not spare. He pours out my bile on the ground.'),
('JOB', 16, 14, 'JOB.16.14', 'He breaks me with breach on breach. He runs at me like a giant.'),
('JOB', 16, 15, 'JOB.16.15', 'I have sewed sackcloth on my skin, and have thrust my horn in the dust.'),
('JOB', 16, 16, 'JOB.16.16', 'My face is red with weeping. Deep darkness is on my eyelids,'),
('JOB', 16, 17, 'JOB.16.17', 'although there is no violence in my hands, and my prayer is pure.'),
('JOB', 16, 18, 'JOB.16.18', '“Earth, don’t cover my blood. Let my cry have no place to rest.'),
('JOB', 16, 19, 'JOB.16.19', 'Even now, behold, my witness is in heaven. He who vouches for me is on high.'),
('JOB', 16, 20, 'JOB.16.20', 'My friends scoff at me. My eyes pour out tears to God,'),
('JOB', 16, 21, 'JOB.16.21', 'that he would maintain the right of a man with God, of a son of man with his neighbor!'),
('JOB', 16, 22, 'JOB.16.22', 'For when a few years have come, I will go the way of no return.'),
('JOB', 17, 1, 'JOB.17.1', '“My spirit is consumed. My days are extinct and the grave is ready for me.'),
('JOB', 17, 2, 'JOB.17.2', 'Surely there are mockers with me. My eye dwells on their provocation.'),
('JOB', 17, 3, 'JOB.17.3', '“Now give a pledge. Be collateral for me with yourself. Who is there who will strike hands with me?'),
('JOB', 17, 4, 'JOB.17.4', 'For you have hidden their heart from understanding, therefore you will not exalt them.'),
('JOB', 17, 5, 'JOB.17.5', 'He who denounces his friends for plunder, even the eyes of his children will fail.'),
('JOB', 17, 6, 'JOB.17.6', '“But he has made me a byword of the people. They spit in my face.'),
('JOB', 17, 7, 'JOB.17.7', 'My eye also is dim by reason of sorrow. All my members are as a shadow.'),
('JOB', 17, 8, 'JOB.17.8', 'Upright men will be astonished at this. The innocent will stir himself up against the godless.'),
('JOB', 17, 9, 'JOB.17.9', 'Yet the righteous will hold to his way. He who has clean hands will grow stronger and stronger.'),
('JOB', 17, 10, 'JOB.17.10', 'But as for you all, come back. I will not find a wise man among you.'),
('JOB', 17, 11, 'JOB.17.11', 'My days are past. My plans are broken off, as are the thoughts of my heart.'),
('JOB', 17, 12, 'JOB.17.12', 'They change the night into day, saying ‘The light is near’ in the presence of darkness.'),
('JOB', 17, 13, 'JOB.17.13', 'If I look for Sheol as my house, if I have spread my couch in the darkness,'),
('JOB', 17, 14, 'JOB.17.14', 'if I have said to corruption, ‘You are my father,’ and to the worm, ‘My mother,’ and ‘My sister,’'),
('JOB', 17, 15, 'JOB.17.15', 'where then is my hope? As for my hope, who will see it?'),
('JOB', 17, 16, 'JOB.17.16', 'Shall it go down with me to the gates of Sheol, or descend together into the dust?”'),
('JOB', 18, 1, 'JOB.18.1', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,'),
('JOB', 18, 2, 'JOB.18.2', '“How long will you hunt for words? Consider, and afterwards we will speak.'),
('JOB', 18, 3, 'JOB.18.3', 'Why are we counted as animals, which have become unclean in your sight?'),
('JOB', 18, 4, 'JOB.18.4', 'You who tear yourself in your anger, will the earth be forsaken for you? Or will the rock be removed out of its place?'),
('JOB', 18, 5, 'JOB.18.5', '“Yes, the light of the wicked will be put out. The spark of his fire won’t shine.'),
('JOB', 18, 6, 'JOB.18.6', 'The light will be dark in his tent. His lamp above him will be put out.'),
('JOB', 18, 7, 'JOB.18.7', 'The steps of his strength will be shortened. His own counsel will cast him down.'),
('JOB', 18, 8, 'JOB.18.8', 'For he is cast into a net by his own feet, and he wanders into its mesh.'),
('JOB', 18, 9, 'JOB.18.9', 'A snare will take him by the heel. A trap will catch him.'),
('JOB', 18, 10, 'JOB.18.10', 'A noose is hidden for him in the ground, a trap for him on the path.'),
('JOB', 18, 11, 'JOB.18.11', 'Terrors will make him afraid on every side, and will chase him at his heels.'),
('JOB', 18, 12, 'JOB.18.12', 'His strength will be famished. Calamity will be ready at his side.'),
('JOB', 18, 13, 'JOB.18.13', 'The members of his body will be devoured. The firstborn of death will devour his members.'),
('JOB', 18, 14, 'JOB.18.14', 'He will be rooted out of the security of his tent. He will be brought to the king of terrors.'),
('JOB', 18, 15, 'JOB.18.15', 'There will dwell in his tent that which is none of his. Sulfur will be scattered on his habitation.'),
('JOB', 18, 16, 'JOB.18.16', 'His roots will be dried up beneath. His branch will be cut off above.'),
('JOB', 18, 17, 'JOB.18.17', 'His memory will perish from the earth. He will have no name in the street.'),
('JOB', 18, 18, 'JOB.18.18', 'He will be driven from light into darkness, and chased out of the world.'),
('JOB', 18, 19, 'JOB.18.19', 'He will have neither son nor grandson among his people, nor any remaining where he lived.'),
('JOB', 18, 20, 'JOB.18.20', 'Those who come after will be astonished at his day, as those who went before were frightened.'),
('JOB', 18, 21, 'JOB.18.21', 'Surely such are the dwellings of the unrighteous. This is the place of him who doesn’t know God.”'),
('JOB', 19, 1, 'JOB.19.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 19, 2, 'JOB.19.2', '“How long will you torment me, and crush me with words?'),
('JOB', 19, 3, 'JOB.19.3', 'You have reproached me ten times. You aren’t ashamed that you attack me.'),
('JOB', 19, 4, 'JOB.19.4', 'If it is true that I have erred, my error remains with myself.'),
('JOB', 19, 5, 'JOB.19.5', 'If indeed you will magnify yourselves against me, and plead against me my reproach,'),
('JOB', 19, 6, 'JOB.19.6', 'know now that God has subverted me, and has surrounded me with his net.'),
('JOB', 19, 7, 'JOB.19.7', '“Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard. I cry for help, but there is no justice.'),
('JOB', 19, 8, 'JOB.19.8', 'He has walled up my way so that I can’t pass, and has set darkness in my paths.'),
('JOB', 19, 9, 'JOB.19.9', 'He has stripped me of my glory, and taken the crown from my head.'),
('JOB', 19, 10, 'JOB.19.10', 'He has broken me down on every side, and I am gone. He has plucked my hope up like a tree.'),
('JOB', 19, 11, 'JOB.19.11', 'He has also kindled his wrath against me. He counts me among his adversaries.'),
('JOB', 19, 12, 'JOB.19.12', 'His troops come on together, build a siege ramp against me, and encamp around my tent.'),
('JOB', 19, 13, 'JOB.19.13', '“He has put my brothers far from me. My acquaintances are wholly estranged from me.'),
('JOB', 19, 14, 'JOB.19.14', 'My relatives have gone away. My familiar friends have forgotten me.'),
('JOB', 19, 15, 'JOB.19.15', 'Those who dwell in my house and my maids consider me a stranger. I am an alien in their sight.'),
('JOB', 19, 16, 'JOB.19.16', 'I call to my servant, and he gives me no answer. I beg him with my mouth.'),
('JOB', 19, 17, 'JOB.19.17', 'My breath is offensive to my wife. I am loathsome to the children of my own mother.'),
('JOB', 19, 18, 'JOB.19.18', 'Even young children despise me. If I arise, they speak against me.'),
('JOB', 19, 19, 'JOB.19.19', 'All my familiar friends abhor me. They whom I loved have turned against me.'),
('JOB', 19, 20, 'JOB.19.20', 'My bones stick to my skin and to my flesh. I have escaped by the skin of my teeth.'),
('JOB', 19, 21, 'JOB.19.21', '“Have pity on me. Have pity on me, you my friends, for the hand of God has touched me.'),
('JOB', 19, 22, 'JOB.19.22', 'Why do you persecute me as God, and are not satisfied with my flesh?'),
('JOB', 19, 23, 'JOB.19.23', '“Oh that my words were now written! Oh that they were inscribed in a book!'),
('JOB', 19, 24, 'JOB.19.24', 'That with an iron pen and lead they were engraved in the rock forever!'),
('JOB', 19, 25, 'JOB.19.25', 'But as for me, I know that my Redeemer lives. In the end, he will stand upon the earth.'),
('JOB', 19, 26, 'JOB.19.26', 'After my skin is destroyed, then I will see God in my flesh,'),
('JOB', 19, 27, 'JOB.19.27', 'whom I, even I, will see on my side. My eyes will see, and not as a stranger. “My heart is consumed within me.'),
('JOB', 19, 28, 'JOB.19.28', 'If you say, ‘How we will persecute him!’ because the root of the matter is found in me,'),
('JOB', 19, 29, 'JOB.19.29', 'be afraid of the sword, for wrath brings the punishments of the sword, that you may know there is a judgment.”'),
('JOB', 20, 1, 'JOB.20.1', 'Then Zophar the Naamathite answered,'),
('JOB', 20, 2, 'JOB.20.2', '“Therefore my thoughts answer me, even by reason of my haste that is in me.'),
('JOB', 20, 3, 'JOB.20.3', 'I have heard the reproof which puts me to shame. The spirit of my understanding answers me.'),
('JOB', 20, 4, 'JOB.20.4', 'Don’t you know this from old time, since man was placed on earth,'),
('JOB', 20, 5, 'JOB.20.5', 'that the triumphing of the wicked is short, the joy of the godless but for a moment?'),
('JOB', 20, 6, 'JOB.20.6', 'Though his height mount up to the heavens, and his head reach to the clouds,'),
('JOB', 20, 7, 'JOB.20.7', 'yet he will perish forever like his own dung. Those who have seen him will say, ‘Where is he?’'),
('JOB', 20, 8, 'JOB.20.8', 'He will fly away as a dream, and will not be found. Yes, he will be chased away like a vision of the night.'),
('JOB', 20, 9, 'JOB.20.9', 'The eye which saw him will see him no more, neither will his place see him any more.'),
('JOB', 20, 10, 'JOB.20.10', 'His children will seek the favor of the poor. His hands will give back his wealth.'),
('JOB', 20, 11, 'JOB.20.11', 'His bones are full of his youth, but youth will lie down with him in the dust.'),
('JOB', 20, 12, 'JOB.20.12', '“Though wickedness is sweet in his mouth, though he hide it under his tongue,'),
('JOB', 20, 13, 'JOB.20.13', 'though he spare it, and will not let it go, but keep it still within his mouth,'),
('JOB', 20, 14, 'JOB.20.14', 'yet his food in his bowels is turned. It is cobra venom within him.'),
('JOB', 20, 15, 'JOB.20.15', 'He has swallowed down riches, and he will vomit them up again. God will cast them out of his belly.'),
('JOB', 20, 16, 'JOB.20.16', 'He will suck cobra venom. The viper’s tongue will kill him.'),
('JOB', 20, 17, 'JOB.20.17', 'He will not look at the rivers, the flowing streams of honey and butter.'),
('JOB', 20, 18, 'JOB.20.18', 'He will restore that for which he labored, and will not swallow it down. He will not rejoice according to the substance that he has gotten.'),
('JOB', 20, 19, 'JOB.20.19', 'For he has oppressed and forsaken the poor. He has violently taken away a house, and he will not build it up.'),
('JOB', 20, 20, 'JOB.20.20', '“Because he knew no quietness within him, he will not save anything of that in which he delights.'),
('JOB', 20, 21, 'JOB.20.21', 'There was nothing left that he didn’t devour, therefore his prosperity will not endure.'),
('JOB', 20, 22, 'JOB.20.22', 'In the fullness of his sufficiency, distress will overtake him. The hand of everyone who is in misery will come on him.'),
('JOB', 20, 23, 'JOB.20.23', 'When he is about to fill his belly, God will cast the fierceness of his wrath on him. It will rain on him while he is eating.'),
('JOB', 20, 24, 'JOB.20.24', 'He will flee from the iron weapon. The bronze arrow will strike him through.'),
('JOB', 20, 25, 'JOB.20.25', 'He draws it out, and it comes out of his body. Yes, the glittering point comes out of his liver. Terrors are on him.'),
('JOB', 20, 26, 'JOB.20.26', 'All darkness is laid up for his treasures. An unfanned fire will devour him. It will consume that which is left in his tent.'),
('JOB', 20, 27, 'JOB.20.27', 'The heavens will reveal his iniquity. The earth will rise up against him.'),
('JOB', 20, 28, 'JOB.20.28', 'The increase of his house will depart. They will rush away in the day of his wrath.'),
('JOB', 20, 29, 'JOB.20.29', 'This is the portion of a wicked man from God, the heritage appointed to him by God.”'),
('JOB', 21, 1, 'JOB.21.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 21, 2, 'JOB.21.2', '“Listen diligently to my speech. Let this be your consolation.'),
('JOB', 21, 3, 'JOB.21.3', 'Allow me, and I also will speak. After I have spoken, mock on.'),
('JOB', 21, 4, 'JOB.21.4', 'As for me, is my complaint to man? Why shouldn’t I be impatient?'),
('JOB', 21, 5, 'JOB.21.5', 'Look at me, and be astonished. Lay your hand on your mouth.'),
('JOB', 21, 6, 'JOB.21.6', 'When I remember, I am troubled. Horror takes hold of my flesh.'),
('JOB', 21, 7, 'JOB.21.7', '“Why do the wicked live, become old, yes, and grow mighty in power?'),
('JOB', 21, 8, 'JOB.21.8', 'Their child is established with them in their sight, their offspring before their eyes.'),
('JOB', 21, 9, 'JOB.21.9', 'Their houses are safe from fear, neither is the rod of God upon them.'),
('JOB', 21, 10, 'JOB.21.10', 'Their bulls breed without fail. Their cows calve, and don’t miscarry.'),
('JOB', 21, 11, 'JOB.21.11', 'They send out their little ones like a flock. Their children dance.'),
('JOB', 21, 12, 'JOB.21.12', 'They sing to the tambourine and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the pipe.'),
('JOB', 21, 13, 'JOB.21.13', 'They spend their days in prosperity. In an instant they go down to Sheol.'),
('JOB', 21, 14, 'JOB.21.14', 'They tell God, ‘Depart from us, for we don’t want to know about your ways.'),
('JOB', 21, 15, 'JOB.21.15', 'What is the Almighty, that we should serve him? What profit should we have, if we pray to him?’'),
('JOB', 21, 16, 'JOB.21.16', 'Behold, their prosperity is not in their hand. The counsel of the wicked is far from me.'),
('JOB', 21, 17, 'JOB.21.17', '“How often is it that the lamp of the wicked is put out, that their calamity comes on them, that God distributes sorrows in his anger?'),
('JOB', 21, 18, 'JOB.21.18', 'How often is it that they are as stubble before the wind, as chaff that the storm carries away?'),
('JOB', 21, 19, 'JOB.21.19', 'You say, ‘God lays up his iniquity for his children.’ Let him recompense it to himself, that he may know it.'),
('JOB', 21, 20, 'JOB.21.20', 'Let his own eyes see his destruction. Let him drink of the wrath of the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 21, 21, 'JOB.21.21', 'For what does he care for his house after him, when the number of his months is cut off?'),
('JOB', 21, 22, 'JOB.21.22', '“Shall any teach God knowledge, since he judges those who are high?'),
('JOB', 21, 23, 'JOB.21.23', 'One dies in his full strength, being wholly at ease and quiet.'),
('JOB', 21, 24, 'JOB.21.24', 'His pails are full of milk. The marrow of his bones is moistened.'),
('JOB', 21, 25, 'JOB.21.25', 'Another dies in bitterness of soul, and never tastes of good.'),
('JOB', 21, 26, 'JOB.21.26', 'They lie down alike in the dust. The worm covers them.'),
('JOB', 21, 27, 'JOB.21.27', '“Behold, I know your thoughts, the plans with which you would wrong me.'),
('JOB', 21, 28, 'JOB.21.28', 'For you say, ‘Where is the house of the prince? Where is the tent in which the wicked lived?’'),
('JOB', 21, 29, 'JOB.21.29', 'Haven’t you asked wayfaring men? Don’t you know their evidences,'),
('JOB', 21, 30, 'JOB.21.30', 'that the evil man is reserved to the day of calamity, that they are led out to the day of wrath?'),
('JOB', 21, 31, 'JOB.21.31', 'Who will declare his way to his face? Who will repay him what he has done?'),
('JOB', 21, 32, 'JOB.21.32', 'Yet he will be borne to the grave. Men will keep watch over the tomb.'),
('JOB', 21, 33, 'JOB.21.33', 'The clods of the valley will be sweet to him. All men will draw after him, as there were innumerable before him.'),
('JOB', 21, 34, 'JOB.21.34', 'So how can you comfort me with nonsense, because in your answers there remains only falsehood?”'),
('JOB', 22, 1, 'JOB.22.1', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered,'),
('JOB', 22, 2, 'JOB.22.2', '“Can a man be profitable to God? Surely he who is wise is profitable to himself.'),
('JOB', 22, 3, 'JOB.22.3', 'Is it any pleasure to the Almighty that you are righteous? Or does it benefit him that you make your ways perfect?'),
('JOB', 22, 4, 'JOB.22.4', 'Is it for your piety that he reproves you, that he enters with you into judgment?'),
('JOB', 22, 5, 'JOB.22.5', 'Isn’t your wickedness great? Neither is there any end to your iniquities.'),
('JOB', 22, 6, 'JOB.22.6', 'For you have taken pledges from your brother for nothing, and stripped the naked of their clothing.'),
('JOB', 22, 7, 'JOB.22.7', 'You haven’t given water to the weary to drink, and you have withheld bread from the hungry.'),
('JOB', 22, 8, 'JOB.22.8', 'But as for the mighty man, he had the earth. The honorable man, he lived in it.'),
('JOB', 22, 9, 'JOB.22.9', 'You have sent widows away empty, and the arms of the fatherless have been broken.'),
('JOB', 22, 10, 'JOB.22.10', 'Therefore snares are around you. Sudden fear troubles you,'),
('JOB', 22, 11, 'JOB.22.11', 'or darkness, so that you can not see, and floods of waters cover you.'),
('JOB', 22, 12, 'JOB.22.12', '“Isn’t God in the heights of heaven? See the height of the stars, how high they are!'),
('JOB', 22, 13, 'JOB.22.13', 'You say, ‘What does God know? Can he judge through the thick darkness?'),
('JOB', 22, 14, 'JOB.22.14', 'Thick clouds are a covering to him, so that he doesn’t see. He walks on the vault of the sky.’'),
('JOB', 22, 15, 'JOB.22.15', 'Will you keep the old way, which wicked men have trodden,'),
('JOB', 22, 16, 'JOB.22.16', 'who were snatched away before their time, whose foundation was poured out as a stream,'),
('JOB', 22, 17, 'JOB.22.17', 'who said to God, ‘Depart from us!’ and, ‘What can the Almighty do for us?’'),
('JOB', 22, 18, 'JOB.22.18', 'Yet he filled their houses with good things, but the counsel of the wicked is far from me.'),
('JOB', 22, 19, 'JOB.22.19', 'The righteous see it, and are glad. The innocent ridicule them,'),
('JOB', 22, 20, 'JOB.22.20', 'saying, ‘Surely those who rose up against us are cut off. The fire has consumed their remnant.’'),
('JOB', 22, 21, 'JOB.22.21', '“Acquaint yourself with him now, and be at peace. By it, good will come to you.'),
('JOB', 22, 22, 'JOB.22.22', 'Please receive instruction from his mouth, and lay up his words in your heart.'),
('JOB', 22, 23, 'JOB.22.23', 'If you return to the Almighty, you will be built up, if you put away unrighteousness far from your tents.'),
('JOB', 22, 24, 'JOB.22.24', 'Lay your treasure in the dust, the gold of Ophir among the stones of the brooks.'),
('JOB', 22, 25, 'JOB.22.25', 'The Almighty will be your treasure, and precious silver to you.'),
('JOB', 22, 26, 'JOB.22.26', 'For then you will delight yourself in the Almighty, and will lift up your face to God.'),
('JOB', 22, 27, 'JOB.22.27', 'You will make your prayer to him, and he will hear you. You will pay your vows.'),
('JOB', 22, 28, 'JOB.22.28', 'You will also decree a thing, and it will be established to you. Light will shine on your ways.'),
('JOB', 22, 29, 'JOB.22.29', 'When they cast down, you will say, ‘be lifted up.’ He will save the humble person.'),
('JOB', 22, 30, 'JOB.22.30', 'He will even deliver him who is not innocent. Yes, he will be delivered through the cleanness of your hands.”'),
('JOB', 23, 1, 'JOB.23.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 23, 2, 'JOB.23.2', '“Even today my complaint is rebellious. His hand is heavy in spite of my groaning.'),
('JOB', 23, 3, 'JOB.23.3', 'Oh that I knew where I might find him! That I might come even to his seat!'),
('JOB', 23, 4, 'JOB.23.4', 'I would set my cause in order before him, and fill my mouth with arguments.'),
('JOB', 23, 5, 'JOB.23.5', 'I would know the words which he would answer me, and understand what he would tell me.'),
('JOB', 23, 6, 'JOB.23.6', 'Would he contend with me in the greatness of his power? No, but he would listen to me.'),
('JOB', 23, 7, 'JOB.23.7', 'There the upright might reason with him, so I should be delivered forever from my judge.'),
('JOB', 23, 8, 'JOB.23.8', '“If I go east, he is not there. If I go west, I can’t find him.'),
('JOB', 23, 9, 'JOB.23.9', 'He works to the north, but I can’t see him. He turns south, but I can’t catch a glimpse of him.'),
('JOB', 23, 10, 'JOB.23.10', 'But he knows the way that I take. When he has tried me, I will come out like gold.'),
('JOB', 23, 11, 'JOB.23.11', 'My foot has held fast to his steps. I have kept his way, and not turned away.'),
('JOB', 23, 12, 'JOB.23.12', 'I haven’t gone back from the commandment of his lips. I have treasured up the words of his mouth more than my necessary food.'),
('JOB', 23, 13, 'JOB.23.13', 'But he stands alone, and who can oppose him? What his soul desires, even that he does.'),
('JOB', 23, 14, 'JOB.23.14', 'For he performs that which is appointed for me. Many such things are with him.'),
('JOB', 23, 15, 'JOB.23.15', 'Therefore I am terrified at his presence. When I consider, I am afraid of him.'),
('JOB', 23, 16, 'JOB.23.16', 'For God has made my heart faint. The Almighty has terrified me.'),
('JOB', 23, 17, 'JOB.23.17', 'Because I was not cut off before the darkness, neither did he cover the thick darkness from my face.'),
('JOB', 24, 1, 'JOB.24.1', '“Why aren’t times laid up by the Almighty? Why don’t those who know him see his days?'),
('JOB', 24, 2, 'JOB.24.2', 'There are people who remove the landmarks. They violently take away flocks, and feed them.'),
('JOB', 24, 3, 'JOB.24.3', 'They drive away the donkey of the fatherless, and they take the widow’s ox for a pledge.'),
('JOB', 24, 4, 'JOB.24.4', 'They turn the needy out of the way. The poor of the earth all hide themselves.'),
('JOB', 24, 5, 'JOB.24.5', 'Behold, as wild donkeys in the desert, they go out to their work, seeking diligently for food. The wilderness yields them bread for their children.'),
('JOB', 24, 6, 'JOB.24.6', 'They cut their food in the field. They glean the vineyard of the wicked.'),
('JOB', 24, 7, 'JOB.24.7', 'They lie all night naked without clothing, and have no covering in the cold.'),
('JOB', 24, 8, 'JOB.24.8', 'They are wet with the showers of the mountains, and embrace the rock for lack of a shelter.'),
('JOB', 24, 9, 'JOB.24.9', 'There are those who pluck the fatherless from the breast, and take a pledge of the poor,'),
('JOB', 24, 10, 'JOB.24.10', 'so that they go around naked without clothing. Being hungry, they carry the sheaves.'),
('JOB', 24, 11, 'JOB.24.11', 'They make oil within the walls of these men. They tread wine presses, and suffer thirst.'),
('JOB', 24, 12, 'JOB.24.12', 'From out of the populous city, men groan. The soul of the wounded cries out, yet God doesn’t regard the folly.'),
('JOB', 24, 13, 'JOB.24.13', '“These are of those who rebel against the light. They don’t know its ways, nor stay in its paths.'),
('JOB', 24, 14, 'JOB.24.14', 'The murderer rises with the light. He kills the poor and needy. In the night he is like a thief.'),
('JOB', 24, 15, 'JOB.24.15', 'The eye also of the adulterer waits for the twilight, saying, ‘No eye will see me.’ He disguises his face.'),
('JOB', 24, 16, 'JOB.24.16', 'In the dark they dig through houses. They shut themselves up in the daytime. They don’t know the light.'),
('JOB', 24, 17, 'JOB.24.17', 'For the morning is to all of them like thick darkness, for they know the terrors of the thick darkness.'),
('JOB', 24, 18, 'JOB.24.18', '“They are foam on the surface of the waters. Their portion is cursed on the earth. They don’t turn into the way of the vineyards.'),
('JOB', 24, 19, 'JOB.24.19', 'Drought and heat consume the snow waters, so does Sheol those who have sinned.'),
('JOB', 24, 20, 'JOB.24.20', 'The womb will forget him. The worm will feed sweetly on him. He will be no more remembered. Unrighteousness will be broken as a tree.'),
('JOB', 24, 21, 'JOB.24.21', 'He devours the barren who don’t bear. He shows no kindness to the widow.'),
('JOB', 24, 22, 'JOB.24.22', 'Yet God preserves the mighty by his power. He rises up who has no assurance of life.')
) as x(osis, chapter, verse, ref, body)
join public.books b on b.osis_code = x.osis
join public.bible_versions v on v.id = b.version_id and v.code = 'WEB'
join public.chapters c on c.book_id = b.id and c.number = x.chapter
on conflict (chapter_id, number) do update set osis_ref = excluded.osis_ref, text = excluded.text;
